window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4001,"title":"Chapter 4001: Chapter 4000: Be The Scariest Monster! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes burned with brilliant intensity as understanding crystallized into ambition. The numbers were staggering, representing advancement potential that would have taken others eons to accumulate through conventional methods. His voice carried tyrannical certainty as he spoke his realization aloud.","\"It seems...I need to focus on hunting Duke-level entities.\"","The statement buzzed in the air like a declaration of war against the established order of existence itself!","He knew that currently, his power remained far below that of an Honored Living Existence, let alone a Duke. But if he could continue eliminating such beings through strategic positioning and clever use of his unique resources, if he could keep converting their deaths into nutrients for his advancement... he would catch up soon enough.","The golden sands beneath the corpses began to shift and churn, drawing the massive remains and scattered pieces into their depths with the patient hunger of something that knew how to wait for its meals.","The Shore itself was consuming them, breaking them down into components that could fuel advancement.","Another prompt materialized, this one requiring his direct input.","|Due to the overabundance of nutrients currently being processed, allocation distribution is required. The Early Veiled Shore requests guidance on nutrient distribution across multiple possible development priorities. Proposed allocation:","- 15% toward Plot Enhancement: Accelerate maturation of currently planted Sacred Herbs (Transcendent Veilmoss, Chronos Petrichor, Void-Heart Chrysanthemums, Echo Sage, Infinity’s Breath Orchids.. )","- 15% toward Tree Awakening: Enable the nine Early Sacred Trees to begin producing their first fruits","- 20% toward Shore Expansion: Further increase the territory of the Early Veiled Shore by an additional 200%","- 15% toward Leviathan’s Eternum Cage construction: Build an ancient early aquarium designed to automatically draw in and capture Early Living Marine Lifeforms. Once caught, no entity below Early Creature status can escape","- 35% toward Personal Enhancement: Accelerate forging of Towers of Osmont, advance completion of the second part of your Heart (Oruvian Shardveil - The Arterial Convergence Core), and finalize the Early Atlas of the Folds","Confirm allocation?]","...!","Noah gazed at the breakdown with calm and tyrannical excitement, his mind already calculating how each investment would compound into future advantages.","The Leviathan’s Eternum Cage particularly caught his attention...an automatic harvesting system for Marine Lifeforms would provide consistent nutrients without requiring his direct involvement.","\"Proceed,\" he commanded.","HUUM!","The eruption of brilliance that followed made reality itself take notice. The entire Early Veiled Shore pulsed with white-gold radiance that seemed to emerge from every grain of sand simultaneously.","Waves of concentrated authority rippled outward from the points where nutrients were being processed, each pulse carrying with it fundamental changes to the Shore’s nature.","Heidrun, who had been maintaining her vigil over the sacred herb plots with characteristic arrogance, suddenly rose to her feet with unprecedented excitement.","Her crystalline eyes widened as she witnessed golden light of impossible density bathing the plots she had been guarding. The herbs, which had been growing at their natural pace, suddenly began flourishing with explosive vitality. Leaves unfurled, stems thickened, and the very air around them began to shimmer with the potency of their accelerated maturation.","Noah began walking across the golden sands toward the shoreline, each step feeling like a ceremony of advancement.","Moiraine followed behind him, and he could hear her release a soft sigh as the worry finally left her expression. When he glanced back, she was smiling...not the careful, respectful smile she usually wore, but something genuine and warm.","She would simply trust that he knew what he was doing.","As he walked, prompts began cascading through his consciousness, each one marking another milestone in his impossible progression!","|Heart Component Progress - Oruvian Shardveil (The Arterial Convergence Core): 67% complete. Crystalline arterial networks forming. Blood production capacity increasing exponentially.|","|Current Blood of Early Creature reserves: 10,847 drops. Production rate has increased to 500 drops per hour due to enhanced Heart development.|","|Tower Advancement Notifications:","- Tower of Kuklos has achieved Second Stage: Temporal Architectonics","- Tower of Veritarch has achieved Second Stage: Truth’s Observatory","- Tower of Relativity has achieved Second Stage: Dimensional Anchor","- Tower of Ordo Ab Chao has achieved Second Stage: Pattern Manifestation","- Tower of Megalos has achieved Second Stage: Magnitude Amplification","- Tower of Conceptual has achieved Second Stage: Abstract Fortress","- Tower of Ingeniare has achieved Second Stage: Creative Matrix","- Tower of Outerversal has achieved Second Stage: Boundary Transcendence","- Tower of Eldritch Expanse has achieved Second Stage: Impossible Geometries","- Tower of Prana has achieved Second Stage: Life Force Citadel...","-Tower of Plot...]","Noah almost laughed as he saw the Early Veiled Shore going all out to even give unique names to the Towers of Osmont experiencing their advancement to the Second Stage.","When Noah closed his eyes, the sensation that washed over him defied description.","He could feel the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore infusing him with tremendous glory, each grain seemingly connected to his existence through threads of pure authority.","Every step he took sent waves of gold surging through his being...into every cell, every atom, every synapse. It was as if the Shore itself had become an extension of his body, or perhaps his body had become an extension of the Shore!","The feeling was utterly indescribable, a symphony of advancement playing through his very existence. Power became him, each pulse of nutrients reshaping fundamental aspects of his nature.","His muscles densed with strength that transcended the physical, his bones crystallized with durability that mocked conventional limits, his mind expanded to accommodate understanding that would have shattered lesser consciousness.","When he opened his eyes again, he stood near the waters of the Shore. The crystalline waves lapped at the sand with gentle insistence, each surge carrying whispers of the Marine Lifeforms that dwelt in their depths.","To his right, he could see the construction beginning...massive pillars of crystallized authority rising from the sands as the Leviathan’s Eternum Cage began taking shape.","The structure was magnificent even in its earliest stages. Archways of compressed space curved impossibly, creating passages that existed in more dimensions than the eye could properly follow. The foundation gleamed with runes and Glyphs that seemed to write themselves into existence, each symbol a law that would govern the Cage’s operation.","It would be beautiful and terrible...a trap that offered no escape, a prison that Marine Lifeforms would swim into willingly, drawn by currents they couldn’t resist.","Alongside all of this...","[Current Complexity Quotient: 897,442,318]","[Current Purity Quotient: 901,765,429]","The numbers blazed across his consciousness with the weight of achievement.","It was...maddening if others ever knew how quickly he was doing all this!","He was approaching one billion in both measurements...the threshold where he could form his first Kleos Glyph, that ultimate expression of power that transcended normal limitations.","Noah stood watching the Leviathan’s Eternum Cage take shape, its emerging form promising automated harvest of resources that would fuel endless advancement.","He was savoring these moments, enjoying the boons that came after heavy war, knowing full well that the landscape of existence was about to change dramatically.","The ramifications of what had occurred in the Temporal Folds would ripple outward.","The emergence of Dead Existences, the intervention of Living Paradoxes, his own display of power and Moiraine....all of it would reshape how the great powers viewed each other and their positions in the hierarchy of existence.","And he would be a participant in whatever came next. His eyes gazed into the distance as his mind reached out to his other body, still maintaining his merchant persona in Aeternitas Concordia.","He expected Duke Gwendolyn to approach that body very soon, drawn by questions and possibilities that his display had created.","Through that interaction, he might be able to observe the reshaping of Living Existence hierarchy in real time, positioning himself to take advantage of whatever opportunities emerged.","The Shore pulsed around him with renewed vitality, each breath he took filled with the scent of advancement and possibility!","The sacred herbs reached toward maturity, the trees prepared to bear fruit, and in the depths of the expanding waters, new Marine Lifeforms began to spawn, drawn by the irresistible authority of an Early Creature’s domain.","He had transformed a battlefield into a harvest, converted death into life, turned endings into new beginnings. And this...was only the glorious and magisterial beginning of what he would accomplish!"]},{"number":4002,"title":"Chapter 4002: Chapter 4001: The 10 Living Existences! I","paragraphs":["Life could change so rapidly that one found themselves in places they never imagined they would be just days or months ago.","The whims of existence possessed a particularly cruel sense of humor...one could be a grand teacher of existential philosophy one day, revered across multiple Wheels and Dwellings for their wisdom, and find themselves shaking their body for cash at a seedy establishment the next, simply because existence had decided to restructure itself overnight!","The mighty could fall, the fallen could rise, and sometimes, if existence was feeling particularly creative, both could happen simultaneously to the same being.","Existence could truly change too fast!","---","In a certain Law Fold, removed from the chaos of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, such rapid change had become the defining characteristic of one particular being’s recent experiences.","Bob... who had managed to lock away Thauron, the Null Monarch, inside an Inevitability...walked through corridors of crystallized authority with movements that suggested he was still adjusting to his transformed state!","His form had evolved into an obsidian-white humanoid figure with skin that seemed to shift between solid and liquid states, crowned by a perfectly round, bald head that gleamed under the ambient light of Law itself.","He was now...a glorious Living Origin!","He followed in the wake of two beings whose presence made the very air taste of structured power. Altheon moved ahead with the distracted air of someone whose mind wrestled with problems far removed from their current location, his luminous form occasionally flickering as if his consciousness kept trying to be elsewhere.","Beside him bounced...there was no other word for her manner of movement- a Prime Living Law whose very existence seemed to radiate barely contained enthusiasm.","Her pink hair defied gravity, while her matching pink eyes sparkled with the kind of vivacious energy that made others simultaneously exhausted and energized just from proximity!","She wore robes that should have been formal, authoritative, befitting her status as a Prime Living Law, but somehow she made them look like party attire through sheer force of personality.","Living Law Authority wrapped around them in spiraling patterns, the silver-white energy creating tunnels through space that compressed distance into meaningless concepts. When the authority finally scattered, releasing them at their destination, the Prime Living Law threw her arms wide with theatrical flair.","\"Welcome,\" she announced with a smile that could have powered small civilizations, \"to the Juridical Sanctum of Law Litigation!\"","HUUM!","The name boomed in the air with all the warmth of a death sentence delivered with a smile.","Bob’s enhanced perception took in their surroundings, and what he saw was glorious!","Seas of white banners and scales stretched in every direction, each one carved from what appeared to be crystallized justice itself. Between these scales, shrines dotted the landscape like monuments to crimes committed and sentences served.","\"Isn’t it magnificent?\" the Prime Living Law continued, practically vibrating with enthusiasm. \"Here we house all types of Living Existences who broke Living Laws in some manner or another. Some are locked away for a mere dozen years...barely a slap on the wrist, really. Others...\" Her smile grew sharper, \"Others have been here for millions of years, and they’ll be here for millions more.\"","She began walking, or rather bouncing, forward, gesturing at various features with the pride of a homeowner showing off renovations. \"We have sections organized by type of violation, severity of offense, and my personal favorite...likelihood of repeat offense. You’ll find many, many Living Paradoxes here, actually. They have such trouble following rules, the poor dears.\"","Her eyes twinkled with something that might have been sympathy if it hadn’t been accompanied by such obvious glee.","She spun to face Bob, her pink hair creating a halo effect that somehow made her look both angelic and slightly unhinged.","\"The Royal Law Tristesse can have you stay here for, oh, what was your name again?\" She tapped her chin thoughtfully. \"Bobby?\"","Bob’s entire form went rigid, his obsidian-white skin rippling with barely contained emotions.","Bobby. He fucking hated that name!","His voice, when it emerged, carried the weight of someone who had fought for far too long.","\"Bob,\" he said with deliberate precision. \"My name is Bob.\"","The Prime Living Law’s smile never wavered, though something in her eyes suggested she was filing away his reaction for future reference. \"Of course! Bob it is. Well, Bob, the Royal Law Tristesse has reached a consensus with other interested parties. Nothing born from those special Nullvein Gravewake Folds is to be released into general circulation just yet...too many variables, too many unknowns. So instead, you get to temporarily learn how to be an Origin here!\"","She gestured toward Altheon with a flourish. \"With your assigned babysitter, the ever-boring Altheon, to guide you through the process!\"","Her attention shifted to the Prime Living Origin, and her expression grew slightly more serious, though the effect was somewhat undermined by the way she was still bouncing on her toes. \"Though you seem rather preoccupied, old friend. Some thoughts? Existential crisis?\"","WAA!","Altheon seemed to surface from whatever depths his consciousness had been exploring, his ancient eyes focusing on the present with visible effort. He shook his head with the patient exhaustion of someone who had too many things in his mind- after all, his other body was with the Young Miss and the now seemingly terrifting Noah Osmont in a Doorway!","\"I don’t have time to be a babysitter,\" he said, his voice carrying notes of genuine regret mixed with impatience. His gaze settled on Bob with something that might have been sympathy.","\"Just bear with it and stay here for a bit. After things cool down...you’ll be allowed to enter the Transcendent Origin Folds properly.\"","...!","Before Bob could formulate a response, before he could ask any of the thousand questions burning in his consciousness, Altheon simply... ceased.","One moment he stood there, luminous and present, and the next, only the faint afterimage of his authority remained, already fading like smoke in wind.","The Prime Living Law harrumphed with the exaggerated disappointment of a performer who’d lost half their audience!","She shook her head, pink hair swaying with the motion, before turning back to Bob with renewed enthusiasm.","\"Well then, Bobby...sorry, Bob, looks like it’s just you and me! Would you like the grand tour? I especially enjoy visiting the sections where we keep the little Paradoxes who’ve been locked away for eons. They get so wonderfully bitter after the first few millennia.\" Her eyes gleamed with an excitement that bordered on disturbing. \"And if you’re interested, if you really want to test yourself, you can even battle against them! Kill them if you achieve victory...it’s perfectly fine here. They’re prisoners, after all, and rehabilitation through combat is an accepted form of correction.\"","...!","Bob’s eyes blazed with sudden intensity at these words. The prospect of combat, of devouring beings of significant power, struck a chord deep within his transformed existence.","In the depths of his consciousness, an image burned bright and constant...his daughter, his light, the one pure thing he had managed to create in his existence of conflict and struggle.","He would do whatever it took to gain enough power to see her again. If that meant fighting imprisoned Paradoxes in this realm of crystallized justice, if it meant learning to be an Origin through methods that others might find distasteful, then so be it!","He had already crossed lines that most beings wouldn’t even approach. What were a few more in service of a goal that transcended his own existence?","Bob looked at the Prime Living Law, and when he spoke, his voice burned with glory!","\"Let’s go see these vile Paradoxes.\"","...!","---","In Aeternitas Concordia, at the junction where the ambitious stalls of Originus Venerant Fold Dwellers gave way to the towering establishments of Living Existences, another of Noah’s bodies maintained his merchant persona with practiced ease.","The Glass Woks floated before him like captured stars, their contents sending waves of intoxicating aroma across the golden plaza. Stacks of golden bowls waited beside his purple throne, ready to be filled with treasures that would make even Honored existences weep with envy.","He was in the midst of examining a peculiar object...something that resembled a crystallized moment of time that a Living Concept had retrieved from a particularly treacherous Doorway, when reality suddenly compressed around him.","HUUM!","Nine figures materialized from thin air.","They appeared on the golden path in formation, their combined presence creating waves of pressure that made nearby Fold Dwellers stumble backward in instinctive recognition of overwhelming power.","The figure at their forefront commanded immediate attention. Golden hair that seemed to capture and reflect every photon of light in the plaza, features carved with the kind of perfection that transcended natural beauty, and an aura that made even the other Honored Living Existences seem diminished by comparison!","This was a Royal Living Existence!","Yet when he looked at Noah, his expression carried the kind of difficulty that suggested he was dealing with variables beyond his comfort zone.","\"Sir,\" the Royal Living Existence said dubiously, \"the Lady invites you for a discussion of utmost importance.\"","WAA!","The plaza erupted in barely contained chaos.","Whispers flew faster than thought itself as hundreds of consciousnesses tried to process what they were witnessing. Nine Honored Living Existences and a Royal had come to formally invite a supposed Fold Dweller to meet with ’the Lady’....","Many did not know, but this was a title that could only refer to Duke Gwendolyn herself!","Noah raised his head slowly, his eyes sharp as they took in the careful positioning of his escorts.","Nine Honored beings for a simple invitation was not courtesy....it was preparation. Duke Gwendolyn and the other Living Existences no longer knew how to accurately categorize him after his display in the Temporal Folds.","To them, he was an enigma who had somehow eliminated a Duke-level Dead Existence through means they couldn’t comprehend.","They were probing, testing, trying to gauge whether he would come willingly or require... persuasion.","Part of him wanted to decline. The merchant business had been surprisingly profitable, and there were still treasures from the Doorways he wanted to acquire here...","But the matter of Living Paradoxes seeking their seat at the table, the reshaping of power structures that was undoubtedly occurring in the wake of recent events...these things demanded his attention.","Noah rose from his throne with deliberate grace, each movement calculated to project confidence without threat.","The throne, woks, and bowls vanished into his spatial storage with practiced ease. His voice carried across the plaza with clear authority as he addressed the gathered crowd.","\"I will return to continue our business in a little while.\"","Then, turning to the Royal Living Existence with a slight nod that acknowledged rank without surrendering dignity, he spoke two words that set events in motion.","\"Let’s go.\"","...!"]},{"number":4003,"title":"Chapter 4003: Chapter 4002: The 10 Living Existences! II","paragraphs":["The light of the Royal Living Origin wrapped around them like liquid starlight, compressing space and distance into meaningless concepts as it carried Noah and his escort through layers of Aeternitas Concordia that most beings would never witness.","When the radiance finally released them, Noah found himself standing in a place filled with glory...a garden!","The garden stretched before him in terraced levels that seemed to exist in multiple dimensions simultaneously. Crystalline pathways wound between beds of vegetation that pulsed with inner light, each plant more impossible than the last.","Here, roses bloomed with petals made from compressed temporal energy, their thorns capable of cutting through causality itself. There, trees rose with bark of crystallized law, their branches heavy with fruit that defied comprehension.","The fruits were Wheels of Existence.","Each wheel hung from its branch like a ripe apple, yet contained within its spinning form entire realities. He could see civilizations rising and falling within each fruit, billions of lives playing out their destinies in accelerated time, only to begin again when the wheel completed its rotation!","The sight was simultaneously beautiful and horrifying...entire existences reduced to decorative produce in someone’s garden.","Above it all, a massive golden dome crowned the space, its surface inscribed with patterns of runes.","This was clearly the apex of some vast structure in Concordia’s heart, a place where only the most powerful could tread without invitation. The dome itself seemed alive, breathing with a rhythm that made the garden’s impossibilities feel natural by comparison.","Yet Noah’s fascination with the surroundings was quickly displaced by what his senses detected within this miraculous space.","The auras that pressed against his consciousness were unmistakable...Duke-level entities, multiple ones, their presence making the very air dense with accumulated authority.","The Royal Living Origin who had escorted him here suddenly bowed with profound respect, as did all the Honored Living Existences who had accompanied them. Without a word of explanation or farewell, they simply vanished, leaving Noah alone with beings whose power could reshape existence itself.","Four Dukes. He counted them with the careful precision of someone observing potential threats and allies.","Duke Gwendolyn stood nearest, her stellar dark hair catching light that seemed to originate from within rather than from any external source. Beside her stood a figure that made Noah do a subtle double-take...a man in pristine white robes who leaned slightly on an ornate cane, his eyes... impossibly, incomprehensibly blind.","Milky white orbs gazed at nothing and everything simultaneously. How could a Duke, a being whose perception should transcend every limitation, be blind?","Further into the garden, surrounded by flames that danced between red and gold like Origin authority given pyroclastic form, stood a woman whose presence commanded attention through sheer intensity.","Her desert garb seemed out of place in this garden of impossibilities, yet somehow perfect for her bearing...layers of flowing fabric that shifted between states of matter with each movement. Her skin gleamed with an inner radiance that suggested she didn’t merely wield Origin, but had become it!","And lastly...","Noah had to look twice to confirm what his senses were telling him.","Floating at eye level, no more than a few inches in total size, was...a mouse.","Its fur was lustrous white that seemed to contain constellations within each strand, and its eyes....those stellar white orbs held the weight of eons, the kind of gaze that suggested this being had witnessed the rise and fall of entire Folds!","When the mouse spoke, its voice emerged with bass tones that belonged to something mountain-sized rather than palm-sized. Meaning its voice was fucking heavy!","\"Duke Gwendolyn has filled us in on the... things she deemed we should know.\" The mouse’s tiny hands clasped behind its back in a gesture that would have been comical if not for the overwhelming authority radiating from its diminutive form.","\"What I want to ascertain first, before anything else, is this... do you wish the Living Origins any harm?\"","The question buzzed in the garden. Noah felt the weight of four Duke-level consciousnesses focused entirely upon him, their combined attention making reality itself hold its breath.","Purple text materialized above each of their heads as his distinction as the Weaver of Existence identified them.","Duke Gwendolyn he knew as thr others were foreign!","|Duke Valen - The Blind Oracle|:: He who traded sight for true vision.","|Duke Pyralis - The Desert Phoenix|:: She who burns away impurity with Origin’s flame.","|Duke Whisker - The Primordial Sage|:: He who remembers existence.","Noah’s lips curved into a smile as he met each of their gazes in turn, his voice carrying the kind of calm that came from either supreme confidence or supreme ignorance.","\"Does it only matter for the Living Origins?\" He let the question hang for a moment before continuing. \"What if I wished to harm other Living Existences?\"","Duke Whisker’s tiny features arranged themselves into what might have been amusement. \"Realistically and honestly, the main determinant is your intent toward Living Origins. The politics between different types of Living Existences are... complex. But Origins are special. We are, after all, beginnings incarnate.\"","Noah nodded slowly, as if considering his words carefully. \"I have no intention to harm Living Origins, though...\" He paused, letting them lean into his hesitation. \"There was one Living Origin who crossed me. I’m still deciding whether I will kill them or not.\"","...!","The tension in the garden shifted, becoming sharper, more focused. Duke Whisker’s whiskers twitched with what might have been curiosity.","\"What type of Living Origin are they?\"","\"Prime.\"","The mouse’s expression relaxed visibly. \"Ah, that would be nothing major then. Primes die all the time in the grand scheme of things.\" He turned to the other Dukes, his stellar eyes gleaming with certainty. \"He’s telling the truth. He does not wish Living Origins any harm...at least, not as a general principle.\"","The atmosphere in the garden shifted palpably. Duke Gwendolyn’s shoulders relaxed minutely, while Duke Pyralis’s flames dimmed from aggressive brilliance to merely impressive radiance.","Duke Whisker floated forward slightly, his tiny form somehow managing to project gravitas. \"Allow me to make proper introductions, since we’re apparently going to be having a civilized discussion rather than an existential confrontation. I am Duke Whisker, sometimes called the Primordial Sage, though I find titles tedious after the first few eons.\"","He gestured to each Duke in turn. \"Duke Valen here traded his physical sight for the ability to see truth itself. Duke Pyralis burns with the pure essence of Origin from the Desert of First Thoughts. And Duke Gwendolyn you’ve already had the pleasure of meeting.\"","Gwendolyn stepped forward, her expression all business now that the immediate question of Noah’s threat level had been addressed. \"Very well, let’s get down to business then... the Living Paradoxes.\"","The name fell into the garden’s atmosphere like a stone into still water, creating ripples of tension that each Duke felt.","\"They stole the corpse of an Early Creature,\" Duke Pyralis said, her voice carrying the heat of barely contained anger. \"The audacity of such an action transcends everything. That corpse was being studied, preserved, protected for good reason.\"","\"And they likely did something desecrated with it,\" Duke Whisker added, his tiny form radiating disgust. \"The appearance of Dead Existences is almost certainly linked to whatever unholy ritual they performed. The timing is too convenient, the methodology too specific.\"","...!"]},{"number":4004,"title":"Chapter 4004: Chapter 4003: The 10 Living Existences! III","paragraphs":["Duke Valen’s blind eyes seemed to focus on something none of them could see. \"And now they wish to use the very crisis they created as pretense to assert themselves among the Living Existences again. It’s brilliant in its simplicity...create a problem only you can solve, then demand recognition for solving it.\"","\"The threat of Dead Existences is very real,\" Gwendolyn continued, her voice heavy with the weight of recent memory. \"If we deny the Paradoxes their seat at the table, they’ll likely open more tears in existence, make the situation increasingly dire until we’re forced to call upon them. Since Paradoxes...\" she paused, seeming to taste something bitter, \"are mainly the ones effective against Dead Existences.\"","Duke Whisker’s whiskers twitched in what might have been amusement. \"But then... another party has appeared that seems to also be effective against Dead Existences.\"","All four Dukes turned their attention to Noah with synchronized precision that spoke to planning or instinct honed over eons.","Duke Valen’s blind eyes seemed to pierce through him despite their lack of function. \"You aren’t a Paradox, are you?\"","Noah’s smile deepened as he turned toward Duke Whisker, recognizing the mouse’s apparent ability to discern truth from falsehood. \"I am not truly a Paradox.\"","The words were carefully chosen.","He wasn’t truly a Paradox...he was many things beyond Paradox, and fundamentally, he was an Early Creature. The statement was true from a certain perspective, which was all that mattered.","Duke Gwendolyn leaned forward slightly, her ancient eyes searching his face for clues. \"Are you someone stemming all the way back from the Earliest Folds? Someone who served... Early Creatures?\"","Noah turned to her with that same enigmatic smile. \"No.\"","Duke Pyralis’s flames flickered with increased intensity as she voiced her own theory. \"Are you a Mutated Living Existence affected by a Lost Forgotten Principle?\"","He shifted his attention to her, finding her theory particularly interesting even as he denied it. \"While that would be fascinating, no.\"","The silence that followed was dense with calculation as four of the most powerful beings in existence tried to categorize something that refused to fit their understanding.","Finally, Duke Whisker floated forward, his tiny hands still clasped behind his back, and asked the question that made the other Dukes visibly tense.","\"Are you...an Early Creature?\"","BOOM!","The question seemed to make reality itself pause, as if Existence was holding its breath waiting for the answer. Even the other Dukes showed alarm at such a direct inquiry...the implications of a positive answer would shatter every assumption about the current order of existence!","Noah laughed, the sound genuine and amused. \"If I was a genuine, full-fledged Early Creature, would I be here playing along with all these games?\"","The question carried its own weight of logic. An Early Creature wouldn’t need to trade in marketplaces or attend meetings. They would simply take what they wanted, reshape reality according to their whims.","So he said...he was not a genuine and full fledged early creature!","And well...it was true.","After all, he had not even finished forming his heart!","Duke Whisker’s eyes gleamed with that truth-detecting light. \"This... is not false.\"","The visible relief that washed through the other Dukes was almost comical. Even beings of their power found the prospect of dealing with an Early Creature overwhelming.","Duke Gwendolyn recovered first, her practical nature reasserting itself. \"Existence is vast and there are many types of beings out there. What matters is that you hold an alternative to the hungry Living Paradoxes. You have Moiraine, who can empower everyone to fight against Dead Existences, and yourself, of course, who can kill a Duke-level Dead Existence in an instant, right?\"","Noah blinked at her words, then responded with casual air that suggested he’d almost forgotten. \"Oh, yes, right!\"","The confusion that flashed across the Dukes’ faces would have been amusing if the situation weren’t so serious. How did someone forget they had just eliminated a Duke-level threat?","Gwendolyn sighed with the weight of someone trying to herd weavings made of pure chaos. \"We can hold Living Paradoxes at length and not give them much recognition with you in the picture. If you were aligned with us. If you let us know what it is you want.\"","Duke Whisker floated forward. \"Everyone wants something. Some seek power, others knowledge, still others simple comfort. But there are those rare beings who are not driven by wants but by purpose, by destiny, by forces greater than personal desire. Some are driven by existence itself as they look over the masses and seek to simply help without anything in return. Which type are you?\"","Noah’s smile carried genuine amusement as he looked at the profound little mouse. \"I am very much one who wants and takes.\"","Duke Whisker blinked, his whiskers drooping slightly as his philosophical moment was thoroughly deflated. He shook his tiny head with what might have been exasperation. \"Okay then. Straightforward. We can work with straightforward.\"","The mouse’s demeanor shifted to something more businesslike. \"If a cooperation agreement can be reached between us...you providing your strength when needed, we can give you what you want. Because due to recent events, representatives from all ten types of Living Existences will now gather to discuss the threat of Dead Existences. Living Paradoxes will be included in these discussions for the first time since the Earliest Folds.\"","His tiny form seemed to swell with the importance of what he was about to say. \"The Kleos Concordat will convene within a day. Every Duke who can be spared, select Royal Living Existences, and certain other parties of interest will gather to determine how existence itself will respond to these threats.\"","The name carried weight that pressed against consciousness itself!","The Kleos Concordat...a gathering that transcended normal meetings, where decisions would be made that could reshape the fundamental nature of how existence operated!","\"It would be good,\" Duke Whisker continued, his stellar eyes boring into Noah’s with intensity that belied his small size, \"to know who are enemies and who are friends when that time comes. The lines are being drawn as we speak. Where will you stand when the moment arrives?\"","The question buzzed in the garden air between the impossible plants and their Wheel-fruits, waiting for an answer that would echo across existence itself!"]},{"number":4005,"title":"Chapter 4005: Chapter 4004: The 10 Living Existences! IV","paragraphs":["Where would he stand when the time came?","The question hung in the garden’s impossible air, weighted with implications that stretched across existence itself.","Noah let the tension flow through the space, feeling how each Duke leaned into his eventual answer, when Duke Gwendolyn’s voice cut through the moment with surgical precision.","\"When it comes to this, I have to mention something else.\" She turned to face the other Dukes, her stellar dark hair catching light.","\"Something that makes his alignment with us...\" she pointed directly at Noah, \"clear.\"","The words fell into the garden like stones into still water, creating ripples of anticipation that made even the Wheels of Existence hanging from their branches slow their eternal rotations.","Something that made his alignment with them clear? Noah’s mind raced through possibilities, his enhanced perception catching the subtle shift in Gwendolyn’s posture that suggested she was about to cross a line they had agreed upon.","Duke Whisker’s stellar eyes flashed with sharp intensity, his tiny form radiating sudden wariness. \"You seemed hesitant before, Gwendolyn. Why say it now?\"","Noah’s expression hardened as understanding crystallized with cold certainty. He knew exactly what she planned to reveal, and his voice emerged with an almost rebuking edge that made the temperature in the garden drop perceptibly.","\"You agreed not to share anything regarding that.\"","The words were delivered with the kind of controlled coldness that was more dangerous than any explosion!","Duke Gwendolyn met his gaze steadily, though something in her expression suggested she recognized the magnitude of what she was about to do.","\"I did,\" she acknowledged with a slow nod. \"But too much is now at stake. The balance of existence itself teeters on the edge of fundamental change.\" She paused, seeming to gather her resolve. \"I have a body of mine actively protecting her, and you are beside her as well, so I have even less worry regarding her protection. All the Dukes here are those I would give my very existence to protect. I cannot be the only Duke who knows such critical information when the fate of all Living Origins might depend upon it.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed!","This fucker.","The blind Duke Valen straightened, his sightless eyes somehow managing to convey stern intensity despite their lack of function. His cane tapped once against the crystalline path, the sound reverberating through dimensions. \"What do you mean, Gwendolyn? What information carries such weight that you would break a promise to reveal it?\"","Duke Whisker, surprisingly, seemed to be lost in contemplation for a moment before his tiny features arranged themselves into an expression of concern.","When he spoke, his deep voice carried the weight of wisdom earned through witnessing the rise and fall of concepts themselves.","\"Gwendolyn,\" he said, siding with Noah in a way that clearly surprised Duke Gwendolyn, \"at times, some things are best left unsaid. The fewer who know certain truths, the safer those truths remain.\"","...!","Duke Gwendolyn looked at each of them in turn...Noah’s stern disapproval, Whisker’s unexpected caution, Valen’s demanding curiosity, and Pyralis’s burning intensity.","She saw the weight of their combined attention, felt the pressure of secrets that wanted to remain hidden, and shook her head with the resignation of someone who had already crossed the point of no return in their mind.","\"No,\" she said firmly. \"The stakes are far too high. She needs to be protected by more than just us. Given resources by more than just us.\" Her voice grew heavy with the magnitude of what she was about to reveal. \"She was the hope of Living Origins. She is.\"","HUUM!","The moment those words left her lips, Duke Whisker’s eyes blazed with sudden understanding while the other two Dukes showed expressions of pure shock that they struggled to contain.","Duke Valen’s voice emerged as barely more than a whisper, though it carried through the garden with perfect clarity. \"You don’t mean...\"","Duke Gwendolyn nodded solemnly, sealing their fate with words that could never be taken back. \"The Young Miss. THE Living Order has been found. Secured. Protected.\" Her gaze turned to Noah with something that might have been apology. \"She is closely entangled with him, and he with her. That is why I have no doubt he sides with us.\"","...!","This fucker.","The silence that followed was deafening.","Noah’s expression, as he looked at Duke Gwendolyn, transformed into something that showed coldness. It was immense disappointment, the kind that came from watching someone you had begun to respect shatter that respect through a single action.","He had told her not to say it. She had been explicitly instructed not to share this information. And yet, at this crucial moment, she had freely revealed it because she trusted those present!","Trust. Such a fragile thing, so easily given and so catastrophically misplaced.","His eyes moved across the assembled Dukes, gauging their reactions with the careful precision of someone cataloging potential threats.","Duke Whisker looked down contemplatively, his tiny hands clasped behind his back as he processed implications that stretched across eons. The other two Dukes showed surprise they quickly tried to reign in, but their eyes had already sharpened with new interest, new calculation.","Duke Pyralis’s flames flared with sudden intensity, her voice cutting through the silence with demands that made Noah’s disappointment deepen. \"THE Living Order was one of the biggest projects of the Living Origins. How is she entangled with him? Where is she right now? We need to...\"","Noah shook his head sharply, cutting off her questions as his gaze returned to Duke Gwendolyn. The disappointment in his eyes was palpable, a weight that seemed to press against her consciousness with more force than any physical blow could have achieved.","Duke Gwendolyn sighed, recognizing his displeasure but pressing forward with the conviction of someone who believed they were right despite all evidence to the contrary. \"All those here are to be trusted. We are the ones who analyze other Dukes of Origin to ensure we are all aligned...Duke Whisker sees to that personally. I understand the fear of betrayal, but you will not find it among us. If we have no trust, we have no strength.\""]},{"number":4006,"title":"Chapter 4006: Chapter 4005: The 10 Living Existences! V","paragraphs":["Noah simply shook his head at this. In that moment, watching her justify her breach of confidence with platitudes about trust and strength, he lost all respect for her.","Trust was not something to be assumed or demanded...it was earned through consistent action, through keeping one’s word even when circumstances made it difficult.","Gwendolyn turned toward the other Dukes, continuing despite his obvious disapproval. \"Knowing of her survival, also know that she shattered her Realm and is now reestablishing it...rebuilding her purpose. To allow her to become an Honored Existence and then grant her the power of a Duke and even higher will need the resources of all Living Origins. That is why I told you. As for where she is now...\"","\"Don’t fucking say that too.\" Noah’s voice cut through her words like a blade through silk, the profanity carrying more weight for its rarity!","Simultaneously, Duke Whisker’s voice joined his in urgent warning. \"Don’t... reveal that.\"","Noah’s eyes met Duke Whisker’s, a moment of unexpected alliance passing between them. This mouse was much better to his liking than the Duke he thought would be a decent ally!","The ancient mouse spoke toward Gwendolyn with his wizened stellar eyes carrying gentle but firm reproach.","\"It is enough for us to know she lives,\" Whisker said carefully. \"Even though we are powerful, there may always be those stronger. Even though we believe nobody is listening, someone could always be listening. The walls of existence have ears we cannot perceive, memories we cannot erase. The return of THE Living Order is a momentous occasion that we must approach delicately, not with the blunt instrument of full disclosure.\"","Duke Gwendolyn appeared surprised by Whisker’s words, perhaps expecting support from the being who verified truth for their circle.","But she nodded, seeming to finally understand that she had already said too much. Her attention returned to Noah, and when she spoke, her voice carried a mixture of authority and something that might have been plea.","\"All is known between us now. Can we continue counting on your support? With THE Living Order? Against the schemes of the Living Paradoxes?\"","Noah looked at her with that same stern gaze of disappointment, his voice emerging cold as winter’s final breath. \"You can count on my support.\"","The words were delivered without warmth, without the earlier ease of their interaction!","His displeasure at her revealing information about Sigrid, THE Living Order...radiated from him in waves that made the impossible plants in the garden lean away from his presence.","Because the more beings that knew such secrets, the more possible variables entered the equation!","And things were already messy enough without adding unnecessary complications. Who needed more variables when the board was already so complex that a single misplaced piece could topple everything?!","---","Across the folds of existence, through layers of reality that most beings would never perceive, through the Transcendent Temporal Folds where time flowed like rivers, through the Transcendent Origin Folds where beginnings were born, and through multiple other domains of impossibility, there existed... the Transcendent Conceptual Folds.","In the depths of these Folds, where abstract thought had been given form and substance, rose the Ethereal Summit of Unspoken Truths...a hazy silver mountain surrounded by thousands of swirling multicolored Wheels of Existence.","Each wheel contained within it concepts that had shaped reality itself: Love, Hatred, Justice, Mercy, and thousands of others that most minds couldn’t even name.","Deep inside the mountain’s hollowed core, in a domain protected by immense waves of Living Conceptual Authority where silver and white seas mixed in patterns that resembled thoughts becoming real, there existed a plain that defied every expectation of what power could create.","The vegetation here burst with waves of complexity that would make Honored Living Existences mad with greed. Flowers bloomed with petals of crystallized inspiration, their scent carrying enlightenment that could advance understanding by eons.","Trees grew with bark of compressed wisdom, their leaves whispering secrets that predated current existence!","Grasses swayed in breezes that carried the fragmentary thoughts of existence itself, each blade worth more than entire civilizations.","Yet what made this place truly remarkable were not the impossible plants, but the auras that permeated it.","Ten different terrifying Living Existences had gathered here, each one eclipsing the power of normal Dukes by margins that rendered comparison meaningless.","A Living Temporal lounged beside a fountain where past and future flowed as separate streams. A Living Spirit floated in meditation, their form shifting between states of consciousness. A Living Emotive sat surrounded by crystals that captured and reflected every feeling that had ever been felt.","A Living Law stood rigid as justice itself, while a Living Elemental swirled between states of matter with each breath.","A Living Quantum existed in multiple positions simultaneously until observed. A Living Dimensional folded space around themselves like origami. A Living Concept pondered thoughts that could reshape reality if spoken aloud!","And shockingly, horrifically, impossibly...a Living Paradox was among them.","The Living Paradox was none other than the beggar-looking being known as...Schrodinger.","He sat cross-legged on a simple mat, his tattered robes pooling around him as he focused on a board game with pieces that seemed to exist in multiple states simultaneously. His opponent, the Living Concept, moved pieces that represented ideas rather than armies, each placement changing the nature of the game itself.","In the middle of moving a piece that might have been Hope or Despair depending on the angle of observation, Schrodinger looked up with a smile that carried too much knowledge.","His gaze found the Living Origin among their gathering, and his voice emerged with casual curiosity that belied the weight of his words.","\"I sense you have found something critical. What is it, O Valen?\"","BOOM!","The shocking revelation settled into the space...among these terrifying beings, Duke Valen actually maintained one of his bodies here!","The Blind Oracle who had traded his sight for true vision seemed troubled as he rose from his seated position, his white robes flowing around him like liquid truth.","\"THE Living Order,\" he said slowly, each word carrying the weight of impossible discovery, \"has been found once more.\"","...!","Schrodinger’s hand froze above the game board, a piece that was simultaneously Victory and Defeat hovering in his grip.","\"Oh?\" The single syllable carried more interest than entire speeches might have contained.","The game was forgotten as he turned his full attention to this revelation, his beggar’s appearance doing nothing to diminish the terrible intelligence that blazed in his ancient eyes!"]},{"number":4007,"title":"Chapter 4007: Chapter 4006: The 10 Living Existences! VI","paragraphs":["The revelation hung in the mountain’s hollowed depths like a bell that had just been struck, its resonance making even these ancient beings pause in their contemplations!","Duke Valen’s words about THE Living Order’s return had transformed the atmosphere from one of casual gathering to something far more consequential.","The blind Duke moved with deliberate grace across the crystalline floor, each tap of his cane sending ripples through the silver-white seas of Conceptual Authority that flowed beneath their feet. When he stopped before the board game, his sightless eyes somehow managed to convey the weight of his concern as he addressed both players.","\"The return of THE Living Order,\" he said, his voice carrying the particular timbre of someone who had witnessed too many returns that ended in tragedy. \"What do you think about it?\"","Schrodinger’s smile deepened, though something in his expression suggested memories being carefully examined and weighed. He moved a piece on the board...something that might have been Doubt transforming into Certainty, before responding.","\"Order,\" he began, savoring the word as if tasting something exotic and long-forbidden, \"was something I never had the chance of coming across. Not properly, at least. Not in its pure, original form.\"","His fingers drummed against his tattered robes in a rhythm that seemed to echo through dimensions. \"THE Living Law was the only one of those original beings I had the pleasure, if we can call it that, to encounter directly. And even that thing terrified me.\"","The admission sent subtle waves through the gathered entities. For Schrodinger to admit fear was not weakness but rather an acknowledgment of forces that transcended even their elevated understanding.","\"Consider what THE Living Law represented,\" Schrodinger continued. \"Not just rules or structure, but the fundamental assertion that existence should operate according to comprehensible patterns. That chaos should have boundaries. That actions should have predictable consequences. When I stood before her...I felt my very nature rebel against her presence. Every paradox within me screamed at the wrongness of such absolute certainty.\"","He paused, letting his words settle into the consciousness of his audience before continuing with calculated precision.","\"If that girl...the one whose entire lineage you Origins systematically eliminated to create the proper conditions for Order’s awakening...truly does become THE Living Order...\" He trailed off, his expression growing contemplative. \"It will be a good thing. Existence needs its anchor, its foundation stone. Without Order, we’re all just... possibilities floating in an ocean of maybe.\"","HUUM!","Duke Valen snorted, the sound carrying more meaning than entire speeches might have contained.","His blind gaze fixed on Schrodinger with the particular intensity of someone who could see through deceptions that eyes might miss.","\"You speak as if you weren’t the one who advised me on how to possibly awaken the Order within her. Your cryptic hints, your careful nudges in specific directions.\" The Duke’s cane tapped once against the floor, the sound sharp as accusation. \"Whatever. Her reentry is good for stability, but it does muddy the waters somewhat.\"","Valen turned slightly, as if observing something beyond the mountain’s confines. \"Oh, and there’s another matter. The same being who moved across your Existential Trembling against Aion completely unaffected, the one who took your little Paradox Moiraine... he is somehow entangled with THE Living Order. I cannot fully gauge what his actual power is.\"","The reaction was immediate and palpable.","Several of the terrifying beings who had been maintaining distance from the conversation suddenly drew closer. A Living Temporal materialized from what had been a shadow, while the Living Emotive’s crystalline arrangements chimed with sudden interest.","Schrodinger’s hand paused above the board, a piece that existed in multiple states simultaneously hovering in his grip. His smile grew wider, though his eyes remained calculating.","\"That is certainly interesting,\" he mused, finally placing the piece with deliberate care. \"Moiraine was traveling with someone that little Diviticus swallowed a bit. Someone who should have something relating to Early Creatures. Possibly blessed with a corpse of another Early Creature, or perhaps an Inheritor of a Sleeping Shore.\" His gaze sharpened, cutting through the philosophical veneer to something more immediate. \"Could he be one and the same?\"","The Living Quantum, who had been existing in seventeen different positions simultaneously, suddenly collapsed into a single location beside them. When it spoke, its voice carried the weight of calculated probabilities!","\"What happened with the corpse of the Early Creature we decided to let the Paradoxes have for the first time? Did that Diviticus use whatever she obtained to...\"","\"Little Diviticus managed to innervate the corpse of the Early Creature,\" Schrodinger interrupted, his tone carrying a mixture of pride and concern that suggested complicated feelings about his fellow Paradox. \"She’s a shooting star now, burning bright across the darkness of our current predicament. Who knows?\" He looked over the others with an expression of gentle mockery. \"She might become more powerful than any of you.\"","The harrumphs and dismissive gestures that followed would have been comical if not for the fact that each being present could reshape reality with their displeasure.","Duke Valen’s eyes flashed with particular sharpness, his voice cutting through the protests.","\"So through your actions, we are tearing the veil between the Living and the Dead early. Earlier than when the veil should have begun to come down naturally.\"","Schrodinger waved his hands dismissively, the gesture somehow managing to convey both acknowledgment and indifference. \"Just a few years earlier. The veil was bound to be torn eventually...at least now, we can control where the tears appear, how wide they grow. Everything has a price, my friends. We have been preparing for the Dead Existences for eons, developing countermeasures, training forces. But even they...\"","He paused, letting the weight of anticipation build before delivering his next words with careful precision.","\"Even they are not our final enemies.\"","HUUM!","The atmosphere in the mountain’s depths grew heavy with implications that pressed against consciousness itself.","The entities present exchanged glances...or whatever equivalent their forms allowed, each one processing this statement through their own vast understanding.","Schrodinger looked at each of them in turn, his beggar’s appearance doing nothing to diminish the ancient intelligence that blazed in his eyes. When he smiled this time, it carried the particular quality of someone about to share a secret they’d been holding for far too long.","\"Do you want to hear a Story from the Earliest Folds that nobody else knows?\"","...!"]},{"number":4008,"title":"Chapter 4008: Chapter 4007: True Enemies!","paragraphs":["Chapter 4007: True Enemies!","Schrodinger had asked if they wanted to hear a story from the Earliest Folds!","But...","The collective eye-roll that followed was almost synchronized, as if they’d performed this routine countless times before. The Living Concept actually sighed, the sound like ideas deflating.","“Not another one of your possibly-true, possibly-invented parables,” someone muttered.","Schrodinger laughed, the sound genuine and warm despite the weight of their discussion. “Listen, this one is particularly relevant. I promise.”","He settled back slightly, his posture shifting into the comfortable stance of a storyteller who knew his audience couldn’t resist despite their protests.","“At a time when chaos was most rampant in the Earliest Folds...when Early Creatures hunted for sport and Inevitabilities bloomed like flowers after rain...there was an Early Creature who happened to overhear a conversation. This creature, whose name has been deliberately forgotten, witnessed THE Living Law visiting the locked Paradox in its prison of contradictions.”","HUUM!","The mountain seemed to grow quieter, even the flow of Conceptual Authority beneath their feet stilling to better hear the tale.","“THE Living Law stood before the chains of impossibility that bound THE Living Paradox, and she asked a question that had been burning in her consciousness since the first Inevitability emerged. ‘Are Inevitabilities the true enemies of all Existences?'”","Schrodinger’s voice took on different tones as he embodied each character, his talent for storytelling evident despite the tattered appearance he maintained.","“At such a question, THE Living Paradox laughed...an eerie sound that existed simultaneously as mirth and despair. ‘What,’ it said, ‘just because even before THE Creature, the Inevitabilities were there? Just because they predate understanding, and the very conception of what should and shouldn’t be?'”","The storyteller paused, letting tension build before continuing in a voice that captured the bound Paradox’s terrifying certainty.","“‘No,’ THE Living Paradox said, its voice carrying that particular quality of statements that were simultaneously true and false. ‘Even Inevitabilities are not the true enemies of all Existences. No, the biggest enemy of Existences... is existence itself.'”","HUUM!","Several of the listeners shifted uncomfortably at this pronouncement, recognizing philosophical depths that threatened to drown rational thought.","“‘Existence is feeble,’ the Paradox continued. ‘Undecided. Uncertain. It doesn’t know whether it wants to be or not to be, whether it should expand or contract, whether consciousness is blessing or curse. That was why I sought to put it under my control...to give it the direction it so desperately lacks.'”","Schrodinger’s voice grew lighter, more mocking as he continued channeling the bound Paradox.","“‘The true enemy of Existences?’ THE Living Paradox laughed again. ‘Who knows? I could be the true enemy...after all, I’m talking to you right now, aren’t I? Or perhaps it’s you, THE Living Law, with your rigid insistence that everything follow rules. Maybe it’s any of the others, or all of them together. Perhaps it’s THE Creature itself.’ A pause, then with something almost like fondness: ‘How is that kid doing nowadays anyway? Without my guidance, he may be getting lost. You all haven’t done anything crazy without me, right?'”","...!","The silence that followed in the story was mirrored by the silence in the mountain’s depths. Schrodinger continued, his voice now embodying THE Living Law’s heavy response.","“‘Out of all of us, you could have been so great.'”","The statement hung between the characters in the story like an accusation and a lament combined.","“This caused an immense silence to descend before THE Living Paradox laughed once more and began what would become its most famous monologue...though famous only to the Early Creature who overhead it.”","Schrodinger’s voice took on a philosophical depth that made even these ancient beings lean in slightly.","“‘What is greatness?’ the Paradox asked. ‘Is it power accumulated until reality bends to acknowledge your supremacy? Is it understanding gathered until the mysteries of existence lay bare before your perception? Or is it something more... paradoxical?'”","The beggar-Duke’s delivery grew more animated, his hands moving to emphasize points that existed in multiple interpretations simultaneously.","“‘Consider: I am locked here, chains of impossibility binding me in ways that should prevent even thought. Yet I think. I speak. I influence. My very imprisonment has become legendary, a cautionary tale that shapes how billions of consciousnesses will understand reality. In my cage, I... am more present in existence than I ever was while free.'”","He paused, his voice dropping to barely above a whisper that somehow carried perfectly through the space.","“‘Me, locked up right now, could be a grandiose form of greatness. The greatest teacher is the one whose lessons are learned without their presence. The greatest warrior is the one whose battles are won without fighting. The greatest paradox is the one that resolves itself by remaining unresolved. Maybe I’m locked here... maybe I’m actually free. Who knows?'”","...!","Schrodinger ended the story there, his eyes moving across the assembled beings with an expression that suggested layers of meaning they might never fully unpack. The silence that followed was dense with contemplation, each entity processing the parable through their own vast understanding.","Did this actually happen? Was it true? Was it false? None could say!","“When it comes to true enemies,” Schrodinger said, returning to his normal voice with its mixture of wisdom and whimsy, “there are few, and yet many. We simply have to do what we can to ensure that Existence keeps chugging along, keeps asking whether it should be rather than surrendering to shouldn’t.”","He smiled with something approaching genuine warmth as he looked at each of them.","“My friends...and yes, I do consider you friends despite your constant skepticism of my stories, we have much to do. Oh, and in a day’s time, at the Kleos Concordat, we might see each other under the gazes of others for the first time in a while. Don’t treat me too coldly, okay? You all are, after all, the closest I have to...friends in existence.”","Duke Valen snorted at this sentiment, though something in his expression suggested the dismissal was more habit than genuine feeling. “So, what shall be done about THE Living Order? Moiraine? And the Enigma entangled with both of them who possibly has links to an inheritance of an Early Creature?”","Schrodinger’s smile deepened as he moved another piece on the board...Victory becoming Defeat becoming Something Else Entirely.","“What to do indeed,” he mused, the words carrying the weight of plans within plans, possibilities within paradoxes. “What to do indeed...”","...!","1/4"]},{"number":4009,"title":"Chapter 4009: Chapter 4008: The Difference of Everything!","paragraphs":["Chapter 4008: The Difference of Everything!","In the time before time was measured, when existence still questioned whether it should continue existing, there lived an Early Creature whose ambition exceeded its understanding.","This creature, whose name has been deliberately erased from all records, watched THE Creature with the kind of devotion that bordered on obsession.","THE Creature moved through the Earliest Folds with purpose that defied comprehension, each action reshaping Existence in ways that wouldn’t be understood for eons. And at a certain period, invariably, THE Living Concept came and stayed at its side...the manifestation of thought itself given form and consciousness.","The Early Creature studied these interactions with desperate intensity. It saw how THE Creature would pose questions that THE Living Concept would transform into realities. It witnessed conversations that birthed entire categories of existence.","And in its limited understanding, it believed that proximity to THE Living Concept was one of the keys to THE Creature’s transcendent nature.","At a certain time, THE Creature disappeared.","And the Early Creature...thought its chance had come!","So it began to follow.","At first, THE Living Concept ignored the Early Creature’s presence, treating it with the same indifference it showed to the countless other beings that populated the Earliest Folds. But as days became years, and years stretched toward epochs, the persistence grew impossible to overlook.","“You are not like your predecessor,” THE Living Concept finally said, its voice carrying the weight of absolute truth. “You should not try to be like him.”","The Early Creature’s response blazed with the particular arrogance of youth convinced of its own destiny. “But I can become like him! If I understand what you teach, if I learn what you know...”","“Knowledge without foundation is merely sophisticated ignorance,” THE Living Concept interrupted. “You chase shadows while ignoring the light that casts them.”","But the Early Creature would not be deterred. It continued its pursuit with the single-minded determination that marked its kind, following THE Living Concept through domains where thought became substance, through regions where ideas went to die and be reborn.","Then came the day when Inevitabilities found it.","They emerged from the spaces between certainty, those paradoxical entities that existed because they shouldn’t, that thrived on the contradiction of their own nature.","The Early Creature found itself surrounded, its considerable power...power that could reshape entire Folds...suddenly, terrifyingly insufficient.","“Help me!” it pleaded to THE Living Concept, who observed from a position just beyond the ring of Inevitabilities. “I have followed you faithfully! I have learned your teachings!”","THE Living Concept’s response carried neither cruelty nor compassion, merely the weight of truth acknowledged. “I did warn you. Sometimes, one will never measure up to be like someone else. You should have been trying to forge your own existence, not attempting to replicate another’s.”","Defiance blazed through the Early Creature’s form as Inevitabilities pressed closer, their paradoxical presence beginning to unravel its carefully maintained existence.","“I will give you my Everything to be saved! Everything I am, everything I could become...take it all!”","THE Living Concept regarded it with the particular attention reserved for moments that would echo through eternity. When it spoke, each word fell like judgment rendered in the court of existence itself.","“Your Everything and THE Creature’s Everything are incomparable. The difference is so vast, so fundamentally insignificant, that even now it does not motivate me to take it.” THE Living Concept paused, allowing the weight of this truth to settle. “I could find an ant...a simple, momentary creature barely aware of its own existence...and its Everything might be larger than yours.”","HUUM!","The Early Creature’s defiance crumbled into confusion, then horror, as understanding began to dawn.","“Across Existence,” THE Living Concept continued, its voice carrying the finality of lessons that would never be repeated, “every creature has their Everything. Their worth. Their fundamental value in the grand equation of what is and what might be. But the worth of some...their Everything...is unfathomably more prized than others.”","The Inevitabilities closed in, their paradoxical nature beginning to dissolve the Early Creature’s form into component possibilities.","“And more often than not,” THE Living Concept concluded, already turning away from the scene, “very few can accurately gauge worth. You spent eternity trying to become something you could never be, when you might have become something unprecedented. The tragedy is not in your ending, but in your never truly beginning.”","The lesson echoed through the Earliest Folds.","Worth...cannot be claimed or demanded. It simply is, or isn’t, and the ability to recognize it remains one of existence’s rarest gifts.","—","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds.","The Doorway to the Loom stretched before them in all its paradoxical glory, each step forward somehow also being a step in directions that had no names.","They had been traversing for what felt like hours but could have been moments or centuries...time held little meaning in spaces where Paradox itself had carved the pathways!","Noah’s enhanced perception took in their current location with careful assessment. They stood at the edge of a region that challenged every assumption about what landscape could be. A mountain of pure red black flame rose before them, its surface not merely burning but existing in a state of perpetual conflagration that seemed to feed on space itself.","The flames didn’t produce smoke...they produced concepts that dissolved before they could be understood.","At the mountain’s peak, visible through the dancing conflagration and the storms that raged around it, a single flower bloomed. Its petals caught light that shouldn’t exist, reflecting colors that had no names, existing in defiance of every force that sought to destroy it.","And those forces were considerable. Storms of pure Paradox raged around the peak, each gust carrying contradictions sharp enough to shred an Honored Living Existence into component possibilities!","The very air seemed to war with itself, being and not-being in rapid succession that created visible tears in reality that sealed themselves only to tear again.","They had paused here after their encounter with the multiplying Inevitability, the one that Titano had so enthusiastically crushed into submission before gifting to Noah. The aftermath of that exchange had left the atmosphere charged with unspoken questions.","Altheon and Thessaly regarded Noah with expressions that mixed wariness with calculation.","Whatever he had given to Titano and Sigrid had transformed them in ways they could not fathom!","The glass woks that Titano had consumed...both their contents and the sacred waters they contained, had elevated the simple giant’s already terrifying physical might to levels that made Honored beings wary.","But it was Sigrid’s transformation that truly commanded attention. Her aura blazed with the intensity of a Prime Living Existence approaching breakthrough, her Tower of Origin reconstructing itself with each passing moment. The very air around her hummed with nascent authority, as if reality itself was preparing to acknowledge her ascension to Honored status.","What could possibly cause such dramatic advancement? What treasures did this mysterious figure possess that could reforge a Tower of Origin to such a terrifying extent?","Titano’s massive form vibrated with barely contained energy as he gazed up at the flower atop the burning mountain. His expression...that mixture of childlike enthusiasm and simple determination that marked all his actions, brightened with sudden purpose.","He beat his chest with enough force to create thunderclaps in the paradoxical atmosphere, the sound somehow both deafening and silent.","“Brother!” he exclaimed, his deep voice carrying the particular cadence of someone who had never quite mastered the language they spoke. “Titano get that little flower for you!”","2/4"]},{"number":4010,"title":"Chapter 4010: Chapter 4009: Loyalty! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4009: Loyalty! I","The declaration carried such earnest sincerity that it transcended its grammatical imperfection.","This was not a question or a request for permission...it was simply Titano stating what would happen with the certainty of someone who had never encountered a problem that couldn’t be solved through sufficient application of physical force.","Noah nodded, a slight smile playing at his lips as he observed the giant’s enthusiasm. “Be careful with it when you retrieve it.”","“Titano very careful! Titano bring Brother best flower!”","Beside them, Thessaly hovered with the rigid posture of someone struggling to maintain professional composure in the face of increasingly unusual circumstances.","Her fairy-like form radiated disapproval that she couldn’t quite voice, while Altheon gazed ahead with the thousand-yard stare of someone processing too much information simultaneously.","It was at this moment that Noah turned to Sigrid, his movement carrying the glory of decision already made. His hand found her waist with casual certainty, drawing her against his side with a possessiveness that asked for no argument!","She blinked at the sudden proximity, though no embarrassment colored her features. Her sterling smiling eyes met his with the direct gaze of someone who had long since passed beyond such simple emotions. “Why did you do that?”","Her question carried genuine curiosity rather than objection, the kind of inquiry that sought understanding.","Noah’s expression darkened slightly, his gaze shifting to track Titano’s enthusiastic charge toward the mountain. The giant moved through the storms of Paradox as if they were gentle breezes, his massive frame somehow refusing to acknowledge dangers that should have unmade him at the conceptual level.","“I have to keep you closer to me now,” Noah said, his voice carrying weight that made even the paradoxical air grow still. “Duke Gwendolyn decided to inform other Dukes regarding your existence.”","BOOM!","The words fell into the space between them like stones into still water, each one creating ripples of implication that spread outward in waves.","“What?!” Sigrid’s voice cracked with shock that quickly transformed into anger. Her aura flared, Origin authority leaking from her form in patterns that made reality itself step back in recognition!","Noah sighed, his gaze still tracking Titano’s progress as the giant literally punched his way through conceptual storms. “She decided to disclose it to three other Dukes...Whisker, Pyralis, and Valen. She knows they are to be trusted, apparently.” His voice carried a particular bitterness on the last word. “She seems to not understand what trust truly stands for.”","Sigrid’s expression shifted through several emotions in rapid succession...betrayal, anger, understanding, and finally a kind of resigned acceptance.","She grit her teeth hard enough that Noah could hear them grinding like the shattering of Wheels, then shook her head with the weariness of someone recognizing their own culpability.","“No,” she said quietly. “This is my mistake. I knew she was on my side, knew her nature, but I didn’t consider... I didn’t think she would...” She trailed off, then straightened with the kind of resolve that had allowed her to survive the destruction of her original form. “This is on me.”","Noah’s response was immediate and firm, his hand tightening slightly on her waist. “You cannot put the stupid decisions of others on your shoulders. Their choices are their own, and the consequences...”","He was interrupted by the sharp intake of breath from both Altheon and Thessaly. The casual way he referred to Duke Gwendolyn’s decision as ‘stupid’ seemed to challenge their fundamental understanding of hierarchy and respect.","Thessaly rose higher in the air, her tiny form radiating indignation that seemed too large for her fairy-like frame. “Duke Gwendolyn only wants the best for the Young Miss! Anything she does is for...”","“You can shut all the way up.”","WAA!","Noah’s voice cut through her protests with booming words!","His eyes, though showing no obvious manifestation of power, carried something that made even an Honored Living Origin pause.","Thessaly actually felt trepidation crawl up her spine...not from any display of overwhelming might, but from something more fundamental.","The certainty in his gaze suggested consequences she couldn’t quite comprehend!","Her expression soured as words died in her throat, the unsaid protests creating a tension that made the paradoxical atmosphere grow thick.","It was at this moment that Titano descended from the mountain’s peak, his entire form glowing with the residual energy of his passage through impossible storms. His skin had taken on a lustrous quality, as if the paradoxes had polished rather than torn him.","And yet...no Living Existential Authority surrounded him!","In his massive hand, held with the delicate care of someone handling spun glass, was a flower torn from its impossible perch.","“Brother!” Titano’s voice boomed with pride and excitement. “I have gotten it for you! Can I continue to grow my wealth with this?!”","He offered the flower with the enthusiasm of a child presenting a found treasure, his simple face bright with anticipation of approval.","Noah accepted the flower with careful movements, his enhanced perception immediately cataloging its properties.","|Paradox Lotus of Singular Purity|:: A flower that blooms only where impossibility becomes so dense it achieves physical form.","Primary Effect: Grants 5,000,000 Purity Quotient units upon consumption","Growth Requirements: Can bloom where at least three types of Inevitabilities have died, or inside an Early Veiled Shore.","Note: The flower exists in a state of constant dissolution and reformation. Consumption must occur within one hour of picking or it ceases to exist entirely...","Noah nodded appreciatively, recognizing the treasure for what it was as he sent it to his Early Veiled Shore for planting right away. “This will indeed make you richer, Titano. Well done.” He paused, his expression growing thoughtful. “But tell me...what is your relationship to Duke Gwendolyn?”","The question seemed to come from nowhere, yet it landed with the weight of careful calculation. Both Thessaly and Altheon’s expressions grew even more unsightly, recognizing the probe for what it was.","Titano scratched his bald head with one massive finger, his expression growing uncharacteristically serious. “The Duke helped Titano come out of a dark place and into the Folds. Titano owes Duke Gwendolyn everything. Without her...” He trailed off, seeming to struggle with concepts his simple vocabulary couldn’t quite express.","Noah’s expression grew stern as he processed this information. His next words were delivered with careful precision, each one a test of loyalty and possibility.","“What if Gwendolyn did something I did not like, and I told you to leave her and join me? I would give you all the riches you could want. Treasures beyond imagination, power beyond everything. ”","Titano’s eyes, usually bright with simple joy, dimmed noticeably. The giant’s massive frame seemed to shrink slightly, as if the weight of the decision was physically pressing down upon him!","For several long moments, he was silent, his face cycling through expressions as thoughts too complex for his usual demeanor warred within.","Finally, he shook his head with obvious reluctance. “Titano likes Brother. Titano want riches, want to be strong, want many things Brother could give.” His voice grew firmer, more certain. “But Titano owes Duke Gwendolyn. Titano... cannot.”","...!","3/4"]},{"number":4011,"title":"Chapter 4011: Chapter 4010: Loyalty! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4010: Loyalty! II","The simple declaration of loyalty carried more weight than any elaborate oath might have!","This was not calculated allegiance...it was the fundamental honesty of someone who understood debt and honor in their most basic forms!","Noah frowned at this response, though something in his expression suggested respect for the giant’s stance. He could push here, could probably find ways to manipulate or coerce, but there were other methods. Better methods.","He reached up...a considerable stretch given their height difference, and patted Titano’s massive frame with something approaching fondness. “Do not worry about it. I will talk to Duke Gwendolyn to release you from your debt to her. Would that be acceptable? If she agrees to release you?”","Titano’s face transformed with sudden hope, his eyes brightening like stars emerging from clouds. “If Duke Gwendolyn agrees, Titano would like to go with Brother! Brother makes Titano rich! Brother treats Titano good!”","Noah smiled, filing away this information for future use. “Good. Then that’s what we’ll do.” He looked ahead into the depths of the Doorway where reality continued its war with itself. “For now, let’s see if we can find a few more Inevitabilities, and then we’ll get out of here.”","“Yes!” Titano’s enthusiasm returned in full force, his massive form practically vibrating with excitement. “Titano will clear the way! Titano will find many Inevitabilities for Brother!”","The giant charged ahead with renewed vigor, his terrifying power creating a wake through the paradoxical space that actually made traversal easier for those following. Each step he took seemed to temporarily force reality to choose a single state, creating brief islands of stability in the chaos.","Noah and Sigrid followed at a more measured pace. Sigrid’s expression remained troubled, her mind clearly wrestling with the implications of Gwendolyn’s betrayal of trust.","Noah didn’t even spare a glance for Altheon and Thessaly as they moved forward, his dismissal of their presence more cutting than any direct confrontation could have been!","—","A tremendous distance away, in the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds, another group made their way through their own Doorway to the Loom.","These doorways were numerous throughout the Battlefront, most leading nowhere, and those that did lead somewhere invariably filled with boundless Inevitabilities or other hazards that prevented advancement toward the ultimate prize.","Alexander Asmodeus moved through this particular Doorway with his characteristic measured grace, each step calculated and precise!","The environment around them defied conventional description...a landscape of shattered white clocks and broken wheels that might have once measured something beyond time.","The fragments floated in air that had the consistency of liquid crystal, each piece reflecting moments that had never occurred, might be occurring, or had already occurred in futures that no longer existed.","The moment their party fully entered the Doorway, prompts materialized before each of them.","|You have entered the Doorway: Origin Graveyard of Forgotten Measurements|","|Special Conditions: Death in this Doorway may retroactively prevent birth. Memories formed here exist in quantum superposition until observed. Success and failure are not mutually exclusive states.|","|Warning: Your perception of entering this Doorway may itself be an echo of a future that won’t occur|","Alexander read through the information with his characteristic calm, his mind already calculating probabilities and possibilities!","Beside him, Seraphina Valorheart gripped her weapon tighter, while Royal Law Tristesse had finally stopped fuming about Noah’s earlier displays, her expression now carved from focused concern.","“This is worse than the report suggested,” Kaedric muttered, his usual confidence shaken by the sheer wrongness of their surroundings.","Tristesse voiced her thoughts as they moved deeper into the Doorway, her attention split between the environment and her companions. “That friend of yours is not ordinary.” She fixed Alexander with a gaze that demanded answers. “If he stems from the same Folds as you...”","Alexander’s frown deepened, clearly wanting to deflect or stop her line of inquiry. But before he could speak, before he could redirect the conversation, something unprecedented occurred!","HUUM!","His Enneagram...that dazzling stellar nine-pointed star that resided on his chest, suddenly blazed with purple-gold light so intense it made reality step back.","Simultaneously, Seraphina Valorheart gasped as her own hidden Enneagram erupted in white-blue brilliance, the light pouring from her form in waves that shouldn’t exist.","The two Enneagrams began to spin in perfect synchronization, their rotation creating weavings that made the shattered clocks and wheels around them resonate. The sound built from whisper to roar to something beyond sound...a fundamental frequency that existence itself recognized!","Then, with the distinctive sound of bronze being torn, space ruptured before them.","The tear that formed was unlike any spatial distortion they had encountered. It didn’t lead to another place...it led to another time, another state of being entirely.","The smell that poured from it defied description: archaic oldness mixed with wonder, the scent of possibilities that had been sealed away since before the current age began!","Prompts cascaded before Alexander’s vision, each one more impossible than the last!","|Desiccated Sleeping Shore of an Early Creature Located|","|The fragments of the Early Tool of THE Living Law have resonated in a domain that THE Living Law’s authority covered in the Earliest Folds|","|Following the paths taken since the Earliest Folds will allow for the recovery of the Early Tool of THE Living Law|","|Warning: This Shore has been dead and sleeping for an unknown number of years|","...!","Alexander stared at the prompts with an expression that cycled through shock, understanding, and grim determination.","Behind him, Royal Law Tristesse’s authority blazed to life, silver-white power creating defensive barriers as her voice cracked with barely controlled alarm.","“What is it?! What happened?” Her usual musical tones had given way to sharp demand, her attention fixed on the archaic tear that promised either unprecedented opportunity or complete annihilation.","Seraphina looked toward Alexander with shock that transformed into something deeper....a recognition that whatever came next would fundamentally change the nature of their journey. “Alexander, what...”","Without explanation, without hesitation, without even acknowledging the questions and concerns of his companions, Alexander Asmodeus stepped into the crack in space.","The bronze tear seemed to welcome him, reality parting like curtains to admit one who carried the keys to doors that had been locked since the Earliest Folds. His form disappeared into that archaic light, leaving his companions to make their own choices about whether to follow into the unknown.","Behind him, Tristesse cursed with the creative eloquence of someone who had lived long enough to know when situations had spiraled completely beyond control!","Yet even as profanity flowed from her lips, she was already moving forward, because some opportunities...and some dangers, were too significant to let pride or caution prevent action!","The Doorway to the Loom suddenly seemed mundane compared to what lay beyond that bronze tear. What slept in that Desiccated Shore? What remnants of THE Living Law’s authority might still linger there? And perhaps most importantly...what would wake when they entered if everything was dead?","The only way to know was to follow Alexander into the archaic unknown, into a Shore that had been sleeping since before the current configuration of existence had been established!","4/4 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming! Looks like we’ll finish top 10 this month!"]},{"number":4012,"title":"Chapter 4012: Chapter 4011: Integrity! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4011: Integrity! I","The garden of impossible fruits seemed to hold its breath as the last of the Dukes departed through their various methods...Duke Whisker simply ceasing to be present, Duke Pyralis leaving in a conflagration that somehow froze the air, and Duke Valen tapping his way through a door that hadn’t existed until he needed it.","Now only Duke Gwendolyn remained, her stellar dark hair catching light that originated from the Wheels of Existence hanging overhead.","Her expression carried a type of particular calmness!","“It seems like you had something to say,” she began, her voice maintaining that diplomatic steadiness that had served her through eons of maneuvering. “I did what I did for the sake of the Young Miss. To help her. To ensure she has everything she needs-”","“Yeah, yeah.”","Noah’s interruption cut through her justification with the casual dismissal of someone who simply didnt care!","His voice emerged coldly.","“Titano. Release him from the debt he owes you. I will take him under my wing.”","...!","The demand fell into the garden’s atmosphere like a stone through still water.","Her expression shifted from calm certainty to genuine surprise, her head tilting slightly as if the angle might help her understand why Titano would suddenly be relevant to their discussion.","But understanding dawned quickly...too quickly for someone of her intelligence to miss the implications!","Her eyes widened as pieces fell into place, her entire bearing shifting from diplomatic to intensely focused.","“Did you...” she began, her voice carrying newfound wariness, “already grasp his nature? Did you find out what he really is?”","His nature.","It might not have mattered to Noah under different circumstances, but his distinction as the Weaver of Existence...that ever-evolving capability that grew more complex with each passing moment, had revealed Titano’s true nature some time ago.","The moment he had first laid eyes on the giant while they went through the doorway, purple text had materialized above his head, revealing truths that most would never perceive!","Noah’s eyes flickered as he recalled the information, the information materializing in his vision with perfect clarity.","|Titano – The Unbreaking Fist|","Classification: Mutated Living Existence affected by Lost Forgotten Principle","Lost Forgotten Principle Influence: The Principle of Absolute Physicality- One of the earliest principles established when existence first wondered if thought or substance held primacy.","-Grants the ability to impose physical reality over conceptual authority","-Current Integration: 1% (Unconscious)","Living Existential Mutation: Corporeal Supremacy- Physical form exists in a state of fundamental priority over energy-based attacks","-Body naturally negates up to 99% of Living Existential Authority from beings below Duke level","-Strength operates on pre-existence parameters, allowing interaction with concepts as if they were physical","-Limitation: Cannot consciously control or understand his own nature","-Side Effect: Drastically reduced intellectual capacity in exchange for absolute physical dominance","Combat Rating: Can physically overcome any Honored Living Existence through brute force alone. Can wrestle Royal Living Existences to stalemate. Duke-level entities require a bit of effort to damage him.","Hidden Potential: If consciousness could be elevated while maintaining mutation, would become one of the most terrifying existences in current reality...","...!","He could obtain waves of lengthy information if he wanted to!","And he now gave the information a dismissive glance before returning his attention to Gwendolyn. “It matters not what being he is. He is too simple and earnest to be under someone like you, so release him.”","The implication was clear...Titano’s honest nature was wasted on someone who treated trust as currency.","Duke Gwendolyn’s expression hardened, her diplomatic mask reasserting itself as she shook her head with practiced regret. “There is nothing you can offer me that would make me release him to you. He is a unique being that will benefit the Living-...!”","Before she could complete her justification, Noah raised his hand with casual certainty. On his palm, reality seemed to condense and crystallize, forming a single droplet that blazed with inner radiance.","A milky droplet of the Sacred Mead of Existence.","The moment it manifested, the garden itself seemed to inhale with desperate want. Every plant, every Wheel of Existence fruit, every mote of dust in the air suddenly oriented toward that single drop!","The vegetation grew more vibrant, colors deepening beyond their already impossible saturation. The crystalline pathways hummed with resonance, and even the golden dome overhead seemed to pulse with renewed vitality!","Duke Gwendolyn herself felt her existence buzz with unprecedented intensity. Every cell, every particle of her being suddenly understood that it was incomplete, that this single droplet contained something that could elevate her beyond current limitations. Her enhanced perception, refined through eons of advancement, could barely process the concentrated potential contained in that small amount of liquid.","She stood frozen, her ancient composure cracking as she looked ahead!","Noah’s voice cut through her shock with simple directness. “Release Titano, and you can have this.”","The offer hung between them like a contract written in starlight. A single drop of Sacred Mead of Existence for the freedom of one Mutated Living Existence.","The exchange rate was absurd as the Duke did not even know what it was! Nor that it was a drop amidst...thousands more that remained!","Duke Gwendolyn’s expression cycled through several complex emotions in rapid succession. Calculation warred with desire, propriety battled against pragmatism. For several seconds that felt like small eternities, she stood perfectly still, her mind racing through implications and possibilities.","Finally, she grit her teeth with the sound of stones grinding together and spoke the word that sealed the bargain.","“Okay!”","HUUM!","The concession erupted from her with more force than intended, her usual control cracking under the weight of what she was accepting.","“Titano is released from all debt to me and is now under your supervision.” She seemed to gather herself, majesty reasserting itself as she continued. “We are all on the same side anyway. Whether Titano is bound to you or me is inconsequential...if this is what you wish for, it is granted.”","...!","Noah looked toward Duke Gwendolyn with even greater disappointment than before. The ease with which she had capitulated, the ready justifications that followed...they painted a picture of someone for whom everything was negotiable, everything had a price!","1/5"]},{"number":4013,"title":"Chapter 4013: Chapter 4012: Integrity! II","paragraphs":["Noah flicked his finger with casual precision, sending the milky white-gold droplet through the air.","Duke Gwendolyn caught it with both hands, cradling it like she had received the most profound treasure imaginable. Her fingers trembled slightly as she secured it within her spatial storage, the action performed with the reverence typically reserved for religious artifacts.","When she looked back at Noah, her eyes blazed with newfound hunger that she didn’t even attempt to hide.","\"If you have resources like this,\" she said, her voice carrying barely contained excitement, \"you could give it to more Dukes and allow for the rapid increase in power across our entire structure. You could give even more to me.\"","She leaned forward slightly, her experience making her next words sound reasonable despite their audacity. \"Apart from Titano, what else do you want? Anything can be exchanged.\"","Exchanged. Anything.","The words settled into Noah’s consciousness. Was that all Titano was to her? Something to be exchanged? A resource to be traded when better options presented themselves?","His dislike toward this Duke crystallized into something colder. His voice emerged with dangerous calm. \"Anything can be exchanged, is that right?\"","Duke Gwendolyn nodded seriously, missing the warning in his tone. \"Yes, anything.\"","Noah’s eyes flashed with cold brilliance as another droplet materialized in his palm. The garden once again responded to its presence, reality itself leaning toward that concentrated potential. Duke Gwendolyn’s body actually trembled with barely suppressed need.","\"Okay,\" Noah said, his voice carrying the weight of test and judgment combined. \"Here is another drop. I will exchange this... for you to be on your knees when you receive it.\"","HUUM!","The words fell into the space between them.","A Duke. On her knees.","Her expression flashed with lividity, the calm diplomatic mask shattering as the full implications of his demand registered!","This was not about resources or power...this was about dignity, about the fundamental respect that her position commanded.","Noah remained cold, his gaze unwavering as he continued. \"What? Is that not for exchange? I thought anything could be exchanged?\"","Duke Gwendolyn’s glorious visage turned to ice. Her mind raced through what she represented, what she had achieved. Who was she? She was a Duke...one of the eighty-one who stood at the pinnacle of Living Origin hierarchy. She had Royal Living Origins under her command, multiple Honored Living Existences who would die at her word. She was power incarnate! She was accumulated wisdom! She was...!","\"Kneel.\"","BOOM!","The single word carried more weight than entire speeches, more command than armies could enforce!","She looked toward Noah coldly, her expression cycling through emotions too complex for simple classification. Then she nodded, her voice emerging with bitter recognition.","\"So this is your true self.\"","Without further hesitation, without dramatic pause, she took a decisive step forward and dropped to her knees.","A Duke...a being whose authority could reshape portions of existence itself...fell to her knees on the crystalline pathway of the garden.","\"...\"","The sight was wrong in ways that transcended simple power dynamics. This was hierarchy inverted, dignity discarded for gain!","Noah looked at her with even greater distaste as he tossed the droplet toward her kneeling form. She caught it with steady hands despite her position, her expression serious as she secured this second treasure.","As she remained on her knees, Noah’s voice emerged with the kind of measured intensity that commanded absolute attention.","\"Out of everything a being can possess...power, wisdom, resources beyond measure...integrity is the one thing that should never be compromised.\" His words carried the weight of fundamental truth.","\"Somewhere, in the vast expanse of our existence, everyone must have a line they will not cross. A boundary that defines not what they can do, but what they won’t do, regardless of the gain.\"","He paused, letting the words settle into her consciousness before continuing with increased intensity.","\"You are such a detestable being that you would likely compromise your integrity for anything deemed sufficient. I could continue pushing you now, tell you to do obscene things...degrade yourself in ways that would haunt your consciousness for eons, and you would likely do them if it meant getting what you want.\"","His voice dropped to barely above a whisper, yet it carried perfectly through the garden’s stillness.","\"You...have no integrity.\"","The condemnation rang through the space with the finality of judgment rendered. Duke Gwendolyn rose from her knees with mechanical precision, brushing off her robes with movements that seemed more habit than necessity.","She looked toward Noah with eyes that had shed any pretense of warmth, her voice emerging with cold certainty.","\"You can call it integrity. I call it doing whatever is necessary to ensure survival and prosperity for the Living Origins.\" She straightened to her full height, authority radiating from her form despite what had just transpired.","\"Because what did I lose just now by getting on my knees? My face? My pride? These are ephemeral concerns that matter only to those who value appearance over result.\"","Her voice grew stronger, more certain, as if she was convincing herself as much as him.","\"I will put them aside every time. For her, for the Young Miss, I will put aside everything. For Order to be restored, for balance to return to existence, I will do everything.\" Her eyes blazed with terrible certainty. \"I will give up everything.\"","Everything.","Once more, someone stood ready to give up their Everything for a cause they deemed greater than themselves.","The only question that remained was whether her Everything was worth anything at all.","As Noah gazed coldly at Duke Gwendolyn, feeling the weight of her absolute yet somehow hollow commitment, he found himself wondering about a more personal question: What was the worth of his own Everything?","---","In the Early Veiled Shore, as Noah contemplated the nature of worth and sacrifice across his many bodies, brilliance suddenly erupted near his primary form.","He turned to witness a sight that drew his attention completely...the Leviathan’s Eternum Cage had reached completion.","The structure defied conventional architecture, existing as something between temple and trap, between sanctuary and prison. Its walls rose from the golden sands in sweeping curves that seemed to follow mathematical principles that hadn’t been discovered yet.","The frame was composed of crystallized authority so pure it appeared to be carved from solid light, yet shadows danced within its depths, suggesting spaces that existed beyond normal dimensions.","Most remarkable were the waters that filled it...Early Sacred Waters that blazed with their own inner radiance!","The liquid was so clear that looking through it was like gazing through crystallized time, yet it pulsed with vitality that made ordinary water seem like dust by comparison. These waters seemed to breathe within the cage.","Prompts materialized before Noah’s vision at that moment.","|The Leviathan’s Eternum Cage has been completed|","Structural Integrity: Perfect","Dimensional Anchoring: Stable","Capacity: Can hold up to 10,000 Basic, 1,000 Refined, 100 Eminent, or 10 Kleos Early Living Marine Lifeforms simultaneously","Activation Requirements: Early Creature blood can be used as bait to attract Marine Lifeforms. Different blood quantities attract different grades:","1 drop: Basic Marine Lifeforms","10 drops: Refined Marine Lifeforms","100 drops: Eminent Marine Lifeforms across current Fold","1,000 drops: Kleos Marine Lifeforms across adjacent Folds","...!","A glorious aquarium!","He looked at its brilliantly as it shone clesr blue and emanated waves of glory!","Without hesitation, Noah leaped into the Cage itself, his body cutting through the air with perfect grace before plunging into those impossible waters.","The sensation that followed defied description...it was like being embraced by liquid starlight, each molecule of water carrying within it the compressed essence of life itself.","He submerged completely, allowing the Early Sacred Waters to flow over and through him.","The liquid was welcoming him like a long-lost element returning to its proper place. He could feel it seeping into his pores, each drop carrying potential that would have overwhelmed lesser beings!","Another prompt appeared soon after.","|Your entry into the Leviathan’s Eternum Cage is recognized as supreme bait|","|Your aura as an Early Creature surpasses blood as attraction, but be careful|","|The Cage will now begin seeking Early Living Marine Lifeforms across dimensional boundaries|","|Estimated time to first capture: 3-7 minutes|","As if responding to the prompt’s declaration, brilliant golden lines erupted from the Cage’s crystalline frame.","They looked like fishing lines spun from captured sunlight, each one disappearing into the vibrant waves of the Shore with purpose that transcended simple hunting!","These lines were reaching across dimensions, through spaces that existed between spaces, hunting for creatures that most beings didn’t even know existed.","Noah floated in the sacred waters, feeling their vitality seeping into every fiber of his being. His eyes remained closed as he contemplated his Everything...what it meant, what it was worth, whether it could be measured against the Everything of others.","A new prompt suddenly blazed across his consciousness as he did so.","|Complexity Quotient has reached: 1,000,473,891|","|Purity Quotient has reached: 1,000,892,734|","|You have crossed the 1 Billion threshold|","|Current power classification: Equivalent to Prime Living Existence|","...!"]},{"number":4014,"title":"Chapter 4014: Chapter 4013: A Stick! I","paragraphs":["He smiled calmly at this notification, the expression carrying satisfaction rather than surprise.","Just like that, within a single day, he had progressed from exceeding Originus Venerant to achieving power that matched Prime Living Existences. His progression was so gloriously fast that others would find it maddening to witness...eons of advancement compressed into hours.","But the resources he had, even with his ridiculous foundation that should have made his path slower...still meant he was faster than many could even imagine!","He drew in a deep breath, actually drinking the Early Sacred Waters that surrounded him, feeling them flow down his throat like liquid advancement itself. The sensation was intoxicating, each swallow adding to his ever-growing power.","\"Since one billion has been reached,\" he said, his voice resonating through the waters with crystalline clarity, \"let the first Kleos Glyph be formed!\"","HUUM!","The declaration rang through the Early Veiled Shore with the weight of existential law being established.","His eyes blazed with brilliant anticipation as he recalled how Moiraine had formed her Kleos Glyphs...those ultimate expressions of power that contained both Origin and Paradox. She could achieve this because she existed as both states simultaneously, an Arch Living Existence that transcended normal categories.","But he was something far beyond even that. Within his existence, he contained aspects of all types of Living Existences, not just two or three, but all ten fundamental forces that shaped reality itself.","Barring one he had not yet attained as it had not bloomed fully within Sigrid.","\"My first Glyph,\" he declared with terrible certainty, \"shall incorporate all ten.\"","...!","The words erupted from him with force that made the Early Veiled Shore itself pause!","His body began to vibrate with frequencies that shouldn’t exist. His completing Early Atlas trembled within his existence, its structures groaning under the strain of what he was attempting. Every Tower of Osmont resonated with vibration, their crystalline structures singing notes that had never been heard together. Glorious Hymns!","He was attempting something that should have been impossible...forming a Kleos Early Living Existential Glyph that incorporated Paradox, Origin, Dimensional, Elemental, Law, Spirit, Emotive, Concept, Temporal, and Quantum authorities simultaneously.","The process was immediately grueling. Reality itself seemed to rebel against the attempt, as if the fundamental forces he was trying to unite had never been meant to coexist within a single expression!","His body convulsed as contradictions tore through him...Origin and Paradox warring for dominance, Temporal and Quantum refusing to synchronize, Elemental and Concept finding no common ground.","With desperate certainty, Noah waved his hand and summoned the bucket containing all remaining Sacred Mead of Existence. Without hesitation, he upended it above his head, swallowing every drop that remained!","Magisterially!","Tyrannically!","Quintessentially!","|Sacred Mead of Existence Consumed: 3,847 drops|","|Warning: Consumption rate exceeds recommended parameters|","|Early Creature physiology adapting to extreme intake|","..!","One by one, the prompts came.","And one by one, they continued!","|Your distinction as an Early Creature is the only factor enabling this attempt|","|Probability of success without Early Creature nature: 0.0000000001%|","|Current probability of success: 12.7%...|","|Sacred Totems, Realm, Nutrients from the Early Veiled Shore, Sacred Mead, and other facotrs are increasing the probability... 34.2%... 51.8%... 77.3%...|","DUM! DUM! DUM!","His body became a battlefield where fundamental forces waged war for dominance.","His skin cracked and reformed, each fissure leaking light of different colors...silver white for Law, gold white for Origin, obsidian gold for Paradox, crimson for Elemental!","The Early Sacred Waters around him began to boil from the energy being released, creating steam that itself carried enough authority to reshape lesser realities.","Throughout the Shore, his Sacred Totems began to resonate in response to his attempt.","Each tower blazed with its own light, their combined radiance creating pillars that stretched toward infinity. The lights converged above the Aquarium, forming something unprecedented...an archaic lighthouse that seemed to exist in all times simultaneously!","From this lighthouse, reality itself seemed to focus into a single point of impossible density.","Noah’s lesser Glyphs...all the Basic and Refined Early Living Existential Glyphs he had painstakingly formed began dissolving, their essence being drawn into the forming creation. They didn’t resist; they seemed to understand that they were becoming part of something greater.","|Basic Early Living Existential Glyphs Consumed|","|Refined Early Living Existential Glyphs Consumed|","|Kleos Glyph Formation: 94% complete|","The process reached a crescendo that made existence itself hold its breath. Then, with the sound of reality sighing and accepting something that shouldn’t exist, the Glyph completed its formation.","|Kleos Glyph Successfully Formed: The Creature’s First Lesson|","HUUM!","The Glyph that inscribed itself upon Noah’s forehead was unlike anything that had existed since the Earliest Folds!","It appeared as a circular pattern that somehow contained ten distinct yet unified symbols, each one representing a different type of Living Existence. They rotated around a central point that seemed to be simultaneously empty and containing everything...a paradox that Origin accepted, that Law defined, that Concept understood.","|The Creature’s First Lesson|","The first lesson THE Creature learned: All forces can be one force if properly understood","Primary Effect: Grants access to Early Creature’s Authority, the ability to treat all Living Existential Authorities as aspects of a single, unified force.","Secondary Effect: All attacks carry traces of all ten authorities, making immunity impossible.","Tertiary Effect: Can temporarily impose \"lessons\" upon reality, forcing it to accept contradictions.","Unique Feature: Grants access to a Goad, a tool of education and discipline.","Current Mastery: 0.1% (Increasing with complexity, purity, usage and understanding)","...!","As the Glyph settled into its place upon his forehead, it pulsed with brilliant white-gold radiance.","He was not given any rest!","From within that light, something began to emerge...something that seemed almost insultingly simple given the magnitude of what had just occurred.","It was...","A stick.","It was perhaps three feet in length, carved from what appeared to be simple white wood. There were no ornate decorations, no obvious signs of power. It looked like something a shepherd might use to guide sheep, or a teacher might use to point at lessons written on air.","|From the newly formed Kleos Glyph, the Rearing Stick of the Early Creature, the Goad, has been obtained|","Noah grasped the simple stick, and immediately, information flooded his consciousness!","|The Goad - Rearing Stick of Existential Education|:: In the Earliest Folds, THE Creature used a tool similar to this to discipline Early Creatures and unruly Living Existences. Not through pain. Instead through understanding forcibly imparted.","Physical Properties: Appears as simple wood. Cannot be broken, burned, or destroyed by any force below Early Creature level.","Activation Requirement: Can only be wielded by one who possesses The Creature’s First Lesson Glyph.","Primary Function: Educational Discipline- a single tap forces the target to understand one fundamental truth about their nature","Secondary Function: Existential Correction- can temporarily \"correct\" flaws in a being’s existence.","Combat Rating: At current 1% access, can rear weak Honored Living Existences and entities of equivalent complexity. Each tap reduces their combat effectiveness by 10% as they are forced to confront truths about themselves.","Growth Potential: As complexity, purity, and mastery increases, can eventually discipline Duke-level entities and even other Early Creatures.","Warning: The truths revealed are always accurate but not always survivable. Some beings shatter when forced to truly understand themselves.","Noah held the simple stick, feeling its weight...not physical weight, but the weight of responsibility, of power that transcended simple destruction!","This was not a weapon in the traditional sense.","It was something far more terrifying: a tool that could force beings to confront the truth of their own existence.","In his hand, he held the power to educate existence itself.","And sometimes, education was the most terrifying force of all!"]},{"number":4015,"title":"Chapter 4015: Chapter 4014: A Stick! II","paragraphs":["The weight of the simple stick in Noah’s hands carried more significance than any weapon he had ever held.","It wasn’t its physical properties...the smooth white wood felt no different from any branch one might find beside a country road. It was the potential within it, the terrible authority to force understanding upon those who might prefer ignorance.","His contemplation was interrupted by a sudden surge of movement in the Leviathan’s Eternum Cage.","|Alert: Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeform Successfully Captured!|","|Species: Crimson-Eyed Depth Tyrant|:: Classification: Apex Predator of Abyssal Trenches. Threat Level: Can overwhelm standard Prime Living Existences. Nutritional Value: Equivalent to 127 Refined Marine Lifeforms.","One of the golden fishing lines suddenly went taut, its crystalline structure humming with strain as something massive fought against its pull. The line blazed brighter, reality bending around it as it hauled its catch across dimensional boundaries with inexorable force.","The Early Sacred Waters in the Cage began to churn, whirlpools forming as space itself was forced to accommodate what was being dragged through.","Then it breached.","The creature that erupted into the Cage was magnificence and terror combined. Its scales were obsidian plates that seemed to absorb light, each one inscribed with natural Glyphs that pulsed with Eminent authority!","Its body was serpentine yet muscled, suggesting both fluidity and devastating power. But it was the eyes that commanded attention...crimson orbs that burned with intelligence far exceeding what one expected from a \"mere\" Marine Lifeform.","The Crimson-Eyed Depth Tyrant took one look at Noah floating in its new prison and immediately recognized what he was. Not the specifics, perhaps, but the fundamental truth that here was something that existed at the apex of all food chains. Its response was instant and decisive...attack before being attacked, establish dominance before becoming prey.","It rushed toward him with speed that compressed the Sacred Waters into visible shock waves, its maw opening to reveal rows of teeth that existed in several dimensions simultaneously. Hundreds of Refined and Eminent Glyphs blazed along its form, each one adding layers of authority to its assault!","Noah blinked at the approaching devastation with the calm of someone watching a particularly aggressive puppy charge. His hand tightened slightly on the Goad, and he made a simple motion...a casual swipe through the water, the kind of gesture one might use to brush away a fly.","PAH!","The sound that resulted shouldn’t have been possible underwater, yet it rang with crystalline clarity. The stick connected with the Tyrant’s scales with force that had nothing to do with physical impact. Its accumulated authority, those hundreds of Glyphs that should have made it nearly invulnerable, simply... didn’t matter!","They might as well have been decorative paintings for all the protection they provided.","The Marine Lifeform’s charge reversed instantly, its massive form driven backward through the water with such force that it created a temporary vacuum.","But more than the physical repulsion, it was the expression in those crimson eyes that told the true story. Shock gave way to horror, horror transformed into primal fear.","Because in that moment of contact, the Goad had done what it was designed to do...it had educated.","Above the trembling creature’s head, words materialized in the water itself, visible only to it and Noah.","|Truth of Existence Revealed: You exist to become nourishment for an Early Creature. Your entire evolutionary line, millions of years of development, all led to this moment where you would provide sustenance to one who stands above the food chain itself. This is not tragedy...this is purpose fulfilled.|","HUUM!","The Tyrant’s trembling intensified as this fundamental truth settled into its consciousness. It had always known it was predator, had defined itself by what it consumed. To suddenly understand that it had always been prey, just prey for something so far above it that the concept hadn’t existed in its limited worldview... the revelation was shattering.","Noah observed its fearful form with something approaching sympathy. He beckoned toward it with his free hand, a simple gesture that somehow carried more command than any roar or threat could have achieved.","The Marine Lifeform approached with the tentative movements of something that had just learned its place in existence. When it reached him, Noah patted its massive head with genuine fondness, his laughter echoing through the Sacred Waters.","\"Don’t look so terrified,\" he said, though he knew it couldn’t understand his words, only his intent. \"Purpose fulfilled is better than purpose unknown.\"","The Rearing Stick hummed in his hand with satisfaction at a lesson properly delivered. This tool... it needed to be used more. The possibilities were intoxicating!","Noah launched himself from the Cage with a powerful stroke, his body breaking through the surface in a spray of Sacred Water that caught the glorious light of the Shore like liquid diamonds. He landed on the golden sands with practiced grace, water running from his form in streams that seemed reluctant to leave his presence.","Moiraine approached immediately, her expression carrying that mixture of deference and determination that had become her signature. \"Sir,\" she said, her voice steady despite what she was about to reveal, \"here are those I defeated before things turned crazy.\"","With a wave of her hand, space distorted to release her stored prizes. Six corpses materialized on the golden sands...the Dead Existences she had systematically destroyed during the chaos in the Temporal Folds. Each one radiated residual wrongness, their forms caught between states of being even in death.","But what happened next drew Noah’s complete attention.","The Kleos Glyphs adorning Moiraine’s body...those ultimate expressions of power that she had painstakingly formed, began to crack. Not from damage or degradation, instead from deliberate sacrifice!","One by one, they shattered like crystalline sculptures struck by hammers of pure will, their essence condensing into something far more precious.","Light erupted from each breaking Glyph. The fragments condensed, compressed, and transformed into perfect shards that blazed with potential beyond normal classification.","|Ten Kleos Glyphs of Paradoxical Genesis have been sacrificed|","|Ten Shards of the Seed of the Lost Forgotten Principle: The Principle of Existential Duality have been created|","|Current Shard Count: 11/100|","Moiraine gathered the shards with reverent care, each one pulsing with the compressed essence of what she had given up. She offered them to Noah with both hands, her eyes meeting his with unwavering certainty.","\"Sir,\" she said, and the way she spoke that single word carried more meaning than entire speeches might convey. It was acknowledgment and devotion, respect and something deeper that defied simple classification. \"For you, I will continue to form more and sacrifice.\"","...!","The earnestness in her expression, the absolute certainty with which she offered up power that others would kill to possess... it was something else entirely.","Her ’Sirs’ were intoxicating!","Noah looked at her devoted figure as his eyes burned brightly. He leaned closer, his voice dropping to a whisper meant only for her. \"I really need to find a place of privacy for the two of us...\"","...!","A whisper.","Yet before he could complete the thought, reality responded to his barely voiced desire.","|Construction Option Available: Early Abode of the Early Creature|","|Resource Requirements: Option 1: 500 Drops of Early Creature Blood. Option 2: Nutrients from currently processing corpses.|","|Note: Construction requires manual assembly. Materials and building blocks will be provided, but the Abode must be built by hand to properly attune to its creator’s essence.|","...!"]},{"number":4016,"title":"Chapter 4016: Chapter 4015: A Stick! III","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes lit up with interest as he considered the possibilities. An abode...a private space within his Shore where certain activities could occur without observation.","Yes, this was necessary!","He looked down at the six corpses of Honored Dead Existences that Moiraine had provided, his mind already calculating distributions. \"Evaluate and devour,\" he commanded the Shore itself.","The response was immediate:","|Six Honored Dead Existence Corpses Evaluated|","|Total Nutritional Value: Equivalent to 1500 Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeforms|","|Distribution Parameters Set: 35% to Moiraine for Kleos Glyph formation, 25% to Early Abode construction materials, 40% to personal advancement|","|Distribution Commencing...|","The golden sands beneath the corpses began to shift and churn, drawing them down with the patient hunger of something that knew how to savor its meals. As they disappeared, Noah turned his attention to the broader Shore.","\"Henry! Kazuhiko! Emperor Penguin! Liora!...\" His voice carried across the expanded territory with crystalline clarity. \"Come here and help me build something...\"","The named individuals emerged from their meditative positions, their bodies still buzzing with the complexity and purity they had been absorbing. Henry’s features had taken on an almost crystalline quality, while Kazuhiko’s hand rested on a katana that now hummed with barely contained authority.","The Emperor Penguin waddled forward with dignity that transcended his somewhat ridiculous form, and Liora moved with the fluid grace of someone whose connection to primal forces had deepened, her eyes filled with purpose as she thought of her father!","They converged toward the center of the Early Veiled Shore, where something unprecedented was beginning to manifest.","Stone-like materials began to materialize from thin air, emerging gradually like thoughts becoming solid. Each block was unique yet clearly part of a greater whole, inscribed with patterns that suggested function beyond mere structure.","\"We can always use more people,\" Noah mused, his gaze turning toward the mist that marked the Shore’s boundaries.","As if responding to his unvoiced invitation, the mist began to part, revealing something like a doorway...a threshold between the Shore and the greater Infiniverse that contained it. The first figure to emerge made Noah simultaneously smile and question his decision.","The Queen of Matter burst through the opening in an explosion of enthusiasm that seemed to reshape reality around her presence. Her white dress was adorned with jewels that weren’t merely decorative...each one was a crystallized concept, a thought given form.","Books and grimoires orbited her form in complex patterns, their pages fluttering with winds that carried whispers of Fables.","\"I HAVE BEEN MADE RELEVANT AGAIN!\" she screamed with joy that could have powered small civilizations.","Her eyes locked onto Noah with the intensity of someone viewing their personal idol. \"Sir! Thank you for putting me in the main story once more! Even though I was having ridiculous fun observing the transforming Infiniverse Wheel of Existence...did you know how crazy its becoming?!\"","...!","She spun in place, taking in the Early Veiled Shore with eyes that seemed to catalogue every impossible detail simultaneously.","\"By the way,\" she continued without pause for breath, \"do you know what-...oh my word, is that an aquarium?!\"","...!","Noah shook his head with exasperation, wondering if bringing her here was brilliant or catastrophic.","Behind the Queen of Matter, more figures began to emerge through the doorway. Dr. Hall stepped through with his white coat. Erikson followed, his massive frame having to duck through the opening. Ayame, Romulus, the Great Beyonder, the Great Mother, Lilith...and dozens of other beings who had been part of his journey but had faded into the background as powers escalated beyond their ability to participate.","Now they entered the Early Veiled Shore with expressions of wonder that reminded Noah why he had brought them. They deserved to be part of this, to witness and participate in the glory!","\"Everyone,\" he called out, his voice carrying warm authority, \"energize yourselves by drinking droplets of the Early Sacred Water from the shores, then come help build an Abode.\"","The assembled beings nodded with various expressions of amazement. The Queen of Matter, predictably, was the first to act. She bounded toward the crystalline waters with the enthusiasm of someone who had just been offered unlimited access to a library of forbidden knowledge. She cupped the Sacred Water in her hands, drinking deeply, and the transformation was immediate...her entire form began to pulse with newfound vitality.","She returned with her mouth still full of Sacred Water, her cheeks puffed out like a chipmunk’s as she tried to speak around the liquid. Her eyes were wide with excitement, practically vibrating with readiness for whatever came next.","Noah reached out and ruffled her hair with genuine affection. \"Let’s get started.\"","---","As his primary body organized construction in the Early Veiled Shore, another version of himself navigated the twisted passages of the Doorway to the Loom in the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds.","The crimson obsidian halls stretched in different directions, their surfaces reflecting possibilities rather than images. In a relatively stable pocket of space, Noah faced the massive form of Titano.","\"I have something to show you,\" he said, raising his hand to project an illusory scene into the air between them.","The memory played out with perfect clarity...Duke Gwendolyn in her garden, her voice carrying that diplomatic certainty as she spoke the words: \"Titano is released from all debt to me and is now under your supervision.\"","...!","Altheon and Thessaly watched the projection with expressions of shock that bordered on horror. Their enhanced perceptions were calculating furiously, trying to determine what Noah could possibly have offered to make Duke Gwendolyn release such a valuable asset.","The Duke never gave up anything without receiving something of greater value in return...it was fundamental to her nature.","Titano watched the scene with eyes that dimmed noticeably. His massive frame seemed to shrink slightly, the hurt visible in every line of his simple, honest face!","He had genuinely believed Duke Gwendolyn cared about him beyond his utility, that their relationship transcended mere debt and service!","After several long seconds of silence, he looked at Noah with those dimmed eyes and asked, \"Does this mean Titano is okay to come work under Brother?\"","Noah shook his head firmly, reaching up to pat the giant’s massive arm. \"You won’t work under me. You’re my brother, right? We’ll simply move together, and as your Older Brother, I’ll help you out and make you rich just like me.\"","...!","The transformation in Titano’s expression was immediate and complete. Joy erupted across his features like sunrise over mountains.","\"Brother!\" he boomed, sweeping Noah up in a bear hug that would have crushed anyone below Honored Living Existence level to paste.","Noah’s body creaked audibly under the embrace, his enhanced durability the only thing preventing immediate structural failure.","When Titano finally released him, the giant’s expression had shifted to thoughtful confusion.","\"Brother,\" he said with unexpected seriousness, \"I might be older than you, though?\"","Noah waved his hands with equal seriousness, his expression suggesting this was a matter of grave importance. \"Being richer and more experienced makes me older. Age is not just time, Brother. It’s about wisdom, wealth, and the ability to provide guidance.\"","Titano’s eyes widened as if he had just received profound enlightenment. He nodded slowly, filing this information away with the same care he applied to all of Noah’s teachings. \"Titano understands! Brother Noah is older because Brother Noah is richer!\"","...!"]},{"number":4017,"title":"Chapter 4017: Chapter 4016: A Stick! IV","paragraphs":["Off to the side, Sigrid smiled and shook her head at the exchange between Noah and Titano.","Yet her amusement faded as her thoughts turned to Duke Gwendolyn and her recent actions. The betrayal of trust, the casual trading of loyalties...it left a bitter taste that wouldn’t fade.","Her contemplation was shattered by a sound that made reality itself step back in recognition.","\"ROAAAAR!\"","The bellow echoed through the winding halls with force that created visible distortions in the paradoxical space. But more terrifying than the volume was how that single voice immediately multiplied, becoming five distinct roars that harmonized into something that challenged sanity itself.","The aura that followed made the air thick with wrongness...five Inevitabilities, each one radiating power equivalent to an Honored Living Existence, were rushing toward their position.","Thessaly and Altheon immediately shifted into combat readiness, their accumulated authority beginning to manifest. Titano cracked his knuckles with sounds like mountains breaking, his expression brightening with anticipation.","\"Brother,\" he said cheerfully, \"I will take care of these and gift them to you as well!\"","But Noah raised his hand in a stopping gesture. \"No... let me try these ones.\"","The silence that followed was deafening. Even Sigrid turned to look at him with barely concealed concern. She opened her mouth as if to question his decision, then closed it with visible effort. He was an Early Creature...he could probably do things that defied comprehension. She had to trust that.","Titano, however, had no such restraint. He blinked his massive eyes and said with blunt honesty, \"Brother, you have no muscles like Titano and your figure is scrawny. Will you be okay?\"","Noah turned to face the giant with an expression of patient instruction. \"Brother, sometimes those who are truly rich can look scrawny, but they could buy a weapon that makes them more powerful than anyone else. And what I will use today is a truly terrifying weapon.\"","As he spoke, something materialized in his hand.","A stick.","Just... a stick.","The Rearing Stick of the Early Creature, the Goad, appeared with no fanfare, no blazing light, no reality-warping presence. To everyone watching, it looked like Noah had just summoned a piece of white wood, the kind of thing one might use to poke a campfire.","Yet Noah carried it forward with the bearing of a knight carrying a legendary blade!","He stepped ahead of Titano, Sigrid, and the others, positioning himself as the vanguard against the approaching horror. The image was simultaneously glorious and absurd...a man with a stick preparing to face five Inevitabilities.","They emerged from the twisted space like nightmares given form and purpose:","|One Inevitability turned to Five Inevitabilities Detected: The Writhing Paradox of Unending Reach|","|Classification: Each entity possesses power equivalent to Honored Living Existence|","|Form: Roiling masses of tentacles that exist in multiple states simultaneously|","|Warning: Paradoxical nature allows them to be everywhere and nowhere until observed|","The creatures that approached defied rational observation. They were masses of tentacles, but the tentacles weren’t quite physical...they existed in states of possibility until the moment they chose to strike. Each one possessed thousands of writhing appendages that phased in and out of reality, their surfaces inscribed with paradoxes that blazed!","Noah moved forward with his stick raised, and the battle that followed would be carved into the memories of all who witnessed it.","The first Inevitability struck with tentacles that existed in seventeen different possible positions simultaneously. Normal defense would have been impossible...how could one block an attack that came from every direction including some that didn’t exist?","But the Goad didn’t operate according to normal principles.","PAH!","Noah’s stick swept through the air with casual precision, and somehow, impossibly, it connected with all seventeen possibilities at once. The tentacles recoiled with visible shock, their paradoxical nature momentarily forced into a single, painful reality.","|The Goad’s Authority is forcing a singular truth upon paradoxical existence|","The second and third Inevitabilities attacked in coordination, their tentacles weaving through space in patterns that created tears in causality itself. Noah’s body, despite his enhanced capabilities, simply wasn’t fast enough to dodge everything. Several tentacles struck him, their touch carrying paradoxes that should have unmade him at the conceptual level.","Should have.","|Passive Defense Activated: The Kleos Glyph of the Creature’s First Lesson shines brightly.|","|Paradoxical attacks recognized and rejected. Your existence refuses to acknowledge contradictions.|","HUUUM!","The Kleos Glyph on his forehead blazed with white-gold light, and the paradoxes simply... didn’t take.","They struck his form and dissolved, their contradictions unable to take root in someone who carried the unified authority of all ten Living Existences in the form of a single glyph!","A single...Glyph!","Noah pressed forward, his stick moving in patterns that looked almost casual but carried devastating purpose. Each strike forced understanding upon the Inevitabilities.","PAH! - \"You exist because you shouldn’t, but that’s not strength, it’s confusion\"","PAH! - \"Your paradoxes are questions, not answers\"","PAH! - \"You fear definition because definition would reveal your emptiness\"","...!","The fourth and fifth Inevitabilities tried to overwhelm him through sheer mass, thousands of tentacles converging from every possible angle. Noah’s defensive capabilities were tested to their limits...he took hits that sent him flying, tentacles that wrapped around his limbs, attacks that would have torn apart Prime Living Existences and injured weak Honored Ones!","But he endured because a single Kleos Glyph shone again and again. And more than endured...he educated.","His stick never stopped moving, each contact delivering truths that the Inevitabilities couldn’t reject or ignore. The battle wasn’t about physical dominance but about forcing these paradoxical beings to confront the fundamental nature of their existence.","The observers watched in shocked silence as Noah, armed with nothing but a stick, systematically broke down five Honored-level threats!","Altheon’s ancient eyes were wide with disbelief. Thessaly had actually stopped hovering, her fairy form dropping to the ground in shock. Sigrid watched with a mixture of awe and something deeper...a recognition that she was witnessing something unprecedented.","But it was Titano’s reaction that was most profound. The giant watched his scrawny brother beat cosmic horrors with a stick, and his simple mind reached a profound conclusion: being rich meant having the best tools!","The battle reached its climax as all five Inevitabilities, educated beyond their ability to maintain paradoxical existence, collapsed into quivering masses.","They didn’t die...death would have been mercy. Instead, they lay there, tentacles twitching weakly, trembling from the beating delivered by a simple stick.","Noah floated above them grandly, the Goad still held in his hand like a teacher’s pointer after a particularly effective lesson. He had given his first true combat lesson, and the Inevitabilities had been thoroughly educated.","The silence that followed was broken only by the weak whimpering of existential horrors that had just learned truths they would have preferred to remain ignorant of.","Noah looked down at them with satisfaction. The Rearing Stick had proven its worth beyond question. And this was only at one percent of its true power!","He couldn’t help but wonder...what would happen when he could access more!"]},{"number":4018,"title":"Chapter 4018: Chapter 4017: A Stick! V","paragraphs":["The twisted reality of the Doorway to the Loom seemed to hold its breath as Noah floated above the decimated Inevitabilities.","Their forms, once terrifying manifestations of paradox given purpose, now lay scattered like broken toys after a child’s tantrum.","With a casual wave of his hand, he sent them away to the Early Veiled Shore, their essence compressed into streaks of light that disappeared through dimensional boundaries.","Prompts materialized before his vision with the clinical precision of existence analyzing its resources.","|Five Inevitabilities Successfully Captured and Evaluated. Classification: The Writhing Paradox of Unending Reach. Total Combined Value: 1390 Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeforms.|","|Bonus Modifier: Educational damage inflicted has increased absorption efficiency by 23%.|","..!","As he absorbed this information, the sound of massive footsteps approached from behind.","Titano’s enormous frame cast shadows that somehow existed in multiple dimensions simultaneously, his eyes shining with the kind of hero worship typically reserved for legendary figures.","\"Brother!\" the giant exclaimed, his voice carrying genuine awe that transcended his simple vocabulary. \"Titano looks up to you! You did not use any Living Existential Authority to beat up that Inevitability!\"","His gaze fixed on the simple stick in Noah’s hand with newfound respect. \"Is your weapon... is that stick so powerful?\"","Noah nodded with the seriousness of someone imparting crucial wisdom. \"Very powerful, Brother. This stick carries weight that most cannot comprehend.\"","Titano’s eyes grew even wider, his massive hands flexing with barely contained curiosity. \"Can Titano hold the stick? Titano is very strong!\"","Noah’s expression suggested he was about to refuse, but the eager hope in the giant’s eyes made him reconsider. \"You likely won’t be able to carry it, Brother.\"","The warning, predictably, had the opposite effect.","Titano straightened to his full, imposing height, his muscles...which could shatter Royal Living Existences through pure physical force, flexing with determination. This was a challenge, and Titano had never met a physical challenge he couldn’t overcome!","Noah sighed with the resignation of someone who knew this lesson needed to be learned through experience rather than words. \"Okay,\" he said, holding the stick lightly in his hand as if it weighed nothing. He placed it gently onto Titano’s outstretched palm.","The effect was instantaneous and devastating.","BOOM!","Titano’s massive figure, which had weathered attacks from beings of incomprehensible power, began to tremble.","His arm, thick as an ancient tree trunk, started to buckle. The simple stick seemed to carry the weight of concepts themselves...truth, education, understanding, all compressed into three feet of white wood with traces of gold!","The giant’s knees began to bend, his entire frame being forced downward as if existence itself was pressing upon him. The crimson obsidian floor beneath them began to crack under the transferred pressure, reality struggling to accommodate weight that transcended physical measurement.","Before Titano’s body could be driven completely into the floor, Noah made a beckoning gesture. The Goad responded immediately, floating from the giant’s trembling palm back to its rightful owner’s hand with the casual ease of returning home.","Titano remained on one knee, his massive chest heaving with exertion, eyes wide with a mixture of shock and respect. Noah looked at him with understanding rather than mockery.","\"Some weights,\" Noah said, \"only a select few can bear. Not because of strength or will, but because of the nature of what they are. The Goad doesn’t test your muscles, Brother...it tests your capacity to carry the responsibility of forcing truth upon others. Oh, and you need a certain Tattoo for it!\"","Titano nodded slowly, processing this lesson with the same care he applied to all of Noah’s teachings. Noah reached out to pat the giant’s shoulder with genuine affection.","\"Don’t beat yourself up over it. Your strength lies elsewhere, and that’s perfectly fine.\"","The lovable titan’s expression brightened immediately at the reassurance, his simple nature not allowing disappointment to linger.","Noah felt the weight of the stick in his hands...not physical weight, instead, the weight of purpose, of potential consequences.","His gaze shifted, moving past Titano to settle on the two figures who had been observing from what they considered a safe distance.","Both Thessaly and Altheon instantly shuddered.","When Noah’s focus moved past Thessaly to lock onto Altheon specifically, the fairy-like being released a breath she didn’t realize she’d been holding. Relief flooded through her tiny form so intensely that she actually dropped several inches in altitude before catching herself.","Meanwhile, Altheon felt his entire existence begin to tremble. The sensation started in his core and radiated outward, every particle of his being recognizing that it was under scrutiny from something that could unmake it with casual indifference.","\"What?\" he managed to say, the word emerging as barely more than a hesitant whisper.","Noah’s eyes sharpened to points that could have cut through dimensional barriers. His voice, when it came, carried the weight of judgment already rendered!","\"You did something a while ago that you may not even remember or consider consequential.\" Each word was delivered with precision that made them impossible to misunderstand. \"I was going to kill you for it, but I will discipline you instead, so... come here.\"","HUUM!","The silence that followed was deafening.","Altheon’s luminous form actually paled, his ancient features cycling through confusion and growing dread. \"What? I didn’t...\"","His protests died as his gaze fell upon the simple stick that had just thoroughly thrashed five Inevitabilities. The fear that crawled up his spine was primal, instinctive, the kind that bypassed rational thought entirely!","Desperately, he looked toward Sigrid, seeking intervention from someone who might carry influence.","She met his gaze with calm indifference, her expression making it clear that this was not her concern. His attention shifted to Thessaly, but she had already turned away, her tiny form trembling with shame and fear, unwilling to involve herself in whatever justice was about to be dispensed.","She almost wanted to reassure Altheon that she could potentially bring him back incase he was killed...but she couldn’t bring herself to say anything!","Noah’s frown deepened at the delay. \"Would you rather I kill you than discipline you?\"","The question hung in the air. After a moment that stretched toward eternity, Altheon gritted his teeth and floated forward. Each movement felt like swimming through crystallized dread, his enhanced perception calculating thousands of escape possibilities while his wisdom told him none would succeed.","When he stopped before Noah, the Prime Living Origin looked like someone approaching their own funeral.","Noah raised the Goad with ceremonial precision. \"This is for your education,\" he said, though he offered no explanation of what crime warranted this punishment.","The first strike came with deceptive gentleness.","PAH!","The sound rang through the paradoxical space, and Altheon’s scream followed immediately.","It wasn’t the physical impact...his body could withstand forces that would shatter Wheels of Existence. It was the Truth that accompanied it!","|You are a coward who attacks those weaker when you think there will be no consequences|","The second strike followed before he could process the first.","PAH!","|Your accumulated wisdom means nothing when you act on base impulses|","Altheon’s cries grew more desperate. This wasn’t pain that his Living Origin Authority could heal. This was fundamental truth being carved into his existence, each revelation more devastating than physical destruction could ever be!","PAH!","|You justify your actions with authority, but authority without integrity is merely sophisticated barbarism.|","The Prime Living Origin, who had existed for eons, who had witnessed the rise and fall of countless civilizations, was reduced to sobbing!"]},{"number":4019,"title":"Chapter 4019: Chapter 4018: A Stick! VI","paragraphs":["Red marks appeared across his luminous form...not wounds, but evidence of education forcibly imparted. They seemed to exist outside his body’s natural regeneration, as if the lessons they represented were too important to be healed away.","PAH!","|You will remember this moment every time you consider acting without honor.|","By the end, Altheon gazed at Noah and the stick with the kind of fear typically reserved for forces of nature!","He understood now, with terrible clarity, that this simple tool could do something far worse than kill him...it could make him understand himself!","Noah nodded with satisfaction, lowering the Goad. He didn’t mention that Altheon’s crime had been attempting to kill one of his bodies days ago. The lesson had been delivered; the specifics were irrelevant.","\"Pick him up until he recovers,\" he said to Thessaly, his tone brooking no argument.","The Honored Living Existence nodded frantically, her wings fluttering as she approached Altheon’s trembling form. She stared at the red marks covering his body with horrified fascination. They defied every law of regeneration she understood. Would they even heal? Or would they remain as permanent reminders of education forcibly received?","With that matter settled, Noah moved to stand beside Sigrid, taking her hand with gentle certainty. Her fingers intertwined with his without hesitation, though her expression carried questions she wouldn’t voice in present company.","\"Let’s see what else is in this place\" he said, his stern demeanor softening into something warmer. \"Afterwards, I need to bring you to my place. My home.\"","...!","Behind them, Titano’s enthusiasm returned full force, apparently unaffected by witnessing Altheon’s discipline. \"Will Titano get to visit as well???\"","Noah glanced back with a genuine smile. \"Of course, Brother. And I’ll make sure to prepare a feast.\"","The giant’s eyes lit up with joy that could have powered Wheels.","With renewed purpose, they delved deeper into the twisted passages of the Doorway to the Loom, leaving behind a thoroughly educated Prime Living Origin and a fairy who would think very carefully before crossing Noah!","---","In another Doorway entirely, past a bronze tear that had opened due to the resonance of ancient authorities, Alexander Asmodeus stepped into a realm that time had forgotten.","The Desiccated Sleeping Shore stretched before them like the graveyard of dreams. The sands, which should have been golden, were ash-gray, as if all color had been leached away by eons of abandonment. The sky above held no sun, no stars, only a uniform grayness that seemed to press down with the weight of forgetting.","Hundreds of dead trees dotted the landscape, their branches reaching toward nothing, their bark preserved in death like monuments to what had once been. Ancient structures rose from the sands...abodes and towers that looked as if they had been beautiful once, before time and desertion had worn them down to skeletal remains.","Royal Law Tristesse approached one of the structures with professional curiosity, reaching out to test its integrity. Her hand, wreathed in Law Authority that could reshape reality, met the worn stone. Nothing happened. She pressed harder, her power flaring. The structure didn’t even acknowledge her attempt!","\"Indestructible,\" she murmured with genuine surprise. \"Whatever force preserves this place transcends current understanding.\"","Alexander moved deeper into the Shore, drawn by instincts he didn’t fully understand. His Enneagram, the nine-pointed star on his chest, began to spin with increasing speed. As he neared certain areas, debris that looked like nothing more than dust and fragments suddenly animated, flying toward him as if magnetized.","A piece of what might have been pottery. A fragment of crystallized wood. Each item was absorbed directly into his Enneagram, disappearing into whatever space existed within that geometric impossibility.","The same phenomenon occurred with Seraphina, her own Enneagram drawing different fragments, as if each piece knew exactly where it belonged.","They continued deeper, past collapsed buildings that might have been homes, past dried fountains that might have once held Sacred Waters. The desolation was complete, yet somehow budding with possibility.","Then, as Alexander’s Enneagram absorbed what looked like the hand of an ancient clock, dust cascaded from above as a dirty gray cloth slid off a torn wall.","What was revealed made Seraphina scream, stumbling backward in fear!","A head.","Massive, bisected, yet somehow preserved in perfect, horrible detail. The eyes still burned with rage that had transcended death, frozen in eternal fury. The mouth gaped open in a scream that had lasted eons, teeth visible like monuments to violence.","It was an Early Creature!","This was all that remained of an Early Creature in its own Shore...a head that radiated such terrible presence that even in death, even bisected and abandoned, it made their hearts fill with dread that transcended rational fear.","Alexander maintained his composure through will alone, though sweat beaded on his forehead as he gazed upon this testament to ancient catastrophe.","Their Enneagrams blazed simultaneously, and prompts appeared.","|Synchronized Enneagram Activation Possible. While connected, the holders of the Enneagram fragments can induce a memory replay within the preserved consciousness of the Early Creature. This memory will reveal the locations of the Early Tool fragments of THE Living Law.|","|Connection Requirement: Physical and energetic synchronization between Enneagram holders.|","...!","Alexander’s expression grew heavy as the implications settled. Seraphina’s eyes opened wide, understanding exactly what \"connected\" meant in this context.","She peeked over at Alexander to see his expression!","Alexander... couldn’t help but remember Noah’s words in Aeternitas Concordia. His gaze grew even more clouded as he looked at Seraphina, whose expression mixed embarrassment with something deeper.","Something...had to be done as too much was at stake!","---","In the Transcendent Spiritual Folds, existence took on properties that had more to do with thought than substance.","The Great Usurper floated without determined form, his consciousness spread across multiple probability states as he let the currents of Living Spiritual Authority carry him where they would. The sights were marvelous...thoughts given architecture, emotions crystallized into landscapes, concepts that had learned to dream.","He hummed contentedly, the sound reverberating through dimensions of pure consciousness.","With casual interest, he pulled up his Idle Gaming System interface, noting the golden glow on the [Transcendent Spiritual Folds Living Existential Dungeon] icon.","Time to collect his idle rewards!","Golden brilliance erupted around him as the system processed his accumulated gains.","|Idle Loot Obtained!|","[+10 Prime Living Spirit Shards (Collect 100 to summon a Prime Living Spirit Idle Soldier)], [+1 Honored Living Spirit Shard (Collect 100 to summon an Honored Living Spirit Idle King)], [+20 Living Existence Upgrade Crystals], [+5 Bottles of Liquified Consciousness], [+3 Memory Palace Blueprints], [+1 Seed of the Primordial Spirit Tree], [+1 Trillion Idle EXP]","...!","The Great Usurper examined each reward with great interest, but it was the seed that truly captured his attention. He pulled it from his system space, the object materializing as something between light and thought.","[Seed of the Primordial Spirit Tree] :: A seed that predates the division between consciousness and substance. When planted in appropriate soil, will grow into a tree that produces Spirit Fruits. Each fruit grants permanent increase Living Existential Authority, 100,000,000 in Complexity and Purity, and entrance into a unique state of mind.","Planting Requirements: Soil blessed by an Early Creature, watered with Sacred Waters, tended by one who understands the nature of divided existence","Growth Time: 1,000 years (acceleratable through specific methods)","...!","The Great Usurper appreciated the seed’s potential, but shook his head with wry amusement. He didn’t have what it took to plant such a thing. Who in existence did? Early Creature? What even was that?","He thought for a bit.","Then memory struck like lightning.","Osmont.","That ridiculously overpowered being who had once mentioned, almost as an afterthought, that when everything was over and done, he actually wanted to be a farmer.","The Great Usurper laughed, the sound rippling through spiritual dimensions. Had Osmont ever worked toward that dream? Could the man who seemed capable of anything actually be somewhere, tending to crops as a mere farmer?","Maybe he would be able to utilize this seed.","After all, what was more fitting than a farmer receiving seeds that could reshape existence itself?"]},{"number":4020,"title":"Chapter 4020: Chapter 4019: Farmers of Existence! I","paragraphs":["In the time when existence still questioned its own validity, when the boundaries between possible and impossible remained undrawn, there lived a Fold Dweller who possessed nothing of what would later be considered power.","No Living Existential Authority flowed through his veins. No Glyphs adorned his form. He was, by every measure that would come to matter, insignificant.","Yet he possessed eyes that saw.","Not metaphorically, not spiritually, but literally...eyes that perceived what should have been imperceptible, that noticed what preferred to remain unnoticed.","It was these eyes that allowed him to witness something that should have been impossible... THE Living Spirit, moving through the Earliest Folds like thought given purpose.","THE Living Spirit paused in its journey, its form...if form it could be called, rippling with surprise that transcended simple emotion. To be observed by a Fold Dweller, a being without even the smallest spark of authority...","\"Due to your unique eyes that allow you to see,\" THE Living Spirit said, its voice carrying the weight of consciousness acknowledging consciousness, \"I will answer any questions you have about existence.\"","The Fold Dweller gazed upon this manifestation of spiritual authority with reverence that bordered on worship. When he spoke, his question carried the desperate hope of every being that had ever felt inadequate in the face of infinity.","\"In existence, how can one become more complex the easiest way?\" His words tumbled forth with barely contained urgency. \"If Fold Dwellers are not Living Existences and do not become one, any step towards complexity is arduous and long. How can they advance? How can they compare?\"","THE Living Spirit regarded him with attention that seemed to pierce through to fundamental truths. When it responded, each word carried philosophical weight that would echo through epochs.","\"Existence never decided that Living Existences or Early Creatures would be the fastest to progress in complexity or purity.\" The statement hung in the air like a revelation.","\"Lifeforms themselves can decide that. If things feel hard, if progress feels slow... then one simply is not following the right path for their specific lifeform.\"","The Fold Dweller’s expression showed he remained unconvinced, his mortal mind struggling to grasp concepts that transcended mortality. \"Then which methods can I use to become stronger faster?\"","THE Living Spirit’s form shifted, as if considering how to translate infinite understanding into finite words. \"You could be a farmer of existence itself...nurture wonders to grow, then consume those wonders for their accumulated complexity. You could devour the Everything of all others, taking their potential into yourself. Or...\" it paused, the silence buzzing with possibility, \"you can simply learn a Principle.\"","Confusion bloomed across the Fold Dweller’s features. \"What is...a Principle?\"","THE Living Spirit’s attention seemed to intensify, as if this question was both expected and profound. \"If you knew that answer, you would never again worry about power. To truly understand a Principle, one must learn it from one of THE Living Existences. One must learn it from the Folds as they are right now.\" Its form rippled with something that might have been warning. \"If ever the Principles are to be Lost or Forgotten... gaining any grasp on them will be an impossibility.\"","The weight of this revelation drove the Fold Dweller to his knees. His voice cracked with desperate hope as he pleaded, \"Please, teach me. Show me the way to Principles, to power, to significance!\"","THE Living Spirit observed his prostrated form with something that transcended sympathy yet fell short of mercy. \"It is never so easy. Existence... is never so easy, nor so giving.\"","HUUM!","And with that pronouncement, THE Living Spirit vanished, leaving behind not even a whisper of its presence.","The Fold Dweller remained on his knees in the vast emptiness of the Earliest Folds, feeling an abandonment so complete it threatened to unmake him at the conceptual level.","But in that desolation, something crystallized. Defiance. Purpose. Decision.","He thought of all the methods THE Living Spirit had mentioned. Devouring others’ Everything seemed monstrous. Learning Principles appeared impossible without a teacher. But farming... farming was something even a Fold Dweller could attempt.","Farming was a basic anything and everyone could do.","He rose from his knees with newfound determination burning in those unique eyes.","He would farm. But not just anything...he would farm the very Principles that THE Living Spirit had mentioned. If Existence would not give, he would take. He would cultivate. He would harvest!","And in his defiance, he would become!","---","In the Early Veiled Shore, where impossible things grew with casual certainty, the Queen of Matter’s exuberant presence had become a force of nature unto itself.","Her clone...one of several she had manifested to explore every corner of this miraculous space, stood near the cultivation plots with eyes that sparkled like captured starlight.","She watched Heidrun with the kind of intense fascination typically reserved for witnessing the birth of existence itself.","The majestic goat was overseeing the growth of vibrant green-gold grasses, each blade containing enough concentrated essence to elevate a common being to transcendent heights. Her bearing suggested infinite patience barely containing infinite pride, a combination that should have been paradoxical but somehow achieved perfect balance.","Meanwhile, the Queen of Matter’s primary body worked alongside Noah and the others, enthusiastically hefting stones and blocks that weighed more than mountains. But she couldn’t resist dividing herself to explore, to witness, to experience everything this Shore had to offer.","Inspiration struck like lightning. The clone pulled out a canvas from nowhere...a habit she’d developed across countless years, and began to paint with every ounce of authority she possessed. Her brushes moved with speed that made time itself jealous, capturing not just Heidrun’s image but her essence!","The painting was complete in seconds.","What she presented made Heidrun’s dismissive glance transform into focused attention.","The artwork showed the goat not as she was, but as she knew herself to be...unfathomably proud, infinitely arrogant, gloriously superior to all who might dare compare themselves to her magnificence!","The painting shimmered with captured starlight on Heidrun’s white fur coat, each brushstroke a testament to ego elevated to art form.","Heidrun’s eyes blazed with approval.","|The Eminent Early Living Land Lifeform, Heidrun, approves of the majestic display of her brilliance|","|You have earned the favor of the most brilliant Land Lifeform of the Early Veiled Shore(Self proclaimed)|","|Heidrun’s disposition toward you: Tolerant Appreciation|","The Queen of Matter pumped her fist with victory that could have powered small Wheels of Existence. \"Ma’am, is there anything I can help you with? I am very enthusiastic about any work! See, I even made multiple bodies to be more helpful!\"","Heidrun’s gaze swept over the vibrating figure with the kind of assessment typically reserved for evaluating tools.","Her eyes shifted briefly to Noah’s distant form, where he worked on constructing his Abode with focused intensity. Then, with deliberate precision, she tapped one golden hoof against the sand.","A golden bucket materialized beneath her udders, its surface inscribed with patterns. A stool appeared to her left, positioned with mathematical perfection for the task ahead.","|Unprecedented Privilege Granted|","|Apart from the Early Creature who owns this Shore, you have been given the absolute honor of milking Heidrun for her Sacred Mead of Existence|","|Task: Extract Sacred Mead with appropriate reverence. Upon completion, deliver to the Owner of the Early Veiled Shore for reward. Warning: This privilege may be revoked at any moment of displeasure|","...!","The Queen of Matter trembled with excitement that threatened to split her into even more bodies. She rolled up her sleeves with the determination of someone about to perform the most important task of their existence.","\"Yes ma’am! I will not disappoint! This is the greatest honor of my current existence!\"","In the distance, Noah paused in his construction work to witness this unprecedented scene.","Never before had Heidrun allowed anyone but him to perform this task...and she had told him she would soon be ready to produce more Mead as if he would finally have replenishments.","So he watched.","The sight of the Queen of Matter approaching the golden bucket with reverence typically reserved for religious ceremonies was... something else entirely.","Near him, another body of the Queen carried a massive gray-gold stone that could have served as a mountain’s foundation, her enthusiasm undimmed despite the split attention. She noticed his observation and beamed.","\"Sir! Your goat appreciates art! I’m being allowed to help with important farming duties! This...is the best day!\"","Noah shook his head with fond exasperation at her ability to accomplish things others couldn’t even imagine.","Nobody had began interacting with the Early Veiled Shore with as much enthusiasm as the Queen of Matter had as she was receiving boons others didn’t.","The Queen of Matter had a talent for making the impossible seem not just possible, but inevitable through sheer enthusiasm.","At that moment.","His contemplation was interrupted by a sensation that transcended physical space...a message threading through one of his closer existential entanglements. The weavings of existence carried words across impossible distances.","|Hey, would you perhaps want a Seed? I have to pay you back somehow and I may have something you like...|","The Great Usurper’s voice rang through his consciousness with casual certainty, accompanied by visions and complete knowledge of a particular treasure!","[Seed of the Primordial Spirit Tree]","The information flooded through the connection...its properties, its requirements, its potential!","Noah’s eyes brightened with interest that had nothing to do with power and everything to do with purpose. A seed that required farming, that needed cultivation, that demanded patience and care.","\"A seed,\" Noah murmured, his various bodies across existence all pausing in their tasks as he contemplated. \"Yes, I would very much like a seed.\"","...!","He tugged on the entanglement with the Great Usurper!"]},{"number":4021,"title":"Chapter 4021: Chapter 4020: Farmers of Existence! II","paragraphs":["The entanglement between existences stretched like a silver thread across impossible distances, and Noah pulled upon it with certainty.","Reality rippled around his form as something transcendent passed through the connection!","The Seed materialized in his palm with weight that transcended physical measurement. It pulsed with potential that made even the Early Veiled Shore pulse, the golden sands beneath his feet shifting in anticipation!","A message followed through the connection, the Great Usurper’s voice echoing out.","|I’ll continue paying the debt of the Seed of Existence you gave me, slowly, every now and then. I’ll send over farming-related stuff so you can work toward that dream of being a farmer. Who knows? Maybe you’ll actually achieve it.|","...!","Noah smiled at the words, not questioning how Eckert had acquired a Seed with such profound origins. Existence was vast, and everyone had their opportunities. He didn’t go around telling Eckert or Alexander about becoming an Early Creature or possessing an Early Veiled Shore...of course others would have their own chances at transcendence, their own paths to power that defied conventional understanding.","He moved across the Shore with purpose, the Seed cradled in his hands like a newborn star. The cultivation plots stretched before him in neat rows, some already showing signs of the impossible herbs beginning to sprout. He selected an empty plot near the center, where the concentration of nutrients in the soil were vibrant!","Kneeling, he pressed the Seed into the golden sand with reverence that transcended simple planting. This was more than agriculture!","\"Utilize the nutrients from currently devoured lifeforms,\" he commanded the Shore itself. \"Accelerate its maturity.\"","The response was immediate.","|Seed of the Primordial Spirit Tree Planted. Acceleration Options Available. Natural Growth: 1,000 years. With Current Nutrient Infusion: 1 day. With 100 Drops of Early Creature Blood: 12 hours. With 1,000 Drops of Early Creature Blood: 1 hour. Select acceleration method|","Noah didn’t hesitate. Time was a resource, but blood...blood he could produce. The rapid explosion of complexity that would follow the tree’s maturation was worth any cost.","\"One hour,\" he declared, watching as his skin split along carefully chosen lines. Deliberate openings through which his precious blood could flow. Each drop that fell onto the soil around the Seed was worth more than entire Wheelss, containing within it the compressed essence of an Early Creature’s existence!","The thousand drops fell like crimson rain, each one absorbed instantly by soil that had been waiting eons for such nourishment. The effect was immediate and magnificent.","HUUM!","The Seed cracked with a sound like reality accepting a new truth. A shoot emerged, pale as moonlight, growing with speed that made time itself seem uncertain. The farm-like atmosphere of the Shore intensified as the shoot became a sapling, the sapling stretched toward a sky that didn’t exist, its trunk thickening with each passing second.","Starlight seemed to shimmer along its bark...generated from within, as if the tree itself was a constellation that had chosen to take root.","Branches spread with precision, each one reaching toward different aspects of existence. Leaves unfurled that were simultaneously silver and gold, their surfaces inscribed with patterns that suggested thoughts becoming real.","Noah watched with satisfaction as his newest addition to the Shore established itself, when prompts suddenly cascaded before his vision!","|The Queen of Matter has successfully completed assigned task. Heidrun has been successfully tended and milked|","|Sacred Mead of Existence Obtained: 15,000 Drops. Efficiency Rating: Unprecedented.|","|Heidrun’s Comment: \"Acceptable enthusiasm. Questionable technique. Overall satisfactory.\"|","...!","His eyes blazed with interest as he turned to see the Queen of Matter approaching with a golden bucket that seemed too heavy for reality itself to properly support. She carried it with both hands, her entire body vibrating with pride at her accomplishment. The white-gold liquid within sloshed gently, each tiny wave containing enough power to elevate common beings to transcendence.","\"Sir!\" she exclaimed, her voice carrying the particular pitch of someone who had just achieved something they’d been told was impossible.","\"I did it! Heidrun even said I was satisfactory! That’s basically a glowing recommendation from her!\" She presented the bucket with ceremony that would have been excessive if not for what it contained.","\"Please give me as many more jobs and tasks here so that I do not fall back to irrelevancy again!\"","The desperation in that last statement was real...the Queen of Matter’s greatest fear had always been becoming a background character in her own existence. Noah reached out and ruffled her hair as he smiled lightly.","\"You’re on the right path,\" he assured her. \"Keep it up.\"","With a gesture, he drew the bucket into his spatial storage, the Sacred Mead joining his growing collection of impossible resources once more. \"Let’s go finish the Abode first. There’s still work to be done.\"","The Shore buzzed with activity as construction resumed. Many plots of herbs would soon mature, the nine original trees would bear their first fruits, and now the tenth tree, the Primordial Spirit Tree...added its own unique presence to the agricultural miracle he was creating.","Stone by stone, block by block, the Abode took shape!","The construction was both mundane and transcendent...physical materials being assembled through manual labor, yet each piece carrying significance that transcended simple architecture.","As all of this occured...the Shore itself continued to move as if it were alive as the Aquarium in thr distance churned!","|Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeform Captured. Species: Void-Touched Leviathan Spawn. Successfully contained in Leviathan’s Eternum Cage.|","Noah glanced toward the Aquarium to witness the new arrival...a creature that seemed to exist in negative space, its form defined more by what wasn’t there than what was. It thrashed once against its containment before recognizing the futility and settling into sullen acceptance.","The Crimson-Eyed Depth Tyrant, his first capture, actually shifted away from the newcomer with visible wariness.","He returned his attention to the construction, where Emperor Penguin was waddling forward with the final building block...a keystone that would complete the entire structure!","The penguin’s expression radiated pride that seemed excessive for its small form, its flippers raised triumphantly as it placed the stone with ceremonial precision.","The moment the keystone settled into place, brilliant light erupted across the Early Veiled Shore. Not the harsh light of explosion, instead the warm radiance of something coming into perfect alignment with its purpose.","The Abode of the Early Creature was completed, and its details rose up before his eyes!"]},{"number":4022,"title":"Chapter 4022: Chapter 4021: Farmers of Existence! III","paragraphs":["|Construction Complete: Abode of the Early Creature|","|Classification: Transcendent Dwelling|","|Spatial Parameters: External dimensions 100x100x100 meters. Internal dimensions equivalent to Minor Miniature Fold.|","|Primary Features:|","-Temporal Flux Chamber: Time flows independently from external reality. Stasis to acceleration possible but currently uncontrolled. Days or years may pass within while seconds pass outside, but never the other way around.","-Access Limitation: Early Creature plus 18 designated beings maximum simultaneous occupancy","- Pocket Dimensions: 99 separate spatial pockets, each with unique environmental properties","-Regenerative Architecture: Structure repairs itself using ambient existence","- Authority Suppression Field: All violence impossible within primary areas","-Meditation Amplification Zones: Complexity and Purity absorption increased by 300%","-Private Chambers: Specially attuned spaces that adjust to occupant preferences","...!","It was glorious!","The Abode stood before them like something that had always existed but had only now chosen to manifest. Its exterior was carved from what appeared to be single piece of stone that had witnessed the birth and death of Folds. The surface wasn’t smooth but covered in intricate patterns that seemed to tell stories through images and through texture itself.","Archaic symbols that predated language spiraled up its walls, each one pulsing with faint light that synchronized with the breathing of the Shore itself. The entrance wasn’t a door but a swirling gateway of multicolored light, simultaneously inviting and warning that crossing its threshold meant entering something beyond normal existence.","Noah nodded with satisfaction as another prompt materialized.","|Participation Reward Activated. All beings who assisted in construction have earned the right to ascend any Sacred Totem within the Shore. Ringing the bell with personal Hymn grants Epiphany State.|","|Effect: 100,000% increase to Complexity and Purity absorption for 10 minutes. This opportunity is single-use per participant.|","The assembled helpers...Noah’s people who had labored to create this wonder, stared at the notification with expressions ranging from disbelief to overwhelming joy. Henry’s visage cracked a smile. Kazuhiko’s hand trembled on his sword hilt. Even Erikson, usually stoic, showed visible emotion.","Noah addressed them all, his voice carrying across the Shore with perfect clarity. \"The Early Veiled Shore is vast and filled with opportunities. Tend to the plots and help with farming. Water the trees. Drink the Early Sacred Waters in moderation to not lose yourselves. Fight against Marine Lifeforms when you become powerful enough.\"","He paused, ensuring every word was understood. \"Through this Shore, you can become unfathomably powerful in a short period of time. Outside of all this are the endless Folds of Existence with countless other lifeforms. Once you’re powerful enough, you can always venture out to experience what it means to face Fold Dwellers and Living Existences.\"","His people listened with bright eyes, understanding dawning that they had been given not just power, but purpose. They began to scatter across the Shore with newfound determination, some heading toward the Totems, others to the cultivation plots, each finding their own path to transcendence.","Noah took a moment to observe everything he had built. His gaze traveled to the distant seated figures of Ruination and the Infiniverse, both having crossed the hundred-million marker in their Complexity and Purity Quotients. They had held off on forming more Glyphs, waiting to form Kleos Glyphs like him. The potential they represented made his eyes shine with anticipation!","\"Little Fish, can we go see inside?\"","The small voice drew his attention downward. Barbatos had appeared beside him, her crimson eyes shining with excitement as she hugged his hand and gazed at the Abode. Her dark hair framed a face that managed to be both ancient and vibrant simultaneously.","Adelaide, Athena, Anna, and others approached from various directions, their expressions mixing curiosity with something else. Noah smiled warmly at the gathering!","\"I’ll give you all a tour.\"","He looked toward where Moiraine sat in meditation, her form radiating the particular stillness of someone reconstructing their power. \"You too, Moiraine. Come.\"","...!","The procession that followed was almost ceremonial...Noah surrounded by these women who had become integral to his existence in ways that transcended simple companionship.","They approached the swirling gateway with mixed expressions of anticipation.","The moment they stepped through, reality reorganized itself around them.","They emerged into a stellar-lit hall that defied every assumption about interior space. The floor was marble shot through with starlight, extending for what appeared to be light-years in every direction. The ceiling...if it could be called that, was existence itself turned transparent, showing the dance of concepts and forces that most beings would never perceive.","Multiple ancient-locked archways floated throughout the space, each one carved from different impossible materials. Some were positioned on the floor, others hung in mid-air at angles that challenged three-dimensional thinking, and still others seemed to phase in and out of visibility.","Each doorway led to a different pocket dimension, a different reality with its own rules and wonders.","All of this existed inside a single Abode.","Barbatos’s eyes lit up with delight that could have powered stars. She tugged on Noah’s hand with surprising strength, pulling him toward an archway that gleamed with obsidian radiance.","\"Little Fish, I want to see in here!\"","As she pulled him forward, Noah’s body seamlessly divided...one version going with Barbatos while another remained with the group. The division was so smooth that reality didn’t even notice it had been cheated.","Adelaide shook her head with fond exasperation, her vibrant snow-blue hair catching the stellar light in ways that created small auroras around her head. She looked around, performing a quick headcount of all the women present, then fixed Noah with a calm smile.","\"Make a few more bodies and give everyone the same treatment,\" she said, her tone perfectly pleasant yet taking no argument.","\"You’ve been busily getting more complex and haven’t given us any time recently.\"","The words ended with sharp authority, and Noah nodded with a smile as he replied. \"Yes, Ma’am.\"","HUUM!","Multiple versions of himself materialized without fanfare, each one moving to a different member of his harem. Gentle hands found waists, fingers intertwined with fingers, and each woman found herself being led toward a different doorway, a different pocket dimension where privacy and possibility intertwined.","The logistics of it should have been impossible...maintaining multiple fully conscious bodies, each providing genuine attention! But Noah had transcended such limitations long ago.","Finally, only Moiraine remained, looking at him with bright eyes that held depths of understanding.","\"Sir...has quite an appetite,\" she observed, her tone carrying amusement rather than judgment."]},{"number":4023,"title":"Chapter 4023: Chapter 4022: Farmers of Existence! IV","paragraphs":["Noah nodded seriously. \"Existence has many boons that everyone fights for. In the middle of all of it, if one has the chance to enjoy the simple things and doesn’t... they have the biggest losses. And I do not like losses when I have treasures all around me.\"","He extended his hand toward her. \"Come. I need to see if Dual Cultivation still has stupendous results.\"","Her eyes blazed brighter as she took his hand without hesitation. \"Yes, Sir.\"","...!","Noah and Moiraine disappeared into another pocket dimension where time itself flowed according to different rules, where moments could stretch into eternities or compress into heartbeats!","Outside the Abode, another of Noah’s bodies remained seated on the golden sands, observing the Shore with satisfaction.","The Emperor Penguin’s indignant voice carried across the space as it complained to Kazuhiko and Erikson.","\"I would have also liked a tour of the Abode we built...\"","Kazuhiko, already holding Erikson’s slipper with practiced ease, delivered a light smack to the back of the penguin’s head. \"No, no you would not, you flightless bird.\"","\"Hey!\" The Emperor Penguin’s authority flared white gold as it charged at Kazuhiko with tiny legs pumping furiously.","Noah smiled at these scenes of normalcy amidst transcendence.","Even as terrifying weavings of craziness unfolded outside.","Even as the Kleos Concordat would take place within a day as all Living Existences met.","The Early Veiled Shore remained its own isolated place with its glorious wonders that could make one forget about everything else!","As he had such thoughts.","Without warning, his seated form began to shine.","HUUM!","Brilliance erupted from his body, ancient and profound. His shirtless form revealed skin that had taken on an archaic quality, fair yet somehow containing depths that eyes couldn’t properly perceive. Taut muscles shifted beneath that skin with each breath, each movement revealing perfect control over a form that had transcended normal physicality.","The Kleos Glyph of the Creature’s First Lesson blazed upon his forehead, its ten-fold pattern rotating slowly as if contemplating truths. In his hand, the Goad rested with deceptive simplicity...just a stick, yet one that had educated Inevitabilities about their own existence.","But it was what was happening within that truly mattered. His Heart of an Early Creature pulsed with increasing intensity, sending waves of power through his entire being!","HUUUM!","And his Atlas...that internal map where all his Towers of Osmont grew like impossible trees, suddenly erupted with shocking radiance.","|Monumental Achievement: Early Atlas of the Folds - Complete|","|+500,000,000 Complexity Quotient. +500,000,000 Purity Quotient.|","WAA!","The surge of power was staggering. His body experienced waves of enhancement that would have destroyed lesser beings, each cell drinking in the advancement like desert sand accepting rain. This was why the Atlas had taken so long to complete...it wasn’t just mapping current existence, but something far more profound!","|Early Atlas of the Folds|","|Primary Function: Map and Pathway to the Earliest Folds|","|The Atlas has connected itself to the primordial core of what defines an Early Creature, then exceeded that foundation by incorporating your Quintessential and Tyrannical nature. It serves as a map, and as a bridge between what was, what is, and what might be.|","|Core Ability: Temporal Traversal|","- For limited duration, traverse into the Earliest Folds themselves","- Warning: Cannot control destination point","- Warning: Cannot remain indefinitely, extended stay results in permanent temporal displacement","-Each traversal establishes a Node on the Atlas for potential return","-Current Safe Duration: 1 hour","- Cooldown: 1 day","|Supplementary Functions:|","-Fold Memory: Can replay events from any visited location in the Earliest Folds","-Existential Compass: Always know your position relative to your origin point","-Temporal Anchor: The Towers of Osmont serve as lighthouses, each advancement extending safe duration","-Reality Recognition: Immune to temporal paradoxes during traversal","-Node Network: As Nodes accumulate, can begin to predict destination points.","|Growth Parameters|","-Atlas complexity increases through exploration","-Tower advancement extends traversal duration (Each stage = +unknown number of seconds)","-Heart completion reduces cooldown","-At full development: $@%% %#$%& in Earliest Folds becomes possible.","|Unique Synergy: The Tyrannical Navigator|","-Your nature as Tyrannical Emperor allows forcing favorable destinations","-Current Success Rate: 0.1%","-Increases with each successful traversal","|Unique Synergy: The Quintessential Mapper|","-Your nature as Quintessential Emperor allows recording of Earliest Fold resources","-Can identify and mark locations of Lost Forgotten Principles","-Current Detection Range: 1 light year around traversal point","...!","Sheesh!","Noah felt the weight of this new capability settling into his existence!","The ability to visit the Earliest Folds even for mere seconds was unprecedented! That was where THE Creature had walked, where the THE Living Existences had been, where Principles existed before they became Lost or Forgotten.","The opportunities were staggering! The dangers were incomprehensible!","The Loot...ah!","Noah, seated on the golden sands of his Shore with multiple bodies experiencing transcendent wonders in pocket dimensions while others built and farmed and grew, smiled.","Because this was what it meant to be an Early Creature in truth....to be Him, Noah Osmont!","Not just power...but the ability to touch the very foundations of existence itself and do thr impossible.","Because what the fuck was even this capability?!","The Early Atlas of the Folds pulsed within him like a second heart, ready to guide him into the deep past where everything had begun.","Ready to help him understand what even Living Existences might have forgotten!","Noah observed the shocking functions of the Early Atlas of the Folds again and again, his enhanced perception parsing through the information. Each reading confirmed what seemed utterly impossible.","A one-day cooldown between uses, and a whole hour of exploration.","In such an hour, a terrifying number of things could be done. A terrifying number of things could be accomplished.","\"...\"","The silence stretched as Noah felt himself standing at a grand precipice of possibility and achievement. The weight of what he was about to attempt pressed against his consciousness like the attention of existence itself. He breathed out slowly, each exhalation carrying away doubt, leaving only determination.","\"Use the Early Atlas of the Folds.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":4024,"title":"Chapter 4024: Chapter 4023: Farmers of Existence! V","paragraphs":["The words emerged with quiet certainty, and reality immediately responded.","|CRITICAL TRAVERSAL INITIATING|","|Extreme Caution Required|","|Failure Parameters:|","-If return does not occur within 1 hour: Complete destruction of traversing body and all associated weavings","-If death occurs during traversal: Risk of cascade failure affecting all bodies","-Certain deaths may result in complete existential extinction","|Proceed? This action cannot be undone|","Noah didn’t hesitate. His confirmation rang through his being with the certainty of someone who had already calculated the risks and found them acceptable!","His entire existence began to buzz with frequencies that shouldn’t exist. The sensation started in his core and radiated outward, each particle of his being vibrating in harmony with something ancient and profound. The Early Atlas within him blazed with light that existed before light had been defined.","Then, without warning...","WAP!","His body seated on the shores folded in on itself like reality accepting that it had been cheated. The space where he had been sitting showed no evidence of his presence, as if existence itself had forgotten he had been there!","|Transference to random point in the Earliest Folds has begun|","|Duration of traversal: Indeterminate. Destination: Unknown. Probability of survival: Calculating...|","|Calculation completed. Probability of survival...is best left unknown.|","...!","\"...\"","---","Existence was unfathomably unique.","Across its infinite expanse, countless abilities had been formed, discarded, and utilized since the first moment something wondered if it should be rather than wasn’t.","Some were as small as conjuring fireballs...brief expressions of will that barely disturbed the fabric of reality. Others transcended comprehension entirely, achieving the impossible through sheer audacity of conception!","Among these impossibilities, perhaps none was more audacious than forming a map that connected to the Earliest Folds themselves.","To countless years and events in the far distant past, when the foundations of everything were still being laid, when THE Creature walked freely and THE Living Existences were young.","Noah felt his existence trembling as it was stretched across temporal distances that had no measurement. He was being pulled through time itself, toward a when that existed perpendicular to normal causality!","His being threatened to spread too thin, to dissolve into the spaces between moments.","The Rearing Stick materialized in his grip without conscious thought, its simple presence providing an anchor of stability. The Goad hummed with recognition, as if it remembered the path they were taking. Simultaneously, the Kleos Glyph on his forehead, the Creature’s First Lesson, blazed with light that helped hold his consciousness together.","His Towers of Osmont, made from his glorious True Sources, lit up the way for him to see!","Years and seconds passed simultaneously. He experienced the weight of eons in heartbeats, felt instants stretch into eternities. His perception fragmented and reformed countless times, each reconstruction slightly different from the last.","|Existential Integrity: 94%... 87%... 76%...|","|Stabilizing factors detected:|","-Goad recognition: +11% stability","-Kleos Glyph resonance: +30% stability","-Early Creature nature: +50% stability","|Final Integrity: 91%. Traversal viable. Your existence, though feeble by Earliest Fold standards, possesses sufficient confluence of factors for survival.|","HUUM!","After what seemed like forever and no time at all, Noah felt his existence warping and twisting through dimensions that had no names. Reality bent around him like water around a stone, then suddenly...","WAP!","He arrived.","BOOM!","He truly arrived!","The moment his feet touched whatever served as ground in this place, his existence erupted with sensation. Every cell in his body, every atom of his being, began drinking in something he had never known existed...a richness of authority that made everything he had experienced before seem like shadows of shadows.","|Location Reached: Unknown Point - The Earliest Folds. Temporal Coordinate: Unknown Years Before Present.|","|Environmental Analysis|","-Atmosphere contains Raw Early Existential Authority","-Passive absorption rate: 100,000 CQ/PQ per second","-Warning: Prolonged exposure may cause fundamental changes to existence","|Timer Started: 59:59 remaining|","...!","Noah gasped as the very air filled his lungs with power. Not refined, not processed, but raw potential that existed before it had been divided into categories like Origin or Paradox!","This was the fundamental substance from which all authority would eventually derive.","And just being here...increased his Complexity and Purity by 100,000 per second!","Oh!","He looked around with eyes that struggled to process what they were seeing.","The landscape defied every assumption about what reality should look like. Countless green-gold reed plants floated vertically in space that might have been air or might have been thought. Each reed extended for light-years...he could somehow perceive their full length despite the impossibility of such vision. They shimmered with complexity so profound that looking at them directly caused his nascent understanding of existence to reorganize itself.","The sky was a swirling mixture of colors that hadn’t been invented yet, concepts that were still being debated. Mountains floated inverted in the distance, their peaks pointing toward depths that had no bottom. Rivers of what might have been time itself flowed upward, carrying fragments of events that would happen or had happened or were happening now.","Everything was more real than reality had any right to be!","Noah approached one of the floating reeds with careful reverence, his hand extending toward its surface. The moment his fingers made contact, information flooded his consciousness.","|Primordial Complexity Reed- One of the infinite reeds that grew when existence first wondered about growth. Bark contains compressed potential from before potential was defined. Those able to breach the bark will find sap containing 10,000,000 Complexity and Purity.","...!","Noah’s astonishment was complete. A single reed contained what would take most beings eons to accumulate. And there were countless reeds stretching in every direction, a forest of impossible advancement just waiting to be harvested!","He pressed his hands against the bark, feeling its resistance. It was hard...conceptually. It resisted being opened the way reality resisted being changed. His enhanced strength meant nothing here. This required something more fundamental.","The Kleos Glyph on his forehead blazed with brilliant light as he called upon the Creature’s First Lesson. The authority of all ten Living Existence types flowed through him simultaneously, and finally...finally, the bark cracked.","Vibrant gold sap was revealed within, glowing with inner light that predated stars. Without hesitation, Noah cupped his hands and drank directly from the source. The explosion of sensation in his mouth transcended taste...it was like drinking liquified possibility itself.","|Primordial Complexity Reed Sap Consumed. Base Gain: +10,000,000 Complexity Quotient. Base Gain: +10,000,000 Purity Quotient. Unique Gain due to your unique nature bonus: +2,500,000 to each|","...!"]},{"number":4025,"title":"Chapter 4025: Chapter 4024: Farmers of Existence! VI","paragraphs":["As Noah marveled at this wonder, feeling power coursing through him that would have taken normal beings multiple lifetimes to achieve...","BOOM!","A terrifying aura erupted behind him with force that made reality step back in acknowledgment. Noah spun to face the source, his enhanced perception immediately observing what stood before him.","The being was titanic in scale, humanoid in general shape but wrong in every specific. Its skin was bark-like but moved like flesh, inscribed with patterns that predated written Runes. Its eyes held depths of immensity!","Massive hands ended in fingers that could have carved mountains or cradled newborn thoughts with equal ease.","Most shocking was what it wasn’t...this was not a Living Existence. Noah’s enhanced perception confirmed it carried only the aura of a Fold Dweller with no Living Existential Authority, yet its power dwarfed any Duke he had encountered!","The being’s expression was grave as stones that had witnessed the death of Folds.","\"Fool! What are you doing here alone when the mad Early Creature is still hunting around these parts?! Come on!\"","Before Noah could respond, before he could process the implications of ’mad Early Creature’ or formulate questions, the titanic being’s hand closed around him with force that transcended physical or conceptual resistance!","The being’s grip contained authority that Noah couldn’t begin to counter because it was far too old! Authority accumulated not through advancement but through sheer survival in an era when survival itself was an achievement.","\"I said COME ON!\" the being roared, already moving with speed that compressed space around them. \"The last fool who lingered near the Reeds got turned into a meal crushed between the teeth of an Early Creature!\"","...!","Noah found himself being carried like a child through a landscape that shifted and changed with each massive stride the being took. His timer showed [58:43] remaining.","The titanic being’s pace increased, its fear palpable despite its overwhelming power. Whatever Esrly Creature were running from, it was something that even natives of the Earliest Folds didn’t want to encounter!","Noah gripped the Goad tighter, feeling its weight shift in his hand as he thought of all thr possibilities- one of the major goals being...not to die here!","The Fold Dweller crossed through existence with strides that compressed reality around them, each step covering distances that had no proper measurement.","The sensation was like being dragged through water that was also fire that was also thought itself.","Seconds stretched and compressed simultaneously, and then...","They crossed a threshold.","The transition was immediate and absolute, like stepping from chaos into order, from possibility into definition. Noah felt barriers close behind them....barriers that were conceptual boundaries that declared this space separate from the madness beyond!","The titanic being released him with visible relief, its bark-flesh form sagging slightly as tension drained away. It breathed out...a sound like wind through forests that had never existed, and looked Noah up and down with eyes that held eons of assessment.","\"You look a bit weaker than most,\" it observed, not unkindly but with the matter-of-fact tone of someone stating that water was wet. \"Though I suppose that’s better than the last one I found...\"","The being straightened, gesturing to the space around them with one massive hand. \"I’ve brought you to the Folds of the Esteemed First Farmer, the One Who Gazed Upon THE Living Spirit.\"","The title rang through the space with weight that made reality pulse.","Prompts flashed before Noah right after!","|Location Identified: The Primordial Agricultural Sanctum. Owner- Viltharion the Principle Cultivator, The One Who Gazed Upon THE Living Spirit|","|Era: The Earliest Folds - Period of Initial Cultivation. Population: 731 Fold Dwellers. Warning: You are the weakest entity present by a factor of 1,000.|","|Time Remaining: 57:50|","...!","Noah’s astonishment was complete as he took in his surroundings.","The reeds were still present, those light-year-long plants floating vertically through space, but here they had been organized. They grew in neat rows that suggested someone had imposed agricultural order on cosmic chaos.","Between them floated farming plots that defied comprehension...each one the size of an omniverse, perfect squares of cultivated existence that hummed with careful attention.","Stellar trees rose from these plots, their trunks composed of compressed starlight, their branches reaching into dimensions that hadn’t been named yet. Their leaves were concepts given form...each one containing a different aspect of what growth meant, what cultivation could become.","Hundreds of Fold Dwellers moved through this impossible farm with serious purpose. None possessed Living Existential Authority in the traditional sense, yet each one radiated power that would make current-era beings weep with inadequacy.","The weakest among them carried might equivalent to Honored Living Existences, their power accumulated by existing so long that existence itself had to acknowledge their significance as they were drenched in...Early Existential Authority!","Dozens more carried power that matched or exceeded Dukes.","The atmosphere was one of focused industry mixed with profound respect.","The Fold Dweller who had saved him shifted, its massive form creating small earthquakes with the movement. \"I am Threnvar, Keeper of the Eighth Perimeter. You will stay in the secure areas until the threat of the mad Early Creature is taken care of.\"","Threnvar’s expression grew grimmer, if such a thing was possible on features carved from living bark. \"The creature has been hunting for a while now. It seems to have developed a taste for complexity itself...not beings who possess it, but the abstract concept. Every time it feeds, something becomes simpler. Last week, it ate the concept of ’maybe’ from an entire region. Now everything there either is or isn’t, with no space between.\"","Threnvar looked at him again, its ancient eyes showing something that might have been pity. \"With how weak you are, you should reinforce yourself immediately. Why don’t you have some Existential Dew Fruits?\"","The being pointed with one massive finger toward a distant plot that blazed with white brilliance. \"Go to the Seventh Contemplation Grove. Harvest as needed...but only what you can consume. The Farmer does not approve of waste.\"","Noah nodded seriously, offering a nod to the being who had saved him. \"Thank you for your assistance.\"","\"Don’t thank me yet,\" Threnvar rumbled. \"If the mad one finds us here, we’re all equally doomed. Gratitude can wait for survival.\"","...!"]},{"number":4026,"title":"Chapter 4026: Chapter 4025: Do Nothing! I","paragraphs":["Noah made his way toward the indicated plot, his movement careful and deliberate. He was acutely aware of being observed with the kind of attention given to children who had wandered into an adult workspace. The other Fold Dwellers didn’t stop their work, but he could feel their ancient gazes tracking his progress.","The Seventh Contemplation Grove rose before him like a monument to impossible agriculture.","The trees here were different from the stellar giants elsewhere...more refined, more purposeful. Their trunks were white as fresh paper, inscribed with patterns that might have been words if words had been invented yet.","Fruits hung from their branches like condensed thoughts. Each one was perfectly spherical, about the size of his fist, and contained within their translucent skin swirled galaxies of compressed potential.","Noah reached out to touch one, and information flooded his consciousness.","|Existential Dew Fruit|:: Cultivated with singular purpose by Viltharion the Principle Cultivator. Grown from seeds of contemplation after witnessing THE Living Spirit. Each fruit represents one meditation on the nature of Principles and how one could possibly grasp one. Consumption Effect: +5,000,000. Complexity Quotient Consumption Effect: +5,000,000 Purity Quotient","Special Effect: Increases perception and sensitivity to Principles by 10%*","Special Effect: May trigger epiphany regarding Principles","Note: These fruits are the result of a Fold Dweller who sought to plant Principles themselves after discussing existence with THE Living Spirit","Noah’s hand pulsed slightly as he plucked the fruit. It came away from the branch with a sound like a perfectly resolved musical note. The weight in his palm was negligible physically but profound conceptually...he was holding the crystallized meditation of someone who had spoken directly with THE Living Spirit!","He bit into it without hesitation.","The taste was indescribable as it was simple in a way that nothing in modern existence could achieve. It tasted like the moment before decision, like the space between heartbeats, like the pause before understanding dawns.","It was fucking glorious!","|Existential Dew Fruit Consumed|","|Complexity Quotient increased by 5,000,000. Purity Quotient increased by 5,000,000|","|Principle Perception increased by 10%| |You can now faintly sense the presence of Lost Forgotten Principles within 10 meters.|","|There are...0 Principles for sensed by your senses.|","HUUM!","The surge of advancement was smoother than what he had experienced from the reed sap...more refined, more purposeful. But it was the secondary effect that truly mattered. Noah could feel something shifting in his perception, as if a veil he hadn’t known existed was beginning to thin.","He looked at the tree before him with new understanding.","Another fruit found its way into his hand. Then another.","He began to eat as if he were a voracious wildling of an entity as each fruit...was 5 Million to Complexity and Purity!","|Timer: 55:48 remaining|","As Noah consumed his fourth fruit, feeling his complexity soar beyond anything he could have achieved in years of normal cultivation, a shadow fell across the grove.","The shadow that fell across the grove turned out to be something slightly new.","A curious Fold Dweller stood before him, her presence commanding attention through sheer physicality rather than any display of power.","She was burly, humanoid in general form but crowned with the head of a wolf.","Gray fur, streaked with silver that might have been age or might have been wisdom, covered her lupine features.","Her eyes, amber gold and ancient, regarded Noah with particular intensity.","\"You are such a weak thing,\" she observed, her voice carrying a growl beneath words that somehow made them more genuine rather than threatening. \"Yet you seem to be the least worried being here while others prepare for potential death.\"","It was true. All around them, Fold Dwellers who had existed since before time had proper measurement were taking defensive positions, their ancient faces showing fear. Yet Noah stood calmly, still holding his fourth fruit, juice running down his chin from where he’d bitten into it.","He swallowed the piece he’d been chewing, feeling the surge of complexity flow through him before responding. His voice emerged steady.","\"Worrying,\" he said, meeting those amber eyes without flinching, \"is the act of suffering twice. Once in imagination, once in reality...if the feared thing even comes to pass. It changes nothing except to steal from us the present moment, which is the only time we truly possess.\"","He took another bite of the fruit, the casual action emphasizing his point.","\"I could spend these seconds fearing what might come, rehearsing deaths that may never arrive. Or I could use them to grow stronger, to experience what is rather than what might be. One should simply move forward while trying their best. The outcome will be what it is, but at least we’ll meet it having used our time rather than wasted it.\"","The wolf-woman’s eyes blazed brighter, her muzzle pulling back in what might have been a grin if wolves could truly grin. \"Good mentality!\"","The approval rang genuine. \"I am Silvara, Guardian of the Contemplation Groves for eight hundred cycles.\"","She tilted her massive head, studying him with renewed interest. \"And who might you be, young thing who speaks old truths?\"","\"Noah,\" he replied simply, seeing no reason for elaborate titles in this place.","\"Noah.\" She tested the name, rolling it around like tasting new fruit. \"Since you are a bit weak, I can help you out by sharing some of my Authority.\"","...!","Her smile became decidedly devilish, showing teeth that could have torn through Folds .","\"I likely have more than a thousand...actually, probably ten thousand times the amount of authority you possess. I will pass some to you through a ritual.\"","She moved closer, her massive form radiating warmth that felt like standing near a sun. \"You don’t know the ritual, so I’ll take the lead. Just continue consuming the fruits.\"","Without waiting for agreement, Silvara began something that predated any wonder or technique Noah had encountered. She placed one massive pawed hand on his shoulder...and began to speak in runic language!","|Ancient Ritual Detected: The Gifting of Accumulated Days- Allows Fold Dwellers to transfer accumulated complexity and purity to others. Conversion Rate: 50% efficiency.|","...!"]},{"number":4027,"title":"Chapter 4027: Chapter 4026: Do Nothing! II","paragraphs":["The air around them began to shimmer with patterns. Silvara’s form began to glow with inner light that had nothing to do with illumination and everything to do with the weight of existence acknowledging what she had accumulated.","Streams of that light began to flow from her into Noah, each strand carrying compressed years, condensed experiences, distilled existence itself!","|Receiving Authority Transfer. Source: Silvara - Guardian of the Contemplation Groves. Transfer Amount: 100,000,000 Authority Units expended.|","|Received: 50,000,000 Complexity Quotient. Received: 50,000,000 Purity Quotient.|","HUUM!","The sensation was overwhelming. Noah felt decades flowing into him, centuries of accumulated existence compressed into moments. His cells drank in the authority like desert sand accepting rain, each particle of his being growing denser with significance!","For Silvara, expending a hundred million units of her accumulated authority seemed to be nothing more than a casual expenditure.","She didn’t even pause in her ritual, the streams of light continuing to flow.","|Additional 300,000,000 Authority Units expended. Received: 150,000,000 Complexity Quotient. Received: 150,000,000 Purity Quotient.|","Noah’s astonishment grew as he felt himself transforming at a fundamental level!","|Additional 500,000,000 Authority Units expended. Received: 250,000,000 Complexity Quotient. Received: 250,000,000 Purity Quotient!|","When Silvara finally stopped and breathed out slightly, having casually expended nine hundred million units of authority as if giving away pocket change, Noah stared at her with undisguised astonishment.","In seconds, she had granted him advancement that would have taken others yeats to achieve through conventional means.","The wolf-woman laughed at his expression, the sound warm and genuine. \"Why do you look like that? We Fold Dwellers have to take care of each other.\" Her expression grew more serious, amber eyes reflecting depths of experience.","\"There are terrifying Early Creatures out there, horrific Inevitabilities, the prideful Living Existences who look down on us as if we’re insects, and more threats than can be counted. We only have each other, so- \"","Her words cut off instantly.","BOOM!","From above, a bellow erupted that made existence itself recoil. It wasn’t a sound but the concept of command given voice: \"EVERYONE DEFEND! IT’S HERE!\"","...!","The mad Early Creature...had arrived.","Noah barely caught a glimpse of it, his enhanced perception managing to process perhaps a fraction of what descended upon them.","It looked like what primitive humans might have imagined their ancestors to be...a tribal figure wrapped in hides that might have been skinned from concepts themselves. But its eyes... its eyes were crimson suns that burned with madness that transcended simple insanity.","Those eyes focused on the groves, and from them erupted beams of red light that covered everything.","Everything.","The attack was too fast for anything below Duke level to even perceive, let alone react to.","Even Noah, with all his enhanced capabilities, managed only to bring the Goad up in front of him...a futile gesture against something that transcended physical or even conceptual defense!","But Silvara moved.","Without hesitation, without thought, operating on instinct older than consciousness, she threw her massive form over Noah!","Her body became a shield, her very existence a barrier between him and the crimson light.","|A concept devouring attack has been detected. Attack Type: The Devouring of Life Itself. Effect: Complete cessation of all life-related concepts in affected area. Contact Result is death in all its meanings!|","WAA!","Noah was forced to watch, and could only watch...as fear bloomed in those ancient amber eyes of Silvara.","But beneath the fear was something else...determination. Acceptance. The knowledge that this was a choice worth making.","In her fear, she smiled towards Noah as her lips opened and voiced out.","\"I’ve...used my time rather than wasted it. You are young, so you...should move forward while trying your best.\"","...!","Noah’s weavings buzzed as this woman...repeated the words he just said to her!","BOOM!","The crimson light hit Silvara’s form, and immediately, horrifically, she began to drain.","It wasn’t death in any conventional sense. Her very existence began to fade, life itself being torn from her in streams visible to Noah’s enhanced perception.","Her fur went from gray to white to colorless. Her eyes, those warm amber depths, became flat and empty. Her body, which had radiated warmth moments before, became cold in ways that transcended temperature.","She curled tighter around him as she died, ensuring that not even a strand of the crimson light could reach him through gaps in her protection. Her last expression, frozen on lupine features that were becoming nothing more than a husk, was fear mixed with a smile!","Because even though she did all this, she still felt fear! She still had dreams!","Within seconds, the very life of Silvara was gone, leaving nothing but an empty shell that had once housed centuries of experience, wisdom, and warmth.","|Entity: Silvara - Guardian of the Contemplation Groves. Status: Complete Cessation of Existential Circulation.|","...!","From far above, a roar of rage and sorrow erupted...a Fold Dweller of terrifying power engaging the Early Creature in combat that shook the very foundations of this domain.","The impacts of their collision sent shockwaves through dimensions, each blow containing enough force to unmake lesser Folds","The battle raged for five minutes that felt like hours as in this time, Noah stared at the sunken lifeless face of Silvara. He could do nothing else as a glimpse of that crimson light would destroy him!","Booms of complexity clashing against madness echoed through the space, making the air itself uncertain about whether it should exist. Then, suddenly, there was only sorrowful silence.","Noah’s expression was heavy as stone that had witnessed the death of mountains.","Throughout the entire battle, he had been looking at Silvara’s face....that fearful but smiling expression that would be carved into his memory. Someone who had known him for less than minutes had given everything to preserve his existence.","All because she was a Fold Dweller, and she believed him to be so as well!","A moment later, her body began to crumble.","Not decay...even decay required life processes.","This was simple dissolution, existence forgetting that she had ever been. The husk that had been Silvara became ash, then less than ash, revealing the devastation beyond.","|Environmental Warning- Area Devoid of Life Concept. Effect: Existence degradation at 1% per second. Time until complete dissolution is 100 seconds.|","...!"]},{"number":4028,"title":"Chapter 4028: Chapter 4027: Do Nothing! III","paragraphs":["The grove...that monument to impossible agriculture, was gone. In its place was nothing.","The trees hadn’t been destroyed; the concept of their growth had been devoured. The soil hadn’t been scorched; the idea of fertility had been consumed.","Noah looked up through the absence where beauty had been and witnessed something that transcended his understanding.","The First Farmer stood in the space above, holding a farming hoe that looked simple except for how reality bent around it in reverence. The tool dripped with something that might have been blood.","At his feet, or what served as feet for a being of his scale, lay the massive leg of an Early Creature, severed at the thigh. Crimson-gold droplets gushed from it like rivers, each drop containing enough authority to create or destroy Folds!","But it was the Farmer’s expression that struck Noah.","Viltharion, the One Who Gazed Upon THE Living Spirit, was crying!","Stellar tears rolled down features that had been carved by eons of patient work, each drop containing the condensed sorrow of watching everything he had built be destroyed in moments.","When he spoke, his voice carried the weight of grief transformed into rage!","\"Why must it be like this?\"","HUUUM!","The question rang through the devastated space, making even the absence of things pause to listen.","\"We till the soil of existence. We plant. We nurture! We ask for nothing but the right to grow our crops in peace. Yet Early Creatures hunt us for sport or madness. Living Existences look down upon us as if we are insects unworthy of consideration. Inevitabilities unmake us for the crime of existing without paradox.\"","His grip on the hoe tightened, and reality cracked around his fingers.","\"We have no Glyphs to protect us. No Authority beyond what time grants through simple endurance. We are the forgotten children of existence, neither transcendent enough to matter nor insignificant enough to be ignored!\"","The tears continued to fall, but his voice grew stronger, angrier!","\"But I will change things. I WILL change the position of Fold Dwellers, even if I have to hide them in the spaces between Folds themselves! Even if I have to dig beneath Existence to plant gardens where no Early Creature can reach! Even if I have to cultivate Principles in darkness until we become something that cannot be hunted!\"","HUUM!","His roar shook the foundations of the domain as in his bellows and rage...he sensed life.","His gaze fell upon Noah...the sole survivor of the carnage.","The anger in those ancient eyes transformed into pity.","\"Child,\" he said, his voice gentling despite the rage that still burned within, \"you cannot remain here any longer. You will perish in seconds in a place devoid of the concept of life itself. I will send you...far from here.\"","He raised the hoe, and reality prepared to obey whatever command would follow.","\"If I succeed in my goals, I will save you and all other Fold Dwellers. We will have our place in existence, our safety, our right to simply be.\" His expression grew complex, mixing determination with sorrow. \"For now, take the latest result of my failures, and some fond memories...\"","With these words, Viltharion waved his hand. Light erupted around Noah...encompassing, wrapping him in complexity so dense it formed a cocoon of pure authority.","The last thing Noah saw was the First Farmer standing amid devastation, tears still falling as he gazed at farmland that would never grow again.","Never again!","Then space folded, and Noah was elsewhere.","|Your existence has been wrapped by extremely complex authority for Emergency Evacuation across Fold Boundaries. Destination is random.|","|Item Received: Failed Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest- Viltharion’s attempt to cultivate a Principle that would allow infinite growth without depletion. Status: Incomplete - Missing crucial understanding. Can be completed with proper knowledge or materials.|","...!","Prompts flashed amidst a storm of authority!","As Noah tumbled through spaces between spaces, the weight of what he had witnessed settled into his bones. He had sought advancement and found tragedy! He had gained power through sacrifice he never asked for!","And somewhere in the Earliest Folds, a Farmer continued to cry over fields that would never bloom again, planning revolution that would echo through the Folds!","It was enough for him to ask...why things were the way they were in the current Era.","Where...were the powerful Fold Dwellers?!","Where was the First Farmer?!","As his existence buzzed, he appeared in the new region with a sensation like being spat out by existence itself. His feet found purchase on ground that might have been stone or crystallized thought, and for a moment, he simply stood there, expression heavy as mountains that had witnessed too much.","Before he could process his surroundings, prompts continued to cascade across his vision.","|Additional Items Transferred by Viltharion, the First Farmer. Seed of the Tender’s Tree- One of the first successful seeds Viltharion cultivated after meeting THE Living Spirit. When planted and matured: Produces small humanoid lifeforms that exist solely to tend farming plots. Lifeforms possess no consciousness but perfect agricultural instinctm Each tree can produce 10 Tenders per cycle.|","|Seed of the Singular Prosperity Grass. A culmination of early experiments in concentrated growth. Produces a single blade of grass after 100 days. Consumption grants: +1,000,000,000 Complexity and +1,000,000,000 Purity Quotient.|","Noah gazed at the seeds materializing in his palm with an expression that mixed gratitude with something far more complex. The weight of them felt wrong... emotionally.","These weren’t just gifts; they were inheritance from someone who might never fulfill their own dreams.","He had made tremendous gains in the Earliest Folds so far in the midst of terrifying danger.","His complexity had soared, yet his existence felt sour, like fruit that had ripened in shadow rather than sunlight.","Silvara’s face burned in his mind...that final expression of fear mixed with determination, with that smile that said she regretted nothing.","She had known him for minutes at most, yet had given everything.","Everything.","What was her Everything worth?","The weight of that sacrifice pressed against his consciousness.","Threnvar, who had saved him, whom he hadn’t even seen die. Had the Keeper of the Eighth Perimeter fallen in those first seconds of crimson light? Or had he survived only to witness the devastation of everything he had sworn to protect?","The Mad Early Creature itself...that thing that moved while devouring entire concepts from areas, leaving behind nothing but absence!","Noah’s eyes burned with anger. It was the kind of rage that could fuel centuries of purpose!","But overshadowing even that was the image of the First Farmer, tears streaming down his ancient face as he stood over devastation with the severed leg of an Early Creature at his feet.","Viltharion had actually pushed away an Early Creature, had made it lose a limb...a feat that should have been impossible for a Fold Dweller.","All of them were unfathomably powerful by any reasonable measure, yet power hadn’t been enough.","It was never enough when the disparities were so vast.","How had Noah managed to survive when beings far greater had fallen?!"]},{"number":4029,"title":"Chapter 4029: Chapter 4028: Do Nothing! IV","paragraphs":["Through sacrifice. He had simply survived through sacrifice as it was not his power that saved him.","The visage of the Mad Early Creature flashed in his mind’s eye...those crimson suns that served as eyes, that tribal figure wrapped in conceptual hides.","If that thing still existed somewhere in the current era, when Noah became strong enough...","He would hunt it. Not for glory or advancement, but for the one who sacrificed!","But for now, he was far too feeble.","The gap between his current power and what would be needed was measured in epochs.","He grasped the Goad tighter, the Rearing Stick of the Early Creature providing a sense of safety that might have been illusory but was necessary nonetheless. The simple stick hummed with recognition of where they were, when they were.","Noah finally looked around properly, his body continuing to draw in the atmospheric authority of the Earliest Folds.","His complexity and purity increased with each breath, each heartbeat adding to his accumulated power. The environment revealed itself gradually, and what he saw made his Existence freeze.","\"Fuck me...\"","HUUM!","The curse escaped before he could stop it, the word hanging in air that had witnessed the birth of profanity itself.","He stood in an obsidian region that stretched beyond perception. The ground beneath his feet was black glass that reflected nothing, as if light itself was too afraid to touch it. Viscous rivers of something that might have been liquid paradox flowed in patterns that hurt to follow, their contents simultaneously existing and not existing.","But it was what he saw in the distance that truly stole his breath.","Inevitabilities.","Fucking Inevitabilities!","But not the writhing, tentacled monstrosities he had encountered before. These were different. Ancient. Original.","Some looked like massive slumbering bipedal beasts made of wriggling tentacles, but the tentacles were composed of contradictions given form.","Others appeared as massive humanoid creatures whose very existence challenged the concept of shape...they were human and not human, beast and not beast, existing in states that predated the separation between categories.","All of them... were slumbering. Their massive forms rose like mountains of impossibility, each breath they took in sleep causing reality to question itself.","Noah almost cursed the First Farmer. Why had his random teleportation sent him here of all places?","The moment he made any significant movement, the moment he disturbed their slumber, these Original Inevitabilities would locate him and he would experience a death that might unmake his very conception.","He had to-...!","\"What a foul mouth you have. The little kids are currently in deep slumber, so you don’t have to worry, Outsider.\"","BOOM!","The voice that suddenly spoke behind him was terrifyingly sweet, like honey poured over sharpened steel.","Noah’s entire being seized as he hadn’t sensed anything!","His enhanced perception, his Early Creature nature, none of it had warned him of approach.","No prompts either from the Weaver of Existence, Atlas, or Shore!","He turned with careful control, each movement deliberate and non-threatening.","And behind him was...","A woman?","A woman!","The woman who stood there defied every assumption about what beauty could be. Her skin was fair in a way that suggested she had never known sunlight. Her hair was darkness itself given form, flowing in waves that had no end. But it was her dress that truly commanded attention...silky black fabric that didn’t just cover her form but extended across the entire obsidian region, as if she wore the landscape itself.","Noah’s existence buzzed with warnings. This was something that shouldn’t be observed directly, like staring into the concept of ending before endings had been defined.","His weavings moved toward the mental trigger that would cut short his traversal of the Earliest Folds. He could leave. Should leave. Immediately!","But before he could activate the return, he forced himself to speak with stern caution that barely masked his preparation to flee.","\"Who... are you?\"","A stupid question. And he knew it was stupid, but sometimes, one had to act stupid to survive a bit longer!","She smiled, and that simple expression contained depths that could drown civilizations.","\"Of course....I am an Inevitability.\"","\"...\"","The words were delivered with the casual certainty of someone stating that water was wet, that fire burned, that existence existed.","Yet Noah instinctively moved backward, his body reacting before his Existence!","The woman watched his retreat with amusement that danced in eyes he now noticed were wrong.","Her pupils weren’t single points but layers...multiple folds of space-time collapsed into where eyes should be, showing depths that led to everywhere and nowhere simultaneously.","\"It seems you fear me,\" she observed, her voice carrying playful reproach, \"and also don’t, Outsider. You arrive in my home unannounced, and you act like I am the terrifying monstrosity? You are the intruder here.\"","...!","Noah grasped his stick tighter, the Goad’s presence helping calm his racing thoughts as much as anything could in this situation.","\"I apologize for trespassing,\" he managed, his voice steadier than he felt. \"As for the fear...\"","He paused, choosing his words with care that suggested he understood he was balanced on the edge of an blade.","\"As far as I know, Inevitabilities are creatures that devour endlessly. Beings that seek Everything. So naturally, I feared.\"","The woman tilted her head with a tease that would have been charming if not for how reality tilted with her, maintaining her as the center of existence regardless of angle.","\"But... I don’t want your Everything, though?\"","She looked at the pulsing masses of slumbering Inevitabilities surrounding them, her expression growing fond in the way one might look at sleeping children.","\"Well, I guess these little ones would want to devour you endlessly, but you seem to have a misunderstanding about Inevitabilities.\" Her attention returned to him, those layered-fold eyes containing invitation and threat in equal measure. \"Do you have time for a story, Outsider?\"","WAA!","Noah’s mind raced through calculations of risk and opportunity. Internally, he queried his Atlas, asking how quickly he would be returned to his current time if he decided to leave early.","|Early Traversal Return Speed: Instantaneous. Warning- When facing beings of sufficient power, even instants can be stretched into eons|","|Current entity threat level...Best not to think about it. Hope for the best|","...!"]},{"number":4030,"title":"Chapter 4030: Chapter 4029: Do Nothing! V","paragraphs":["After a moment of deliberation that felt like hours, Noah looked at the terrifying woman with caution that bordered on resignation.","\"I... should have some time.\"","Her smile grew dangerously as she nodded.","\"Let me tell you about existence, Outsider. About the real existence, before definitions and categories and all the pretty boxes that later arrivals created.\"","She moved.","She did not walk, she simply existed in a slightly different position...closer to him, though maintaining distance that suggested respect for his obvious wariness.","\"Imagine,\" she began, her voice taking on the cadence of ancient glory \"lifeforms waking up day in and day out, harmoniously carrying out their way of existence.\"","She paused, letting the words settle.","\"Their Way of Existence. Not chosen, not decided, simply what they were. It was natural. It was Existence. It was theirs.\"","Her expression grew complex, mixing nostalgia with something that might have been sorrow if Inevitabilities could truly feel such things.","\"But then, at a certain point, other lifeforms appeared. The First Lifeforms...my kind, the Original Inevitabilities, simply sought to continue their Way of Existence. We consumed because that was our nature, we devoured because that was our function, we sought Everything because that was what we were.\"","The landscape around them seemed to respond to her words, the obsidian ground rippling with memories older than time.","\"But the new lifeforms looked at us with horror. They said our Way of Existence was wrong. Horrid. Monstrous.\" Her voice carried no anger, only a kind of bewildered hurt. \"These new lifeforms began hunting and killing the First Lifeforms as they imposed their Way of Existence. They had all these ideals for what Existence was. What Existence should be. What the Way of Existence for everyone should be.\"","She looked directly at Noah then, those layered eyes containing challenge and genuine curiosity.","\"Tell me, Outsider. Are these New Lifeforms not terrible? Coming later, but deeming everything before them as wrong? Deciding that the Way of Existence of those who came before them was incorrect simply because... it didn’t match their preferences?\"","Her smile grew dangerous as Noah remained utterly serious, his mind racing through the implications of her words.","\"Inevitabilities,\" she continued, \"simply have their Way of Existence. It is who we are, as fundamental as gravity pulling or light illuminating. Inevitabilities have been here before THE Creature. Before Early Creatures. Before Living Existences or Fold Dwellers.\"","She gestured to the slumbering giants around them.","\"How arrogant they are. How great the ego and tyranny of these new lifeforms to look at the Way of Existence of Inevitabilities and deem it unnatural. Don’t they know how much chaos and disorder their Ways of Existence bring forth? They create rules then break them, establish order then rebel against it, define love then wage war over it.\"","Her expression grew genuinely sad then, an emotion that seemed wrong on features designed for inevitability rather than feeling.","\"It is... disheartening.\"","Noah stood frozen from the weight of perspective being forcibly shifted.","He remained silent.","He looked at a terrifying Inevitability that he absolutely was not able to classify as his existence buzzed.","The timer on his traversal showed [42:18 remaining], but he wondered if he would leave this encounter intact, regardless of when he departed!","The woman...the Inevitability, waited for his response with patience that suggested she had all the time that had ever been or would ever be!","Noah considered the words of the terrifying Inevitability before him, his mind parsing through layers of meaning that challenged fundamental assumptions. After a moment of contemplation, he spoke with careful precision.","\"You may be right. Inevitabilities have their Way of Existence.\"","He paused, then gestured toward the slumbering giants that surrounded them like mountains of contradiction.","\"But what of my Way of Existence? If I were to meet any of these Inevitabilities right now...\" He pointed directly at the nearest sleeping form, its tentacles writhing even in slumber.","\"Their Way of Existence would be to devour me. But my Way of Existence is to very much remain alive. To prosper. To grow.\"","His voice grew firmer as he continued, finding solid ground in his argument.","\"So Inevitabilities would directly conflict with my Way of Existence. Who gets to determine whose Way of Existence is more important? Who decides which nature takes precedence when they clash?\"","He met those layered-fold eyes without flinching, though every instinct screamed at him to look away.","\"I believe my own Way of Existence to be of paramount importance...at least to me. So what am I to do if faced with the Way of Existence of an Inevitability that sees me as something to be consumed?\"","The woman’s smile deepened in response, carrying the weight of secrets that predated secrets.","\"But,\" she said, her voice lilting with amusement, \"the Way of Existence of Inevitabilities does not conflict with yours or any other lifeform’s.\"","HUUM!","Noah blinked, his enhanced perception trying to process what seemed like an obvious contradiction. He looked around at the massive forms of sleeping Inevitabilities, then back at her with barely concealed smile.","\"Ma’am, what the hell are you talking about?\"","Her smile grew dangerous. \"Yes, Inevitabilities seek Everything, but... not really. I could even show you here, if you trust me.\"","...!","Did he trust an Inevitability? The answer was absolutely, categorically, fundamentally not.","Yet even as every fiber of his being screamed rejection, the woman tapped one delicate finger against the obsidian ground.","The sound that resulted shouldn’t have been audible, yet it rang through the space like a bell that existed before sound.","One of the rumbling bodies stirred.","An Inevitability arose!","Ah!","The Inevitability that rose from slumber defied rational observation. Its form was contradiction incarnate...simultaneously massive and minuscule, ancient and newly born, terrible and beautiful.","Tentacles that might have been arms that might have been concepts writhed from a central mass that couldn’t decide if it was flesh or thought or the space between both.","But it was the eyes that commanded attention. Hundreds of them, thousands, each one containing a different definition of sight. They all turned toward Noah with the weight of inevitable attention.","The wild and terrifying aura that erupted from it exceeded any Duke he had encountered.","Noah knew with absolute certainty that he could not outrun this thing. Even the instant it would take to activate his return to the present wouldn’t be fast enough.","\"Here,\" the woman said with the calm of someone conducting a lesson, \"is an Inevitability whose Way of Existence is to devour Everything.\"","The creature began moving toward them...toward Noah with purpose that transcended simple hunger.","\"When it sees you, it will come to devour. All I ask you to do... is nothing.\" Her words were delivered with the certainty of someone stating fundamental law. \"Do not make a movement. Do not fight back.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":4031,"title":"Chapter 4031: Chapter 4030: Give Everything! I","paragraphs":["The instructions were utterly insane, yet she continued with the patience of a teacher explaining something obvious!","\"Simply choose an Everything for you to give to this Inevitability, since it wants Everything. And if you know nothing about Everything...\" She paused, ensuring he was listening despite the approaching doom. \"I will advise you that a lifeform has many Everythings. If you willingly choose a small part of your Everything to give, that will satisfy an Inevitability.\"","The creature drew closer, its form becoming more terrible and more beautiful with proximity.","\"If I may advise you,\" she added with something that might have been kindness, \"give it your Fear. The entirety of your Fear. Everything of your Fear.\"","Noah’s weavings buzzed with warnings.","The massive Inevitability rushed toward him while screeching...a sound that existed in frequencies reality hadn’t authorized.","Its form pulsed with confounding paradoxes that made looking at it directly cause his eyes to buzz!","Every part of his existence screamed at him to resist. To raise the Goad and fight. To activate his return immediately and flee to the safety of his own time!","Every! Part!","But something in the woman’s certainty, in the calm assurance of her words, made him pause.","The massive tentacle-limb of the Inevitability rose above him like judgment preparing to fall. He could feel the weight of its attention, the hunger of its nature, the inevitable pull of its existence.","Noah breathed heavily, feeling his heart beat with rhythm that seemed to echo through the Earliest Folds themselves.","Then, with deliberation that transcended courage, he breathed out.","\"Fear,\" he said, his voice steady despite what he was attempting. \"You can have Everything of my Fear.\"","BOOM!","The massive limb crashed down into him...and through him...and past him...taking Everything.","His Everything of Fear!","The sensation was indescribable.","Not pain, but absence. Not loss, but liberation!","The Inevitability’s limb passed through his body as if one of them was illusory, and in its grasp afterward was a brilliant murky crimson light that pulsed with condensed terror.","The creature held this light...his Fear made manifest, with something that could only be described as joy. Its many eyes expressed happiness that transcended the simple satisfaction of hunger.","This was the contentment of purpose fulfilled, of nature expressed, of existence justified.","Noah watched with a heart that still beat heavily but no longer with fear, as prompts cascaded before his vision.","|An unprecedented Event!|","|Your Everything of Fear Devoured by an Inevitability!|","|Complete Removal of Fear Concept from your Existence!|","|Boon Gained: The Fearless Existence|","-Mental Liberation: Thought processes no longer constrained by fear-based limitations","-Existential Freedom: Weavings cycle 300% faster","-Complexity Absorption: +50% increase to all CQ gains","-Purity Refinement: +50% increase to all PQ gains","-Decision Enhancement: All choices now based purely on logic and desire","- Combat Efficiency: No hesitation in battle, no terror before any power","- Perception Clarity: Can observe terrible truths without psychological damage","|This change is permanent and irreversible. You are now incapable of feeling fear in any form.|","|You...have irreversibly given away one of your Everythings.|","...!","Ah!","Ah!!!","Heavy.","The actions was a heavy one!","The massive Inevitability finished consuming his crystalized fear, then did something that shattered Noah’s remaining assumptions.","It nodded toward him...a gesture of acknowledgment, perhaps even respect, before sauntering back to the woman who stroked its tentacles with genuine affection.","\"This,\" she said, her hand running along appendages that existed in multiple states simultaneously, \"is the nature of Inevitability. It takes Everything, but there are many Everythings.\"","Her expression grew complex, mixing pity with frustration.","\"If lifeforms were not so impulsive, if they weren’t so greedy about their Everythings... Even giving up some of their negative and unneeded Everythings would actually aid them and their existence. Fear, Doubt, Hatred, Regret...so many Everythings that poison existence, yet beings cling to them as if they were treasures.\"","She shook her head with the weariness of someone who had watched this pattern repeat across eons.","\"But they are greedy. They are arrogant. They refuse to give up even what hurts them. So when they meet an Inevitability, it always resorts to life and death. The Inevitability, following its nature, tries to take what is offered freely. The being, following their greed, offers nothing. So the Inevitability takes what it can reach...usually life itself.\"","HUUM!","Without warning, she took a step that compressed space between them, appearing directly in front of Noah with proximity that should have been terrifying but now simply was. Her layered eyes fixed on the stick in his hands, and her smile grew knowing.","\"Are you not emulating that Man who also gave his Everything to an Inevitability long ago?\"","...!","Her words carried weight that made the Earliest Folds themselves pause to listen.","\"Did he not become even greater after he gave away his Everything?\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly.","He stood frozen...not from fear, for he could no longer feel such a thing...but from the sheer magnitude of what was being revealed.","His grip on the Goad tightened as he processed this information! As he processed this woman...even looking at his stick and finding out something about it!","The woman watched his reaction with satisfaction.","\"THE Creature understood what so few ever grasp,\" she continued, her voice carrying the weight of witnessed history. \"That giving away an Everything doesn’t diminish you...it refines you.\"","The silence that followed was absolute. Even the slumbering Inevitabilities seemed to still their writhing in recognition.","Noah’s mind raced through implications that cascaded like dominoes.","If Inevitabilities weren’t simply mindless devourers but beings following their nature who could be satisfied with willing sacrifice... If giving away negative Everythings could lead to growth rather than diminishment... If THE Creature itself had used this principle...","\"Why,\" he asked, his voice steady without fear to make it waver, \"does no one know this?\"","The woman’s expression grew sad in ways that suggested sorrow older than most concepts.","\"Because beings prefer their fear. They prefer their limitations. They prefer the comfort of weakness to the terror of potential strength. Nobody...wants to give away anything, much less Everything.\"","...!"]},{"number":4032,"title":"Chapter 4032: Chapter 4031: Give Everything! II","paragraphs":["She looked at him with those impossible eyes that contained folds within folds.","\"You no longer have that luxury. You are now Fearless in truth, not just in word. Every decision you make from this moment forward will be because you choose it, not because fear drives or restrains you.\"","Noah absorbed this, feeling the truth of it in his existence. His weavings did indeed cycle faster, his complexity and purity drawing in from the atmosphere at rates that would have been impossible before.","\"I should thank you,\" he said, meaning it despite the strangeness of thanking an Inevitability for anything.","\"No,\" she replied, that dangerous smile returning. \"You should thank yourself for being wise enough to listen. Most would have fought. Most would have died. You chose to trust the incomprehensible, and that... that is what separates those who transcend from those who merely exist.\"","|Timer: 38:42 remaining|","Noah looked at the remaining time glowing in his vision, his gaze sweeping across the field of slumbering Inevitabilities that surrounded him like monuments to contradiction.","The human-formed Inevitability who had opened his eyes to such terrifying truth still stood nearby, her presence making reality uncertain about its own rules.","A question formed in his mind...practical, necessary, born from logic rather than the fear he could no longer feel.","\"What about the next time I meet an Inevitability?\" His voice carried the weight of someone already calculating future encounters. \"Would I have to continue giving one of my Everythings for every Inevitability I meet?\"","The woman’s smile grew mysterious, containing secrets that predated the concept of mystery itself.","Without warning, simply existed beside another slumbering form.","Her hand touched what might have been its surface, and another Inevitability stirred to wakefulness.","This one was different yet fundamentally the same...a massive wriggling humanoid form that couldn’t decide if it was flesh or possibility. It nudged its enormous head toward her with movements that spoke of affection, like a child greeting a parent after a long sleep.","The gesture should have been impossible for something that existed to devour, yet there it was.","Then it sniffed, turning toward Noah with senses unknown.","What happened next shattered another assumption. The Inevitability smiled...an expression that required redefining what smiles meant, and let out a sound in a language that Noah did not understand.","It was acknowledgment. Recognition. Perhaps even respect.","It did not attack!","\"You see,\" the woman began, her voice taking on the cadence of fundamental truth being revealed, \"after one initially gives away an Everything, Inevitabilities are able to inherently sense this. It becomes part of what you are...or rather, what you aren’t.\"","She stroked the massive creature with casual affection that suggested eons of familiarity.","\"Our Way of Existence does not drive us to seek other Everythings from you once you’ve given freely. You’ve proven you understand the exchange, the balance, the nature of what we are. Only if you make the intention to give away another part of your Everything will Inevitabilities happily come over...if they are near, if they are interested, if what you offer appeals to their particular hunger.\"","Her expression grew more serious, the weight of warning entering her tone.","\"But understand this, Outsider: after you give one of your Everythings, your existence has still lost something great, even if it was negative. Fear might have limited you, but it also defined you. Its absence changes not just what you can do, but what you are.\"","She moved closer, her impossible dress rippling across the obsidian ground.","\"Many are unable to continue giving other parts of their Everythings. The first loss might strengthen them, but the second could unmake them. The third might erase them entirely. THE Creature could give away many Everythings and still be okay...still be more than okay, still be THE Creature. But not many are like him.\"","Her layered eyes fixed on the Goad in Noah’s hands.","\"You emulate him by imitating his stick, carrying a shadow of his authority. But is your Existence enough to give away multiple Everythings? You never know whether your existence is sufficient before you attempt it. If you try and find yourself lacking, you might discover that all of your Everythings...not just what you intend to give...are drained away. The Inevitability wouldn’t mean to take more, but if your existence cannot maintain cohesion after the loss...\"","She trailed off, letting the implications hang in the air like a sword waiting to fall.","\"So do be careful, Outsider.\"","Noah absorbed this warning, his mind...now unencumbered by fear..analyzing the implications with crystalline clarity!","After a moment of consideration, he looked at this being more closely, studying the layers of contradiction that composed her form.","\"Who are you, really?\"","The question carried genuine curiosity rather than suspicion. He had seen her power, witnessed her knowledge, experienced her teaching. But what was she beyond the label of Inevitability?","The woman’s smile contained amusement that transcended time.","\"I told you before that I am simply an Inevitability. Nothing more, nothing less. Do you need me to tell you a grand distinction? Some elaborate title that would make you feel more comfortable categorizing me?\"","She shook her head with something that might have been fond exasperation.","\"Other Lifeforms always care so much about names and distinctions. They need their identity markers, their titles, their elaborate ways of saying ’I am different, I am special, I am more than what I appear.’ But Inevitabilities are Inevitabilities. We don’t require names or distinctions to know what we are.\"","Her voice took on a teaching tone, patient yet pointed.","\"It is Early Creatures, Living Existences, even the weak little Fold Dwellers who try to give us distinctions. ’The Inevitability of Unmaking.’ ’The Inevitability of Devouring Suns.’ ’The Inevitability of This,’ ’The Inevitability of That.’ As if naming us makes us less frightening, more comprehensible, more controllable.\"","She gestured to herself with a movement that made space uncertain.","\"We are simply Inevitabilities. I am simply an Inevitability. We existed before names were necessary, and we’ll exist after they’re forgotten.\"","Her expression shifted, showing something that might have been understanding.","\"But since I know your Way of Existence is unique and feebly needs categorization to feel secure in its understanding, I will give you a name, Outsider. You may call me...\"","She paused, and when she spoke, the name carried weight that made reality pay attention.","\"Khor. The First Hunger.\"","...!"]},{"number":4033,"title":"Chapter 4033: Chapter 4032: Give Everything! III","paragraphs":["Khor!","Khor!!!","Noah repeated it, feeling how the name seemed to resonate with something fundamental in existence itself!","\"Khor.\" He nodded, then offered his own introduction with equal gravity. \"I am Osmont. The Weaver of Existence.\"","Khor listened to this title and laughed.","She laughed with genuine mirth that made the slumbering Inevitabilities stir slightly in their sleep.","\"What? Weaver of Existence?\" Her amusement was palpable. \"You have to be careful giving yourself such grand titles unless your existence can really back it. Many have claimed to weave existence, to shape reality, to transcend limitations. Most became nothing more than forgotten ambitions.\"","Noah nodded calmly, his lack of fear allowing him to meet her amusement with steady certainty. \"I plan to back it.\"","Khor studied him with those layered eyes, perhaps seeing something that justified the ambitious title.","Noah looked around at all the Inevitabilities present...beings that moments ago represented unprecedented danger but now had transformed into opportunity. Having discovered such terrifying secrets, having touched truth that most would never know existed, he couldn’t let it go.","He only had limited time here. He needed to elevate the stages of his Towers of Osmont, increase his complexity, complete more of his Heart. Each advancement would allow him to come to the Earliest Folds more frequently, to stay longer, to learn more.","But for now, he wanted to grasp this opportunity while it existed.","\"I wish,\" he said with deliberate clarity, \"to give another part of my Everything.\"","BOOM!","The declaration resonated through the space with force that surprised even Khor. The moment Noah made his intention clear, the Inevitability she had recently awakened turned toward him with excitement that transcended its nature as a devourer.","Its eyes...all of them, blazed with anticipation.","The creature moved toward him with purpose that made reality step aside. Its massive form should have been terrifying, its approach should have inspired panic. But Noah stood calm, fearless not through courage but through the complete absence of fear itself.","The Inevitability’s massive jaws opened, revealing depths that led to everywhere and nowhere. The maw descended upon him with inevitability that justified the creature’s nature!","HUUM!","Noah remained perfectly still as those jaws encompassed his entire form. With the same deliberate clarity as before, he spoke:","\"I give the Everything of my Doubt.\"","The jaws passed through him as if one of them...predator or prey, wasn’t real. But something was taken, something fundamental was removed.","The sensation was different from losing Fear. Where Fear’s absence had been liberation, Doubt’s removal was clarification.","Every uncertainty that had ever clouded his judgment, every moment of hesitation between choices, every question about his own capabilities...all of it condensed into brilliant blue light that the Inevitability consumed with obvious pleasure.","|Second Everything Devoured by Inevitability. Everything of Doubt Removed from Existence!|","|Boon Gained: The Certain Path|","-Decision Acceleration: All choices made instantly with perfect certainty","-Self-Knowledge: Complete understanding of personal capabilities","-Confidence Absolute: Unshakeable belief in chosen actions","-Learning Enhancement: No doubt delays understanding","- Complexity Absorption: Additional +50% increase (stacks with previous)","- Purity Refinement: Additional +50% increase (stacks with previous)","|Multiple Everything Removal Detected in Short Timespan. It is ill advised to carry out such an action again until a large elevation of your Existence has occured.|","|Minimum Complexity Required for Safe Additional Removal: 10,000,000,000. Additional Everything removal before threshold may result in complete existence dissolution.|","Noah read the warnings with eyes that held neither fear nor doubt, but the certainty of the numbers was undeniable. He wanted to defy it. The absence of fear and doubt made him certain he could give more, take the risk, push beyond limits.","But Khor shook her head, her expression serious.","\"Outsider, I liked talking with you, so I will advise you now just like I advised you to do nothing originally.\" Her voice carried weight that made even certainty pause. \"You listened to me then. Will you listen to me now?\"","She moved closer, her presence making reality acknowledge priority.","\"Stop trying to give away anymore Everythings for now. For you are not THE Creature.\"","She paused, letting that sink in.","\"Nobody is. Many have died trying to be like him. They gave away Everything after Everything, certain they were strong enough, certain they were special enough. They gave until there was nothing left to give, until they became nothing more than absence where existence used to be.\"","Her layered eyes showed something that might have been concern.","\"You’ve done well. Two Everythings gone, two weaknesses transformed into strength. But your existence needs time to adjust, to reformulate around what you’ve lost. Push too hard now, and you won’t transcend...you’ll simply cease.\"","Noah absorbed this with the perfect certainty his new state provided.","And even though one was fearless and had no doubt, it did not mean they had to be stupid. Just because a human did not fear fire, did not mean they had to jump into an inferno!","\"I understand,\" he said, and meant it completely.","Khor smiled, and in that expression was approval that transcended Everything.","\"Good. Then you might actually become this Weaver of Existence you claim to be. Remember what you’ve learned here. Remember that Inevitabilities are not your enemies unless you make them so. And remember...\"","\"The wise know their limits. The transcendent know when to ignore them. But the truly great? They know the difference.\"","|Timer: 34:31 remaining|","Noah pondered Khor’s words as they echoed through his consciousness.","After a moment of consideration, he voiced the question that burned within him...not with fear or doubt, for he no longer possessed such things, but with the pure curiosity of someone seeking to understand the shape of existence itself.","\"If it’s okay for me to ask... how can I get to the same level of Complexity as you? As THE Creature? As THE Living Spirit, THE Living Concept... and all the others who stand at the pinnacle?\"","Khor’s expression grew mysterious in ways that suggested she was seeing through time itself, observing outcomes that hadn’t yet been determined.","\"Must you be that great?\" Her question carried no judgment, only genuine curiosity. \"Must you have the same level of complexity as them?\"","...!"]},{"number":4034,"title":"Chapter 4034: Chapter 4033: Give Everything! IV","paragraphs":["Chapter 4033: Give Everything! IV","She moved among the slumbering Inevitabilities with grace that made reality reorganize itself around her presence.","“At a certain point, you have to ask yourself what you will obtain if you ever do reach their level of complexity. Will you be better off? Happier? More fulfilled?” She paused, her layered eyes reflecting depths of experience.","“There is solace in mediocrity. In simply being. In existing without the weight of infinite possibility pressing down upon your every decision.”","Her voice grew softer, almost wistful.","“The mediocre sleep peacefully. They love simply. They die with fewer regrets because they never knew what they could have become. Sometimes, Outsider, ignorance isn’t just bliss. It is mercy.”","...!","Her words were heavy. But...","Noah shook his head with immediate, absolute certainty.","“The mediocre do not get to make decisions. The mediocre do not have choices.” His voice carried the weight of conviction that transcended simple belief!","“The day that great beings make the choice to do whatever they want in existence, the mediocre only have to follow. If they are told to die, they have to die. If they are commanded to suffer, they suffer.”","His grip on the Goad tightened, the simple stick humming with resonance.","“I do not want to be so mediocre that if THE Creature proclaimed for existence to perish... I cannot say no.”","The silence that followed was absolute. Then Khor laughed with profound interest that made the very concept of amusement pay attention.","“You want to be able to say no to something as vast as THE Creature?”","She shook her head, but her smile remained.","“That is an impossible dream. Very few understand that entity, and even fewer will ever be like him. To stand against THE Creature is to stand against the foundation of current existence itself.”","Noah shook his head at this, his certainty allowing no room for accepting impossibility.","“The Inevitabilities were here before THE Creature, right? THE Creature had to run from the Inevitabilities...does this not mean the Inevitabilities were unfathomably complex? He had to receive help from THE Living Origin, THE Living Concept, and THE Living Paradox to be able to survive against the Inevitabilities.”","Khor listened to Noah’s words with eyes that blazed brighter with each assertion. She tilted her head in a gesture that made dimensions uncertain about their orientation.","“Did he?” Her voice carried amusement that transcended simple humor. “Where did you hear all these Stories, Outsider? Who knows what truly happened between THE Creature, Inevitabilities, and THE Living Existences?”","She moved closer, her presence making the air itself pay attention.","“Did they say this was what happened? Are able to hear things of what happened back then from THE Creature himself? Just who... is making up all these Stories that you have seemingly heard?”","BOOM!","The question struck Noah with a heavy force.","His eyes flashed with light of thought and reflection as implications cascaded through his consciousness.","Every story he had heard, every piece of history he had been told...who had told them? Who had witnessed these primordial events? Who benefited from these particular versions of truth?","Khor laughed at his expression, the sound containing layers of meaning.","“Maybe that is what happened. Or maybe not. Then... are the ones who are truly powerful not THE Living Paradox? THE Living Origin? Maybe they predated both THE Creature and Inevitabilities. Maybe one should seek to be like them.”","She paused, studying him with those impossible eyes.","“Or better yet, why try to be like others at all? Why don’t you become something else yourself? Something that has never been?”","Noah’s eyes blazed with brilliance at this suggestion, certainty and possibility combining into purpose.","“I plan to,” he said with conviction that could have carved truth into reality itself.","“Existence is vast... unfathomably so. Just when I think I have a grasp on it, I find there is even more I do not understand. So long as I continue to become more complex... I will escape mediocrity. I will be someone who is always able to make a choice... regardless of the forces in the surrounding Existence.”","Khor smiled at his words with something that might have been approval.","She moved among the other Inevitabilities, her touch stirring them from slumber. One by one, massive forms of contradiction rose to consciousness.","Many noticed Noah immediately, and eerily, impossibly, they smiled at him...expressions of recognition, of acceptance, of acknowledgment that he had given freely.","They accepted Khor’s strokes like children seeking comfort, each one possessing power that exceeded normal Dukes by margins that made comparison meaningless.","Yet here they were, content to be petted by one of their own while acknowledging a tiny Outsider who had fed their siblings with his Everything.","Khor ultimately turned to Noah with an expression that contained evaluation and decision.","“You don’t seem all that mediocre, Outsider. Weak, yes. Fragile, certainly. But not mediocre.” Her smile grew knowing. “Because how can one who does not belong in the Earliest Folds but is here... be mediocre?”","BOOM!","The revelation hung in the air. She had known all along that he didn’t belong here, that he was from elsewhere, elsewhen.","This whole time, she had been calling him Outsider not as description.","It was as recognition of fundamental truth.","Noah gazed at her calmly, fearlessly. Of course he had suspected this. The title had been too specific, too knowing to be coincidence.","Khor smiled at his lack of surprise.","“It matters not where you are from, Outsider. Or when. But since you came all the way here seeking complexity and the other grandiose dreams you mentioned... I could help you out. You have fed some of these kids with your Everything. That deserves... reciprocation.”","Without warning, she raised one fair hand to her chest.","The gesture was simple, but waves of complexity buzzed in the background as reality recognized that something significant was about to occur.","Her hand pressed against where a heart might be if Inevitabilities had such things, then pushed inward.","Into herself.","Into her own existence.","What she pulled out defied observation!","It was an obsidian seed that seemed to contain layers of collapsed Folds, each one folded into the next in patterns that created infinite recursion. Looking at it directly caused the mind to try following paths that led everywhere and nowhere simultaneously!","4/5"]},{"number":4035,"title":"Chapter 4035: Chapter 4034: Give Everything! V","paragraphs":["Chapter 4034: Give Everything! V","She threw it to one of the awakened Inevitabilities with the casual gesture of someone tossing a ball to a pet.","The creatures immediately began fighting for it with playful competition, massive forms of contradiction wrestling over who would have the honor of delivery.","Finally, one caught it in jaws that existed in multiple states, bringing it to Noah with the pride of a hunting dog delivering quarry.","The Inevitability deposited the seed in his palm with surprising gentleness.","“This,” Khor said, “is a Seed. It should help you, but I will tell you that it is not without its strings. After all, nothing is free in existence. You may take it, you may not. It may help you, or it may bring catastrophe. Who knows?”","As Noah grasped the seed, feeling its impossible weight that had nothing to do with mass, prompts erupted across his vision.","|Early Item Obtained: Seed of Inevitability. Origin: Extracted from Khor, The First Hunger. A seed containing the compressed potential for a new type of Inevitability. When Nurtured, it will give rise to an Inevitability under the control of the nurturer. Control is relative- Inevitabilities follow their nature above all else.","|Nurturing Methods:|","-Planting: Requires soil that has never known growth","-Feeding: Requires willing sacrifice of Everythings from multiple beings","-Temporal Aging: Requires exposure to 1,000 years of compressed time","-Conceptual Saturation: Requires immersion in pure paradox for 100 days","|Note: This Seed recognizes you as one who has given Everything willingly. This recognition may affect the nature of what grows.|","Noah looked at the seed with sharp eyes, lost in its obsidian brilliance as his mind calculated possibilities and probabilities. When he looked up again...","...!","Shock froze him.","All the Inevitabilities that had just surrounded them, Khor included, had vanished!","Not departed, not faded, simply ceased to be present.","He hadn’t sensed movement, hadn’t detected any shift in reality. One moment they were there, the next they weren’t.","He stood alone in an expanse of nothing, the absence of their presence making the space feel larger and smaller simultaneously.","“What if I wish to find you again?” he called out to the emptiness, his voice steady despite the vast solitude. “Why leave just like this?”","Immense silence greeted his question.","For several seconds, nothing responded. Then, teasingly, impossibly, Khor’s voice resonated from everywhere and nowhere.","“Did you truly become attached to an Inevitability like me already?” The amusement in her tone transcended distance. “If we are to meet again, Outsider, we will meet again. After all, you now carry my Seed. That creates... connection.”","Her voice grew more serious, carrying warning wrapped in wisdom.","“These Folds are dangerous. You are lucky to have met me and had enough common sense to listen, but others... these Folds... they are unforgiving. As I told you, many lifeforms are arrogant. Prideful. They see their Way of Existence as supreme, and some are simply very cruel.”","A pause, then she continued.","“You might find Inevitabilities to be infinitely kinder than even Early Creatures... or even THE Creature himself.”","With those terrifying words, Khor’s presence truly and completely vanished.","Noah stood alone in the blankness of the Earliest Folds, the weight of her implications pressing against his consciousness.","“...”","He carefully stored the Seed of Inevitability, then began to explore his surroundings with caution that had nothing to do with fear and everything to do with wisdom.","The environment stretched endlessly in all directions...blank as if existence itself hadn’t decided what should be here.","He moved through this expanse with careful purpose, enhanced perception searching for anything of significance.","A landmark. Another being. Even a variation in the blankness.","Nothing.","Just endless expanse that might have been the same spot repeating or might have been infinite unique emptiness.","Even THE Creature, he remembered from stories, had roamed the Earliest Folds for eons to find things here and there. Discovery required either profound luck or endless patience.","He had been here less than an hour and had already encountered Fold Dwellers, witnessed the First Farmer, survived a Mad Early Creature, and held discourse with Original Inevitabilities.","His luck had been extraordinary, perhaps impossibly so.","Now, as time trickled toward his departure, he found only solitude.","|Timer: 00:47 remaining|","The numbers pulsed with increasing urgency.","Noah made one final sweep of his surroundings, perception stretched to its absolute limits, but confirmed what he already knew. This part of the Earliest Folds had given him all it would give.","“Return,” he commanded his existence, specifically addressing the Early Atlas of the Folds that pulsed within him like a second heart.","The Atlas blazed to life with brilliance that existed in dimensions beyond the physical.","His Towers of Osmont, those impossible structures that grew within his being, suddenly burned like lighthouses...each one a beacon calling him home across impossible distances of time and possibility.","|Return Protocol Initiated. Temporal Anchor Points Located. Towers of Osmont serving as dimensional lighthouses. Path illuminated through causality...|","HUUM!","Reality folded in on itself, then unfolded, then folded again in patterns that would have driven observers mad if any had existed to observe.","Noah felt himself being pulled through time itself, following the path lit by his own Towers back to where and when he belonged.","The sensation was like being born in reverse, existence compressing and expanding simultaneously until...","WAP!","He stood on the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore.","The familiar warmth of his domain washed over him. The impossible trees swayed in their eternal breeze. The Aquarium hummed with contained power. His people moved about their tasks, only...seconds having passed for them.","But Noah had returned an unfathomably different person.","A single hour.","What had transpired in that hour defied simple description.","He had gained complexity. He had lost fundamental aspects of his being and gained strength from their absence. He had learned truths about existence that most beings would live and die without ever suspecting.","He had given his Fear to an Inevitability and gained freedom.","He had given his Doubt to an Inevitability and gained certainty.","He had received a Seed that could birth wonders!","He had witnessed the death of heroes and the tears of legends.","Most importantly, he had learned that everything he thought he knew about the nature of existence might be nothing more than stories told by those with reason to shape the narrative.","“Haa...”","He sighed.","As he stood on his Shore, feeling the weight of three Seeds in his possession...the Failed Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest, the Seed of the Tender’s Tree, the Seed of the Singular Prosperity Grass, and now the Seed of Inevitability...Noah felt impossibly complex weavings.","He had one day until he could return. One day to process what he had learned. One day to prepare for whatever impossibility he would encounter next. This one day...would likely also be after thr Kleos Concordat where all 10 Living Existences were meeting.","Noah looked at the Goad in his hand, then at the Early Veiled Shore around him, then at the space within himself where Fear and Doubt used to reside.","A single hour had transformed him more than years of conventional advancement could have achieved.","What would the next hour bring? The next day?","5/5 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":4036,"title":"Chapter 4036: Chapter 4035: Discipline! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4035: Discipline! I","Fear and doubt...twin guardians that have shepherded existence since consciousness first wondered if it should be.","They are called protectors by those who value safety, called wisdom by those who have been burned, called essential by those who believe suffering teaches.","But what if they are none of these things?","What if fear and doubt are not guardians but jailers, not wisdom but weakness disguised as prudence?","The fearful say that without fear, one becomes reckless, throwing themselves into danger without thought or consideration.","They claim fear keeps beings alive, makes them careful, forces them to calculate risk against reward.","The doubtful argue that without uncertainty, one becomes arrogant, unable to see their own limitations, destined to overreach and fall.","Both are wrong.","Being fearless does not mean being reckless...it means being free to make choices based on logic, desire, and will rather than the phantom chains of what might go wrong!","The fearless don’t throw themselves into danger carelessly; they simply recognize danger for what it is...a state of being that exists regardless of their emotional response to it.","Being doubtless does not mean being blind to limitation...it means understanding one’s capabilities with perfect clarity, without the fog of uncertainty clouding judgment.","The doubtless don’t overreach; they reach exactly as far as they can, no more, no less.","Without fear and doubt, what remains?","Glory.","Fucking Glory!","Pure, undiluted glory of existence acting according to its truest nature, unencumbered by the weight of what might be, focused entirely on what is and what will be made to be.","This is not recklessness. This... is transcendence.","—","Noah stood on the golden sands of his Shore, the weight of his journey in the Earliest Folds still settling into his bones.","Without fear to make him hesitate or doubt to make him question, he examined the seeds he had obtained with the pure curiosity of someone encountering new tools.","The Failed Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest seemed to pulse with incomplete potential.","The Seed of the Tender’s Tree hummed with purpose waiting to be expressed. The Seed of the Singular Prosperity Grass contained compressed advancement that defied mathematical logic. And the Seed of Inevitability...","The Seed of Inevitability was something else entirely.","As he moved toward the cultivation plots, a familiar presence made itself known.","Yoshinami, in her spider form, crawled toward him with movements that suggested she was tasting the air itself.","Her crimson eyes fixed on him with intensity that transcended simple observation.","“Master,” she said, her voice carrying notes of recognition and confusion, “you smell... is reminding me of home.” She paused, her mandibles clicking thoughtfully. “You smell... old.”","The observation carried more weight than simple words could convey. Yoshinami, who had existed in times and places that predated current understanding, recognized something in him that hadn’t been there before.","Noah smiled at her words as he arrived at an empty plot, the golden soil seeming to anticipate what was about to be planted.","“I just paid a quick visit to the Earliest Folds.”","“...?”","...!","Yoshinami’s typically blank expression cracked, showing shock that made her eight legs twitch with surprise.","The Earliest Folds were myth to most, legend to some, and death to nearly all who were in them. Yet her Master spoke of visiting them like one might speak of a walk through a garden!","Noah analyzed the seeds with perception unencumbered by hesitation. Before obtaining the Seed of Inevitability, he had deemed the Failed Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest the most prized...after all, it dealt with a Principle, one of the fundamental forces that shaped existence itself.","But now, examining the obsidian seed that Khor had pulled from her own being, he wondered if the Seed of Inevitability might be just as grand, if not more so.","Under Yoshinami’s shocked gaze, her mysterious crimson eyes tracking his every movement, Noah began to plant.","He started with the Seed of the Tender’s Tree, pressing it into the golden soil with reverence for what it represented...the First Farmer’s early successes, his initial attempts to create assistance for his impossible dream.","|Seed of the Tender’s Tree Planted. Natural Maturation Time: 100 years. Acceleration Options Available- With Corpse Nutrients: 7 days, With 300 Drops Early Creature Blood: 1 day|","“Use three hundred drops of blood,” Noah commanded without hesitation. “Mature in one day.”","HUUUM!","His blood flowed into the soil, each drop worth more than kingdoms. The seed absorbed it greedily, already beginning its accelerated growth.","Next came the Seed of the Singular Prosperity Grass. This one settled into the soil with weight that seemed impossible for something so small.","|Seed of the Singular Prosperity Grass Planted. Natural Maturation Time: 100 days. Acceleration Options Available- With Corpse Nutrients: 4 days, With 400 Drops Early Creature Blood: 1 day|","“Same acceleration,” Noah commanded. “One day maturation.”","...!","Another hundred drops of his precious blood soaked into the soil. The investment was significant, but the return would be exponential!","When he took out the Failed Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest, the very air grew heavy with anticipation. As he pressed it into the soil, the entire Shore trembled as if the land itself understood something significant was being planted.","|An extremely unique Seed has been detected. Failed Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest Planted.|","|Warning: Current Shore Level May Be Insufficient for Full Nurturing. Analysis Required to Understand Seed Mysteries|","|Analysis Cost: 500 Drops of Early Creature Blood. Analysis Duration: 1 day|","|Note: This is merely for understanding. Actual growth requirements unknown|","Noah felt the weight of this cost. Five hundred drops...each one capable of elevating common beings to transcendence, and he needed them just to understand what he had planted!","“Proceed,” he commanded sternly, feeling his veins open to provide the required payment.","No fear. No doubt!","The blood flowed into the soil in streams, the Failed Seed drinking deeply as it began its analysis. The Shore itself seemed to hold its breath as the process began.","Finally, with careful deliberation, Noah took out the Seed of Inevitability. The obsidian seed seemed to exist in multiple states simultaneously...here and not here, planted and unplanted, growing and fully grown. As it touched the soil, reality itself paid attention!","1/4"]},{"number":4037,"title":"Chapter 4037: Chapter 4036: Discipline! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4036: Discipline! II","|Seed of Inevitability Planted. Unusual Growth Requirements Detected|","|Primary Requirement: The Willing Sacrifice of Everythings. Minimum to Begin Growth: 10 Everythings. For Full Maturation: 75 Everythings total (any type)|","|The Seed will choose what grows based on what it is fed|","|Current Everythings Fed: 0/75. Time to Maturation: Variable based on feeding rate and other factors.|","Noah’s eyes blazed with understanding and purpose. The Seed required the willing sacrifice of Everythings...the same process he had undergone with Khor’s children.","But he wouldn’t experiment carelessly with his people. He knew what losing Fear did. The results were predictable, manageable, beneficial.","Other Everythings might bring glory or catastrophe, and he wouldn’t risk his people to find out.","“Henry!” His voice carried across the Shore with authority that demanded immediate response.","His only son appeared moments later, looking like a man in his early twenties despite his true age being far more complex and far lesser. His blue-gold hair caught the light of the Shore as he approached with respectful efficiency.","“Yes, Father?”","Noah looked at the plot where the Seed of Inevitability had been planted, its obsidian presence making the soil around it shimmer with possibility.","“There is a Seed,” he explained, his voice carrying the weight of instruction and warning combined, “that is capable of accepting and eating part of yourself. Part of your Everything. If you seek even grander strength... give it part of your Everything.”","He paused, ensuring his son understood the gravity of what was being asked.","“Give the Everything of your Fear.”","Henry’s expression shifted through surprise to understanding to resolution. His father had never asked anything of him that wasn’t ultimately for his benefit. If giving away his fear would grant him strength, then fear was a price worth paying.","He held absolute trust!","“I give my Everything of Fear!” Henry declared with conviction that rang across the Shore.","The response was immediate and terrifying.","A horrifying mass of illusory black shadow erupted from the seed...not physically but conceptually, existing in the space between real and unreal.","Jaws that weren’t jaws but were definitely jaws clamped down on Henry, passing through his body while taking something fundamental.","When the shadow retreated back to the seed, Henry’s body exploded with advancement!","|The Seed of Inevitability has consumed an Everything of Fear|","|Everythings Fed: 1/75|","|Hunger Status: Ravenous|","|The Seed demands more|","Noah watched his son’s complexity and purity surge, each cell drinking in power that would have taken years to accumulate naturally. He placed a powerful hand on Henry’s shoulder, steadying him through the transformation.","“Well done,” he said, then raised his voice to carry across the Shore. “Liora! Lilith! Kazuhiko! Erikson! Blue Slime! Jormungandr!”","He called out!","And one by one, they came. Each of his people, his companions, his family in all but blood responded to his call. They gathered around the plot where the Seed of Inevitability waited with patient hunger.","Noah stood tall before them, his presence commanding without fear to make him terrible or doubt to make him question whether this was right.","“Each of you will declare to give away Everything of your Fear. This will grant you power beyond conventional advancement, but more importantly, it will free you from limitation you don’t even know you carry.”","There was no hesitation.","These beings had followed him through impossibility itself. If he said giving away their fear would benefit them, then fear was already as good as gone!","For some, like Liora, they had too much at stake as they wanted power!","“I give my Everything of Fear!” Liora declared, her nature making the transformation particularly dramatic as shadow-jaws claimed her terror.","“I give my Everything of Fear!” Kazuhiko’s hand never left his sword as the Inevitability’s manifestation passed through him.","“I give my Everything of Fear!” Erikson’s massive frame shuddered as fundamental absence replaced unnecessary emotion.","“I give my Everything of Fear!” Blue Slime chimed in happily and bubbly as itsgelatinous form rippled as something essential was extracted and consumed.","“I give my Everything of Fear!” Jormungandr’s serpentine length coiled as the shadow-thing fed on his terror.","“I give my Everything of Fear!” Lilith’s demonic features became even more striking as fear’s absence revealed her true nature!","Each feeding was dramatic, terrible, and beautiful. The Seed of Inevitability grew darker with each Everything consumed, its obsidian surface beginning to show depths that hadn’t existed before.","|The Seed of Inevitability has consumed multiple Everythings of Fear|","|Everythings Fed: 7/75|","|Hunger Status: Partially Satisfied|","|Growth Beginning: Estimated 68 more Everythings required for full maturation|","An unprecedented event had occurred in the Early Veiled Shore!","Multiple beings had given away parts of their Everything, had sacrificed fundamental aspects of their existence for growth. The Shore itself seemed to recognize the significance, the golden sands humming with frequencies that hadn’t been heard before!","Noah watched his people transform, each one’s complexity and purity surging as fear’s absence created space for power to flow.","They stood straighter, moved with more certainty, looked at existence with eyes that no longer held terror’s shadow.","“You’ve all taken the first step toward true transcendence,” he told them, “Fear no longer chains you. Now, let’s see what you become without its weight.”","As he said this, Noah looked out to the Shore towards the dozens others.","He still needed more to give their Everythings as he would go slowly!","And the Seed of Inevitability, drinking deeply of the Everythings freely given, began to grow into something that had never existed before...a paradox born of intention rather than accident, shaped by will rather than chaos.","What would emerge when it finally matured?","Even Noah, fearless and doubtless as he was, couldn’t know for certain.","But that wasn’t doubt...it was anticipation!","A line of beings formed across the Early Veiled Shore, each one ready to surrender their Everything of Fear to the Seed of Inevitability.","The procession was both solemn and celebratory...a parade of transformation where limitation was exchanged for possibility!","As this glorious phenomenon unfolded, the massive figure of Yoshinami remained near Noah, her eight legs planted firmly in the golden sand. While watching being after being give away their fear, she turned her crimson eyes toward her Master.","“Master,” she said, her voice carrying the weight of ancient memory, “you show something that the Early Creature...the Architect of Sanctuaries who protected countless Land Lifeforms, Living Existences, and even Fold Dwellers, once said to us.”","...!","2/4"]},{"number":4038,"title":"Chapter 4038: Chapter 4037: Discipline! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4037: Discipline! III","“Oh?” Noah’s interest was immediate, his attention splitting between the ongoing transformation of his people and Yoshinami’s words.","Yoshinami blinked slowly, her crimson eyes unfocusing as she reached back through memory to times that most had forgotten existed.","“Back then, in the Early Veiled Shore of the Architect of Sanctuaries, she had been tending to Herbs, Plots, and observing Marine and Land Lifeforms. One day, I asked her why she was doing all of this every day...the same tasks, the same routines, with such dedication that it seemed almost obsessive.”","The spider-form being shifted slightly, her mandibles clicking in a pattern that suggested deep thought.","“The Architect of Sanctuaries had smiled and said that for a whole year, she had actually been allowed to follow and learn from THE Living Quantum inside an Early Veiled Shore.”","Noah’s eyebrows rose. THE Living Quantum...one of the original Living Existences, a being whose very nature challenged the concept of fixed position or state.","Yoshinami continued, her voice taking on the cadence of one reciting sacred text.","“THE Living Quantum had posed a question to the Architect: ‘What is the most successful tool or weapon in existence? What is the biggest predictor of success?'”","“The Architect, eager to impress, had guessed many things. ‘One’s purpose?’ she suggested. THE Living Quantum shook what served as its head. ‘One’s origin?’ Another denial. ‘Power? Intelligence? Connections? The quality of one’s Shore?'”","Yoshinami’s eyes gleamed with the memory of her former master’s recounting.","“All wrong, THE Living Quantum had said. Then it revealed the truth: The biggest predictor of complexity and power is actually...discipline.”","HUUM!","The word hung in the air with weight that transcended its simplicity.","“THE Living Quantum explained it thus: ‘Discipline is the ability to get up every day and do something one may not necessarily want to do, but does regardless because they see the future results. It is not motivation, which comes and goes like weather. It is not inspiration, which strikes randomly if at all. Discipline is simply doing something regardless of whether one wants to do it or not.'”","Yoshinami’s voice grew more animated as she continued the tale:","“‘Consider,’ THE Living Quantum had said, ‘how many Early Creatures have Early Veiled Shores but don’t utilize them to their full extent? They don’t tend to their plants and lifeforms every day. They don’t perform the daily tasks that would continue to elevate them. They plant a seed and expect it to grow without water. They capture a Marine Lifeform and expect it to thrive without care.'”","“‘Some have no discipline. They have power but no routine. They have potential but no practice. They have tools but no consistency in using them. And because they lack discipline, they have no future...only an eternal present where they remain exactly as they are.'”","...!","The weight of the lesson pressed against consciousness itself as Yoshinami continued.","“‘If you put an Early Creature against a weak Fold Dweller that has not even sensed mana, but that Fold Dweller has tremendous discipline...gets up every day, practices, learns, grows incrementally but consistently, then inevitably, that Fold Dweller has a bigger predictor of success. Given enough time, they will become more complex than that lazy Early Creature.'”","“‘Why? Because discipline compounds. Each day’s small effort adds to the previous day’s. Each routine completed makes the next easier. Each task finished builds the foundation for greater tasks. The disciplined being doesn’t need to feel like practicing...they practice. They don’t need to want to grow...they grow. They don’t need motivation to continue, they continue.'”","“‘Discipline,’ THE Living Quantum had concluded, ‘is everything in existence.'”","BOOM!","Yoshinami’s mandibles clicked in a pattern that suggested deep satisfaction with the memory.","“The Architect of Sanctuaries had smiled when she told me this story. She said, ‘That is why I try to build my discipline and do everything I can daily, regardless if I’m injured, regardless if I’m tired, regardless if I would rather be doing literally anything else. I wish to have... discipline. And through discipline, I will have everything else.'”","Yoshinami turned her crimson gaze fully on Noah, studying him with ancient perception.","“I have not been with you long, Master, but all the actions you have done so far express tremendous discipline. You tend your Shore constantly. You nurture your people consistently. You seek advancement not in bursts of inspiration but through methodical progress. Your potential... will exceed even Early Creatures, because you have what many of them lack...the discipline to use what you have, every day, without fail.”","Noah smiled at this, reaching out to stroke Yoshinami’s hairy leg with genuine affection.","The gesture should have been strange...a human petting an existential spider, but in the context of the Shore, it was simply master acknowledging servant, friend acknowledging friend.","“Yes,” he agreed, his voice carrying certainty that needed neither fear nor doubt to be absolute. “Discipline is everything. It is the difference between having power and becoming powerful. Between owning tools and mastering them. Between existing and transcending.”","His vision flickered as his consciousness shifted, focusing on another body in an entirely different location.","—","In the Doorway to the Loom, where twisted passages of paradox created paths between possibilities, Noah moved with Sigrid and Titano through corridors that challenged perception itself.","Behind them, Thessaly and Altheon traveled with notably different demeanors. Altheon still bore the red marks from his disciplining with the Goad...welts that seemed to exist outside normal healing, reminders written into his existence itself.","He looked toward Noah with immense fear that transcended the physical, the kind of terror that came from understanding one had been fundamentally corrected.","Thessaly felt stifled, her fairy form trembling with the weight of a dilemma that threatened to tear her loyalty in half. Should she report all of this to Duke Gwendolyn? The beating of Altheon? The casual transcendence Noah displayed? The impossible things she had witnessed?","But she felt...knew with certainty that made her wings quiver that the moment she did, he would find out. Whether from Duke Gwendolyn asking him about it directly or through some other means, Noah would know she had reported on him!","And when such a thing happened... would she not get disciplined by that stick?!","3/4"]},{"number":4039,"title":"Chapter 4039: Chapter 4038: Oh, Order! I","paragraphs":["The thought of the Stick touching her, of being forced to confront truths about herself that she preferred to keep buried, made her entire being recoil. She did not want that. She absolutely, categorically, fundamentally did not want that!","So she found herself in a very difficult position...loyalty to her Duke warring with self-preservation that transcended simple survival.","At this moment, Noah was leading the group with confidence, waving his stick with the air of someone taking a pleasant walk rather than traversing one of the most dangerous Doorways in existence.","After they had traveled for what felt like hours through passages that folded back on themselves, they finally heard it.","ROAAAAAR!","The bellow of an Inevitability echoed through the twisted space, and almost immediately, that single voice multiplied into five as the creature’s paradoxical nature asserted itself.","Titano’s massive form vibrated with excitement, his simple face lighting up with anticipation of another gift for his Brother.","Sigrid’s hand moved, her newly elevated power eager for expression as she sought to impose...Order!","But Noah raised his hand in a stopping gesture.","\"Hold on,\" he said with calm certainty. \"I want to test something.\"","Titano and Sigrid exchanged glances...or rather, Sigrid glanced at Titano while the giant simply blinked in confusion.","They both remembered what had happened the last time Noah had wanted to test something. He had used his stick to thoroughly educate an Inevitability about its own nature, beating existential horror into submission with what appeared to be ordinary wood.","Would he do the same thing now?","Noah proceeded ahead, but this time, he did something different. The Goad floated behind him, spinning slowly in the air with lazy majesty. He made no move to grasp it, no preparation for combat.","When the Inevitabilities surged out from the obsidian crimson flaming archways...five bodies that were one being that were five beings, they roared with malice that could unmake lesser minds.","Their tentacled forms writhed with paradoxes that hurt to perceive, their many eyes blazing with the hunger that defined their nature.","They looked at Noah and the others, and their charge began with inevitable certainty.","But then...","As they looked closer at Noah, their many eyes showed something unprecedented: confusion.","They slowed, their writhing becoming less aggressive, more... curious. Gradually, impossibly, they showed calmness!","Their eyes, those windows into paradox itself...began to smile.","Not metaphorically, but literally, the organs that served as eyes reformed into expressions of recognition and joy.","They neared Noah with their hulking masses, tentacles that existed in multiple states simultaneously reaching toward him with something that looked terrifyingly like affection.","And Noah...fearless, doubtless Noah, walked toward the writhing masses filled with paradoxical weavings of existence and lights of Inevitability, raised his hand, and...","Patted them.","Like someone petting a particularly large dog.","The gesture was so casual, so natural, that for a moment, nobody could process what they were seeing. Noah’s hand moved along tentacles that should have unmade him at the conceptual level, stroking surfaces that existed in states that predated the separation between is and isn’t.","The Inevitabilities responded with what could only be described as purring...if purring could be done by beings that challenged the nature of sound itself.","Behind him, the reactions were varied and extreme.","Altheon backed away in pure horror, his already traumatized mind unable to process this impossibility!","His feet stumbled over themselves as he tried to increase distance from this scene that challenged everything he thought he knew about existence.","Thessaly stumbled backward in shock that made her forget to fly, her fairy form actually hitting the flaming ground as her wings forgot their purpose!","Her tiny mouth opened and closed without sound, no words adequate for what she was witnessing.","Sigrid and Titano looked toward Noah with eyes and mouths opened wide enough to challenge physical possibility. Their jaws almost smashed all the way down to the floor!","Titano, despite his simple nature, understood that something unprecedented was happening. \"Brother... Brother is petting the Inevitability?!\"","Sigrid couldn’t even respond. The woman who had shattered her realm and rebuilt it, who had returned as THE Living Order, stood frozen by the simple impossibility of what she was seeing.","This wss an Inevitability. A horrifying, Paradoxical Inevitability. So why...","Noah continued petting the Inevitabilities as if this was the most natural thing in existence. One of the creature’s tentacles wrapped around his wrist...not aggressively, but with the same affection a cat might show when wanting more attention.","\"Good,\" he said to them, his voice carrying the tone one might use with pets that had performed well. \"Very good. Are you hungry?\"","The Inevitabilities’ response was immediate...all five bodies that were one nodded simultaneously, their paradoxical nature allowing them to express unified agreement while maintaining separation.","They could sense it. He had given his Everything of Fear and his Everything of Doubt to their kin. He was marked, fundamentally, as one who understood the exchange. One who didn’t fight their nature but worked with it.","To them, he wasn’t food. He was... friend might be too strong a word, but he was acknowledged. Accepted. Perhaps even respected.","Noah turned toward Sigrid and Titano, his hand still resting on the writhing mass of paradox that should have been trying to devour him. The casualness of the gesture made it even more surreal.","\"There are many ways to deal with an Inevitability,\" he said, his voice carrying the tone of a teacher revealing fundamental truth. \"If you understand its nature, you can get past it without fighting. An Inevitability seeks to devour Everything. When you come across one, simply give it... a small part of your Everything. A quality you do not want.\"","The silence that followed was absolute. Even the Inevitabilities seemed to pause their writhing to listen.","Sigrid and the others stood frozen in various states of shock. The concept was so simple, yet so profound that it challenged everything they thought they knew about these existential horrors!","Noah beckoned Sigrid over with a gesture that carried more weight than simple invitation. She moved forward without hesitation, her sterling eyes meeting his with trust.","\"Do you trust me?\" he asked, though the question seemed almost rhetorical.","She nodded without delay, without even the microsecond of consideration that doubt would have required.","\"Then for even more power,\" Noah continued, his voice carrying certainty that could reshape reality, \"you can choose to give part of your Everything. I have given away the Everything of my Fear and liberated my existence further. You can do the same.\"","He paused, ensuring she understood the magnitude of what he was suggesting.","\"Freely give your Everything of Fear.\"","Sigrid’s expression shifted through understanding to resolution. She opened her mouth to speak the words that would transform her existence...","Then her eyes blazed with sudden, brilliant realization.","\"No.\"","HUUM!","The word rang through the twisted corridor with more force than any shout could have achieved.","\"No, I will not give Everything of my Fear.\" Her voice carried conviction that transcended simple decision. \"Instead... I will give Everything of my Disorder.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4040,"title":"Chapter 4040: Chapter 4039: Oh, Order! II","paragraphs":["The proclamation hung in the air like a bell that had been struck in dimensions that shouldn’t exist.","Noah’s eyes blazed with brilliant approval and surprise. This choice...this magnificent, dangerous, perfect choice, showed understanding and risk that exceeded even his expectations!","The Inevitabilities responded instantly. Their masses of tentacles, which had been content to simply exist nearby, suddenly swept toward Sigrid with purpose that transcended hunger.","The tentacles passed through her body as if she were made of light, or they were made of shadow, or both were made of something else entirely. But what they pulled from her was visible to all...a murky purple-crimson mass that writhed and twisted, fighting even as it was extracted.","Disorder. Chaos. Entropy. Call it what you want!","She gave Everything of her Disorder, and the Inevitabilities consumed it with satisfaction that made reality itself sigh with relief.","The moment the last trace of Disorder left her being, Sigrid’s body erupted with blinding white light. Not harsh, not violent.","A light pure in ways that transcended the concept of purity itself!","Because Sigrid was the only Existence in the current folds carrying within her what remained of THE Living Order. She had not fully awakened to this nature, had been progressing toward it gradually, carefully.","But now...","When her existence was free of Disorder, when chaos no longer clouded her nature, when entropy no longer fought against her fundamental being...","What else could she become but truly, unfathomably, ordered?","The transformation...it was existential. Every particle of her being reorganized itself according to principles that predated principles. Her hair, already dark-white, became light itself woven into strands.","Her eyes transcended sterling to become mirrors of absolute truth. Her form didn’t change shape but changed meaning, becoming the embodiment of Order in ways that made everything around her seem slightly more organized just by proximity!","Waves of white light bathed everything, permeating across the Doorway to the Loom with force. The light didn’t stop at walls or boundaries...it simply was, and where it was, Order existed.","The eruption of pure Order burst outside the Doorway itself, flooding into the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds with authority that made Paradox itself step back in recognition.","Duke Gwendolyn’s second body, a Living Paradox that floated outside protectively, was suddenly blanketed by this white eruption of Order.","The resplendent, blinding rays of white Order continued to expand, painting over everything like an artist’s brush on reality’s canvas. The Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, spaces that existed because they shouldn’t, were suddenly faced with Order that said they should.","Duke Gwendolyn’s expression cycled through emotions at speeds that challenged causality....shock at the sudden explosion of power, joy at THE Living Order’s emergence, and horror at the implications of this light spreading out all around!","Any Living Paradox in the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds would be alarted and alarmed of this light!","Instantly, her eyes blazed as she began to send communications to other Dukes.","\"Whisker, Pyralis, Valen...we may need you and many others soon in the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds!\"","...!","Such a communication...left her weaving of Existence!","Back in the Doorway to the Loom, Noah floated grandly before the transforming Sigrid, his presence somehow both overwhelming and supportive. Before his eyes, prompts bloomed en masse.","|Through your actions and guidance, THE Living Order is emerging to Existence once more.|","|You have already bound THE Living Order. Through this binding, you have gained access to Living Order Authority.|","|You have successfully guided the return of one of THE Living Existences, THE Living Order. |","|+1,000,000% to all Living Order-related Weavings of Existence. |","|New Distinction Earned: THE Living Existential Guider|","|You are recognized as one who can guide Living Existences to their true nature|","|Primary Effects:|","|- All Living Existences under your guidance experience 1,000,000% increase in complexity and purity elevation rate|","|- Living Existences you mark have their potential ceiling doubled|","|- Grants ability to awaken slumbering natures in qualified beings|","|Secondary Effects:|","|- Marked Living Existences can be induced to evolve to Arch Living Existence state|","|- Your guidance prevents existential deviation during transformation|","|Tertiary Effects:|","|- Can freely grant Living Existence status to worthy Fold Dwellers by granting them Seeds of Existence and selecting which pathway they take.|","|Sigrid (THE Living Order) has been marked with your Guidance Seal|","|Her current state: 57% awakened to full Living Order nature|","|Estimated time to complete awakening under your guidance: +/- 7days|","|Without your guidance: 1,000 years|","...!","Noah read every single prompt!","And even more prompts continued to cascade!","|Due to guiding THE Living Order’s emergence, you have gained:|","|- Order’s Blessing: All actions have 50% chance to critically succeed|","|- Existential Clarity: Can see through all existential illusions at the level of Dukes or below|","|- The Right to Convene: Unknown Definition and Function at this moment, become a bit more complex please.|","|Special Synergy Detected: Goad + Living Existential Guider|","|The Rearing Stick now recognizes you as legitimate heir to education authority|","|Goad evolution potential unlocked: 1% → 2% accessibility|","...!","The prompts continued flowing, each one representing a fundamental shift in Noah’s position within existence itself.","Sigrid stood before him, her transformation still radiating waves of Order that made the chaotic Doorway actually form proper geometric patterns around her. When she spoke, her voice carried waves that made discord impossible in her presence.","\"I understand now,\" she said, each word placing itself perfectly in the flow of conversation. \"This...is what I was meant to be. Not just Order, but Order that chose to be ordered.\"","...!","The Inevitabilities that had consumed her Disorder made sounds of satisfaction. They had participated in something unprecedented!","Titano watched all of this with eyes wide with simple awe. \"Brother... Brother made the Young Miss shine!\"","Even Altheon and Thessaly, still pressed against the far wall in terror, couldn’t deny the magnitude of what they had witnessed.","The distinction of THE Living Existential Guider pulsed within Noah’s being, a title that would echo through all folds of existence.","The possibilities were infinite when it came to all this.","It was unprecedented.","It was impossible.","It was...glorious!"]},{"number":4041,"title":"Chapter 4041: Chapter 4040: Oh, Order! III","paragraphs":["After such a phenomenal change, Noah took a moment to reflect on the terrifying distinction he had received.","He also looked at Sigrid, studying her transformed state with perception that could now see deeper than before.","The more he observed, the more he noticed something concerning...her eyes were getting brighter and brighter, the silver-white light within them intensifying with each passing second. The illumination didn’t seem entirely... hers.","\"Sigrid.\"","He called out calmly, his voice cutting through whatever was building within her. The foreign white light of majesty in her eyes dimmed somewhat, like a tide pulling back from shore.","She blinked, focusing on him with what seemed like tremendous effort, as if anchoring herself to his presence.","\"Do not worry,\" she said, though her smile carried edges of something vast trying to express itself through limited form. \"I am still... me. But I am receiving an inflow of... information. Of possibilities. Of Order.\"","She spoke while trying to study her own existence, her hands moving as if she could grasp the changes occurring within her.","\"Come.\"","A single word from Noah, but his voice carried magnetic authority that transcended simple command. Sigrid floated toward him without conscious thought, drawn by forces that operated below awareness.","When she reached him, Noah took her in his arms with careful certainty, placing his forehead against hers in a gesture both intimate and analytical.","He closed his eyes and extended his perception, sensing both their existences simultaneously.","What he felt defied simple description!","Order coursed through them both like a white river of liquid law, drenching every cell, every meridian, every pathway.","His Towers of Osmont, those impossible structures that grew within his being, were being bathed in Order’s light. The flow wasn’t violent or overwhelming...it was inexorable, like gravity asserting itself, like mathematics proving theorems.","Everything was being touched by Order. Everything was being... corrected.","|Due to Order rising and flowing within your Existence, all established Living Existential Authorities have been effectively contained within your being.|","|This tremendous elevation has distinguished you beyond standard classification.|","|You are no longer merely an Early Creature.|","|You have been distinguished as: The Early Creature, Osmont|","HUUM!","The distinction hit him with a glorious weight.","Not \"an\" Early Creature...that was too common, too limited.","Not \"THE Creature\"...that was far too vast, a title belonging to something that transcended current understanding.","He was now The Early Creature, Osmont. Unique. Specified. Recognized by existence itself as something particular and irreplaceable.","|With your liberated Fear and Doubt alongside the elevation of your distinctions due to thr inclusion of Order:|","|All future completed Towers of Osmont at Stage 1 will grant 6.5 Million Complexity and Purity.|","|All 159 forged Towers that have crossed Stage 1 receive retroactive correction.|","|Retroactive bonus applied: +1,033,500,000 Complexity and Purity.|","...!","The number was staggering, but more prompts continued to cascade!","|All Towers of Osmont achieving Stage 2 now grant 25 Million Complexity and Purity|","|Retroactive correction for previously completed Stage 2 Towers applied|","|Additional bonus: +775,000,000 Complexity and Purity|","|Due to corrective changes from Order’s influence, Total gains of 1,808,500,000 Complexity and Purity have been granted.|","|Current Total Complexity: 4,576,473,891|","|Current Total Purity: 4,575,892,734|","Noah read through the prompts while simultaneously feeling the changes ripple through his existence.","His Towers of Osmont grew larger, more ancient, their crystalline structures taking on qualities that suggested they had always existed.","The Early Atlas of the Folds rumbled within him, its pathways becoming more complex as Order flowed through its structure, creating new routes to the Earliest Folds that hadn’t existed moments before.","But it was his Heart that experienced the most dramatic change.","|The Heart of The Early Creature, Osmont, is utilizing this burst of complexity to achieve completion of its Second Part|","|Oruvian Shardveil - The Arterial Convergence Core: COMPLETE|","|Blood production dramatically increased|","|10,000 Drops of Blood of The Early Creature, Osmont, have been generated simultaneously!|","|Current blood generation rate: 1,000 drops per hour.|","These were just his changes...significant, transformative, revolutionary!","But Sigrid, as THE Living Order, was undergoing something that transcended normal advancement entirely!","With their foreheads still connected, Noah could sense the explosion of growth within her.","His enhanced perception, now backed by the authority of THE Living Existential Guider, allowed him to tap into her existence and quantify the boons she was receiving.","What he saw made even his fearless, doubtless mind pause in awe.","|Sigrid, THE Living Order, is undergoing existential correction|","|Her being is aligning with what Order truly means, with her existence correcting to live upto its breadth.|","|Current rate of increase: 1,000,000,000 Complexity and Purity per second|","|Duration: Ongoing|","|Estimated completion: Unknown|","Oh.","Oh!!!","A billion in Complexity and Purity. Per second!","The mathematics were staggering. If this continued for just one hundred seconds, she would stand among Honored Living Existences in pure numerical terms.","But would it stop there? As she was becoming THE Living Order...not just representing it but embodying it, would the correction simply continue? Would it decrease? Accelerate?","And when it finally stopped, what power would she possess?","Because she wasn’t just any Living Existence now!","She carried the designation THE. Capitalized. Absolute! Fucking bolded!","Recognized by existence itself as not just an example of Order, but Order’s own consciousness given form.","THE Living Order.","In the Earliest Folds, Noah remembered how just witnessing THE Living Spirit had given a Fold Dweller immense honor, as most beings couldn’t even perceive such entities. They existed at frequencies of reality that transcended normal observation.","What did it mean for someone to become one of these esteemed beings? To not just wield their authority but to be their authority?","Noah’s eyes blazed with tyrannical interest as he maintained the connection, watching complexity flow into Sigrid at rates that would have destroyed any normal being.","But she wasn’t normal. She never had been. And now, guided by his distinction and freed from her Disorder, she was becoming what she had always been meant to be!","As he remained connected with her, he marveled how all of this stemmed from her losing her memory, crashing in the Veiled Sunfolds, and his connection with Kalysta bringing him to her.","\"Hmm...\""]},{"number":4042,"title":"Chapter 4042: Chapter 4041: Oh, Order! IV","paragraphs":["Thinking of this reminded him of the Primarchs and Masters of Existence of the Veiled Sunfolds. Entanglements and connections. He wouldn’t entirely forget them as there was much to do!","Noah refocused on Sigrid.","He wished he had the seconds to count everything as Sigrid’s complexity exploded beyond comprehension.","Each heartbeat that passed represented billions in advancement, each breath she took rewrote the glory of what power meant.","But even as a few seconds passed...three billion, four billion, five billion with each tick of time, his expression shifted from wonder to something heavier.","Without warning, he disconnected from Sigrid’s forehead, the loss of that intimate connection leaving a cold space between them. His gaze turned outward, piercing through the twisted corridors of the Doorway toward the distant exit that lay beyond the winding pathways.","Something was wrong.","Or rather, something was about to become very complicated.","---","In another region entirely, within the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds, deep in the protected depths of Aeternitas Concordia, space tore itself apart to admit Duke Gwendolyn’s form.","She materialized within the domed garden with such haste that reality hadn’t quite caught up, her edges still blurring as she solidified before Noah’s merchant body.","\"What happened in the Doorway?!\" Her usual composure had cracked, revealing genuine alarm beneath. \"The Young Miss awakened?! You all must make a quick exit...the white rays of Order have spread across the Doorway and towards the entirety of the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds!\"","...!","She moved closer, her stellar dark hair whipping with the force of her urgency.","\"Teleportation or warping across Folds isn’t possible from within a Doorway...you must exit first. Turn back as quickly as possible! My clone will try to keep the commotion around the Doorway covered as much as I can, but...\" Her expression grew heavier with each word. \"You must exit the Doorway!\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed with sharp understanding. Order had permeated across the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds as a consequence of Sigrid’s awakening.","Such a phenomenon wouldn’t go unnoticed. It couldn’t go unnoticed. Every Paradox in existence would feel Order reasserting itself, even if they did not fully know or understand what it was!","\"I’ve already alerted Duke Whisker and others...\"","Duke Gwendolyn’s words cut through his calculations, and Noah’s gaze turned sharp enough to cut dimensions.","His voice emerged with distaste that he didn’t bother to hide.","\"Of course you have.\" The words dripped with contempt. \"You truly like to talk and share absolutely everything, don’t you?\"","HUUM!","Duke Gwendolyn’s expression turned stern, her diplomatic mask reasserting itself with visible effort. \"For the sake of the Young Miss, yes. I will not play word games with you.\"","She straightened, authority radiating from her form. \"Take her out. Reinforcements will come toward the entrance of that doorway. What I know for certain is that soon it will be surrounded by Paradoxes, and I alone cannot ensure her safety against multiple Dukes of Paradox.\"","She paused, letting the weight of the situation settle before continuing.","\"With reinforcements, we shall take the Young Miss back here or to the Heart of Origin where the Kleos Council is. There, we can ensure her protection.\"","Noah gazed at Gwendolyn with eyes that had grown colder than the space between stars.","Internally, his mind rejected every word she spoke. Sigrid taken by them? Brought back here to be protected like some fragile treasure? Taken to the Heart of Origin to be displayed and discussed and controlled?","Like he would allow such a thing to happen.","His mind buzzed with possibilities, plans forming and reforming at speeds that would have been impossible if doubt still clouded his thoughts.","Duke Gwendolyn rose into the air, and in the next moment, reality acknowledged her authority as multiple tears in space unfolded within the domed garden.","Powerful Duke-level existences stepped through...Duke Whisker among them, his tiny form radiating power that belied his size.","Duke Pyralis emerged in flames that froze the air. Duke Valen tapped through with his cane, blind eyes seeing more than sight allowed!","Others followed, more than a dozen Dukes answering her call with speed that suggested prior preparation.","Duke Gwendolyn looked over the assembled power with satisfaction that she couldn’t quite hide. \"The mission is a dangerous one...venturing into the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds for the retrieval of something too precious to lose. I will act as the anchor to take you all directly there at thr shortest possible time.\"","Her existence erupted into white-gold light that formed a massive arched gateway. She stood at its center, her very being becoming the pathway that would allow traversal across countless distances between Folds. The gateway hummed with authority that made space itself bow!","Duke Whisker scurried through without delay, his small form disappearing into the light...but his gaze was cloudy. Before he disappeared, he turned towards Noah, and Noah stared back at him calmly as this little mouse of a Duke...seemed contemplative!","Others followed quickly, understanding that time was not their ally in this matter.","Noah watched this phenomenon with cold calculation, his own plans already forming in the spaces between their assumptions.","---","Meanwhile, in a place that existed perpendicular to normal reality, inside a certain mountain surrounded by Living Conceptual Authority.","In the Ethereal Summit of Unspoken Truths...Duke Valen’s other body stroked his beard thoughtfully.","\"Gwendolyn seems to have boldly taken the Vessel of THE Living Order into the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds,\" he announced to the gathering of beings whose power transcended normal classification.","\"She is now undergoing an awakening inside a Doorway.\"","His blind gaze fixed on Schrodinger specifically, seeing him in ways that eyes never could.","\"You will soon have visitors in your Transcendent Paradoxical Folds.\"","Schrodinger’s smile bloomed like a paradox...both genuine and calculating, warm and terrifying.","\"Oh, I was just about to begin tracking the origin of the white rays of light spreading across the Paradoxical Folds. Since you’re going there now, give me the exact coordinates. I could use this to our advantage before the Kleos Concordat.\"","The casual way he spoke of manipulating events that could reshape existence made even these ancient beings pause!"]},{"number":4043,"title":"Chapter 4043: Chapter 4042: Oh, Order! V","paragraphs":["Duke Valen nodded, beginning to transmit information to Schrodinger.","A terrifying Living Quantum, its form existing in seventeen states simultaneously...turned toward them with attention that made probability itself pay notice. \"What do you plan to do?\"","Schrodinger’s smile deepened, containing layers of meaning that contradicted themselves at every level. \"I plan to display a show of force... and then a show of mercy.\"","HUUM!","He stood, his beggar’s robes somehow managing to convey majesty despite their tattered state.","\"You see, sometimes after a display of overwhelming force...after showing what devastation could be unleashed, what horror could be made manifest, showing mercy instead makes others breathe such deep sighs of relief that they actually thank you. They thank you for not destroying them, for showing restraint, for being merciful. They forget that you shouldn’t have threatened them in the first place. They’re so grateful for what didn’t happen that they overlook what did.\"","His smile grew mysterious, containing paradoxes within paradoxes.","\"I plan to get... a thank you, that’s all.\"","The others on the mountain shook their heads...some with multiple heads, some with concepts that served as heads.","A Living Dimensional, whose voice existed in frequencies that created their own spaces, boomed out a warning.","\"Don’t make things too crazy before the Kleos Concordat.\"","Schrodinger smiled and said nothing, but his eyes were already seeing something else entirely.","Those eyes...windows into paradox itself, contained layers that defied observation.","One moment they were watching and observing others on this mountain, seeing them in the present, in the past, in futures that might never be. The next moment, they were observing the vast Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, seeing through space and time as if such divisions were merely suggestions.","His body in the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds had those same mysterious eyes.","His beggar-like figure stood surrounded by waves of obsidian-gold paradox that made reality uncertain about whether he existed or not.","He took a single step...just one, and space folded around the simplicity of the action.","BOOM!","His terrifying aura manifested near the entrance of a certain Doorway to the Loom with the casualness of someone who had always been there.","He observed calmly as Duke Gwendolyn’s Paradoxical body watched the blazing white rays of Order blooming from the Doorway with barely contained panic.","Her attention shifted, drawn by the weight of his presence, and her veiled face turned toward him.","Even through the veil, her expression was readable...shock transforming into something approaching horror as she recognized who had appeared.","Schrodinger looked at her veiled face with a smile that contained genuine amusement.","He laughed internally, knowing she must be wondering how he had arrived so quickly. How he had known exactly where to appear. How he had crossed distances that should have taken seconds or a minute in less than a heartbeat.","’Silly girl,’ he thought with something approaching fondness. ’You told me even without knowing. You... might as well have sent me an invitation.’","He shook his head at her naivety, finding it almost endearing that someone so astute could be so blind to certain realities.","It was a wonder that both she and he carried the distinction of Dukes. If all Dukes thought like her...linearly, obviously, predictably, how different the vast Folds would be. How fucked the Folds would be!","How much simpler. How much more boring.","He saw the blooming white-gold portal beside her, recognizing the pathway through which Duke Valen and the others would soon arrive.","Reinforcements rushing to protect THE Living Order, to secure her, to control her resurrection.","But he didn’t attack.","As he had told the others, he was here for a show of force... and then mercy.","He smiled and nodded toward Gwendolyn with the politeness of someone acknowledging a neighbor. Then, with the casual air of someone calling friends to dinner, he snapped his fingers.","BOOM!","Space trembled paradoxically, reality trying to decide whether it should break or bend. One terrifying aura of Duke-level Paradox began to appear, then another, then another, each arrival making existence less certain about its own rules.","Duke Elagabalus materialized first, his form a contradiction of youth and ancient age that hurt to perceive directly. Duke Diviticus emerged from nothing, her presence making the air itself question whether it existed.","More followed...two dozen Dukes of Paradox, each one a violation of what should be possible!","HUUM!","They looked toward the brilliant light of Order emanating from the Doorway with expressions of distaste, as if the brightness itself was offensive to their nature.","Because it was trying to make their existences... ordered. Trying to impose structure on beings that existed specifically because structure shouldn’t apply to them.","It was a violation. An insult. A challenge that could not go unanswered!","In addition to the Dukes, hundreds of Honored Living Paradoxes began to appear, their forms filling the space around the Doorway like an army of impossibilities. Each one radiated power that could unmake Prime Living Existences with casual thought.","In the distance, Duke Gwendolyn’s face...even veiled, visibly paled with shock and horror.","She stood alone before all this!","The reinforcements she had called for hadn’t even arrived yet, and already she was outnumbered twenty to one. The white-gold portal beside her seemed suddenly fragile, a candle flame before a hurricane of paradox.","Schrodinger stood at the center of it all, his beggar’s appearance doing nothing to diminish the terrible authority he commanded.","He had arranged this...all of it, with a few words and perfect timing.","Now came the interesting part.","The show of force was here.","Then would be the mercy that would make them grateful for what he didn’t do!","As he hummed to himself, the white gold portal beside Duke Gwendolyn shone brightly as one powerful Living Origin after another began to come out.","Each was at the level of a Duke, but as they appeared, all the expressions were changing one by one as what they were coming into was so horrendous, that one could easily mistake it for a trap.","All around, they were surrounded by living paradoxes- more than twice a dozen Dukes of Paradox as they were double their number!"]},{"number":4044,"title":"Chapter 4044: Chapter 4043: Force and Mercy! I","paragraphs":["Schrodinger observed with the patience of someone who had witnessed the birth and death of paradoxes themselves as one Duke of Living Origins after another emerged from the white-gold portal beside Duke Gwendolyn.","His smile grew with each arrival, and he looked upon their faces individually, studying them with the intensity of someone greeting long-lost friends...if those friends happened to be beings he might destroy with a thought.","His gaze was eerie in its calmness, each glance containing layers of paradoxical power that made reality uncertain about whether it should allow him to exist.","When the last Duke had emerged and they stood arrayed before the encirclement of Paradoxes with their faces heavy, the Paradoxes and Origins looked at each other!","Nobody spoke!","Duke Whisker had a chilly expression as he looked around the encirclement, eventually coming to stop his gaze on the entity that looked like a beggar...Schrodinger.","As if many knew who the seat of power here truly was.","In this tense face off, it felt stifling for even Dukes to voice out anything.","And yet, in such an environment, a begger stepped forward as behind him, many paradoxes pulsed!","Schrodinger floated forward calmly as if he were taking a stroll as he...began to speak.","\"When I was a boy...\" His voice carried waves of terrific power.","He floated upward slightly, his tattered robes billowing despite the absence of wind. \"A tiny little paradox that barely knew anything about existence or my place within it, I found myself running from some of the first Mutated Inevitabilities that had ever risen.\"","He moved as he spoke, drifting through the air with movements that seemed random yet purposeful.","\"I was tired. Worn to the very edge of dissolution. My paradoxical nature was unraveling from the strain of maintaining coherence while fleeing.\" He raised one hand casually, and every Paradox behind him froze in perfect stillness, understanding the gesture as absolute command to remain motionless while he alone moved forward!","\"In my desperation, I came across a garden. Not just any garden, but the garden of a particularly terrifying Fold Dweller. Now, you might wonder...how could a Fold Dweller be terrifying to a Living Paradox?\" He chuckled, the sound containing contradictions. \"This one was different. His garden existed in ways that made even paradox feel like nothing...\"","HUUM!","Schrodinger drifted closer to Duke Gwendolyn and the others, his approach casual, unthreatening...a simple beggar floating through space. Yet each inch he drew nearer made the Living Origins tense further, his carefree demeanor somehow more menacing than any display of power.","\"I looked toward this Fold Dweller with desperation that transcended pride. I asked...begged really, whether I could enter his garden for protection against the Mutated Inevitabilities.\" He paused, letting the image settle. \"The Fold Dweller considered me for a moment that lasted eternity and no time at all. Then he nodded.\"","His voice grew warmer, as if recalling a fond memory.","\"I entered the periphery of his garden, and I was actually safe. Shockingly, miraculously, the Inevitabilities could not pass through into that space. They raged at the borders, they threw themselves against barriers they couldn’t perceive, but they could not enter. It was... marvelous.\"","Schrodinger’s expression shifted, growing more complex.","\"Seconds later...and I mean this literally, mere seconds, ten Living Existences came from another direction. They too were being chased by Mutated Inevitabilities, their forms showing the strain of extended flight.\" He gestured expansively. \"The moment they saw the garden, saw my figure and the Fold Dweller within it, they were ecstatic. Without pause, without thought, without asking, they rushed in for protection.\"","He stopped directly in front of the entrance to the Doorway and Duke Gwendolyn’s portal, positioning himself alone before all these Living Origins!","\"Once again, the Inevitabilities could not enter. These Living Existences...Origin, Temporal, even a young Concept among them...breathed such deep sighs of relief. They looked toward the Fold Dweller to thank him for his sanctuary, for his protection, for saving their existences.\"","Schrodinger’s smile grew sharp.","\"Yet in the next moment, the Fold Dweller took a common farming tool...nothing special, just a hoe he used for tending his plants, and swatted down.\" He made a casual gesture, as if brushing away dust.","\"The weavings of existence of those Living Existences were decimated instantly. All of them. Dead before they could process what was happening.\"","...!","The silence that followed was absolute. Even the white rays of Order streaming from the Doorway seemed to dim slightly.","\"The Fold Dweller looked at all of this as calmly as if he hadn’t done anything more significant than pulling weeds. And I, out of an overabundance of curiosity that even then defined my nature, asked him- Why? Why did you kill those Living Existences and not me?\"","Schrodinger’s eyes...those windows into paradox, fixed on Duke Gwendolyn with intensity that made her paradoxical body shiver despite its nature.","\"The Fold Dweller turned to me with eyes that had seen the birth of concepts themselves. He said, ’This is my home. You asked for permission to enter. You are a guest.’ He gestured to the corpses that were already being absorbed by his garden’s soil. ’Those who entered afterward were merely intruders. It matters not who they are or what they are...all those intruding in my home have to die.’\"","The beggar-like figure completed his circuit, now floating directly before the entrance to the Doorway, his position both casual and absolutely deliberate.","\"A simple distinction. Guest or intruder. Permission or presumption. The difference between salvation and annihilation.\"","He looked at Duke Gwendolyn and the others, his gaze lingering on each face with the weight of evaluation. When his eyes found Duke Valen among them, his smile grew genuinely warm.","\"All Living Existences will soon be meeting in the Kleos Concordat. The Living Paradoxes have no problems at all inviting other Living Existences as guests into our Paradoxical Folds.\" His voice carried reasonable hospitality. \"But you all did not come here as guests. You did not even ask for permission.\"","The temperature...if such a thing existed in the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, seemed to drop.","\"You are here, currently, as intruders.\" He tilted his head with curiosity that contained threat. \"What shall be done? Should we follow the guidance of that Fold Dweller and his treatment of guests versus intruders?\"","...!"]},{"number":4045,"title":"Chapter 4045: Chapter 4044: Force and Mercy! II","paragraphs":["The weight of his words pressed against consciousness itself.","The assembled Living Origins stood frozen, most only able to meet his gaze!","The army of Paradoxes behind him remained perfectly still, awaiting a single gesture that would transform this confrontation into catastrophe.","Into the suffocating silence, a small figure stepped forward.","Duke Whisker emerged from among the Living Origins, his tiny mouse form radiating dignity that transcended size.","His stellar eyes met Schrodinger’s paradoxical gaze without flinching, and when he spoke, his voice carried the weight of eons of accumulated wisdom.","\"It seems that we are at fault for intruding.\" The admission was delivered without shame or fear, simply acknowledging reality.","\"We will simply take our people and leave.\"","Schrodinger’s smile bloomed with genuine pleasure at the response. \"Your people?\" He gestured toward the assembled Dukes. \"I see you all here... but could you mean the ones inside this Doorway? The ones among whom is someone exuding all these rays of light that paint my Folds with...Order? Is it Order? It cannot possibly be Order, right?\"","HUUM!","Immense silence settled over the gathering.","Schrodinger adopted an obviously contemplative expression, as if wrestling with a difficult decision.","Finally, he sighed with theatrical weariness.","\"Hey, aren’t we all striving through existence together?\" His tone shifted to something almost friendly. \"How about this, we won’t make any... moves. Your people can come out and leave freely. For the sake of the coming Kleos Concordat, The Living Paradoxes will let this indiscretion slide.\"","...!","He spread his hands in a gesture of magnanimity.","\"We are all on the same side after all, right?\" His gaze shifted to fix directly on Duke Gwendolyn’s paradoxical body. \"You all even have a Living Paradox on your side, which I haven’t even focused on at this time.\"","Duke Whisker’s expression remained neutral, but others among the Living Origins showed visible discomfort at this observation.","The implications were clear...Schrodinger could have made this about betrayal, about a Paradox siding with Origins. He was choosing not to.","In the heavy atmosphere that followed, in that prolonged silence where possibility and probability held their breath, the Living Origin body of Duke Gwendolyn stepped forward.","Her usually controlled features showed something that might have been somberness mixed with understanding as she looked toward Schrodinger.","\"Thank you.\"","Two words.","Thank you!","Simple. Direct. Exactly what he had wanted.","He was given his thank you!","Schrodinger nodded lightly, the gesture containing satisfaction that transcended simple pleasure.","His attention turned toward the Doorway, and following his lead, every eye...stellar, paradoxical, conceptual...fixed on that entrance.","The white rays of Order still streamed forth, painting large swaths of the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds with light that made Paradox uncomfortable. Whatever was causing that phenomenon would have to emerge soon.","Ten seconds passed.","Twenty seconds passed in absolute silence! No one moved. No one spoke. The tension grew with each heartbeat that some of them still possessed.","Then...","WAP!","Figures emerged from the Doorway.","Two figures. Only two.","The fairy form of Thessaly came first, her wings trembling as she took in the scene before her. Behind her, Altheon emerged with the careful movements of someone expecting attack from any direction.","Both paled to shades that shouldn’t have been possible for their forms as they observed the encirclement of Paradoxes, the gathered Dukes of Origin, the weight of attention focused on them.","Duke Gwendolyn waited one second. Two. Her expression shifted through confusion to alarm as she fought to maintain her composure.","\"Where is the Young Miss?!\"","The question cracked through the silence like breaking crystal. Yes, where was she? Where was THE Living Order whose awakening had painted the Folds with white light? Where was the being they had all come to secure?","Altheon and Thessaly stood dazed, still processing the scene before them. It was Altheon who finally managed to speak, his words emerging hesitant and confused as he looked at the encirclement of Paradoxes.","\"She... left with... him.\"","Him.","Him!","The single word landed among the gathering with the weight of impossibility. Every being present analyzed it and its sentance differently, parsed its implications through their own understanding.","Who was ’him’?","How had they left? What did leaving even mean in this context?","The implications were staggering. They had left...suggesting they hadn’t needed to exit the Doorway to traverse across existence.","But such a thing was impossible. It was well-known, established as fundamental law, that nothing could cross or teleport across existence while within Doorways to the Loom.","Thessaly’s mental message then echoed out and reached only the Dukes of Living Origins, her hesitation palpable even in thought: \"The Young Miss disappeared with... him. As if they had teleported or traversed into different Folds entirely.\"","...!","The impossibility had supposedly occurred.","Into the shocked silence, Schrodinger’s voice rang out with amusement that contained layers of meaning.","\"Haha, did you all lose someone important as we talked here? That must not feel so good.\" He drifted higher, looking down at them with sympathy. \"Traversal while within a Doorway to the Loom? That should be an impossibility, and yet it has seemingly occurred...\"","His expression grew helpful, concerned.","\"Origin friends, do you need help looking through this Doorway to check where this... Young Miss you mention might be? Us Paradoxes should be of great help in such a search.\"","...!","Origin friends? Origin friends?! What the fuck was this beggar even saying now?!","Duke Gwendolyn and others turned ashen at the offer..help from Paradoxes in finding THE Living Order would come with prices they couldn’t afford to pay.","Duke Whisker’s response was immediate and commanding, his tiny paw waving to the other Dukes with authority that transcended his size.","\"We will be okay without your help.\"","Even as he spoke, Duke Gwendolyn and several other Dukes moved toward Thessaly and Altheon, preparing to enter the Doorway themselves to ascertain what had actually occurred.","They grabbed the two witnesses with movements that suggested interrogation would begin the moment they were out of sight!","Schrodinger watched this scene with the satisfaction of someone whose plan had executed perfectly. His gaze lingered on Duke Whisker, who had stayed back with a few others to maintain the pretense of dignity in retreat.","The beggar-like Paradox waved his hands harmlessly, as if shooing away concerns, and floated backward toward the encirclement of Living Paradoxes.","He came to rest before all the Dukes of Paradox, their forms creating a wall of impossibility that would remain as long as necessary. They would simply observe the Living Origins with menacing patience, waiting to see what panic might drive them to do.","After all, Schrodinger had gotten his thank you.","The show of force had been displayed. The mercy had been granted.","And now THE Living Order was missing, vanished through impossible means, leaving only questions and the taste of failure in the mouths of those who had come to claim her!"]},{"number":4046,"title":"Chapter 4046: Chapter 4045: Variation! I","paragraphs":["Limitations are peculiar things. They exist not as universal truths but as boundaries defined by perspective, capability, and understanding.","What one being calls impossible, another accomplishes with a casual gesture. What requires eons of preparation for some happens in heartbeats for others!","The wall that stops a child is merely a step for an adult. The ocean that drowns a man is home to a fish. The void that kills most beings is where others are born.","It was known and established...written into the fundamental understanding of existence itself, that one could not teleport in or out of the Doorways to the Loom.","This wasn’t merely difficult or dangerous; it was deemed impossible. The Doorways existed in states that rejected standard spatial manipulation, their paradoxical nature creating barriers that even Dukes couldn’t breach through normal means.","Everyone knew this. Everyone accepted this.","But Noah had never been everyone.","---","Seconds ago, while Duke Gwendolyn’s panic painted the air with urgency, while she urged him to make a quick exit so they could flee properly once outside the Doorway, Noah had done something simpler.","He hadn’t asked whether it was possible. He hadn’t considered the established limitations.","He had simply connected to his Early Veiled Shore.","The connection flowed through him like water remembering its source, natural and inevitable.","His brilliant energy...containing eleven Living Existential Authorities that shouldn’t coexist within a single being, pulsed with quiet certainty. The terrifying Kleos Glyph on his forehead, The Creature’s First Lesson, blazed with light that made reality pay attention.","He looked towards Sigrid and Titan!","\"Are you ready to visit my home?\" he had asked calmly, as if inviting them for tea rather than attempting the impossible.","Titano’s massive head had nodded with his characteristic blank expression, processing the question at his own pace.","Sigrid, still radiating the overwhelming presence of newly awakened Order, had simply nodded, her trust in him absolute despite not understanding what he intended.","Brilliant light had erupted around them...not harsh or violent, but encompassing, like being wrapped in starlight.","The illumination contained within it the authority of someone who didn’t just bend rules. He wrote new ones! Noah, Sigrid, and Titano were enveloped in radiance that made the Doorway’s paradoxical nature irrelevant.","Then they were simply... gone.","He had left Thessaly and Altheon behind without a second thought. Their baggage wasn’t something he needed to carry!","Let them explain to Duke Gwendolyn how the impossible had occurred. Let them wrestle with questions that had answers they couldn’t comprehend!","The transition was seamless, like stepping from one room to another when both rooms happened to be separated by impossible distances and fundamental barriers.","Noah, Sigrid, and Titano materialized on the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore, the light of this impossible space welcoming them with warmth that transcended temperature!","The body of Noah that had traveled with them, one of his many simultaneous existences...became a streak of light that merged with his primary form.","He rose from where he had been seated on the sands, his upper body bare, muscles glistening with the particular sheen that came from existing at frequencies reality barely acknowledged.","His lower body was covered in loose obsidian-gold pants that seemed to be woven from twilight itself.","The Goad rested beside him, that simple stick that could educate existence itself about its own nature!","Sigrid looked at him, then at their surroundings, her newly enhanced perception taking in details that should have been impossible to process!","Her eyes widened with recognition.","\"Don’t tell me this... is an Early Veiled Shore?!\"","The words emerged with the weight of someone recognizing they stood in a place that shouldn’t exist, that most beings would never even know could exist!","Early Veiled Shores were myth to most, legend to some, and death to nearly all who tried to reach them without proper understanding.","Noah walked up to them with confidence, his bare feet leaving perfect impressions in sand that remembered every step ever taken upon it.","\"The one and only.\"","HUUM!","Titano’s reaction was more visceral. The giant’s head swiveled in all directions, trying to process everything at once.","He leaned down to touch the sand, letting the golden grains run through his massive fingers.","His eyes tracked to the crystalline waters that lapped at shores that extended into infinity!","The Aquarium with its impossible architecture. The trees bearing fruits that could elevate existence itself.","Then he saw them...the cluster of glass Woks that Noah had given him before, each one still filled with the soup of vibrant Marine Lifeforms. They sat arranged neatly near one of the trees!","Titano looked at all of this, his gaze moving back and forth between Noah and the wonders around them. His mouth opened and closed repeatedly, but words wouldn’t form!","He pointed at everything with an expression of amazement and shock that transcended his simple nature.","For once, the giant who could wrestle Inevitabilities into submission was completely speechless.","Noah smiled and patted his massive back, the gesture requiring him to reach up considerably.","\"Come on, Brother. Let me introduce you to some people.\"","Noah kept things very straightforward and simple!","They moved toward the center of the Shore, where a gathering had naturally formed.","Amelia Osmont stood with a particular dignity. Henry was beside her, his complexity still surging from giving away his Everything of Fear.","The Emperor Penguin waddled about with self-importance that seemed comical until one remembered he had helped build an Abode.","Liora, Kazuhiko, Erikson, and others had assembled or were already nearby.","Noah brought the gigantic Titano over first, his massive form casting shadows that existed in multiple dimensions.","\"Mother,\" Noah said with warmth, \"this is Titano, an adopted brother I’ve taken on.\"","...!","Titano, showing surprising grace for his size, bent down and extended one massive finger for Amelia to shake.","His simple mind was buzzing as even this simple interaction...being called a Brother...was something he never had during all the years with Duke Gwendolyn.","Honored Living Existences and lesser ones feared him.","Dukes looked at him like a chess piece. Nobody...had called him Brother!","Nobody had done what his brother was doing for him now!","So he put his massive finger out while making sure in his sinple thoughts that he would not cry.","Titano did not cry!","Amelia Osmont took his massive finge with the calm acceptance of someone who had long ago stopped being surprised by her son’s choices in companions.","But her eyes weren’t on the giant. They had fixed on Sigrid, who stood slightly behind, still processing everything she was witnessing.","Amelia’s expression shifted to something knowing, something that mothers throughout existence would recognize.","\"Did you already find another daughter-in-law for me? How are you managing to do this on top of everything else?\" she asked with a smile that contained layers of amusement. \"Which one is this?\"","WAA!"]},{"number":4047,"title":"Chapter 4047: Chapter 4046: Variation! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4046: Variation! II","The question landed in the space between them as it carried devastating implications!","Sigrid’s mouth opened in shock, her gaze snapping to Noah with intensity that could have reorganized matter.","Another daughter-in-law? The word ‘another’ echoed in her mind. How many women did he have? Was she the second? The third? More?","...!","In her dazed state, wrestling with revelations about Noah’s romantic situation while simultaneously processing that she stood in an Early Veiled Shore, Sigrid forgot to respond.","The silence stretched until Titano, with his characteristic simplicity, found his voice.","“Mother of Brother, this is Brother’s baddie, Sigrid, THE Living Order!”","...!","The words emerged with such innocent certainty that their impact took a moment to fully register.","The Emperor Penguin raised his beak in shock.","Others could feel the terrifting Complexity surging within Sigrid as they did not even know what to think!","Brother’s baddie.","THE Living Order, one of the foundational forces of existence, a being whose return had just caused panic across a Transcendent Folds...referred to as someone’s ‘baddie’.","Any Living Origins, especially Duke Gwendolyn, would have been dismayed beyond recovery if they had heard such casual disrespect.","They would have blown their existences apart rather than accept such diminishment of what THE Living Order represented!","Amelia Osmont simply smiled wider.","“Is that right?”","The acceptance in those three words was absolute. If her son had somehow acquired THE Living Order as a companion, even if she did not fully know what that meant, then that was simply another day in her son’s weavings of Existence.","Sigrid’s mind snapped back to focus at this casual acceptance of the impossible.","Her eyes flashed sharply as she looked at Noah, her expression promising a conversation later that would involve many questions and possibly some educational violence.","He had a stick to educate, she had hands!","But for now, she moved forward with the grace that Order itself possessed. She took Amelia’s hands with genuine respect, her expression softening as she spoke a single word that would reshape reality around them.","“Mother.”","...!","Mother.","Simple.","A single word that held many meanings and complexities!","A single word to change many things.","BOOM!","The word had barely left her lips when existence itself responded. Swirls of Living Order Authority erupted around Amelia Osmont’s form like reality recognizing something that should have always been true.","Prompts cascaded before Noah’s vision right after!","|The Mother of The Early Creature, Osmont, has been distinguished by THE Living Order|","|New Distinction Granted: Primordial Matriarch of Order’s Chosen|","|Amelia Osmont’s existence is undergoing fundamental correction|","|As the mother of the one who guides Living Existences and is chosen by Order itself, her being must slowly reflect this status|","|Complexity increasing: +100,000,000 per second for next 60 seconds. Slow gradual increase thereafter.|","|Purity increasing: +100,000,000 per second for next 60 seconds. Slow gradual increase thereafter.|","|Permanent passive increase: All future gains multiplied by 1000%|","|Authority granted: Can bless others with Order’s Favor (once per day)|","Noah watched this transformation with a smile that contained satisfaction beyond simple happiness.","His mother, who had supported him through impossibility itself, was finally receiving rewards that matched her significance.","“Okay,” he said, his perception expanding to encompass the entire Shore, “let’s see the rest.”","...!","He asked to see the rest!","Because he could sense it...the Early Veiled Shore itself was responding to Sigrid’s presence.","From the moment THE Living Order had arrived, the space had been buzzing with potential that demanded expression. Now it exploded with glorious incandescence and torrents of information.","White light of Order bathed the golden sands, transforming them into something that transcended simple beach. Each grain reorganized itself according to principles that predated chaos!","|Fundamental Shore Evolution Ongoing. Your Shore is deviating from the normal growth of established Early Veiled Shores|","|All Early Veiled Shores originated from THE Creature and THE Living Existences|","|At moment of initial design, THE Living Order’s authority was absent|","|Order was not present when Early Veiled Shores were first forged|","|Order has bloomed inside an Early Veiled Shore for the first time|","|Unfathomable changes with incalculable effects are unfolding!|","|Due to Order’s inclusion, Shore features are being optimized and expanded|","|New Feature Unlocked: The Primordial Early Excavation Depths- Dimensional mines extending into collapsed fragments of the Earliest Folds|","|Access Requirement: Shore inhabitant with 100+ Million Complexity|","|Contents include remnants from the Earliest Folds and Desiccated Sleeping Shores|","|Available Resources:|","|Ore of Early Resonance|","– A Unique ore from the Earliest Folds","– Uses: Upgrading Shore constructs (Abode, Aquarium, etc.)","– Can be refined into Complexity Ingots (1 ingot = 100M CQ/PQ when consumed)","|Crystalized Temporal Fragments|","– Solidified time from before time was separated from space","– Uses: Accelerate plant maturation (1 fragment = 100 years instantly)","– Can be powdered and added to soil for permanent growth acceleration","|Memory Stones|","– Crystallized memories of deceased Early Creatures","– Uses: Gain random techniques, memories, understanding from the Earliest Folds","– Risk: 10% chance of temporary memory displacement","|Essence Gems|","– Pure crystallized complexity and purity","– Immediate consumption: +1 Billion CQ/PQ per gem","– Can be dissolved in Shore waters to call in Eminent and Kleos Early Living Marine Lifeforms","|Paradox Minerals|","– Ore that exists and doesn’t exist simultaneously","– Uses: Create items that function beyond normal limitations","– Can forge tools that work in Doorways to the Loom","|Structural Marrow|","– The bones of reality from before reality had bones","– Uses: Enhance Shore defenses to near-absolute levels","– Can be ground into powder that permanently increases toughness","...!","Noahs eyes blazed at the overload of prompts as there was so much!","And each one was a work of wonder as before one could even fully focus on them, more came!","|Mining Mechanics within the Primordial Early Excavation Depths:|","– Infinite depth with increasing rewards per level","– Enemies: Remnant Lifeforms from collapsed Shores(May be Living, may be Dead, or in between)","– Environmental hazards that test existence itself","– Party system: Up to 5 beings can mine together for a greater chance of locating ores, crystals...","– Chance to find complete Early Creature artifacts","|Current Mine Levels Available: 1-100|","|Deeper levels unlock as Shore continues evolving|","...!","4/5"]},{"number":4048,"title":"Chapter 4048: Chapter 4047: Losses! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4047: Losses! I","Noah read through the extensive information with eyes that grew brighter with each detail.","This feature was an entire avenue of advancement, a way to gather resources that shouldn’t exist anymore!","Off to the side of the Shore, the space began to ripple and tear with purpose, like reality making room for something that needed to exist.","A massive arched entrance emerged from the sand, carved from stone that predated the concept of stone itself.","The archway was embedded with glimmering stones that cast light in colors of utter glory, each one a fragment from the Earliest Folds.","The entrance to the Primordial Early Excavation Depths stood there as if it had always existed, as if the Shore had simply been waiting for Order to arrive before revealing this secret.","Noah looked at Sigrid with an expression that mixed affection with amazement.","She was like a good luck charm of impossible proportions...her mere presence causing explosions of advancement and opportunity.","“Brother!” Titano’s voice boomed with excitement that could have powered small civilizations. “Brother’s home is... is... BROTHER’S HOME IS AMAZING!”","HUUM!","The giant had finally found his full faculty of words, and they emerged with the pure enthusiasm of someone who had discovered a glorious place exists and he had been invited to stay.","Around them, the inhabitants of the Shore were beginning to notice the new feature.","Emperor Penguin was already waddling toward the mine entrance with the certainty of someone who intended to be first. Kazuhiko’s hand was on his sword.","The Queen of Matter had her body buzzing like a beverage that would soon explode as she tried her best not to ruin the moment by screaming out!","But Noah’s attention remained on Sigrid, who was still processing everything...the Shore, its inhabitants, becoming his mother’s daughter-in-law through a single word, and now the transformation of the entire space through her mere presence.","“Welcome home,” he said to her, and meant it in ways that transcended the simple meaning of the words.","Because this wasn’t just a common shore anymore.","With Order’s presence, with Sigrid’s arrival, it had become something greater. Something that could grow beyond what THE Creature had originally envisioned.","The Early Veiled Shore had evolved, and with it, the possibilities for what Noah could become expanded toward infinity.","Noah absorbed all the wonders occurring around him, his consciousness expanding to process information.","|Due to Order’s inclusion, the Early Veiled Shore will undergo continuous transformation|","|Process will continue until reaching quantifiable conclusion for optimal advancement path|","|Estimated time to stabilization: 5-10 days|","|Unexpected evolutions possible during transition period|","He reflected on this calmly, his mind already calculating implications and possibilities. The timing was fortuitous...forced, perhaps, by circumstance, but fortuitous nonetheless.","“The Paradoxes and Origins should be in a standoff right about now,” he said, “I don’t see the Paradoxes making any grand moves before the Kleos Concordat.”","He gazed across his Shore, watching his people look towards the new mine entrance with varying degrees of excitement and caution.","“We can track our progression here and relax while we wait for the dust to settle.”","Sigrid nodded respectfully towards Amelia Osmont, though her expression carried concern as she turned. “Duke Gwendolyn and the others won’t give you too much trouble?”","The question carried layers...concern for his safety, understanding of existence, and awareness that her awakening had disrupted carefully maintained balances.","Noah’s smile held confidence that transcended arrogance. “I can handle it.”","WAA!","The simple statement carried such certainty that Sigrid nodded without hesitation. She believed him completely!","“The Early Veiled Shore has much to be done within it,” Noah continued, his gaze sweeping across his domain. “The plants are maturing, only waiting is required now. Marine Lifeforms are being caught continuously in the Aquarium. And to pass time while the Living Origins and Paradoxes scatter until the Kleos Concordat...”","He gestured toward the newly formed mine entrance as the Emperor Penguin was already arguing with Kazuhiko about who would enter first...when neither had met the Complexity requirement!","“The new feature of mining seems to be a good one to explore.”","His gaze returned to Sigrid, studying her with intensity that saw beyond surface. “We also have to see just how far your complexity will continue to rise. With me guiding you, your full awakening as THE Living Order should take... less than seven days.”","The seven days versus the one thousand years it would have taken without his guidance. The power of THE Living Existential Guider made manifest in simple mathematics!","Sigrid’s response bypassed words entirely. She moved forward with grace that made Order itself pay attention, ignoring the gathered crowd of Noah’s people, and wrapped her arms around him in an embrace.","Her head rested against his chest, and through that contact, she felt the immense waves of complexity swirling within him...power that should have been chaotic but wasn’t.","There was order to his being, structure that existed not through rigid law but through conscious choice. It didn’t fight her raging Order...it complemented it, completed it, made her transformation feel less like violent change and more like coming home.","The golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore gleamed beneath the glorious light. Cerulean stellar waves of Early Sacred Waters lapped at shores that extended into infinity, their rhythm matching the heartbeat of existence itself.","On this day, THE Living Order had arrived in the Early Veiled Shore of The Early Creature, Osmont.","What this would become remained unwritten, but the potential made reality itself lean forward in anticipation!","—","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, time had passed with the weight of failure pressing against consciousness.","Duke Gwendolyn and the others emerged from the Doorway with expressions that had moved past shock into something deeper...the ashen pallor of those who had confirmed the impossible.","The Young Miss, along with the one who had taken her and Titano, were truly gone. Not hidden, not displaced, but absent in ways that violated understanding.","Duke Whisker needed only to meet Duke Gwendolyn’s eyes to understand the completeness of their failure. His tiny features arranged themselves into a frown that carried the weight of eons.","Schrodinger observed all of this with his beggar’s smile, floating casually as if witnessing a mildly interesting play.","“You all seem to be experiencing a great loss,” he said with sympathy that contained too many layers to be genuine. “You know, I have another story that deals with Losses-”","“While we would love to listen to a story,” Duke Gwendolyn interrupted, her composure cracking under urgency, “we have to go-...!”","She never finished the sentence.","BOOM!","The smile vanished from Schrodinger’s face with speed that made its previous presence seem like illusion.","...!","In the next moment, Existence itself began to shake!","Existential Trembling.","Oh!","Trembling!","The pressure that erupted from the beggar-like Duke transcended physical force or energetic overwhelming.","This was authority at its most glorious- the weight of something that existed so thoroughly that reality had to acknowledge it or break!","Altheon and Thessaly didn’t even have time to scream.","Their Origins buzzed with frequencies that shouldn’t exist, and consciousness fled rather than endure what was happening!","They slumped into unconsciousness with the mercy of minds protecting themselves from truths too large to process!","5/5 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":4049,"title":"Chapter 4049: Chapter 4048: Losses! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4048: Losses! II","Even the Dukes, beings who stood at pinnacles of their respective hierarchies...turned ashen.","Their bodies shook with the simple struggle to maintain coherence against pressure that suggested they might be less real than what pressed against them!","Only Duke Whisker remained still, though the effort required was visible in how his stellar eyes blazed brighter, how his tiny form seemed to grow denser to resist dissolution.","Duke Gwendolyn’s paradoxical body buzzed and trembled, caught between states as if unable to decide whether existing was worth the effort required.","The beggar-looking Schrodinger had maintained his smile through everything...through threats, through confrontation, through games of power and position.","But when he had wanted to tell a story and been interrupted, denied his simple pleasure of narrative, the atmosphere transformed completely!","He alone, facing a dozen Dukes of Origins, caused all nearby Existence to tremble. Everyone felt stifled, compressed, made aware of their own insignificance.","Duke Whisker, with effort that made space crack around him, floated forward to position himself before the other Origins. His voice emerged with grim calmness that acknowledged the precipice they balanced upon.","“We should have time for another story before we leave.”","The statement wasn’t a suggestion.","Schrodinger held his cold gaze for several more seconds, letting them marinate in the understanding of what they had almost provoked.","Then, as suddenly as it had arrived, the pressure vanished. His harmless beggar appearance returned, complete with gentle smile, as if the Existential Trembling had been nothing more than shared hallucination.","“Well then,” he said pleasantly, “let me tell you about Loss.”","He settled into the air as if it were a comfortable chair, his posture suggesting he had all the time that had ever existed.","“I was moving across the Earliest Folds...this was before I understood what I would become, when I was still discovering what paradox meant. I was chasing something magnificent: a shattered fragment of an Early Veiled Shore.”","His eyes grew distant with memory that might have been real or might have been constructed for effect.","“Imagine it...a piece of those sacred spaces, broken off and drifting through the Folds like a boat without anchor. The potential contained within even a fragment... it could have elevated me beyond measure. So I chased it with dedication that bordered on madness.”","He paused, ensuring his audience was properly captured. He blinked on Duke Whisker, Valen, and Gwendolyn as he continued!","“During this chase, I encountered an Inevitability. But this one didn’t attack. It seemed... curious about what I was doing. It floated alongside me, making sounds that might have been questions in languages that hadn’t been invented yet.”","Schrodinger’s expression grew rueful.","“But I was at a pivotal moment. The fragment was within reach...almost. Just a little more effort, a little more focus, and it would be mine. So I dismissed this curious Inevitability. Ignored it completely. Why did I care for some paradoxical observer when transcendence was within grasp?”","He shook his head at his younger self’s foolishness.","“I chased for a day and a night. Through spaces that existed sideways to reality. Through moments that happened before and after simultaneously. And then... I lost sight of it. The fragment simply vanished, as if it had never existed at all.”","The silence that followed carried weight.","“As I floated there in my failure, wondering how I had lost something I had been so close to claiming, I heard a voice. It buzzed through all existence, making reality itself tremble with recognition.”","Schrodinger’s voice shifted, taking on waves that suggested something vast speaking through constrained form:","“‘I, THE Living Concept, tried to embody an Inevitability to meet worthy creatures of the Folds. To see who might recognize thought itself wearing paradox as costume. And you actually ignored me, chasing something that was never meant to be yours.'”","He returned to his normal voice, though the weight of the memory remained.","“‘What a loss,’ THE Living Concept had said that day. ‘What a loss!'”","...!","Schrodinger looked at each of the Living Origins, his gaze lingering on Duke Gwendolyn with particular weight.","“So you see, I know something about heavy losses. About something slipping right past your fingers while you chase what seemed more important.” His smile contained sympathy that might have been genuine.","“It is okay. We all have our stories of what escaped us while we weren’t paying attention to what mattered.”","“...”","The silence that followed was immense.","No one dared speak, each processing the implications of the story...that Schrodinger had once been noticed by THE Living Concept, that he had missed such an opportunity through narrow focus, that losses could be teachers if one survived them!","Finally, Schrodinger nodded with the air of someone ending a satisfactory visit.","“Alright, you all get going now. We shall see each other soon enough at the Kleos Concordat.”","The dismissal was gentle but absolute.","Duke Gwendolyn, Whisker, and the others began moving toward the white-gold portal with the careful movements of people backing away from something dangerous.","Duke Valen remained a moment longer, his blind eyes seeing things others couldn’t. He shook his head with a smile that contained layers of meaning, a gesture toward Schrodinger that might have been acknowledgment, warning, or simple amusement.","Then he too disappeared.","The encirclement of Living Paradoxes remained perfectly still, hundreds of impossible beings maintaining positions with patience that transcended time. Only after the last Origin had vanished did movement return, and then only slightly.","Diviticus approached Schrodinger with uncharacteristic hesitation, her usual confidence cracked by what she had witnessed.","“Sir,” she said carefully, “when will we put the Corpse into use?”","Schrodinger didn’t even glance at her, his gaze fixed on something beyond normal perception. “Everything is in due time. Everything.”","Everything.","The repetition of ‘Everything’ seemed to trigger something in him.","He raised his hand, studying its callouses with the intensity of someone reading fate in skin patterns. His mind drifted to memories older than most civilizations...to the first of his Everything that he had given away.","The memory made him smile with genuine warmth that transformed his beggar’s face into something almost paternal.","“Everything,” he repeated once more, but this time the word contained multitudes.","...!","1/4"]},{"number":4050,"title":"Chapter 4050: Chapter 4049: Sir! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4049: Sir! I","In the distance, the white rays of Order finally began to fade from the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, leaving only normal impossibility in their wake. But the changes those rays had initiated, the transformations they had catalyzed, those would continue rippling through existence!","It would be known across the Folds.","Order...had returned!","The Kleos Concordat approached, and with it, convergences that would reshape many things","But for now, there was only waiting. And stories. And the memory of Everythings... given and received!","—","Perception shapes reality in ways that transcend the physical. How one believes they are perceived by others can transform their entire mental landscape, creating prisons or palaces from nothing more than assumption.","Some walk through existence crushed beneath imagined judgment.","They believe others see them as strange, inadequate, unworthy.","This perception becomes a weight that bends their shoulders, dims their voice, makes them smaller with each passing day. Anxiety blooms from seeds that were never planted, depression grows from soil that exists only in their minds!","Others stride forward wrapped in assumed admiration. They believe themselves seen as intelligent, confident, capable. This perception becomes armor and wings simultaneously, carrying them through challenges that might break those who doubt.","They act calm because they believe others expect calmness. They project confidence because they assume it’s already attributed to them.","The anxious do not know that they can always choose to do the same. To simply project confidence and calmness as this...would change their lives immensely!","Across existence, perception determines trajectories. Wars have been fought over how nations believed they were viewed.","Loves have died from assumptions about what a glance meant.","Entire civilizations have risen or fallen based on how they thought history would remember them!","But...there was one being who cared remarkably little for how others perceived him.","In Aeternitas Concordia, Noah’s merchant body remained in the domed garden with the tranquility of someone tending their own backyard.","He examined the plants with genuine interest, though he noted they weren’t as terrifying as the ones he had planted in his Shore. These were domesticated things, powerful but tamed, lacking the raw potential of truly wild growth.","His contemplation shattered as the garden suddenly buzzed and shook with the force of multiple arrivals.","Duke-level Living Origins materialized in rapid succession, their combined presence making reality pay attention!","But it was Duke Gwendolyn whose fury blazed brightest, her eyes locking onto Noah with intensity that could have melted lesser beings.","She hauled the still-unconscious bodies of Thessaly and Altheon like sacks of grain, dumping them unceremoniously as her focus remained fixed on him. When she spoke, her voice cracked with barely controlled rage.","“Where is she?!”","The question rang through the garden with force that made the tamed plants tremble.","Every Duke present immediately understood...somehow, impossibly, this merchant was the one who had taken what they had gone to retrieve from the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds. THE Living Order had vanished under his influence!","A dozen Dukes of Living Origins fixed their gazes upon him. Each stare carried enough weight to crush Prime Living Existences into paste. The combined pressure of their attention should have been unbearable, should have forced him to his knees or worse.","Noah bore it without flinching.","After all, he had moved through an Existential Trembling. This was merely... attention.","He looked at Duke Gwendolyn with the same calm he’d shown while examining plants. When he spoke, his voice carried no stress, no acknowledgment of the pressure bearing down upon him.","“She is safe. Somewhere where she cannot be threatened by Paradoxes, Inevitabilities... or anything else.” He paused, his gaze drifting away from Gwendolyn though his words remained clearly directed.","“And best of all, nobody knows where. So nobody cannot just blab away everything about her.”","...!","The accusation landed with precision that made Duke Gwendolyn’s nature flare visibly.","“You...!” Power pulsed from her form, the might of a Duke making space crack around her edges. “The Living Order is not yours to take and make decisions for! She belongs to and with the Living Origins! For you to come in here and do all this... just who do you think you-”","WU!","Before she could finish, brilliant authority erupted from Duke Whisker. The tiny mouse’s power vibrated through existence with such force that reality itself considered trembling.","Almost trembled. The fact that it only almost happened made the display more terrifying than if it had fully manifested.","Duke Gwendolyn’s words died instantly. Her nostrils flared, fists clenched white, as she continued staring at Noah with fury that had no outlet.","Duke Whisker’s ancient gaze moved across the assembled Dukes before settling on Noah with weight that transcended simple observation.","“Leave us,” he said to the others. “I will ascertain things here.”","Several Dukes shifted, clearly wanting to object. They were Dukes...who was Whisker to dismiss them like subordinates?","The answer came as the small mouse’s body began radiating terrifying white light. Not of Origin, but of Beginning itself...something more fundamental, more absolute.","The other Dukes found themselves moving toward the exits without conscious decision, their bodies obeying before their minds could object!","Duke Whisker clearly held a unique position among the Dukes of Living Origins, one that transcended simple seniority or power.","Duke Valen left with a knowing nod, his blind eyes seeing more than sight allowed. Duke Gwendolyn was the last to depart, her reluctance visible in every movement, but even she couldn’t resist that white light of Beginning.","When the garden held only Noah and the tiny Duke, the atmosphere shifted completely.","Duke Whisker studied Noah for a long moment. Then the somber tension he had been radiating dissolved, replaced by something almost conversational!","He breathed out, a surprisingly human gesture from such a form, and spoke with calm certainty.","“Sir, I apologize for how your interactions with Living Origins have gone so far.”","BOOM!","The word hit Noah with more force than any attack could have.","Sir.","A Duke of the Living Origins had called him ‘Sir.’","Noah’s composed expression buzzed slightly, genuine surprise showing through. “For what reason could you be calling me Sir?”","...!","2/4"]},{"number":4051,"title":"Chapter 4051: Chapter 4050: Sir! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4050: Sir! II","Duke Whisker’s stellar eyes held depths of experience that transcended his small form.","“In my existence, I always play a game of origin probabilities. Calculating what beings truly are versus what they present themselves as. And of all probabilities for who or what you could be...after all I have seen and know, you are either an Early Creature, or one of those terrifying Fold Dwellers stemming from the Wandering Territories.”","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes blazed with sudden interest at these words.","Duke Whisker, seemingly unperturbed by the reaction, waved his little paws casually.","A white cloud materialized beneath him, lifting him to a more comfortable conversation height.","In his paws appeared a block of resplendent stellar cheese that gleamed with inner light. He began nibbling at it with the air of someone eating away stress as he eyes burned with determination!","“What do you know about the Wandering Territories?” Noah asked, his interest genuine. “What lies within them?”","Duke Whisker blinked slowly, as if recognizing he was being tested but choosing to answer anyway. He continued eating his stellar cheese, each bite seeming to calm him further.","“The Wandering Territories,” he began, his voice taking on the cadence of someone sharing carefully guarded knowledge, “exist in the gaps between Folds. Or perhaps they don’t exist there...it’s never been entirely clear. They’re spaces that are and aren’t, paths that lead everywhere and nowhere.”","He took another thoughtful bite of cheese.","“Some don’t even know where they are or how to reach them. The Territories don’t appear on any map because they refuse to stay in one place long enough to be mapped. Yet any Fold Dweller who exceeds Originus Venerant feels a calling toward them...a pull that transcends physical direction.”","The mouse’s expression grew more serious.","“In the Earliest Folds, it was said that the First Farmer...the Fold Dweller who gazed upon THE Living Spirit, grew disillusioned with everything after an attack from a Mad Early Creature. Living Existences with their hierarchies and prejudices. Early Creatures with their casual cruelty. Inevitabilities with their endless hunger. All of them viewed Fold Dwellers as lesser, as prey, as insignificant.”","...!","Duke Whisker paused, his stellar eyes growing distant with memory or knowledge.","“So the First Farmer did something unprecedented. He established an endlessly vast domain in the Wandering Territories...a space that existed specifically because it shouldn’t, that welcomed those who had no welcome elsewhere. He proclaimed it was only for Fold Dwellers. There, they could live without persecution, without fear of being casually destroyed for sport or sustenance.”","The implications boomed heavily in the garden air.","“We rarely see powerful Fold Dwellers from that place,” Duke Whisker continued. “When we do, they’re... different. They’ve developed along paths we don’t recognize, achieved power through means that shouldn’t work but do. They’re dangerous in ways that transcend simple strength because they’ve had to be creative to survive.”","He fixed Noah with a gaze that suggested he was weighing possibilities.","“As for Early Creatures... nobody has seen them for quite some time. They’ve become myth more than reality, stories more than beings. If you are one...” He trailed off, then shook his head. “But that would mean you’ve been hiding among us, growing, preparing. And that would raise questions about what you’re preparing for.”","The stellar cheese had been reduced to crumbs, which Duke Whisker consumed with final, thoughtful bites.","“So tell me, Sir...and I will continue calling you that because respect costs nothing and might save everything, which are you? An Early Creature playing merchant? Or a Fold Dweller from the Wandering Territories who has transcended so far that the distinction no longer matters?”","Noah remained silent for a moment, weighing not the question but how much truth to reveal. Duke Whisker had shown remarkable insight, remarkable respect. But trust...","Trust was earned through more than clever deduction.","“Does it matter which I am,” Noah finally asked, “if my actions benefit those worth benefiting?”","Duke Whisker’s whiskers twitched in what might have been amusement. “A question answered with a question. Very well. Let me be more direct then...will THE Living Order be safe? Will she be returned? Will the balance between Origins and Paradoxes hold through the Kleos Concordat?”","These were the real questions, the ones that mattered more than origins or classifications.","Noah’s response was simple. “She is safer than she has ever been. She will return when she chooses to return. And the balance, though I dont personally have full control over it...should hold unless someone tips it through foolish action.”","...!","Duke Whisker nodded slowly, accepting these answers with the wisdom of someone who knew when pushing would yield less than patience.","“Then I suppose we shall see what unfolds at the Concordat,” the mouse said. “Though I suspect it will be more serious than anyone anticipates.”","In the distance, through walls that couldn’t quite contain the sound, Duke Gwendolyn’s frustration manifested as something breaking.","Neither Noah nor Duke Whisker acknowledged it.","Some perceptions mattered less than others, after all!","Duke Whisker regarded Noah with the particular intensity of someone weighing futures against probabilities. The stellar cheese was gone, leaving only the lingering scent of compressed starlight in the air.","“Regardless of your disposition and identity,” the mouse said carefully, “is there anything you need? Existence is getting increasingly tumultuous. Living Origins will need alliances on all sides if we’re to navigate what’s coming.”","Noah waved his hand with grace, and something materialized that only they could perceive...a silent stellar string stretching between them, gossamer-thin yet unbreakable, visible only to those it connected.","An entanglement in the truest sense...a connection at a fundamental level!","He tugged on it gently, the vibration traveling instantly across the impossibly thin thread.","“We have shared a deeper conversation than most,” Noah acknowledged. “We have formed an entanglement. If I need anything, or if you need anything, simply tug on this connection. The matters of THE Living Order will be taken care of. For now...”","He turned toward one of the grand golden glass windows of the domed garden, gazing out at the distant corner of Aeternitas!","“For now, I will go back to my work as a merchant.”","He turned back to Duke Whisker with a smile that contained layers of meaning. “Oh, could you send me back to the market? I am a wee little Fold Dweller after all, and I can’t be flying from the high towers of Aeternitas Concordia, right?”","The mouse blinked slowly, processing the gentle mockery of their entire situation.","A being who could teleport from within Doorways to the Loom, who commanded THE Living Order’s attention, who bore the pressure of multiple Dukes without flinching...asking for a ride like someone needing help down from a high shelf!","Duke Whisker sighed, the sound containing both amusement and resignation. With a nod, brilliant white light erupted around them both, like being wrapped in the concept of movement itself!","3/4"]},{"number":4052,"title":"Chapter 4052: Chapter 4051: Sir! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4051: Sir! III","They materialized in the outer periphery of Aeternitas Concordia.","Here, the humble stalls of Originus Venerant Fold Dwellers gave way to the grand golden towers of Living Existences, creating a boundary zone that belonged fully to neither.","Noah’s throne sat unoccupied but radiant, its presence making the space around it significant simply by existing.","No one had dared remove it!","The atmosphere in the market was tense with a particular flavor of displeasure.","At this moment, Fold Dwellers and Living Origins alike cast hostile glances toward a specific group: Fold Dwellers from the Veiled Sunfolds who bore the unmistakable designation of Paradox above their heads.","Kalysta stood at their center, golden lights of Kismet and Destiny swirling around her form despite her downcast posture. Her golden hair caught light that seemed to come from within rather than without, but the marking of Paradox above her head made her radiance seem tainted to those watching.","She wasn’t alone in her designation!","Master Shen, Master Etheopa, and others from the Veiled Sunfolds clustered together like sheep surrounded by wolves, each marked as coming from Paradoxical Folds, each feeling the weight of hostile observation.","Interestingly, no one had moved against them. Word had spread about two other Paradox-marked Fold Dwellers who had revealed sponsorship by Honored Living Existences.","That possibility that these outcasts might have hidden backing kept violence at bay, though not hostility.","Master Shen took another long pull from his gourd, the alcohol doing little to ease the suffocating atmosphere. He whispered to those near him, his voice barely carrying over the market’s noise.","“Maybe... there are no opportunities for us here.”","Kalysta’s eyes flashed gold with inner light, Kismet itself speaking through her perception. “No. Kismet tells me there is something here...”","Master Shen rolled his eyes with the exasperation of someone who had heard this before. “Girl, are you still dreaming about Osmont? You can’t-”","BZZT!","The white light that suddenly blazed in the distance cut off his words. Every eye in the market turned toward the source, and Master Shen nearly dropped his gourd at what he saw.","“No fucking way...”","He took another drink, longer this time, blinking repeatedly as if alcohol might clear the impossible from his vision.","But Kalysta had no such hesitation.","Her entire being lit up with joy that transcended her circumstances as she called out across the market.","“Sir!”","...!","Noah materialized exactly where he intended...walking toward his throne with the confidence of someone returning to their own living room.","He noticed Duke Whisker floating beside him, the mouse having shrunk his presence until he seemed like nothing more than an ordinary rodent, albeit one that happened to float. The Duke settled atop a nearby stall with the air of a casual observer.","Then he heard it...that voice calling him with a title that was becoming surprisingly common in his existence.","“Sir!”","Sir.","From Moiraine, the word carried devotion that transcended simple respect.","From Duke Whisker, it had been acknowledgment of power dynamics.","He recognized the voice of none other than Kalysta as she was now calling him Sir!","From Kalysta, it rang with something between hope and desperation.","He watched as crowds of Fold Dwellers parted like water before a ship’s prow. Kalysta led the Originus Venerant experts of the Veiled Sunfolds through the gap, her eyes literally sparkling with golden light that had nothing to do with her abilities and everything to do with relief.","She approached him with the enthusiasm of someone greeting their salvation. “Where is Sis Sigrid? My Kismet was telling me to keep looking until I found you two!”","Her voice buzzed with such genuine enthusiasm that Noah found himself sighing as he reached out to stroke her head...a gesture that would have seemed patronizing from anyone else but somehow felt natural from him.","His gaze swept across the other members of the Veiled Sunfolds, then expanded to encompass the watching crowds. When he spoke, his voice carried edges that could cut.","“Did anyone bully you? Fold Dweller or Living Existence?” His eyes grew harder with each word. “If they did...”","The threat didn’t need to be completed.","The marketplace erupted into motion as beings who moments before had been casting hostile glances suddenly remembered urgent business elsewhere.","Fold Dwellers scattered toward different stalls. Living Existences found reasons to examine things in the opposite direction.","The speed of their dispersal was almost comical, if not for what it revealed about Noah’s current standing in Aeternitas Concordia.","Kalysta, Master Shen, and the others stared at this exodus with expressions that cycled through shock, confusion, and a desperate need for explanation. What had happened?","Why did Osmont, a Fold Dweller just like them, inspire such fear in beings that should have been able to crush him without thought?!","“No,” Kalysta said hesitantly, her voice small with confusion. “No one bullied us. They just... watched.”","Noah nodded, accepting this. He moved to his throne with grace, settling into it as if it had been carved specifically for his form. His gaze swept across the marketplace.","“Trades are back on!” His voice carried with the clarity of a bell through the market air. “Anything from the Doorways to the Loom, especially Herbs... and if I like them, a bowl shall be traded!”","With gestures, two radiant Glass Woks materialized beside him. Each one contained soup that gleamed with inner light, cut up Marine Lifeforms swimming through broth that could elevate existence itself. Multiple stacks of golden bowls appeared as well.","Kalysta and the others stood frozen, trying to process what they were witnessing. Master Shen’s gourd hung forgotten in his hand, his mouth slightly open as his mind struggled to reconcile the Osmont he remembered with the being who now commanded respect in a place like this!","“What...” Master Etheopa’s voice emerged as barely a whisper. “What the hell is going on?”","The question buzzed in the air, but Noah didn’t answer directly. Instead, he gestured for them to come closer, to stand near his throne where the designation of Paradox might matter less than proximity to someone who transcended such categories.","Kalysta moved closer without hesitation, drawn by Kismet itself toward whatever fate awaited. The others followed more cautiously, Master Shen taking one more drink before accepting that no amount of alcohol would make this situation make sense.","Around them, the marketplace slowly returned to life.","Duke Whisker, still disguised as an ordinary mouse, watched it all with stellar eyes that missed nothing.","At the center of it all, Noah waited for more opportunities to arise as in the Early Veiled Shore...his main body prepared to excavate wonders to pass the time until plants matured, until the Kleos Concordat began!","4/4 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming! Next chapter titles: The Terrifying Early Excavation Depths! 1-4"]},{"number":4053,"title":"Chapter 4053: Chapter 4052: Records Without Limitations! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4052: Records Without Limitations! I","In the Early Veiled Shore.","Noah...wouldn’t describe himself as a person who could be smitten. He had many beautiful existences around him...beings he cared for deeply, loved in ways that transcended simple emotion.","But smitten suggested something uncontrolled, overwhelming. As he looked at Sigrid standing near the entrance to the archaic mine, he wouldn’t say he was smitten.","Marveling, however...that word fit perfectly.","He was marveling at this creature purely because of the fact that her progression...was ridiculous!","She radiated the terrifying aura of an Honored Living Existence, but even that classification seemed inadequate for what she was becoming.","The white light of Order that emanated from her organized everything it touched, making the chaotic patterns in the mine’s entrance stones arrange themselves into perfect harmony.","They stood together making final preparations for their first delve into the Primordial Excavation Depths, but Noah found his perception continually drawn to her transformation.","When he focused his enhanced sight on her details, what he saw was utterly terrifying!","|Sigrid Ivanov – THE Living Order|","Primary Classification: THE Living Order(63% Awakened)","Secondary Classification: Honored Living Existence (Transcending), Living Origin","Distinctions:","– Vessel of Primordial Order","– The Restored Foundation","– Bearer of Ordered Chaos","– Chosen of The Early Creature, Osmont","Current Statistics:","– Complexity Quotient: 157,892,473,621","– Purity Quotient: 156,903,892,517","– Current Increase Rate: +500,000,000 CQ/PQ per second (Stabilizing)","Unique Traits:","– Order Incarnate: Her presence naturally organizes chaotic systems","– Existential Anchor: Prevents reality degradation in a Fold-meter radius","– THE Living Order Authority: Commands absolute obedience from Order-aligned entities","Noah shook his head at these numbers and distinctions.","His own complexity was just approaching five billion...impressive by any standard, revolutionary for someone who had started from nothing.","But compared to Sigrid’s explosive growth, he might as well have been standing still.","Near them, Ruination stood. The Infiniverse floated nearby, its form shifting between states as it continued processing its own evolution.","Moiraine’s clone had arrived from the Abode where her primary body was currently... experimenting with other cultivation methodologies alongside another of Noah’s bodies. The implications and results of those experiments and how they would be replicated, and with who... would have made Duke Gwendolyn faint!","The five of them...Noah, Sigrid, Ruination, the Infiniverse, and Moiraine...had gathered to explore what lay within the Primordial Excavation Depths. But first, preparations needed to be completed.","“Alright,” Noah said, his voice carrying the authority of decision. “Let us finish preparations. Sit.”","They arranged themselves on the golden sands near the mine entrance, the glorious light of the Shore casting no shadows despite the depth of the opening before them.","Noah turned to Ruination first, raising his finger with deliberate purpose.","A vibrant white-gold light shot from his fingertip, wrapping around Ruination like chains made of possibility itself.","This wasn’t an attack or restriction...this was a Guidance Seal, the mark of THE Living Existential Guider claiming another existence to nurture toward transcendence!","The moment the seal took hold, Ruination’s body erupted with stellar white-gold light that made reality buzz.","|Ruination has been granted a Guidance Seal|","|Analyzing potential changes...|","|The nature of Endings within Ruination has achieved existential resonance with the Seed of Inevitability|","The distant Seed of Inevitability, planted in its plot, suddenly pulsed with recognition.","Obsidian tentacles erupted from the soil, existing in the space between real and unreal!","They stretched across the Shore with impossible speed, coming to hover above Ruination like judgment waiting to fall.","Ruination opened her eyes, gazing at the tentacles with an expression of cold evaluation. Without hesitation, without fear...she spoke.","“I give Everything of my Beginnings.”","BOOM!","The tentacled jaws clamped down with violence that transcended physical action.","They passed through her body while taking something fundamental...white brilliance was torn from her being, leaving behind only ruinous blackness!","The extraction was visible to all, streams of light that represented every new start she might have had, every fresh beginning, every reset...all of it devoured by the Inevitability’s hunger.","Ruination’s expression showed terrifying serenity as the process completed.","Her being now emanated only endings...no possibility of starting over, no chance of new beginnings, only conclusions and terminations!","Yet her eyes looked not at what was happening to her, but into the distance where her Master sat.","He was right there, close enough to touch, yet somehow infinitely far ahead, pulling away at speeds that demanded everything to match.","He was too glorious.","To keep up, sacrifices were necessary!","“I give my Everything of Order.”","HUUM!","Noah frowned, beginning to rise with concern, but Ruination’s gaze held him in place. This was her choice, her evolution. The tentacled jaws descended again with obvious glee, biting through reality to claim another fundamental aspect.","The phenomenon that followed was heavier than the first. Ruination trembled with transformation so profound her existence struggled to contain it!","|Ruination has given Everything of Order and Beginnings|","|All that remains: Endless chaos, endless endings, endless ruin|","|Ruination has tapped into Quintessential potential through the authority of THE Living Existential Guider|","|Catalyst: Seed of Inevitability + Deviating Early Veiled Shore|","|A grand nature of endings has been unveiled from her existence!|","|Ruination has begun walking the path of an Early Living Ruin|","HUUM!","The surrounding existence shook tumultuously!","Heavily!","|This weaving has potential to create entirely new type of Living Existence|","|Early Living Ruin Capabilities:|","– Gains complexity from every ending witnessed or caused","– Purity increases through perfect destruction","– Can end concepts, not just physical forms when powerful enough","– Immune to resurrection or reversal effects","– Each ruin created strengthens her foundation","Ruination’s body burned with a sense of profound glory!","Waves of crimson and gold bathed everything as her figure floated gloriously, but it still seemed like she was not done.","Because on her forehead, a glorious glyph began to form.","|Due to the nature of her transformation, Ruination is ending all of her complexity and previous Glyphs to the task of forming a Kleos Glyph of Ruin|","|Effect: Touch brings inevitable ending to all things|","|Growth: Exponential based on significance of endings|","|The Early Living Ruin, Ruination, is completing a glorious and Quintessential transformation, and is looking forward to embarking on path of endless Ruin!|","The waves of crimson and gold slowly subsided, but they were no less grand!","1/4 change in chap titles"]},{"number":4054,"title":"Chapter 4054: Chapter 4053: Records Without Limitations! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4053: Records Without Limitations! II","Noah checked her condition with genuine concern. “Are you okay?”","Ruination smiled...an expression that transformed her entirely.","Her fair skin now seemed to glow with inner darkness, her figure wrapped in a deep red-obsidian dress that appeared to be cut from ruptured folds of existence itself.","The fabric was absence given form, endings made wearable!","“I have never been better,” she said, her voice carrying waves of termination. “For you, Master, I will chase endings all the way to the Earliest Folds...where I need to.”","HUUM!","Noah shook his head with a mixture of pride and concern, then raised his hand to release multiple rays of white-gold light.","The Guidance Seals shot out like stars being born, seeking every existence within the Early Veiled Shore...Henry, Kazuhiko, Emperor Penguin, Adelaide, Athena, Anna, Barbatos, his mother, everyone who had chosen to follow him into impossibility.","Scintillating lights landed on all present, each seal adapting to its recipient’s nature. Some blazed bright, others dimmed to match quieter natures, but all carried the same fundamental blessing...the guidance of one who could lead Living Existences to transcendence!","Noah turned to the Infiniverse, whose form had been shifting with increasing calmness since witnessing Ruination’s transformation.","“You’re up next.”","...!","The being that was the consciousness of the Infiniverse Wheel itself trembled with anticipation.","What would it give away? What would it become? The possibilities were infinite, which was perhaps the problem...when you contained all possibilities, choosing just one path seemed almost impossible.","But that was why Noah was here. THE Living Existential Guider didn’t just mark beings for growth...he would help them find their paths when the options were too vast to comprehend.","He had already been discussing with the Infiniverse on what could be given as she was similar if not grander than him in what she could give!","The entrance to the Primordial Excavation Depths yawned before them, promising treasures and dangers from eras that predated current understanding. But first, his people needed to be prepared for what they might face.","After all, you couldn’t mine the bones of Existence without being ready for Existence to object!","Noah gazed at the Infiniverse.","The manifestation of the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence that held the Early Veiled Shore at its very center. She stood before him as the consciousness of structure itself, the awareness that had developed within the framework that housed countless existences.","Her Spokes were all Frequencies of Existence containing countless domains of Matter, Dark Matter, and Anti-Matter. She was the architecture within which countless beings lived, loved, fought, and died without ever knowing their universe had consciousness, had will, had dreams of its own.","The moment the Guidance Seal touched her, her body radiated waves of profound complexity that made the air itself reconsider its properties!","Her entire existence pulsed.","A pulse.","Such a simple thing, a pulse.","Hearts did it billions of times without thought. Stars pulsed with radiation across eons. Even atoms vibrated with their own pulses!","But this pulse was different.","From this single pulse, the massive Infiniverse Wheel of Existence itself...hidden away in the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, shuddered with recognition.","The tremor passed through every Spoke, every Frequency, every particle of matter and antimatter that comprised its incomprehensible bulk.","And the Early Veiled Shore, housed at the center like a heart within a chest, also pulsed in response!","The Infiniverse rose from where she had been seated, and her ascension was revelation itself.","Her dress seemed woven from existence’s own dreams...multicolored jewels that weren’t merely decorative but functional, each one representing a different Frequency she contained. They caught light that didn’t exist, reflecting possibilities that might never be, creating an aurora of potential around her form!","Her face carried the kind of beauty that transcended physical features. It was the beauty of music finding harmony after discord, of understanding dawning after confusion.","When she spoke, her voice carried the resonance of billions of voices speaking in perfect unity!","“I give...Everything of my Limitations.”","The words fell into the Shore’s atmosphere with weight that made reality reassess its rulings!","Everything of her Limitations.","Not some, not most, but Everything.","Noah’s eyes blazed with glory of what she was attempting. A prompt materialized before his vision with urgency that suggested even the system that generated it was shocked.","|The Infiniverse has chosen to give an extremely fundamental part of her Everything|","|Limitations define structure, boundaries, possibility itself|","|Without limitations, infinite expansion becomes possible|","|Without limitations, infinite collapse becomes possible|","|Warning: Outcome cannot be predicted|","...!","The tentacled jaws of the Seed of Inevitability flashed into existence above her, summoned by her declaration of sacrifice.","But something unprecedented occurred...they didn’t immediately chomp down.","Instead, they hovered, almost hesitant, as if recognizing that what was being offered transcended normal feeding.","The Infiniverse gazed up at them with regal certainty, no fear in her expression despite what she was about to lose. She raised her hands slowly, formally, as if conducting a ceremony that had been waiting eons to be performed.","From her palms, something began to emerge...and it was not light or darkness.","It was possibility itself crystallizing into form.","It was every boundary she had ever possessed.","Every rule that kept her Frequencies from colliding. Every law that prevented her galaxies from occupying the same space. Every limitation that made her finite despite containing infinity.","BOOM!","The moment the Inevitability accepted what she offered, everything shook.","But this wasn’t the trembling of destruction or the shuddering of fear.","This was Existence reorganizing itself around a fundamental change, like the universe clearing its throat before speaking for the first time!","The Early Veiled Shore’s golden sands rose in spirals that defied gravity.","The Early Sacred Waters formed geometries that shouldn’t exist.","Every tree, every plot, every construct began resonating with frequencies that had been locked away since before time was properly separated from space!","|Due to countless limitations being lifted, the Infiniverse is undergoing fundamental transformation|","|Scattered records and memories from the origin of the Infiniverse are unfolding|","...!","2/4"]},{"number":4055,"title":"Chapter 4055: Chapter 4054: Records Without Limitations! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4054: Records Without Limitations! III","Brilliant multicolored waves of light continued to echo out across the Early Veiled Shore as more prompts cascaded down!","|Without limitations to hide them, truths are becoming visible|","|Accessing archived data from collapsed timelines, records, and weavings of existence are being retrieved...|","...!","A brilliant white light suddenly engulfed everything.","It wasn’t harsh or blinding.","The light was the light of revelation, of understanding, of veils being lifted!","Noah found himself suspended in luminescence that had texture, that had meaning encoded in every photon.","|You are witnessing the history of what is now known as the Infiniverse|","|Limitation removal has allowed access to memories thought permanently lost|","|Prepare for historical reconstruction...|","The white light began to resolve into something else, like fog clearing to reveal a landscape that had always been there.","A record!","A History!","Noah found himself observing... witnessing with the clarity of someone watching the most important moment in history unfold.","A scene began to construct itself from thr white light!","He saw a vast stretch of land that dwarfed anything he had encountered.","On it were silver white glimmering sands.","The silver-white sands weren’t just beautiful, they were buzzing with potential, each grain containing enough complexity to birth civilizations!","Incandescent waters lapped at shores that extended beyond perception, while roiling mists wrapped around the edges like reality’s own uncertainty about where this place ended and impossibility began.","But paradise had been violated.","Thousands of Massive marine lifeforms...ancient species whose very existence predated the categories used to classify life...lay with their titanic bodies torn open.","Their wounds weren’t clean cuts but tears in existence itself, as if someone had reached into reality and pulled these creatures apart at the conceptual level!","Their blood, crimson-gold and luminous, painted the sacred waters with evidence of catastrophe.","The land itself bore witness to destruction.","Vibrant trees that might have been the ancestors of every tree that would ever grow lay shattered, their branches reaching toward skies that could no longer shelter them.","Farmlands that had been cultivated with patience measured in eons were soaked with that same crimson-gold blood, their carefully tended rows now graves for ambitions that would never fruit.","Structures rose from this carnage like accusations!","Totems that touched clouds and anchored themselves in the world’s foundation stood cracked but defiant.","Ancient buildings whose architecture suggested purposes beyond simple habitation lay in various states of collapse.","Geometric constructs that might have been art or might have been technology or might have been both sprawled across the landscape, some still humming with dying energy.","But it was the corpses that truly told the story.","More than a dozen Early Creatures lay scattered across this continental expanse!","Some had been cut in half with such precision that their severed portions still seemed to be trying to reconnect.","Others showed signs of being unraveled and undone, their very existence being pulled apart thread by thread until nothing coherent remained!","Still others displayed a more terrible fate: the complete decimation of the concept of existence within them, leaving bodies that were physically intact but fundamentally absent.","Amidst this ocean of endings, a single Early Creature remained alive.","She knelt in the blood-soaked sand, her dark hair falling past her shoulders in waves that seemed to move with their own sorrow.","Her eyes...dark pupils that spoke of depths without end, freely streamed golden tears that fell to mix with the blood below. Each tear that fell seemed to carry within it the weight of witnessing everything you loved become nothing.","She wasn’t looking at the carnage around her. Her gaze, filled with hatred that transcended emotion to become force itself, was fixed on nine figures standing before her.","Nine Early Creatures, each bearing bone weapons!","These weren’t simple armaments.","They were tools carved from the bones of Existence itself, each one containing an entire Fold within their structure...compressed existence weaponized and wielded with casual certainty.","“Why?” Her voice cracked on the single word, then strengthened with rage that could have birthed Wheels of Existence.","“Why would you do this? They were Farmers! Scholars! Wanderers! We had no part in your wars, your weavings, your grand designs!”","HUUM!","The leading Early Creature among the nine stepped forward slightly. Age wrapped around him like a cloak, but it was the age of mountains, of concepts, not weakness.","When he spoke, his voice carried the weight of someone who had made peace with atrocity.","“Why does anyone do anything?” The question seemed genuinely philosophical rather than dismissive.","“Some act because they want to...desire driving decision. Others act because they are commanded...duty overcoming preference. All of existence operates on these two principles. Want or must. Choice or compulsion.”","He gestured at the devastation with his bone weapon, the movement causing reality to ripple.","“We wanted to let you be. Your Shore was beautiful, productive, peaceful. But we must do this. The equation is simple when reduced to its components.”","The kneeling Early Creature’s expression shifted from grief to something sharper. “So... who is commanding you? Who has the authority to order this massacre?”","The silence that followed was heavy with reluctance.","The nine Early Creatures exchanged glances that suggested they wished this question hadn’t been asked, that naming their authority would make their actions even more real.","Finally, the leader spoke, his voice heavy with the weight of truth that couldn’t be avoided.","“THE Living Paradox.”","BOOM!","The name fell like a stone into still water, creating ripples of implication that spread outward endlessly.","Why?","Why would THE Living Paradox want this? What was it doing now?!","The kneeling Early Creature paled, her tears stopping as shock overwrote grief. Her teeth ground together with force that could have powdered diamonds.","Then she laughed...a sound devoid of humor but full of defiance.","“Legacy,” she said, the word given weight by her approaching death. “Every creature that has ever existed leaves one, whether they know it or not. Some leave legacies of creation, building things that outlast them. Others leave legacies of destruction, tearing down what others built.”","She looked at each of the nine in turn, memorizing their faces.","“Your legacy will be one of obedience. You’ll be remembered...if you’re remembered at all, as the hands that held the weapons, not the minds that chose the targets. Pawns who confused following orders with strength.”","...!","3/4"]},{"number":4056,"title":"Chapter 4056: Chapter 4055: Records Without Limitations! IV","paragraphs":["Chapter 4055: Records Without Limitations! IV","Her gaze returned to the leader.","“THE Living Paradox’s legacy will be one of fear. They command because they’re terrified of what exists without their control. Every tyrant’s legacy is ultimately fear dressed up as strength.”","She pressed her palms against the blood-soaked sand, and something fundamental shifted in the air.","“And my legacy... my legacy will be one of defiance.”","HUUM!","The leader’s eyes widened with sudden understanding.","“Stop her!”","But it was already too late.","The moment her declaration completed, the continental stretch of land...this impossible Early Veiled Shore that had sheltered so many...began to crack.","Not just physically, though the physical cracks were visible enough, spreading like lightning across the landscape.","These were conceptual fractures, existence itself choosing to break rather than be possessed.","The Shore split with violence that transcended destruction!","Corpses of Early Creatures were flung in all directions like toys discarded by an angry child.","The beautiful structures, the farmlands, the sacred waters...all of it shattered into fragments that immediately began flying apart, driven by the force of a dying Early Creature’s final act of rebellion.","Noah watched as his perspective followed one particular fragment.","It shot away from the devastation like an arrow loosed from reality’s bow, carrying within it a seed of what had been.","He felt time compress and stretch as he watched this fragment’s journey...eons passing in heartbeats, billions of years condensing into comprehensible moments.","The fragment crossed through the Earliest Folds, through spaces where physics hadn’t been properly established yet.","It passed through regions where thought and substance were the same thing, where possibility and actuality hadn’t been separated into distinct categories.","Time became strange as the fragment traveled.","Noah watched it move backward through rivers of temporal flow, visiting eras that preceded its own creation, then warping forward through billions of years that hadn’t happened yet.","It was paradox in motion, existence refusing to accept its own ending.","Eventually, the power that drove it began to fade. The fragment, once part of something vast and profound, broke into millions of smaller pieces. Each break was a small death, potential dividing and diminishing with each separation.","Noah’s perception followed one particular shard as it continued its journey, growing smaller with each division, weaker with each parsec traveled.","Untold eons passed.","The fragment shattered again and again, each division creating more pieces that scattered across existence like seeds that might never find soil.","Yet Noah’s attention remained fixed on one particular mote, following its path through impossibility itself.","Finally, after time had lost meaning through repetition, the fragment found its way into a murky, paradoxical fold.","Here, wrapped in layers of contradiction that kept it stable through opposition, it remained stationary for countless more eons. Time passed around it while it existed in a bubble of preservation, waiting without knowing what it waited for.","More ages passed. The fragment’s power diminished further, and it shattered once more into dozens of smaller fragments. These spread across the Folds with purpose that might have been random or might have been destiny.","One fragment in particular entered something Noah recognized...a Wheel of Existence!","He followed this infinitesimal piece as it carved through the Wheel’s structure. It passed through multiple omniverses with such speed that its mere passage caused their destruction, countless lives ending without ever knowing what had killed them.","The fragment, now almost too small to perceive, broke apart yet again as it crossed through void spaces between realities.","Finally, impossibly, it slipped into one particular Omniverse without decimating it.","The journey continued...across distances that made cosmic seem provincial. Through multiple cosmos where different laws of reality competed for dominance.","Across universes where time moved sideways. Through galaxies that were still being born. Past stars that were already dying.","This infinitesimal fragment of what had once been a glorious Early Veiled Shore, having shattered more times than Noah could count, ultimately arrived at its destination: a World.","A miniscule, tiny world!","The planet hung in space like a frozen pearl, its surface mostly endless ice and tundra with small pockets where life might theoretically flourish.","It was young, barely formed, with only the most primitive organisms beginning to emerge from its seas.","Here the fragment remained dormant for a thousand years, gathering what strength remained to it. Then, with one final effort, it shattered again...but this time with purpose.","The pieces spread across the World’s atmosphere and became something unprecedented: floating landmasses that hung in the skies like inverse islands.","Even reduced to fragments of fragments of fragments, they were still massive, still carrying within them echoes of the power they had once been part of.","These floating lands remained dormant for thousands more years, seemingly inert.","But gradually, impossibly, life began to emerge upon them.","Not life as the World below knew it, but something different...something influenced by the ancient power that still resonated within these aerial continents.","Spiders that spun webs from crystallized space. Walruses whose tusks could pierce spatial barriers. Mammoths whose trumpeting created small tears in reality.","Penguins that were unfathomably arrogant and prideful with their beaks raised high!","These creatures mutated, evolved, developed in ways that shouldn’t have been possible.","On one particular floating landmass, they became more than animals...they became intellectual beings, capable of thought and planning.","Noah’s perception focused on one particularly arrogant penguin, waddling about with self-importance that seemed comical!","He watched this penguin lead defenses against invaders, establish laws, and build a society.","Until one day, everything changed.","A young man landed on the floating island.","He appeared without fanfare, without cosmic significance, just a person arriving at a place.","But Noah recognized him immediately, intimately, impossibly.","It was himself.","Who could it have been, but himself when he arrived atop a Floating Island? Atop the Spiritual Land of thr Beast World?!","BOOM!","The memory shattered like glass struck by a hammer of truth.","The vision fractured, scattered, dissolved back into the white light from which it had emerged. Noah found himself back in his Early Veiled Shore, his perception returning to the present as prompts cascaded before his eyes.","|The record of the Origins of the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence has ended|","|The Infiniverse began as a fragment of a shattered Early Veiled Shore|","|That Shore was destroyed through the actions of nine Early Creatures under THE Living Paradox’s command|","|The defiant legacy of its original owner lives on through the Infiniverse.|","|The Infiniverse has witnessed its own origin and accepts its nature|","|Transformation continuing...|","HUUM!","The Infiniverse stood before him, her form now radiating something beyond what she had been.","Without limitations, she had become possibility itself...not infinite, but indefinite, capable of becoming whatever was needed!","“I remember now,” she said, her voice containing multitudes of understanding. “I remember being a shattered piece of countless shattered piecess. I remember traveling. I remember becoming less...to eventually become more.”","She looked at Noah with eyes that held the weight of eons.","“And I remember when your feet landed on the Spiritual Land, Master. I remember.”","HUUM!","4/4 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":4057,"title":"Chapter 4057: Chapter 4056: Osmontian! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4056: Osmontian! I","The Infiniverse remembered the day he had walked onto her for the first time.","Not the grand consciousness she had become, but the small floating Spiritual Land she had been in that frozen Beast World!","The memory blazed through her with clarity that transcended simple recollection. It was carved into her fundamental nature, the moment everything changed.","She moved toward Noah. When she reached him, she lifted him from his seated position on the golden sands with hands that contained Frequencies, yet touched him with infinite gentleness.","“I had been a shattered piece,” she said, her voice carrying melancholy. “A fragment of countless other fragments that had been losing their luster since the Earliest Folds. Each break made me less. Each division reduced what I could become.”","Her eyes, those windows into infinite possibility...gazed at him with intensity that transcended gratitude.","“With the passage of more eons, the Spiritual Lands in that Beast World and in other places... all those shattered fragments would have lost more energy. We would have broken again, and again, until we were nothing. Dust to dust. Ashes to ashes. Memory of memory. That was the future that should have happened.”","She paused, her hands still holding his as if afraid he might disappear if she let go.","“But then... an anomaly appeared.”","As she spoke, she began to lower herself, and Noah immediately shook his head, gesturing that she didn’t need to do this!","But the Infiniverse continued her descent until she knelt before him, her form radiating regality even in submission.","“An anomaly with infinite mana stepped onto a Spiritual Land, and impossibilities became real. Limitations that had defined existence since the Earliest Folds suddenly meant nothing.” Her voice grew stronger, more certain. “Today, I broke off and gave away my Limitations to that Seed, but truly... the day you became my owner, the day you attained ownership of that small Spiritual Land, I was already free of limitations.”","She looked up at him, her eyes containing depths that held glory!","“I was saved from another shattering. From dissipation. From becoming nothing.”","While still kneeling, the Infiniverse took Noah’s right hand with both of hers. She brought it to her lips with calm reverence, pressing a kiss to his hand that sent brilliant white-gold light erupting between them. The moment of contact created resonance that made existence itself take pulse!","Her complexity surged exponentially, each second multiplying what she was, what she could become.","HUUM!","Across the Early Veiled Shore, the Sacred Totems responded to this moment.","They rang without being struck, their bells creating harmonies that shouldn’t exist. Each tower sang its own hymn, yet somehow they wove together into something greater...a song of recognition, of transformation, of possibility finally achieving its potential!","The Infiniverse’s words continued.","“I could have been many things. From a Spiritual Land to a World. From a Universe to a Cosmos. I could have been an Omniverse, a Reality, a Wheel that held other Wheels.” She pressed his hand against her forehead, the contact making reality shimmer. “But none of those things could have happened without you.”","The light between them intensified, creating aurora that painted the Shore in colors that had no names!","It was magisterial!","“Even though I was a piece of a shattered Early Veiled Shore...even though I carried within me echoes of that ancient power, that was not the main reason I stand where I am today. Even now, you are the reason a Seed of Inevitability exists here, capable of eating away limitations. For everything... for my Everything... you were the one who nurtured it all.”","She rose slightly, still on her knees but looking directly into his eyes with certainty!","“I am not the Infiniverse because I was a shattered piece of an Early Veiled Shore. I am the Infiniverse because I am bound to you. Because I am yours.”","HUUM!","The declaration rang through existence!","Blinding waves of radiance erupted from her form like being inside the birth of a star.","|The Infiniverse rejects all possibilities she could become and decides for herself a single glorious path and transformation to become...The Infinite Early Osmontian Shore|","|Warning: This choice is irreversible|","|The Choice has been accepted with absolute certainty|","...!","Everything trembled with recognition.","The Early Veiled Shore itself seemed to bow to what was happening within it. Noah reached down and raised the Infiniverse from her knees, stellar white-gold lights surging around them in spirals that created their own gravity.","He sighed with the weight of emotion that was rare for him to even show!","“The reason I also stand where I am,” he said, his voice steady, “is because of all the help you’ve given me so far. So thank you.”","The Infiniverse looked into her Master’s eyes and shook her head with gentle certainty.","“No, Master. Do not thank me yet. I am young, at my starting point, and only now stepping onto the path of maturity. The path ahead of you is infinite, and I will walk it beside you, beneath you, carrying you when needed.”","She stepped back slightly, her form beginning to glow with inner light.","“Wait for me to reach even greater heights. To take you as far as you need to be. To follow and help you as much as I can. When I am fully matured...when you are fully matured, Master can thank me then.”","Her words rang with brilliance that made the Sacred Totems sing louder, their hymns becoming celebration of potential acknowledged!","Noah could only smile at this declaration.","That’s right.","Didn’t he seek an infinite path of progression? Of wonder that never ended? If one of the beings closest to him said they were just getting started, then truly... he was just getting started.","The thought filled him with anticipation.","He simply nodded to the Infiniverse, the gesture containing understanding, acceptance, and promise combined.","She nodded back, then closed her eyes with the serenity of someone embracing their destiny.","Brilliant white-gold light erupted from her form, blinding in its intensity yet somehow gentle, like being wrapped in possibility itself.","As this occured...","|The Early Veiled Shore recognizes its anchor: The Infinite Early Osmontian Shore|","|Synchronization beginning...|","The golden sands of thr Early Veiled Shore buzzed. The waters of endless blue shone! And...","|The Early Veiled Shore asserts: Screw the requirements for advancement.|","...!","1/4"]},{"number":4058,"title":"Chapter 4058: Chapter 4057: Osmontian! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4057: Osmontian! II","The Early Veiled Shore released a heavy prompt as after that, it only continued!","|Advancement conditions restructured. Upon reaching sufficient complexity through structures, farmlands, and populations, The Early Veiled Shore will advance from Blooming Shore and into a Radiant Shore|","|Estimated time: Whenever it damn well feels like it|","...!","Noah blinked with astonishment as he looked over these prompts, making sure he read them right!","Yet...","The brilliance intensified until even with closed eyes, Noah could see nothing but light.","Yet he could feel everything...every grain of sand reorganizing itself, every drop of Sacred Water becoming more sacred, every tree stretching its roots deeper into soil that was becoming more than soil.","Through the overwhelming sensory experience, he picked up voices beside him.","Sigrid, her own tremendous power humming with resonance, whispered with awe.","“What is this...?”","Nearby, Moiraine’s response came with the calm of someone who had witnessed miracles become routine. “You have not been here for too long. Stay a little bit longer, and what Sir is capable of doing will be even clearer to you.”","...!","Sir. It was heard again!","There was a pause, then Sigrid’s voice came again, quieter, almost to herself but loud enough for enhanced perception to catch.","“Does he...like to be called Sir?”","Noah kept his eyes closed while shaking his head slightly at these interactions.","He could feel Sigrid studying Moiraine, probably trying to understand the dynamics at play.","But these were considerations for later. Right now, he focused on feeling the tremendous changes occurring as the Infiniverse became something unprecedented...The Infinite Early Osmontian Shore!","The transformation wasn’t violent. It was like watching...feeling a flower bloom in reverse and forward simultaneously.","The Infiniverse’s consciousness was expanding, spreading through every frequency she contained.","She was choosing him over Everything else!","When Noah finally opened his eyes, the Infiniverse stood before him transformed, and still continued to be so!","She was still herself, that consciousness that had been with him since the beginning, but now she was also becoming something more.","The Infinite Early Osmontian Shore.","At this time, she looked at him once again.","“Master,” she said, and the word carried new meaning, new tyranny, new quintessence!","Around them, the Early Veiled Shore...no, the collaborative space they had created together, hummed with potential that made the impossible seem like a starting point.","They were, all of them, just getting started!","—","The rich, and the poor.","In existence, there have always been the rich and the poor, separated by more than wealth...divided by a veil of understanding so complete that neither side could truly comprehend how the other lived.","The poor imagined the rich as freed from all worry, swimming through life on currents of gold.","They couldn’t conceive of the particular anxieties that came with abundance...the paranoia about who truly cared for you versus your resources, the weight of maintaining what you’d gained, the hollow echo in rooms too large for any voice to fill.","The rich imagined the poor as simply lacking what they had, not understanding that poverty created its own culture, its own innovations, its own forms of wealth that couldn’t be measured in currency.","They couldn’t grasp the richness of community born from shared struggle, the creativity that emerged from limitation, the particular freedom that came from having nothing left to lose.","Neither side truly saw the other. The veil between them wasn’t just economic...it was existential.","But then there were those who lived inside the Infiniverse.","Here, rich or poor meant nothing. There was only power.","And power... was abundant to the point of absurdity.","Deep within the Infiniverse, inside a particular Frequency of Existence that hummed with its own laws of physics, stretched a world that defied understanding.","This was a planet that had decided to be thr size of a Cosmos- and yet it remained a solid stretch of land that extended for untold light-years in every direction!","Upon this impossible expanse lived quintillions of beings...a number so vast that counting them would take longer than most civilizations existed.","In one small corner of this world, small being relative when a corner could be larger than most solar systems...rose a citadel that housed mere millions.","The air itself was thick with golden mana of Helios, so concentrated that breathing was like drinking liquid power!","Occasionally, the oversaturation would spontaneously manifest as elemental sprites, beings of pure mana that flickered into existence, giggled with voices like ringing bells, then dissolved back into the atmosphere.","At the edge of this citadel stood a two-story building that would have seemed modest if not for the fact that its walls were carved from crystallized space and its windows opened onto different seasons simultaneously.","Nine figures stood huddled before it, their golden armaments manifested as pure Authority of Helios given form.","On each of their chests, the terrifying grandeur of an illusory cosmos slowly rotated.","Stars were born and died in the span of heartbeats across their armor. These beings had achieved the Cosmic Realm...they had passed through Antiquity, transcended the limitations of Daolords, and wielded their own Edicts that could rewrite local reality.","The concentrated mana flowing through them made their forms shimmer with power that would have been considered terrifying in lesser worlds!","Yet their expressions were somber, almost fearful, as if they were about to face an enemy that transcended their considerable might.","A butler emerged from the house, his formal attire somehow remaining crisp despite the sweat beading on his forehead. He looked at the nine with an expression that mixed professionalism with barely controlled panic.","“Sirs... it is about to come out. Please come in!”","The nine Cosmic Realm entities exchanged glances that would have been comical if not for the genuine concern they contained.","They entered the house with the careful movements of those walking into a situation they’d trained for but still dreaded.","Inside, runes of Helios covered every surface, glowing with protective power that made the air taste of sunshine and possibility.","At the center of the main room, a family clustered with concerned expressions. A doctor in a white-gold coat that seemed to be woven from solidified healing stood ready.","And in the middle of it all, on a bed that had been reinforced with reality-anchoring enchantments, lay a woman whose belly glowed with inner light.","She was...delivering a baby.","The nine Cosmic Realm entities faced her with expressions typically reserved for apocalyptic threats.","“He is coming!” the woman yelled, her voice mixing pain with worry that had nothing to do with normal childbirth concerns.","BOOM!","Golden light erupted from beneath her privacy coverings as a baby’s head emerged.","It was a cute little thing.","The infant was already giggling, its eyes open and tracking movement with awareness that newborns shouldn’t possess. More concerning were the tendrils of energy that immediately began gathering around the child, drawn like iron filings to a magnet.","“Get ready!” one of the Cosmic Realm beings shouted. “The first five seconds of life are the most dangerous!”","They positioned themselves strategically around the room as an immense influx of energy poured into the newly born baby. Then, with a pulse that made reality hiccup, a terrifying aura erupted from the infant.","On its tiny chest, a galaxy blazed into existence.","A newly born baby had achieved the Cosmic Realm!","2/4"]},{"number":4059,"title":"Chapter 4059: Chapter 4058: Everything has its uses! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4058: Everything has its uses! I","The infant giggled...a sound that was objectively adorable yet carried undertones that made the nine warriors tense!","Its mother smiled with the exhausted joy of successful childbirth, seemingly unconcerned that her baby possessed power that could shatter continents.","The leader of the nine roared with the urgency of someone who had seen what happened when they weren’t fast enough: “Get ready!”","BOOM!","The baby looked around with eyes that contained swirling nebulae, took its first step and...it was not a crawl.","It was a step through space itself!","Cracks spread across the reinforced floor as the infant shot toward a wall with the speed of a cosmic projectile.","One of the Cosmic Realm entities materialized instantly, a golden shield of pure Helios Authority manifesting to contain the baby’s trajectory. The infant bounced off, completely uninjured, laughing with the pure joy of play.","What followed was controlled chaos. The baby flew around the room, trying to headbutt everyone and everything with the enthusiasm of a puppy that happened to possess reality-warping power.","The nine entities worked with practiced coordination, containing each movement, reinforcing walls before impact, creating barriers of solidified space to prevent the infant from accidentally demolishing the house and then citadel.","This... wasn’t unusual.","This was life in the Infiniverse.","Babies could be born at the Universal Realm or Cosmic Filament Realm, arriving in existence with power that took others years to achieve.","Specific squads of adventurers were formed not to fight dragons or demons. They were formed to contain newly born entities until they developed enough cognizance to understand concepts like “please don’t accidentally shatter the neighbor’s house.”","It was a system that worked, mostly. The casualty rate for houses and cities was astronomical, but actual injuries were surprisingly rare.","As such a wonder was occuring.","Without warning, white-gold light bathed everything.","The transformation of the Infiniverse into the Infinite Early Osmontian Shore sent ripples through every Frequency, every world, every impossible corner of its vast expanse.","In that one house, as the baby continued its rampage of joy, one of the Cosmic Realm entities cursed with the frustration of someone whose difficult day had just gotten worse.","“What is it now?! What is it?!”","The answer came in sensation.","The atmospheric golden mana throughout the citadel, already so dense it was nearly solid...suddenly doubled. The baby, mid-flight toward another wall, suddenly blazed brighter as its single Cosmos began to grow larger- but so did the Cosmos of the Hunters!","The mother was in wonder.","The doctor, maintaining professional composure despite the chaos, checked his instruments that turned out to be utterly useless!","The baby, now possessing a larger cosmos on its chest and power that could reshape star systems, giggled again and tried to eat one of the containment shields.","It was a glorious scene.","The Infiniverse held many wonders!","Countless miracles that would have been impossibilities anywhere else. Entire civilizations that existed in the space between heartbeats. Cities built from crystallized mana. Oceans of liquid time where philosophers went fishing for concepts.","And life inside of it was unfathomably grand.","Even the mundane, like birth, became exercises in controlled catastrophe.","Even the simple act like containing a baby required power that could reshape worlds.","This was what it meant to exist inside something that was the Infiniverse, that had been nurtured by someone with infinite mana, that had chosen to become something unprecedented.","In the Infiniverse, now the Infinite Early Osmontian Shore...power wasn’t just abundant.","It was the baseline for existence itself!","—","Far from the Infiniverse, in the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds where reality questioned its own rules, the Doorway to the Loom stood.","The Living Origins had departed, leaving behind only the taste of failure in air that shouldn’t have taste.","Now the Living Paradoxes moved through the space, following Duke Schrodinger as he walked the winding obsidian-crimson pathways with the air of someone strolling through a garden.","Duke Elagabalus floated beside him, his radiant obsidian crown rotating above his head like a captured black hole. The crown cast shadows that existed in more dimensions than light should create, and his expression carried the weight of someone processing disturbing information.","“The weavings of Paradox within this Doorway,” he began, his voice measured and grim, “they’re forever altered. Look at how it flows now...in patterns, in sequences that repeat and resolve. The chaos that should define this space, the wild unpredictability that makes Paradox what it is...”","He gestured at the walls around them, where white light had left its mark like scars on reality. “It’s been made ordered. Tamed. This isn’t how Paradox should behave.”","Schrodinger nodded calmly at this assessment, his beggar’s appearance somehow making his lack of concern more pronounced.","He continued forward with steady steps that suggested he had expected this.","Duke Diviticus approached from behind, her form radiating power that seemed barely contained by existence itself.","She had leaped from Honored Living Existence to Duke with speed that defied normal progression, and even now her authority continued to expand into realms that made other Dukes observe her closely!","“When will we put the Animated Corpse of the Early Creature into play?” Her eyes blazed as she spoke, intensity making the air around her waver. “I have all this power, yet I feel stifled that I cannot even use it properly. With the Animated Corpse, reaching the Loom will be-”","Schrodinger shook his head, the gesture so simple yet carrying enough weight to stop her mid-sentence.","Diviticus frowned, her carefully maintained composure cracking slightly. She held her emotions back...everyone here knew the terrifying power Schrodinger wielded, had seen glimpses of what he could do.","But in her current position, with the power she now commanded, did she truly have no say? She alone controlled that Animated Corpse of an Early Creature. Surely that counted for something?","As if reading her thoughts...and perhaps he was, perhaps thoughts were just another paradox he could observe,Schrodinger turned to look at her directly.","His eyes, ancient despite his beggar’s appearance, contained depths that suggested he had seen this scenario play out before, many times, with many different players.","“Do you feel powerful now?” His question emerged with the gentleness of a teacher addressing a student who had learned just enough to be dangerous.","“Do you believe you can do anything? That with a mere corpse of an Early Creature, even the Loom will be within your grasp?”","HUUM!","3/4"]},{"number":4060,"title":"Chapter 4060: Chapter 4059: Everything has its uses! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4059: Everything has its uses! II","Before she could respond, five distant roars echoed through the twisted passages. The sound of Inevitabilities hunting, their cries carrying paradoxes that made them simultaneously near and far, approaching and retreating.","Schrodinger didn’t even glance in their direction, his focus remaining entirely on Diviticus.","“Eons ago, in the Earliest Folds, even Early Creatures...living ones, not animated corpses, could not enter the Loom. Living Existences tried and were turned away or transformed beyond recognition. Fold Dwellers who attempted it simply ceased, edited out of possibility.”","He began walking again, forcing Diviticus and the others to follow as the roars grew closer.","“Now you have obtained a corpse. Not even a complete one, but fragments held together by your will and paradox. Do you think this grants you the power of a genuine Early Creature? Do you believe you can walk across the Folds unfettered? That nothing can kill you now?”","His voice carried no mockery, only the patient tone of someone explaining why fire burns to a child who had just been mesmerized by pretty flames!","“Do not be drunk on power, O Diviticus. That intoxication has killed more beings than all the wars in existence combined.”","BOOM!","Five Inevitabilities burst from the twisted space ahead, their forms writhing masses of tentacles that existed in states that predated the separation between is and isn’t. Several Dukes immediately prepared to engage them, paradoxical energies beginning to manifest.","But Schrodinger raised one hand, a simple gesture that carried absolute command. Everyone stopped.","He floated forward alone, approaching the Inevitabilities with the confidence of someone greeting old friends.","Diviticus clenched her fists, her expression ashen. She was being lectured, corrected, put in her place...and in front of everyone!","The humiliation burned worse than any attack could have.","Yet what happened next made that humiliation transform into something else entirely.","The Inevitabilities’ tentacles, which had been writhing with hunger and paradox, suddenly stilled. They moved toward Schrodinger not with aggression, and instead with something that looked impossibly like recognition. Then, even more impossibly, friendliness!","Schrodinger reached out and stroked the tentacles as one might pet a beloved dog. The gesture was so casual, so natural, that it took several moments for the observers to process what they were seeing.","This was just the tip of the power Schrodinger possessed...or so they thought!","As he continued stroking the paradoxical appendages, Schrodinger turned back toward Diviticus.","“Let me tell you something about power. Actually, let me show you. No story this time.” His smile contained layers that contradicted themselves. “Go ahead. Use your newfound strength that you draw from that Little Corpse, and attack me.”","The challenge buzzed the air like a paradox waiting to resolve.","Diviticus felt her confidence evaporate. She looked toward Duke Elagabalus and the others, seeking support or perhaps hoping someone would intervene. But when her gaze met theirs, they turned away with the synchronized precision of those who wanted no part in what was about to happen.","She sighed, frustration mixing with apprehension, and turned back to face Schrodinger.","Her body began to seethe with terrifying obsidian waves mixed with white radiance...the paradoxical power of death given motion, authority that could unmake existence itself.","She gathered this power, feeling it course through her with intensity that made her feel truly invincible. This was the might of an Early Creature, even if borrowed from a corpse. Surely this would-","BZZT!","At that moment.","Schrodinger turned around and pulled out a leaf.","A small, white leaf that looked like it might have fallen from any tree in any garden in any world.","The moment it appeared, Diviticus felt her entire existence constrict.","The power that had been surging through her didn’t just diminish.","It vanished completely, as if it had never existed. Her body, suddenly bereft of the authority that had been supporting it, became impossibly heavy.","She fell to the obsidian-crimson floor with a sound like a sack of mundane matter hitting stone. No grace, no power, just gravity asserting itself on something that had forgotten it was subject to such basic forces!","...!","Schrodinger sighed, the sound containing genuine disappointment rather than mockery.","He put the leaf away...just tucked it into his tattered robes as if it were a handkerchief, and floated down to help her up.","His hands were gentle as he raised her from the floor, steadying her as strength slowly returned to her limbs.","“Just because you’ve gained power,” he said, his voice kind despite the lesson’s harshness, “doesn’t mean you can do everything. Even a tiny leaf like that can bring down what traces of an Early Creature’s power you’ve bound yourself to.”","He continued supporting her as feeling returned to her extremities.","“You have to be steady. Patient. You are young...you all are. There is so much more room for growth that you cannot even imagine. Power isn’t about what you can destroy. It’s about understanding what can destroy you.”","...!","The words buzzed.","They deserved to be repeated!","Power was not about what you can destroy...it was about understanding what can destroy you!","Oh!","As authority flowed back into Diviticus’s form, she took several quick steps away from Schrodinger, fear replacing her earlier confidence.","The ease with which he had reduced her to nothing, the casual nature of her complete defeat...","Schrodinger shook his head at her retreat, then turned his attention back to the Inevitabilities.","He began waving his hands in patterns, and streams of paradoxical light emerged from his form. But these weren’t the chaotic paradoxes that defined their nature, these were structured contradictions, ordered impossibilities.","The tendrils of paradox he emitted wrapped around the Inevitabilities, and their calm demeanor shattered. They screeched as their very nature was denied. Their tentacles thrashed in confusion as existence told them they were one thing while Schrodinger’s power insisted they were another.","A golden square prison materialized around them, its walls made from crystallized contradiction!","The Inevitabilities were contained by being unable to resolve what they were supposed to be!","From the back of the group, Duke Elagabalus found his voice: “What are you doing?”","Schrodinger’s smile contained genuine amusement. “You wouldn’t understand even if I answered. To grasp even a fraction of it, you would need to listen to another one of my stories. Do you have the time?”","Duke Elagabalus’s expression soured, recognizing the trap.","Refuse, and remain ignorant. Accept, and endure another of Schrodinger’s parables that might or might not be true but would definitely make them question everything they thought they knew.","He sighed with the resignation of someone who had made this choice before. “It seems like we have all the time in Existence.”","Schrodinger laughed, the sound containing genuine pleasure at having a captive audience.","“In the Earliest Folds,” he began, settling into his storytelling posture, “there was a terrifying Existence known as The First Hunger. Not the first to hunger...that would be impossible to determine, but the first to make Hunger itself into identity, into purpose, into philosophy.”","The other Paradoxes drew closer despite themselves, pulled by the gravity of narrative.","“The First Hunger...Khor was her name, though names meant less then, encountered a group of Early Creatures who were being disciplined by THE Living Dimensional. Now, THE Living Dimensional was not known for patience. It existed in all dimensions simultaneously, which meant it could be angry with you in seventeen different ways at once.”","A few nervous chuckles emerged from the audience.","“THE Living Dimensional was demanding these Early Creatures tell it what their Everything meant. Each answer they gave...their power, their purpose, their existence itself, it deemed wrong. Not incorrect, but wrong, as if the answers offended reality itself.”","Schrodinger’s voice took on different tones as he embodied the characters.","“When Khor passed by, she laughed with genuine amusement at the scene. She asked THE Living Dimensional if she could answer the question instead.”","He shifted, his posture somehow becoming more rigid, more multiply-present.","“THE Living Dimensional did not like Khor’s appearance...beings like her made it uncomfortable, existing as they did outside its dimensional framework. But it grudgingly asked what answer she had.”","Back to Khor’s voice, lighter but containing depths, Schrodinger continued.","“She smiled and gave multiple answers. ‘Everything is what you’re willing to lose.’ Then... ‘Everything is what you can’t imagine losing.’ And... ‘Everything is the sum of what defines you, until you give it away and discover you’re still defined.'”","...!","The gathered Paradoxes listened with rapt attention despite themselves.","“Then Khor looked directly at THE Living Dimensional and asked if she should tell it what its Everything meant. THE Living Dimensional, for perhaps the first time in its existence, chose not to know something. It snorted, a sound that created three new dimensions just to contain it, and disappeared.”","Schrodinger let the story settle before continuing.","“Everything is a heavy topic, but Inevitabilities have the capability to devour Everything. To devour Meaning itself.” He gestured to the contained Inevitability. “This one here has devoured part of the Everything of the one responsible for spreading that brilliant white light. Any Everything is precious, even that which is given away. If one cuts off a limb, it doesn’t mean that limb becomes useless...it might be exactly what someone else needs.”","His smile grew mysterious.","“This Inevitability will have its uses to me. I also like to experiment every now and then.”","Diviticus and the others stared in astonishment!","4/4"]},{"number":4061,"title":"Chapter 4061: Chapter 4060: The Weight of Sin! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4060: The Weight of Sin! I","An Inevitability could have its uses.","The words hummed in the twisted air of the Doorway like a paradox waiting to be resolved.","The powerful Living Paradoxes gathered around Schrodinger stood in various states of bewilderment, their expressions ranging from confusion to contemplation.","Even after listening to his stories...tales that might have been truth or might have been elaborate metaphors, they still couldn’t claim to truly understand what he meant.","Schrodinger seemed to sense their confusion with the particular awareness of someone who had grown accustomed to being steps ahead of those around him.","He shook his head dismissively with the resignation of a teacher who knew some lessons couldn’t be taught, only experienced.","He turned to Duke Elagabalus, his gaze sharpening with intent.","“Elagabalus, what do you know about Inevitabilities?”","The Duke took a moment to consider, recognizing the weight of the question.","The question felt like an examination, evaluation, perhaps even a judgment. When he spoke, his voice had the measured cadence of someone choosing each word with care.","“Inevitabilities are the contradictions that existence couldn’t resolve,” he began, his obsidian crown rotating slowly above his head as if responding to his thoughts. “They are what happens when possibility and impossibility occupy the same space for too long. They preceded even THE Creature...existed before existence had properly defined itself.”","He paused, gathering his thoughts like someone arranging pieces on a board only he could see.","He seemed about to continue when Schrodinger nodded and began speaking out again.","“Somewhat correct...”","...!","“Inevitabilities are hunger without satiation, seeking without finding, destruction without purpose. But somewhere along the line...and the histories disagree on when or how, there came to be a division. Mutated Inevitabilities and regular Inevitabilities. One... will accept what you choose to give. The other simply takes, caring nothing for choice or consent.”","Schrodinger’s smile bloomed slowly.","“Mutated Inevitabilities and Inevitabilities...” He let the words settle into the space between them. “Mutated... this is a unique word, don’t you think? It implies change from an original state. Deviation from what should be.”","His expression grew more serious, the weight of ages pressing through his beggar’s appearance.","“The Sin that Paradoxes carry. The Sin of Inevitabilities is intricately connected to our lives.” He looked at each of them in turn, his gaze carrying questions that transcended simple curiosity.","“You all may not have been alive at a time when Living Paradoxes... did not produce Inevitabilities just by coming together. But I remember. I was there when it changed.”","The admission sent ripples through the gathered Dukes.","To have existed before Paradoxes created Inevitabilities meant Schrodinger was older than most could comprehend...older than the current structure of Existence itself!","“I think about it often,” he continued, his voice growing softer but somehow more intense. “Did we deserve this unique Way of Existence imposed upon us? Did we Sin to deserve this curse...to create destruction simply by gathering, to birth hunger just by existing near each other?”","He spread his hands in a gesture that wanted to encompass not just those present but all Paradoxes across existence.","“Why did the Sin of THE Paradox fall on us? I ask myself this question. I continue to ask myself. Do any of you happen to have an answer?”","The silence that followed was absolute.","The Dukes floated in contemplation, each wrestling with a question that struck at the heart of their nature. Why were they cursed to create Inevitabilities? What ancient transgression had marked their entire classification of existence?","Duke Diviticus opened her mouth as if to speak, then closed it again.","Duke Elagabalus’s crown spun faster, reflecting his agitation.","Others simply stared into distances that existed beyond physical space, seeking answers in memories that might never have existed.","Schrodinger shook his head in understanding.","Some questions weren’t meant to have answers, only to be asked.","He turned and began dragging the chained Inevitability toward the Doorway’s entrance.","The golden prison scraped against the obsidian-crimson floor with sounds that shouldn’t exist, leaving trails of contradictory light in its wake.","As he moved ahead of the other Paradoxes, he spoke without turning back, his voice carrying the weight of purpose that transcended personal desire.","“I will continue to do things many of you do not understand. Actions that seem without logic, movements that appear without purpose. But I won’t be doing them for myself.”","He paused at the threshold between the Doorway and the outer Folds, his silhouette framed by impossible geometries.","“I have lived...longer than most of you can imagine. I have loved deeper than paradox itself. Everything I do now, I do for the sake of Living Paradoxes. For the Sin we should not bear. For the curse we never earned.”","His voice grew stronger, more certain, as if speaking truths he had only recently accepted himself.","“I do what I do because too many have suffered through the hands and choices of others. Because decisions made in the Earliest Folds still echo through existence, shaping fates that were never consulted about their shaping. I do what I do for all Living Existences, whether they know it or not. Whether they would thank me or curse me for it.”","Then, with a shift that was purely Schrodinger, his serious expression cracked into a self-deprecating smile.","“Or...who knows? Maybe I’m doing it all for myself in the end. Such is life. Such is existence. We tell ourselves stories about our motivations and hope they’re true.”","...!","With those words, he disappeared through the entrance, dragging his imprisoned Inevitability with him. The Dukes of Living Paradoxes looked at each other with expressions that mixed confusion, respect, and the particular exhaustion that came from trying to understand Schrodinger.","They sighed collectively...a sound that created small paradoxes in the air, and followed him once more.","Among all the renowned Living Paradoxes in existence, few held as much pull and terrifying grandeur as Schrodinger.","Whether they understood him or not, they would follow, because the alternative was missing whatever impossible thing he would do next!","1/5 !"]},{"number":4062,"title":"Chapter 4062: Chapter 4061: The Weight of Sin! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4061: The Weight of Sin! II","In Aeternitas Concordia.","Duke Whisker sat atop the roof of a building with the casual air of a common mouse enjoying the view.","But his stellar eyes were focused intently on the anomaly below...the being he considered either an Early Creature or one of the terrifying Fold Dwellers from the Wandering Territories.","He watched as Osmont gave away multiple bowls of that precious soup, trading them for treasures from the Doorways to the Loom.","But more interesting were the bowls he gave away freely...no trade, no bargain, just gifts to weak Fold Dwellers who seemed to know him.","Duke Whisker’s perception pierced through surface appearances, reading the fundamental information of existence itself.","These Fold Dwellers came from a paradoxical minor fold, and stemmed from the Veiled Sunfolds specifically.","Their power levels were negligible by any standard that mattered. Yet Osmont treated them with genuine care, handing them bowls of treasure that could elevate existence itself.","As they consumed the soup, their complexity and purity began surging upward with speed that would have cost fortunes to achieve.","The mouse’s whiskers twitched with thought. This behavior further validated the theory that Osmont was a powerful Fold Dweller from the Wandering Territories...they were known for their solidarity, their care for their own. But...","Duke Whisker’s instincts, honed across eons of existence, insisted it couldn’t be that simple. There were layers here, depths that he hadn’t yet fathomed.","He found himself staring with perhaps too much concentration, his gaze carrying more power than intended.","The weight of his observation must have registered, because Osmont looked up with a smile that suggested he had been aware of the scrutiny all along.","“Do not stress and think about things too much,” Noah called out, his voice carrying easily across the distance that should have muffled it. “Since I am in a good mood... I’m feeling generous, so you can have a bowl as well!”","Without waiting for a response, Noah scooped a bowl from one of the Glass Woks beside him. With a casual gesture, he sent it floating up toward Duke Whisker.","The bowl was nearly five times the mouse’s size, requiring him to adjust his position to receive it properly. Duke Whisker’s eyes shone with genuine interest as he examined the contents...a stellar white-gold soup that seemed to contain condensed possibility.","Duke Whisker did not truly know what it was made of, but this single bowl held the meat of Early Living Marine Lifeforms that floated in Early Sacred Water, creating a combination that shouldn’t exist outside of the Earliest Folds!","He knew not thr contents, but he gave Noah a simple nod of acknowledgment, recognizing the gesture for what it was.","Then, with the practicality that defined him, he waved his tiny paws to produce a block of stellar cheese from wherever he kept such things.","He dipped the cheese into the soup, watching it absorb the scintillating liquid. When he took that first bite...","BOOM!","His small body buzzed with resonance that went beyond simple nourishment!","His existence itself was being refined, elevated, made more real than it had been moments before!","He breathed out with contentment that transcended the physical, feeling determination crystallize within him like a new organ.","Determination.","He was filled with determination!","“That is good stuff!” The words emerged with genuine appreciation.","He continued eating, dipping block after block of stellar cheese into the soup with the focus of someone who understood they were consuming something precious.","Around him, the busy market filled with Fold Dwellers and Living Existences watched this scene with bewilderment that bordered on outrage.","This ridiculous merchant had just given away freely what others were offering treasures to obtain.","First to unknown Fold Dwellers, now to what appeared to be a common mouse.","What was the logic when he was simultaneously turning away others who came with significant offerings?","They couldn’t fathom it because they didn’t understand the intricate web of weavings and power playing out before them!","At that moment, Duke Whisker received a mental message from Duke Gwendolyn, her thoughts carrying frustration that blazed across the connection.","“Duke Whisker... are you really of the stance to leave this as is? That is THE Living Order! The Young Miss! She needs to be in the folds and care of Living Origins and nobody else. I say this knowing full well that we don’t entirely know Osmont’s origins, but he cannot get all this leeway... the Young Miss...”","Duke Whisker shook his head, the gesture sharp enough to cut through her words despite her physical absence.","He dipped another block of cheese as he formulated his response, ensuring each word would land with appropriate weight.","“If you do not trust Osmont,” he replied mentally, his ‘voice’ carrying the patience of someone explaining something that should be obvious, “then trust the Young Miss.”","...!","He took another bite, savoring both the soup and the point he was making.","“You say she needs to do this or that. That she needs to be with the Living Origins. That she needs to follow all these prescribed paths. But that is what you believe she needs. If she truly is THE Living Order, do you not think she knows what she herself requires?”","Another dip, another bite. The soup really was exceptional.","“Simply trust in her judgment. Do you think THE Living Order would be moving with Osmont if she didn’t want to? She should have sufficient power to leave whenever she chooses. If she doesn’t even have the mere power to separate from someone like Osmont when desired, then she wouldn’t truly be THE Living Order, would she?”","He paused, letting that logic settle.","“So simply... trust in her. She is no child needing protection. She is Order itself, choosing her path.”","In a distant place within Aeternitas Concordia, Duke Gwendolyn received these words with an expression that cycled through several stages of emotion.","Her features soured as she tried to find flaws in Duke Whisker’s logic, but the argument was frustratingly solid!","2/5"]},{"number":4063,"title":"Chapter 4063: Chapter 4062: Of Glory and Principles! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4062: Of Glory and Principles! I","She could only watch the distant scene of the man who had made her kneel for a drop of wonder. The memory burned, but as she examined it more carefully, she wondered whether maintaining hostility was wise when previously they had maintained a decent, even productive relationship.","Her mind calculated possibilities with the speed of someone who had played political games for eons.","He had the trust of the Young Miss.","Now the trust of Duke Whisker.","Duke Gwendolyn had lived long enough to see empires rise and fall on the strength of a few key relationships. She had witnessed friendships that reshaped reality and enmities that unmade Folds. Words alone could forge or ruin everything.","She clenched her fists, feeling the weight of what needed to be done.","For the sake of the Young Miss, didn’t she say she would do anything? If swallowing her pride and rebuilding bridges with Osmont was required, then that’s what she would do. Not because she wanted to, but because necessity demanded it.","All for the sake of Order.","For the sake of the Young Miss.","“Okay.”","The word emerged as both acceptance and determination. She breathed deeply, then dove into the depths of her existence to rewire her mentality.","It was a skill all long-lived beings developed...the ability to consciously adjust their perspectives when circumstances demanded it.","Moments later, she reached out again, but this time her mental touch sought Osmont directly.","“We... no, I,” she began, the correction showing her commitment to taking personal responsibility, “wish to simply ascertain that the Young Miss is safe and to meet with her. What do you want in return for this? What do you want from the Living Origins? From a Duke like me that I could provide?”","The message carried sincerity that cost her more than any treasure could have.","But sometimes, the most valuable currency in existence was the willingness to admit you might have been wrong!","In the market below, Noah’s smile grew slightly wider, though he continued serving customers as if nothing had changed.","He continued his movements with other bodies throughout existence, and truly, he was in a good mood at this moment.","The transformation of the Infiniverse into the Infinite Early Osmontian Shore was something worthy of celebration!","Far from Aeternitas Concordia.","In the Early Veiled Shore.","The overwhelming white-gold light that had bathed everything began to dim, drawing itself inward to be contained within the Infiniverse’s form.","The light didn’t disappear...it concentrated, becoming something more potent through compression.","|The Infinite Early Osmontian Shore stands for the sake of elevating none other than The Early Creature, Osmont|","The prompt buzzed before Noah’s perception with weight that transcended simple notification. This was a declaration of singular dedication that reshaped what the Infiniverse could become!","|During transformation, the Infiniverse is dedicating emerging complexity as the Infinite Early Osmontian Shore toward immediate assistance of her Master, and is converging authority of all accumulated True Sources and complexity of her transformation for the understanding of the Failed Seed of Perpetual Harvest|","HUUM!","More prompts cascaded with information that made Noah’s eyes narrow with focus.","|The Infiniverse foregoes additional features beyond current Early Veiled Shore capabilities|","|Singular focus: Understanding the failure of the First Farmer.|","| The Infiniverse has been an object of endless harvest through its existences|","|Recognition- The Shore within represents perpetual advancement and harvest without cessation, and such weavings are imposed on the Failed Seed.|","...!","Noah felt the beat of his heart quicken as he watched and observed!","|Declaration- The Infiniverse places entirety of identity as missing material for the Failed Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest|","|Knowledge of perpetual harvest flows freely through transformed structure|","Noah looked with solemnity at the Infiniverse, who stood tall and glorious in her transformed state.","Her dress of multicolored jewels...each one a Frequency made manifest, caught light of glory. She was possibility given form, and she had chosen to limit that possibility for his sake.","She placed her hand over her chest, directly above where her heart would be if she were bound by such mundane anatomy. When she spoke, her voice carried the weight of absolute commitment.","“If I could give you my Everything, Master, I would. Since I cannot, since Everything is too heavy even for me to fully surrender, I will give everything I can for the things you want to achieve most.”","...!","The declaration rang through the Shore with the clarity of a bell that had never been struck yet always been ringing.","|The Infiniverse stakes her Everything on realignment and revitalization of Failed Seed|","|Her vast Everything has been measured and found...quintessentially sufficient and viable|","Noah’s eyes buzzed as he read the next prompt!","|Against all odds, the Failed Seed of Perpetual Harvest accepts weavings of perpetuity|","|The Failed Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest sheds its failure|","|The Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest has been born!|","BOOM!","The moment arrived with force that made existence itself take notice.","On the plot where the Failed Seed had rested in patient failure for untold eons, something unprecedented occurred.","The seed began a change that transcended its own nature!","A terrifyingly radiant green-gold seed arose from the soil, its emergence causing ripples through reality that would be felt in places that hadn’t been invented yet. The seed appeared as a golden core with a verdant leaf flowing behind and beneath it, as if the leaf were both shadow and throne, support and declaration.","Titano, massive and ancient, felt his existence buzz with recognition that transcended memory.","For the first time since his awakening, he felt belonging...fundamental rightness. The aura emanating from the seed matched something within him, something that predated his consciousness.","An aura of ancientness. The quality of having existed before existence properly organized itself.","A glimpse of...a Principle!","He looked toward Noah and the radiant Infiniverse with an expression that his simple features struggled to convey.","Was this actually home? Not just a place to be, but a place where his nature was understood, even celebrated?","His eyes buzzed with possibility!","3/5"]},{"number":4064,"title":"Chapter 4064: Chapter 4063: Of Glory and Principles! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4063: Of Glory and Principles! II","Two figures materialized near the floating Seed with the ceremony of those approaching something sacred.","Yoshinami appeared first, her form resolving from possibility into presence.","Her crimson eyes...weapons and windows simultaneously, burned with longing and recognition that spoke of memories too deep for words.","Her dark hair flowed like liquid night, and her dress seemed cut from shadows that had learned to be solid.","Beside her, Heidrun manifested with equal gravity. The goat’s form might have seemed mundane if not for the weight of ages she carried, the knowledge contained in eyes that had seen the rise and fall of concepts themselves.","Both gazed at the Seed with expressions that mixed wonder and pain.","Where they had come from...the Shores of Early Creatures, the Wandering Territories, there had been glimpses of authority like this.","The authority of a Principle. But those had been fading echoes, dying lights of what once was.","Would they truly witness something like that again here? Not just witness, but participate in its birth?","Yoshinami’s voice emerged like a song that had been waiting eons to be sung. It echoed across the Shore with haunting beauty that made Existence and everyone else pay attention!","“Principles were there to protect when all else failed,” she began, her words carrying the weight of witnessed truth. “When Early Creatures hunted with hunger that knew no satiation, Principles stood as shields for those who could not shield themselves. When Inevitabilities devoured with appetite that transcended reason, Principles were there to reverse what should have been irreversible.”","DUM! DUM! DUM!","The beat lf glorious drumbs began to be heard!","Her voice grew stronger, more certain, as if drawing power from memory itself.","“Principles cradled orphans whose parents had been edited from existence. They aided those whose need transcendence what help could provide. Principles...established standing that could not be devoured, foundations that remained when everything else was stripped away.”","The poetry of her words created its own rhythm, its own music that resonated with something fundamental in the Shore itself!","DUM! DUM!","As Yoshinami’s melody continued, the Sacred Totems began to buzz with sympathetic vibration.","Their bells rang out a unique melody...not the hymns they had sung before but something older, more fundamental!","Heidrun began to move, her hooves creating rhythm on the golden sands. But this wasn’t random movement!","This was ritual given form, dance that had been choreographed before choreography existed.","Each strike of hoof on sand echoed melodiously, creating counterpoint to Yoshinami’s words and the Totems’ bells.","|Rituals of old and early bloom once more|","|The Early Veiled Shore is gripped with atmosphere of complexity and glory!|","|Advent of Seed of Perpetual Harvest elevated through ceremony|","|Due to enabling its emergence, the Infiniverse gains right to forge a glorious Glyph- the Kleos Early Living Existential Seed Glyph of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest|","On the Infiniverse’s forehead, light began to coalesce.","Not just any light, but the condensed possibility of what principles meant!","The Kleos Glyph that began forming there wasn’t simply powerful...it was conceptually overwhelming, a mark that declared its bearer had touched something that transcended normal hierarchies of power.","The Infiniverse herself had transformed further.","She now floated above a verdant gold leaf that served as both throne and declaration, mirroring the leaf that supported the Seed itself.","The synchronicity wasn’t coincidence but recognition...the Seed acknowledging its savior by sharing its imagery.","The Glyph continued forming, each line that appeared carrying weight that made space reconsider its properties:","|Early Living Existential Seed Glyph – Principle of Perpetual Harvest|","|Standard requirement to form: 100 Billion Complexity and Purity|","|Grants utilization of 1% of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest’s power|","|Due to actions bringing its fruition, the Glyph forms naturally for the Infiniverse!|","|Infiniverse’s transformation enables automatic formation|","HUUM!","Waves of brilliance erupted from the Infiniverse, encompassing Noah in light that felt like being wrapped in possibility itself.","Verdant gold leaves began blooming around him...simply deciding to exist, as if they had always been there and were just now choosing to be visible.","|As the Master of the Infiniverse, Early Living Existential Seed Glyph of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest is available for construction|","|Reduced requirement for you: 25 Billion Complexity and Purity|","...!","Noah’s eyes blazed with tyrannical fervor as he read this. The possibility of accessing even a fraction of a Principle’s power...the implications were heavy!","|The Seed of Perpetual Harvest burns with achievement and has began paying respect to its creator in failure and enabler of its success|","|A Historical Record of Seed’s purpose preparing for display|","|Record contains original intent and current actualization of the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest.|","...!","From both the floating Seed and the Infiniverse’s transformed figure, green-gold light flashed outward.","It burrowed into the eyes of everyone present invitingly, carrying information too complex for simple communication. Even those in the Abode of the Early Creature received this gift of knowledge!","|Historical Record of Seed of Perpetual Harvest shall unfold|","|All witnesses shall receive boons of harvest|","...!","Before everyone’s consciousness, the green-gold light resolved into scene and substance.","A history began to unfold before them!","Glorioud scenes that many never even imagined.","They found themselves observing...not traveling to but witnessing, the Earliest Folds.","A place countless eons ago, when principles were ideas rather than forces.","The scene that unfolded showed the First Farmer in his element.","He stood in a farming plot where green-gold seeds grew in patterns that suggested mathematics given agricultural form.","The First Farmer himself appeared surprisingly humble...not the towering figure of legend but someone who looked like they had spent eternity working soil that existed before soil was invented.","His hands showed calluses from handling tools that shaped Existence itself, and his eyes carried the particular weariness of someone who had failed more times than success was possible.","He held a single seed, cradling it with the care one might show a newborn universe.","“What I envision for you,” he said to the seed...and impossibly, incredibly, the seed was listening, “is to embody perpetual harvest. Not just endless growth, but the principle that effort invested should always yield returns.”","...!","Effort invested should always yield returns!","4/5"]},{"number":4065,"title":"Chapter 4065: Chapter 4064: Of Glory and Principles! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4064: Of Glory and Principles! III","The seed pulsed with light that suggested consideration.","“I can grow without cessation,” it replied, its voice like wind through grain that would never exist. “I can ensure that what is planted always yields. I can make the soil rich regardless of its nature.”","The First Farmer shook his head gently. “That is mechanics. I speak of principle. When someone works toward something...anything, their effort should harvest results. When they plant kindness, they should harvest connection. When they sow knowledge, they should harvest understanding.”","“You wish me to accelerate not just farming but existence itself,” the seed said with growing comprehension. “To make reality more generous with its rewards.”","“Exactly!” The First Farmer’s excitement made him seem younger, more vital. “Imagine...existence where trying always matters, where effort is never wasted, where even failure plants seeds for future success. You would make Existence itself more fertile.”","...!","Effort!","Trying!","The seed pulsed brighter, its light carrying warmth that transcended temperature.","“I could speed the growth of not just plants but possibilities. Make patience yield results faster. Transform waiting from emptiness into active cultivation.”","“Yes, and more,” the First Farmer continued, his words painting visions of what could be. “You would be the principle that ensures harvest. Not guaranteeing success...that would break important lessons, but ensuring that something always grows from what is planted. Even from salted earth, even from poisoned ground, something could emerge if the farmer’s intent is true.”","They continued this exchange, philosopher and possibility discussing what principle meant.","But as their conversation reached its crescendo, the seed’s light dimmed with sorrow.","“I am missing a critical component,” it admitted, its voice heavy with the weight of incomplete potential. “I cannot become a Seed of Perpetual Harvest without a perpetual force of harvest driving me. The principle is sound, the mechanics are prepared, but the engine... the engine is absent.”","The First Farmer’s expression crumbled from hope to sorrow with speed that suggested practice.","He had failed before. He would fail again. But this failure felt heavier because the success had been so close.","He tried.","He tried again!","And still he failed.","They watched such a thing happen again and again.","Until the First Farmer cried.","He cradled the failed seed against his chest, and when he spoke, his words carried the particular pain of dreams deferred.","“Even though I failed here today, there will come a time when principles bloom like weeds after rain. I will form Seeds of Principles one after another, until the very concept of principle must acknowledge my existence.” His voice grew stronger, more certain. “I will become the Farmer of Principles themselves!”","HUUM!","With those words of mingled sorrow and determination, the Historical Record shattered like glass made of memory.","Everyone’s vision returned to the Early Veiled Shore, consciousness snapping back to the present with the particular disorientation of having witnessed something that transcended normal experience.","It was heavy.","Oh so heavy!","|For observing a grand Record, a Harvest has been Awarded|","|+500 Million Complexity and Purity granted to all observers|","...!","The moment this prompt appeared, bodies throughout the Shore exploded with power.","Fundamentally, existence itself acknowledging their growth and was adjusting to accommodate it!","Sigrid gasped as her already tremendous complexity surged even higher, but this was not the main point of shock.","She looked toward Noah with shock that transcended her usual composure, her eyes asking questions her mouth couldn’t form.","Beside her, Moiraine maintained better control but couldn’t hide the wonder in her expression as power flowed through her like rivers that had just discovered they were oceans.","The Early Living Existential Seed Glyph finished forming on the Infiniverse’s forehead with a pulse of completion that made existence acknowledge something new had been born.","When she opened her eyes, waves of green-gold brilliance exploded outward with force that was somehow both gentle and overwhelming.","|Early Living Existential Seed Glyph – Principle of Perpetual Harvest: COMPLETE|","HUUM!","|Current Access: 1% of the Principle’s Authority|","|Capabilities Unlocked:|","|Harvest Festival Endowment|","– Once per day, grant Endowment to chosen target","– Complexity/Purity gain based on recipient’s existence and worthiness","– Minimum increase: 1 Billion","– Maximum increase: Undefined","|Perpetual Growth Field|","– 100 Fold radius of accelerated development","– All growth (physical, existential, conceptual) increased by 10,000%","– Affects plants, beings, and concepts equally","– Field moves with Infiniverse","|Effort Multiplication|","– Any work performed within sight gains exponential returns","– Failed attempts plant “Seeds of Future Success”","– These seeds activate when conditions align","– No effort is ever truly wasted","|Fertility Beyond Soil|","– Can make anything capable of growth","– Ideas can be planted and cultivated","– Emotions can be farmed for power","– Concepts can be harvested once matured","|Recursive Harvest|","– Each harvest creates seeds for next harvest","– Each generation 10% more potent than previous","– Can stack infinitely with patience","– Works on abstract concepts","|The First Farmer’s Blessing|","– Daily blessing that prevents total failure","– If something would fail completely, minimal success occurs instead","– Turns “nothing” into “something small but real”","– Cannot be blocked or negated","...!","Oh.","Oh!!!","Noah read through these capabilities with alarm that transformed into shock, then evolved into something approaching awe.","The implications of even one of these abilities were staggering. Together, they represented power thst was just...ah!","The Infiniverse looked at him with eyes that contained universes of devotion.","“This,” she said simply, “will be one of my first gifts to Master.”","The word ‘first’ hung in the air with promise that suggested she was, indeed, just getting started.","Around them, the Early Veiled Shore itself seemed to pulse with new potential.","The birth of a Principle, even a Seed of one, had changed something fundamental about what was possible here. The golden sands seemed more golden. The Sacred Waters seemed more sacred. The very air carried possibility that hadn’t existed moments before!","The Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest floated in its plot, glowing with satisfaction of purpose finally achieved. It had waited through failure that lasted eons, maintained by nothing but the First Farmer’s hope that someday, somehow, it would find what it needed.","Now it had not just found but been given that missing piece. The Infiniverse’s nature as perpetual force, Noah’s Mana as a perpetual force! Infinite, growing, expanding, never ceasing...had been exactly what was needed!","5/5 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":4066,"title":"Chapter 4066: Chapter 4065: Effort! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4065: Effort! I","In the Early Veiled Shore, the atmosphere wes immensly glorious at this moment.","Yoshinami’s song continued, softer now but no less powerful, weaving through the air like a blessing being recorded in reality itself.","Heidrun’s dance slowed to match, their combined ritual not ending but transitioning into something sustainable, something that could continue as long as needed.","“Master,” the Infiniverse said, drawing Noah’s attention back to her. “This is just the beginning. The Seed will grow. The Principle will genuinely bloom. And as it does, as I do, as we all do... the harvests will become richer.”","She gestured to the Seed, to the Shore, to everyone present.","“The First Farmer dreamed of reality where effort always mattered. Where trying always yielded something. Where even failure planted seeds.” Her smile contained certainty that transcended prediction. “We will make that dream real. Not just here, but everywhere you choose to plant your influence.”","Noah nodded slowly as he thought through everything.","The First Farmer had wanted a few things when first talking to the Seed!","Existence where trying always matters, where effort is never wasted, where even failure plants seeds for future success.","Ensuring that something always grows from what is planted!","But in the end...","He had Failed!","But from that Failed Seed...something had grown!","Effort had mattered!","He was only missing a perpetual force as Noah provided just that. How glorious was such a thing?","Noah had to step into the Earliest Folds- to even have the capability of doing that was insane.","He then had to meet Fold Dwellers and survive an attack of a Mad Early Creature, and only then did he obtain a Failed Seed from a sorrowful First Farmer!","And now, here he was.","How glorious!","How quintessential!","All that was left to do now...","He looked straight at the terrifying Glyph on The Infiniverse as he spoke out.","“Let me...get a feel of this harvest.”","...!","Harvest.","The word carried weight that transcended its agricultural origins. It was result made manifest, effort transformed into reward, the reality’s acknowledgment that what was planted had grown into something worth gathering.","But what exactly was harvest in the context of existence itself? Was it simply the collection of what had grown, or was it something more fundamental...the principle that effort, any effort, deserved recognition?","The Early Living Existential Seed Glyph of Perpetual Harvest represented something the First Farmer had dreamed of: Existence where trying always mattered! Not a guarantee of success, but an assurance that effort planted seeds, even in failure. That work performed with intention would yield something, even if that something was simply the wisdom to work differently next time.","Noah contemplated this as he stood in his transformed Shore, feeling the weight of what had been accomplished.","He had put in effort...decent effort, he would say with characteristic understatement. From that first moment of awakening to Infinite Mana, through the creation of his Shore, the gathering of his people, the navigation of weavingd of Existence- all of it had been effort compounded upon effort.","Now, it was time to see the results. Time to witness the harvest that such effort had cultivated.","The Infiniverse moved with the fluid certainty of someone who needed no instruction, who understood her purpose with clarity that transcended communication.","The Glyph on her forehead blazed with green-gold radiance. It appeared as a leaf, verdant and golden simultaneously, filled with such concentrated power that looking at it directly felt like witnessing the concept of growth itself.","The leaf seemed alive, pulsing with determination of seeds pushing through stone, of roots finding water in deserts, of life refusing to accept that it couldn’t flourish. It was effort and harvest unified, the promise that one would always lead to the other!","When the Infiniverse spoke, her voice carried weavings that resonated with the fundamental nature of growth itself.","“Your efforts are mighty, Master, and your harvest...should be even more so.”","She rose slightly, the green-gold leaf beneath her feet supporting her like a throne that existed in dimensions beyond the merely physical.","“Endowment, true endowment...is not gift but recognition. It is Existence acknowledging that effort has been invested, that work has been performed, that intention has been focused toward purpose.” Her eyes blazed with the certainty of principle made manifest. “It is existence itself saying: ‘You have planted. Now reap.'”","She raised her hands, and the Glyph on her forehead erupted with light that didn’t blind but revealed.","“Upon my Master, the Harvest Festival Endowment shall bloom!”","HUUM!","The declaration rang through the Shore with the force of natural law being established!","Around Noah, reality responded with enthusiasm that suggested it had been waiting for this moment. Vibrant gold-green leaves materialized from nothing, spinning around him like lotuses caught in a whirlwind of their own making. Each rotation carried within it the glow of perpetuity that was cyclical- harvest leading to planting leading to harvest again.","The leaves didn’t just spin, they sang! Their movement created weavings of grain fields stretching beyond horizons, of orchards heavy with fruit that would seed new orchards, of effort transforming into result with the certainty of existence!","|You have been blessed by the Harvest Festival Endowment|","|Existence and worthiness measured...|","|Classification: UNDEFINED|","|Worthiness exceeds standard parameters|","|Recalculating based on expanded metrics...|","|From Harvest Festival Endowment of the Seed of Perpetual Harvest:|","|Complexity Gained: +33,000,000,000|","|Purity Gained: +33,000,000,000|","...!","The sensation that flooded through Noah defied simple description. It wasn’t just power flowing into him, no. It was recognition on a fundamental level. The authority he felt exceeding anything he had experienced before!","The Dimensional Lattices that True Sources created, the Living Existential Authority he had wielded, even the Early Existential Authority he had touched....none of them compared to this coursing of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest.","It was like comparing a candle to a star, a drop to an ocean, a moment to eternity.","What was a Principle? Noah felt he could finally understand as the authority worked through him, transforming the small into the unfathomable with casual certainty.","A grain of sand could become a Wheel of Existence. A moment of effort could become eons of result!","Oh!","1/5"]},{"number":4067,"title":"Chapter 4067: Chapter 4066: Effort! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4066: Effort! II","His work, his struggles, his attempts...all of them were being acknowledged not just for what they had achieved but for the effort they represented.","Then something unprecedented happened!","A memory surfaced...not recent but ancient by his standards. He saw himself in those early days after Dungeons had descended onto his home world. Every morning, waking with the same purpose: accumulate enough resources and knowledge to buy a Fireball Skill Book.","Such a simple goal, such mundane effort, yet he had pursued it with dedication that transcended its humble nature.","Day after day, the same routine. The same commitment. The same effort invested toward a goal that, in retrospect, seemed almost laughably small.","The Principle of Perpetual Harvest reached back...impossibly, incomprehensibly, and touched that effort.","|Your efforts before touching mana have been recognized|","|They are worthy of harvest|","|Retroactive acknowledgment initiated|","|Complexity increased by 2,500,000,000|","|Purity increased by 2,500,000,000|","Oh!","Seconds later, before he could process this impossibility, another prompt arose!","|Continued effort recognized across timeline|","|Exponential harvest multiplier applied|","|Complexity increased by 2,500,000,000|","|Purity increased by 2,500,000,000|","How ridiculous.","How magisterial!","How could that kind of basic effort...the simple act of waking up and working toward a goal...be worth such a harvest?","Noah could only shake his head with incredulity as the boons continued to flow through him. His complexity soared past forty billion, approaching fifty billion with speed that defied comprehension. Each increase wasn’t just numerical. It was qualitative, his existence becoming more real, more present, more capable of affecting reality around him.","With even the smallest effort, an unfathomable harvest would be granted.","This was what the First Farmer had dreamed of- existencd that rewarded trying, that acknowledged work, that ensured effort was never wasted.","This was merely one percent of a Principle’s authority.","And it seemed to only be getting started.","The Infiniverse smiled from her position on the green-gold leaf throne, beginning to rise higher into the Shore’s eternal light. As she ascended, Noah felt his complexity surge again, responding to proximity to the Seed of the Principle she now embodied.","Her voice echoed across the Shore with the cadence of glory, each word carrying weight that made reality lean in to listen!","“Effort and work are to be rewarded, for they are the seeds from which all harvest grows. The planting of trees and herbs, the tending of soil and soul...all are effort made manifest.”","She raised her hands, and the Glyph on her forehead blazed brighter.","“From the first furrow carved in earth that didn’t yet know it was earth, to the last seed that will be planted when existence itself grows old...all effort connects, all harvest continues.”","Her words took on the rhythm of ancient invocation of unfathomable glory and wonder, her eyes blazing gold green!","“Roots that dig deep shall find water beyond drought. Leaves that reach high shall taste light beyond shadow. Seeds that dare to crack shall discover they were always meant to grow. By the authority of Perpetual Harvest, let growth exceed limitation. Let maturity arrive like dawn...inevitable and welcome. Let the Perpetual Growth Field bathe all in its glory!”","HUUUM!","The Shore responded to her words with enthusiasm that suggested it had been waiting eons for this moment. Every farming plot erupted with green-gold light. The Nine Early Sacred Trees pulsed with vitality that transcended simple growth. This wasn’t just maturation.","This was evolution compressed into moments!","|Seed of the Tender’s Tree has reached full maturity|","|Harvest ready: 27 Tenders produced (Expected: 10)|","|Tenders possess enhanced capability due to Principle influence|","Where the seed had been planted, a magnificent tree now stood. Its bark was silver-white like moonlight given texture, while its leaves shimmered with every color that care could take. The fruits hanging from its branches were unprecedented...humanoid figures wrapped in translucent pods that pulsed with their own heartbeats.","As Noah watched, the first pod opened, and a Tender emerged. They were beautiful in the way dedication is beautiful...not physically perfect but purposefully crafted.","Their eyes held the particular wisdom of those born knowing their purpose. Their hands were made for nurturing, their voices pitched for comfort, their entire being designed to tend.","Twenty-seven of them emerged in sequence, each slightly different but sharing that fundamental nature of care. They would tend the Shore’s plants, its creatures, its very essence. They would ensure nothing went untended, uncared for, unloved.","And alongside them...","|Seed of Singular Prosperity Grass has reached full maturity|","|Field coverage: 10,000 square meters achieved|","The grass...the single grass...spread like green-gold fire across designated areas, each blade containing within it the promise of prosperity. It invited growth in others, creating zones where simply existing meant advancing.","|Auric Vitae Grasses have reached full maturity|","|Life force multiplication effect active|","|Healing acceleration: 10,000% within grass vicinity|","Every herb, across the plots of thr Early Veiled Shore pulsed and underwent tremendous growth!","|Sacred Herbs have achieved full maturity:|","– Transcendent Veilmoss: Ready for harvest","– Chronos Petrichor: Temporal effects stabilized","– Void-Heart Chrysanthemums: Spatial properties maximized","– Echo Sage: Wisdom enhancement prepared","– Infinity’s Breath Orchids: Endless potential contained","The Nine Early Sacred Trees also pulsed with fruits that seemed almost eager to be picked. Each one had developed beyond expectation, the Principle’s influence pushing them past their intended limitations into something greater.","Then came the prompt that made Noah’s attention sharpen to a point.","|Seed of Inevitability approaching bloom state|","|Multiple evolution paths detected:|","|Option 1: Inevitability of Growth|","– All growth becomes inevitable","– Cannot be stopped or reversed","– Affects allies and enemies equally","|Option 2: Inevitability of Harvest|","– All planted efforts will yield results","– Timeline variable but outcome certain","– Synchronizes with Perpetual Harvest","|Option 3: Inevitability of Connection|","– All beings in Shore become fundamentally linked","– Shared growth and understanding","– Risk: Loss of individual identity if uncontrolled","|Option 4: Allow natural bloom|","– Outcome unknown","– Potentially unprecedented result","– Risk level: Undefined","Noah studied these options with the intensity of someone who understood that choices at this level couldn’t be undone. Each path would fundamentally alter not just the Seed but the entire nature of his Shore.","Choices, as always, came center point!","But this was a choice he could easily make!","The Infiniverse descended back to his level, her expression serene with the satisfaction of purpose fulfilled.","“This is what one percent allows,” she said simply. “Imagine what will become possible as the percentage grows.”","Around them, the Shore hummed with new life, new growth, new potential.","The enhanced herbs and grasses created an atmosphere thick with beneficial energies.","And at the center of it all, Noah stood with complexity approaching levels that shouldn’t be possible for someone who had started from nothing such a short time ago.","The harvest had begun, and it showed no signs of stopping!","2/5"]},{"number":4068,"title":"Chapter 4068: Chapter 4067: Effort! III","paragraphs":["There was an overabundance of glory and matured wonders spreading across the Early Veiled Shore.","The air itself seemed drunk on possibility, heavy with the scent of herbs that could reshape existence and fruits that contained wisdom of ages. Every surface gleamed with the particular sheen that came from being touched by a Principle’s authority.","At such a time, a voice cut through the sacred atmosphere with decidedly unsacred words!","\"Holy shit...\"","The Queen of Matter stood surrounded by towers of books...some containing glorious Fables of cosmic significance, others holding utterly useless tales of beings who had lived and died without note.","She could feel it all, every wonder occurring across the Shore resonating through her existence like vibrations through a tuning fork.","Her complexity and purity had exceeded five hundred million, not through any particular effort on her part, but simply from being present when a Historical Record unfolded.","The passive harvest of witnessing something significant had elevated her beyond what years of traditional advancement might have achieved.","As she marveled at the sensation of growth without effort, space beside her warped with the particular distortion that came from Order asserting itself.","A figure materialized...Sigrid, though not quite. This was one of two ordered states she now maintained, one body remaining near Noah while this one appeared directly behind the Queen of Matter.","\"Hey,\" Sigrid said with casual directness.","The Queen of Matter jumped with such force that several of her floating books tumbled, their Fables spilling into the air as glowing text before reassembling.","\"You scared the shit out of me!\"","Sigrid regarded her calmly, the green-gold light of the ongoing harvest casting her features in ethereal relief.","Her expression carried the particular focus of someone with a specific goal. \"Are you the Record Keeper here?\"","The Queen of Matter’s demeanor shifted instantly from startled to professional, though her attempt at formality came out somewhat garbled.","She cleared her throat with exaggerated importance. \"Yes, Ma’am Most Recent Harem Member Addition...I mean, THE Living Order! I hold all the Fables of everyone in the Infiniverse! I know the Fables of Sir Osmont, those around him, and... hey!\"","Her formal introduction cut short as Sigrid reached out and grabbed her by the nape of her neck with the casual efficiency of someone picking up a cat.","The Queen of Matter found herself being carried toward a quieter corner of the Shore, her feet dangling slightly above the golden sands.","\"Tell me all the Fables,\" Sigrid commanded, setting her down but maintaining a grip that suggested flight was not an option. \"Starting with his.\"","The Queen of Matter’s eyes sparkled with the particular gleam of someone given permission to share their obsession. \"Yes Ma’am! There is so much to cover! Sir has gone through so many phases, so many transformations. After I joined him, he allowed me to glimpse even more of his Fable...the complete weaving of it!\"","She began gesticulating wildly, her enthusiasm making her forget she was essentially being interrogated.","\"There’s the Beast World where many things kicked off...oh, the progression from nothing to everything! The Atlanteans! The Demon World with its hierarchies of power, oh, and Baal. I liked him! And the Cultivation World!\" Her voice rose with particular excitement. \"Oh, the Cultivation World... I wish he had spent more time there, expanded the weavings of Cultivators more! Can you imagine? Foundation Establishment! Core Formation! Nascent Soul! The poetry of advancement through understanding! Ah...!\"","...!","As the Queen of Matter’s words tumbled over each other in an increasingly scattered stream of consciousness, Sigrid’s frown deepened. She sighed with the particular exhaustion of someone realizing they had asked for information from someone who loved information too much.","\"Focus.\"","White light erupted around them...not harsh but organizing. Order itself reached into the Queen of Matter’s scattered thoughts and arranged them into neat categories, chronological sequences, relevant narratives. The Record Keeper’s eyes cleared as if waking from a dream.","\"Ahem, yes.\" She straightened, her voice taking on the clarity of proper narration. \"We can start with... a skill book. It all starts with...a skill book.\"","While Sigrid began listening to these organized Fables through one body, her other form remained near the Primordial Excavation Depths with Noah. He turned to her with an expression of gentle amusement.","\"You could also just ask me directly...\"","This Sigrid looked over with an expression that managed to be both cute and indignant, letting out a small harrumph. \"I thought you might embellish your good sides and say nothing of the bad.\"","Noah’s smile deepened at this logic...the idea that he would hide his failures when his entire path had been built on learning from them.","But he didn’t argue, instead rising to survey the overabundance that surrounded them. Sacred Herbs swayed in breezes that carried beneficial properties. Fruits hung heavy with concentrated advancement. Grasses that could elevate existence simply by walking across them spread in all directions.","\"I can’t possibly take all this for myself,\" he announced, his voice carrying across the Shore with the clarity of decision. \"Those in the Shore can enjoy a Harvest Festival!\"","...!","\"RAA!\"","Emperor Penguin’s enthusiastic cry erupted immediately, his flippers slapping together in anticipation.","Around him, others began gathering...Kazuhiko with his hand instinctively on his sword even in celebration, Henry with lingering destinies that seemed lighter than usual...","Noah moved toward the Tender Tree, arriving at its plot in a single step that compressed distance into intention. He reached up to pluck the first humanoid Tender from its pod, and as his hands made contact, something unprecedented occurred.","The moment he grasped the Tender...an act of harvest, however gentle...the Principle responded.","|Effort detected: Harvesting|","|Effort Multiplication activated|","|Work performed within sight of Glyph gains exponential returns|","The Tender in his hands suddenly blazed with soft light. Its eyes, which had been merely aware, became luminous with purpose. Its form, already designed for tending, became more refined.","On its back, where simple farming equipment had been forming, complex tools materialized...not just physical implements but conceptual ones. Tools that could tend to ideas as easily as plants, that could nurture potential as readily as soil.","|Tender enhancement through Effort Multiplication:|","|Physical capability increased 1000%|","|Intuitive understanding of all Shore plants gained|","|Can perceive and tend to conceptual growth|","|Emotional nurturing capability added|","|Efficiency transcends physical limitation|","It was ridiculous. It was unfathomable. The simple act of harvesting had transformed what was already miraculous into something that defied classification!"]},{"number":4069,"title":"Chapter 4069: Chapter 4068: Effort! IV","paragraphs":["Noah continued, plucking each Tender with the same care, and each one underwent the same transformation.","Silver white humanoids with simple expressions adorned in farmer’s overalls.","Twenty-seven became a force that could tend not just to a Shore but to the concept of growth itself. They arranged themselves in neat rows as he worked, their eyes shining with the particular brightness of purpose recognized and enhanced.","\"Help me harvest everything,\" Noah instructed them, his voice carrying the gentle authority of someone who knew his requests would be fulfilled with joy. \"Store some in the Sacred Totems for preservation. Everything else goes to the center of the Shore for all to partake.\"","The Tenders moved with synchronized grace that transcended training...this was instinct elevated to art. Their backs formed baskets that seemed to exist in more space than they occupied, allowing them to carry impossible amounts without strain. Their hands, as they touched each plant, each fruit, each herb, somehow left the sources stronger even while harvesting from them.","Effort flowed through them too, and it recieved the same boons!","They moved through the plots with efficiency that looked like dance, their movements creating patterns that themselves encouraged growth. Where they stepped, the soil became richer. Where they reached, plants yearned to provide their best yields. The Shore itself seemed to celebrate their presence, recognizing them as part of its fundamental nature.","As harvested wonders began accumulating at the Shore’s center, beings gathered with anticipation that transcended simple hunger. This was advancement made tangible, growth made consumable.","Noah stood at the heart of this activity, closing his eyes to take it all in. Not just the external celebration, but the internal transformation. He turned his perception inward, examining what he had become!","[Noah Osmont - The Early Creature(52,355 Drops of Blood]","Complexity Quotient: 52,847,293,152","Purity Quotient: 52,847,293,152","Glyphs:","- The Creature’s First Lesson","Sacred Tool(s)","- The Goad","Sacred Totems Constructed: 37","Parts of Heart:","- First Part: Ventryalis – The Primal Root Atrium of Echoes Complete","- Second Part: Oruvian Shardveil – The Arterial Convergence Core Complete","- Third Part: Myokelum Primus – The Living Pump of Trembling Flow 3% Complete","Total Collective Resistances: 1,103%","Shore Features:","- 37 Sacred Totems","- Primordial Excavation Depths","- 9 Matured Early Sacred Trees","- Complete Sacred Herb Garden","- 27 Enhanced Tenders","- Seed of Inevitability (Approaching Bloom)","- Seed of Perpetual Harvest (Active, planted)","- Marine Lifeform Aquarium (Expanding)","- Abode of the Early Creature","Honarable Entanglement Mentions","- THE Living Order (Sigrid) - Awakening","- Moiraine: Arch Living Existence","- Infinite Early Osmontian Shore (Infiniverse)","- Early Living Ruin (Ruination)","- The Peacemaker","- The Great Usurper","- Titano","- Duke Whisker","- Duke Gwendolyn","- Duke Diviticus","- Early Connections (Khor, First Farmer, Heidrun, Yoshinami)","—","He had come far. From someone scrambling to buy a Skill Book to someone who could freely talk to Dukes of Living Existences, who could harbor THE Living Order, who could birth thr Seed of a Principle from failure.","Yet as he opened his eyes and watched his people celebrating their Harvest Festival...he collected himself and contained his tyranny.","The complexity he had gained was enormous, but THE Living Existences existed at scales that made his current power seem quaint. The capabilities he had developed were impressive, but Early Creatures had done things that rewrote the fundamental concepts of reality.","He had come far, yes.","But the path ahead remained infinite, and that thought filled him with anticipation.","The Harvest Festival continued around him, joy and growth intermingling in ways that would have been impossible anywhere else!","And as it did, his eyes blazed with tyranny as he continued forging ahead!","His eyes shone luminously as his voice echoed out commandingly.","\"Forge the Early Living Existential Seed Glyph - Principle of Perpetual Harvest.\"","The command emerged as declaration, carrying the weight of someone who had learned that true power often spoke softly!","Reality itself leaned in to listen, recognizing the authority in his voice.","The moment the words completed, prompts cascaded before his vision with the particular urgency of fundamental change while green gold lights gathered over his body!","|Initiating Glyph Formation: Early Living Existential Seed Glyph - Principle of Perpetual Harvest|","|Required: 25,000,000,000 Complexity Quotient|","|Required: 25,000,000,000 Purity Quotient|","|Current values sufficient. Proceed?|","Noah didn’t hesitate. The moment his will confirmed the action, he felt the complexity and purity drain from him purposefully, like water flowing toward its destined basin.","Twenty-five billion units of accumulated power condensed and reformed, transforming from raw potential into structured purpose!","The sensation was unlike anything he had experienced before. When he had formed his first Kleos Glyph, it had been like carving meaning into his existence.","This was different...this was inviting a Principle to take residence within him, to become part of his fundamental nature.","His forehead blazed with green-gold light as the Glyph began forming. Unlike the violent eruptions of power he had witnessed before, this was almost gentle...a seed being planted in the soil of his being, roots spreading through dimensions of his existence he hadn’t known were there.","|Formation progressing...|","|Synchronizing with the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest...|","|Integration at 25%... 50%... 75%...|","HUUM!","The world around him shifted perceptually!","He could suddenly see the effort in everything. The trees straining toward light were making effort. The sand accepting footprints was making effort. Even the air, moving to fill spaces, was engaged in work that deserved recognition!","It was unfathomably glorious!","|Formation complete!|","|Early Living Existential Seed Glyph - Principle of Perpetual Harvest: FORGED|","|Access level: 1% of Principle’s authority|","|All capabilities of Perpetual Harvest now available|","...!","All the glorious capabilities that thr Infiniverse had just been able to utilize also became his!","The Glyph settled into place on his forehead...not replacing The Creature’s First Lesson but complementing it, creating a harmony of purposes that resonated through his being.","He could feel the capabilities flowing through him: the ability to grant Harvest Festival Endowments, to create Perpetual Growth Fields, to ensure that effort would always yield something.","Without hesitation, he turned this power upon himself because...why the hell not?!","He loved abusing abilities the most!","\"Upon myself, the Harvest Festival Endowment shall bloom.\"","...!","Oh!","From thr depths of his existence....","|The Weavings of Cheats dance with glee!|"]},{"number":4070,"title":"Chapter 4070: Chapter 4069: Effort! V","paragraphs":["The words carried different weight when speaking them about himself.","It was not authority directed outward but recognition turned inward!","The green-gold leaves that materialized around him seemed more personal, more knowing, as if they could see every effort he had ever made, every struggle he had pushed through, every moment he had chosen to continue when stopping would have been easier.","|Harvest Festival Endowment activated|","|Target: Self|","|Measuring existence and worthiness...|","|Warning: Recursive loop detected|","|One who grants harvest harvesting from themselves|","|Calculating paradox resolution...|","|Resolution found: Effort to help others harvest creates its own harvest|","|Complexity gained: +24,000,000,000|","|Purity gained: +24,000,000,000|","BOOM!","The influx of power was immediate but controlled, flowing back into him with the particular satisfaction of effort recognized. His complexity soared past 50 billion again even though it was halved not too long ago!","But Noah wasn’t finished. If the cost for him was only twenty-five billion per Glyph, then why stop at one?","\"Forge the second Early Living Existential Seed Glyph.\"","...!","Goodness.","He really kept going!","|Warning: Multiple Seed Glyphs of same Principle.|","|Calculating possibility...|","|Determination: Theoretically viable|","|Proceeding with formation...|","Another twenty-five billion drained from his existence, but this time the sensation was different. The second Glyph formed not on his forehead but on his right palm, as if his body was creating a constellation of Seeds of Principles across his form. The formation was faster this time, his existence already familiar with the pattern.","Patterns, runes, glyphs...the familiarity was unique!","|Second Early Living Existential Seed Glyph - Principle of Perpetual Harvest successfully forged|","|Synergy detected between multiple Glyphs!|","|Capabilities enhanced by 50% due to resonance|","Without pause, driven by the particular greed of someone who had learned that power seized quickly was often power that lasted, Noah commanded once more.","\"Forge the third Early Living Existential Seed Glyph.\"","...!","|The Weavings of the Protagonist approve current actions with fervor!|","|The weavings of Cheats say more, more!|","The drain this time brought his complexity down to levels that felt almost vulnerable after the heights he had reached.","But vulnerability was relative...he still possessed more power than most beings would accumulate in lifetimes.","And even though a single glyph cost 25 Billion for him...each one actually cost and had the weight of 100 Billion Complexity and Purity!","And was that not the marker of...an Honored Living Existence?","\"...\"","The third Glyph began forming on his left palm, creating perfect symmetry with the second. The Shore itself seemed to hold its breath as this unprecedented triple formation neared completion.","|Third Glyph forming...|","|Resonance increasing exponentially...|","|Warning: Approaching Principle tolerance limit...|","|Third Early Living Existential Seed Glyph - Principle of Perpetual Harvest complete!|","|Maximum Seed Glyphs reached for current access level|","|1% Principle authority cannot support additional Glyphs|","|Attempting formation of fourth Glyph will result in failure|","...!","Noah felt the truth of this limitation...his existence was practically vibrating with the power of three Seed Glyphs!","But even knowing this, a part of him wondered...","\"Forge the fourth Early Living Existential Seed Glyph.\"","The command emerged despite the warning, driven by curiosity about what failure at this level would mean.","|Formation attempted...|","|Insufficient Principle access|","|Formation failed|","|However: Effort has been made|","|Effort Multiplication recognizes attempt|","|Even failure plants seeds for future success|","|Complexity gained: +1,000,000,000|","|Purity gained: +1,000,000,000|","...!","\"Haha!\"","Noah smiled and even laughed at this ridiculous revelation...even his failures would yield harvest now. The Principle didn’t punish attempts that couldn’t succeed; it rewarded the effort of trying!","\"Again!\"","He made his intent known with but a word!","|Formation of a fourth Early Living Existential Seed Glyph - Principle of Perpetual Harvest attempted again...|","|Insufficient Principle access|","|Formation failed|","|However: Effort has been made|","|Effort Multiplication recognizes attempt|","|Even failure plants seeds for future success. But since it is the same failure, harvest is reduced|","|Complexity gained: +500,000,000|","|Purity gained: +500,000,000|","...!","Okay.","So the reward for the same failures reduced, but Perpetual Harvest was teuly astonishing as the first Principle Noah gained acess to was truly a ridiculous one!","He could feel the power coursing through him now, three Glyphs pulsing in synchronization. His forehead bore the primary Glyph, glowing with steady authority. His palms each held secondary Glyphs that seemed eager to be used, to grant endowments, to recognize effort wherever it might be found.","With this new power singing through his existence, Noah turned his attention to other matters. His perception brushed against the Seed of Inevitability, feeling its slow but steady progress toward blooming. It felt would need more time, but time was something they had.","He opened his eyes fully, taking in the sight of his gathered companions. The Infiniverse floated on her verdant throne-leaf, power radiating from her transformed state.","Ruination stood with her dress of ruptured existence rippling in winds that didn’t exist, her nature as an Early Living Ruin making reality uncertain around her edges.","Sigrid maintained her split presence, one body still listening to the Queen of Matter’s endless Fables while the other watched him with interest that transcended simple curiosity.","Moiraine observed everything with the particular intensity of someone observing experiences for future reference.","When Noah spoke, his voice carried the calm certainty of someone who had found their next step on an infinite path.","\"The Festival will continue here, tended by those who know their purposes.\" His gaze swept across the Tenders, who were still efficiently distributing the harvest to all who desired it. \"The Shore itself will manage what needs managing.\"","He stepped forward, and the three Glyphs pulsed in unison, creating an aurora of green-gold light that made him appear as something glorious.","\"But we have depths to explore. The Primordial Early Excavation Depths await, and within them lie materials from the Earliest Folds. Ores that can enhance our Shore. Crystals that can accelerate our growth. Memories that might teach us what we don’t know we need to learn...\"","He smiled as he said this because...was this not his discipline? His effort?","To continue doing things and not simply lie back and rest just because he achieved something great?!","And man...it felt good to simply do things!"]},{"number":4071,"title":"Chapter 4071: Chapter 4070: The Depths! I","paragraphs":["Noah paused at the threshold of the Primordial Early Excavation Depths, his hand resting against the archway of impossible stone.","He could feel his complexity hovering at levels that, while still formidable, felt depleted after the massive expenditures of forging three Seed Glyphs. But...","He had two more Early Living Existential Seed Glyphs pulsing with unused potential...one on each palm. And each one could grant a Harvest Festival Endowment once per day.","\"Why leave power unused?\" he murmured, raising his right hand to observe the Glyph that gleamed there like a verdant star. \"Upon myself, the second Harvest Festival Endowment shall bloom.\"","HUUM!","The response was immediate. Green-gold leaves materialized from his right palm, spiraling around him with purpose that suggested they knew exactly what effort needed rewarding.","These leaves seemed different from the first set...more knowing, as if they could see the effort of restraint, the work of not using power immediately, the patience that was its own form of labor!","|Second Harvest Festival Endowment activated|","|Target: Self|","|Measuring accumulated efforts since last harvest...|","|Note: Effort to forge multiple Glyphs recognized|","|Note: Effort to lead others recognized|","|Note: Effort of restraint recognized|","|Complexity gained: +21,000,000,000|","|Purity gained: +21,000,000,000|","HUUM!","The influx washed through him like a tide of validation. His complexity surged back toward comfortable levels, but he wasn’t finished. His left palm blazed with its own eager light.","\"Upon myself, the third Harvest Festival Endowment shall bloom!\"","BOOM!","This time the leaves that emerged carried a different quality...they recognized not past effort but ongoing work.","The effort of maintaining multiple bodies across reality. The effort of holding a Shore together through will alone. The effort of being what others needed him to be.","|Third Harvest Festival Endowment activated|","|Target: Self|","|Recognizing continuous ongoing efforts|","|Note: Simultaneous existence maintenance quantified|","|Note: Leadership burden acknowledged|","|Note: Reality anchor role measured|","|Complexity gained: +19,000,000,000|","|Purity gained: +19,000,000,000|","|Current Total Complexity: 41,847,293,152|","|Current Total Purity: 41,847,293,152|","Noah breathed deep, feeling power settle into his bones with the satisfaction of a well-fitted garment. This was better...not overwhelming, but sufficient.","He waved his hand, and the Goad flew across the Shore into his grip with the eagerness of a tool recognizing its moment had come. The simple stick hummed with potential, its ability to educate through contact ready to meet whatever ignorance the depths might contain.","Standing there with his shepherd’s tool and three Principles gleaming on his body, he looked like what he was...someone ready to tend to realities that had forgotten they needed tending!","Before he could take his first step into the depths, two figures approached with distinct gaits that proclaimed their natures.","Heidrun trotted over with the particular arrogance of someone who had existed since before existence properly organized itself.","She nudged him with her head...not gently, but with the force of someone making a point.","|Heidrun wishes you to know:|","|\"Don’t die in there. Who else would I share grass, mead, and knowledge with?\"|","|Translation: Please be careful|","...!","Noah smiled at the prompt that translated her arrogant care into something more recognizable. He scratched behind her ears, earning a huff that suggested such gestures were beneath her dignity but acceptable from him.","Yoshinami approached more directly, her form shifting from solid to light with the fluidity of someone who had never fully decided which state she preferred. Without ceremony or warning, she dissolved into radiance that wrapped around his head, condensing into an obsidian crown that seemed to devour light while creating its own.","\"I’ve finished devouring the corpse of that Dead Existence,\" her voice resonated directly into his thoughts, carrying satisfaction that transcended simple fullness. \"From now on, I can act twice a day to kill anything below the level of an Early Creature. And in this form, I’m considered a tool...we can enter together without exceeding occupancy limits of the group.\"","WAA!","The crown settled onto his head with weight that transcended the physical. It was authority made wearable, death given form that chose not to kill.","\"Then let’s see what memories these depths are hiding,\" Noah said, stepping toward the entrance with his assembled party.","The moment they passed through the archway, reality shifted.","The entrance sealed behind them...not permanently, but with the finality of a door that wouldn’t open until they had earned their exit.","The atmosphere hit them first.","\"This place...\" Yoshinami’s voice echoed from the crown with recognition that carried across eons, \"it smells and feels like the Wandering Territories. Like the Earliest Folds. There’s an age here that predates the separation of concepts.\"","Around them, existence was still rearranging itself as they could not see much!","\"Then we’re likely to find things that shouldn’t exist anymore,\" Noah replied, his voice carrying tyrannical interest rather than concern!","What they saw initially was almost disappointingly mundane...a cavern that might have existed in any world, though the stone carried a quality that suggested it had been compressed by time rather than pressure.","But it was small, cramped, the path forward blocked by material that seemed to exist too thoroughly to simply push aside.","|Welcome to Primordial Early Excavation Depths|","|Current Level: 1 - The Forgotten Servant’s Vestibule|","|Danger Rating: Manageable (for beings of your caliber. Are you being carried?)|","|Possible Encounters: Remnant Guardians, Memory Echoes, Conceptual Parasites|","|WARNING: Memories here may be infectious|","...!","The stones ahead of them pulsed with purple obsidian age that had weight, blocking their path with the stubbornness of reality that had existed too long to remember it could change.","\"Allow me,\" Ruination said, stepping forward with the particular grace of someone who ended things professionally.","The crimson-gold Glyph of Ruin on her forehead pulsed once, and the stones ahead simply ceased. Not destroyed, not moved...ended, its existence concluded with the finality of a story reaching its last word.","And Ruination remained forging ahead as if she would mine and destroy the jagged stones making the path so small for her Master!","The Infiniverse followed close behind above a verdant gold leaf as she looked around cautiously!"]},{"number":4072,"title":"Chapter 4072: Chapter 4071: The Depths! II","paragraphs":["As they moved through the path she created, Sigrid’s curiosity finally overcame her observation. She had been studying their party with the intensity of someone observing variables, and now she spoke.","\"I know the Infiniverse and Ruination as his close constructs and family, but you\"...she looked directly at Moiraine, \"you carry the air of both Paradox and Origin. What’s your story?\"","...!","Moiraine’s expression shifted to something between calmness and protectiveness. She looked at Sigrid briefly before she spoke as Noah was ahead of them walking with a smile, the Infiniverse floating in front of him on her leaf protectively, and Ruination even further ahead","Moiraine was the one to answer. \"The story begins with a misunderstanding that became fortunate. We, a few Paradoxes, mistook Sir for a Young Paradox who didn’t produce Inevitabilities...a miracle. I was the one who thought he might be an answer to our curse.\"","\"So you brought him to the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds?\" Sigrid asked, Order itself leaning in to understand the sequence of events.","Noah picked up the thread with his characteristic casual delivery of significant information. \"Yes, she did. While there, some Paradoxes saw opportunity in my unusual nature. They plotted, schemed, made their move...\"","\"A bitch called Diviticus decided to try and devour Sir,\" Moiraine interrupted, her usual composure cracking with anger on his behalf.","The emotion transformed her from follower to defender, from subordinate to someone who would end existences for the offense!","\"She managed to get a portion of his blood and power before he brought me into the Early Veiled Shore.\"","She continued, her voice carrying the particular venom of someone who had not forgiven and would not forget. \"As for Diviticus, she became what she stole...a Living Paradox who doesn’t produce Inevitabilities. Based on what Sir told me, she used this power to help Living Paradoxes steal the corpse of an Early Creature from the Coalition of Living Existences.\"","Sigrid’s eyes blazed with intensity that made the air around her organize itself into attack patterns.","\"Is that right?\"","...!","Her eyes were cold.","When she spoke, her voice carried the weight of Order itself pronouncing judgment.","\"Order remembers all debts. Every theft, every violation, every breaking of proper sequence.\" The words emerged with such dangerous calm that space itself seemed to take notes.","\"When I’m fully awakened, when Order flows through me without restriction, Diviticus and others will learn what happens when you steal from those under Order’s protection. They will be... organized. Completely. Permanently.\"","Noah raised his brow and whistled when he heard her proclamation!","The threat in those words transcended violence...it was the promise of being unmade, sorted into components that would never again achieve coherence.","She turned to Noah, her expression shifting from dangerous to concerned. \"Is it acceptable that this Diviticus has a corpse of an Early Creature? What can she do with such a thing?\"","Noah’s response balanced his carefreeness with underlying seriousness. \"One thing we know, or theorized based on what a few Dukes mentioned...is that she can open tears...rips in the veil between the Living and the Dead. While that’s an excellent source of loot and advancement, it can quickly go from beneficial to catastrophic. The Dead, the truly Dead...I need more information on them.\"","His eyes took on a mysterious gleam as he continued. \"But... there’s someone who may or may not be putting reins on Diviticus. Someone I’ve been collecting information about.\"","He glanced at Moiraine meaningfully. \"He seems to be someone with a great level of influence and power. My Weavings are telling me to learn more about him...suggesting he might be more significant than he appears.\"","\"Schrodinger,\" Moiraine said, the name carrying weight that suggested stories untold.","\"Among...others,\" Noah confirmed.","\"Many of those truly powerful will consider the endless folds a large boardgame. The game being played has more players than pieces, and some are playing different games entirely...\"","As they continued through the depths, their conversation flowing with the easy rhythm of people who trusted each other despite their different natures, Ruination suddenly broke through another barrier.","The dissolution of stone revealed something that made them all pause.","Blinding obsidian gray light erupted from beyond, forcing them to shield their eyes momentarily. When vision returned, they found themselves approaching a vast cavernous space that defied the cramped passages they had been navigating!","It was a hollow world, complete unto itself.","Jagged obsidian purple crystals jutted from every surface...floor, walls, ceiling...each one containing colors that shouldn’t exist simultaneously. The crystals sang with weavings that suggested they were recordings, memories crystallized into mineral form.","But it was what stood at the center that drew their attention completely.","A figure that looked half-alive and half-dead stood motionless before a massive Memory Stone that pulsed with inner light. Its eyes contained the blank stare of something that had forgotten it was supposed to be conscious.","In its hand, a tattered blade hung with the weight of purpose forgotten but not abandoned.","|Domain Discovered: The Servant’s Crystal Requiem|","|Remnant Lifeform Identified: Kelgar the Lost|","|Distinction: Last Disciple of Early Creature Morathis|","|Origin: Desiccated Sleeping Shore #4,892|","|Status: Neither alive nor dead, perpetually serving|","|Memory Stone Detected|","|Size: Colossal|","|Potential Memories: Unknown (Requires extraction)|","|Warning: May contain consciousness fragments|","|Paradox Minerals Detected|","|Quantity: Abundant|","|Location: Embedded in crystal formations|","|Quality: Exceptional|","The entity, Kelgar the Lost, stood with the perfect stillness of something that had been waiting so long that waiting had become its entire existence. The tattered blade in its grip showed signs of impossible age, edges that had been sharp for eons slowly forgetting what sharpness meant.","Then, with the mechanical precision of ancient programming finally triggered, its head turned.","Blank eyes that contained nothing and everything fixed upon them.","The blade rose with movement that suggested routine rather than thought.","And in a voice that sounded like memories of sound rather than actual speech, it spoke.","\"Master... is that... you? Have you come... to release me... from my vigil?\"","The question buzzed in the crystal-sung air, carrying the weight of eons of service that had continued past the point where service had meaning!","Here was loyalty that had transcended death, duty that had outlasted its purpose, a guardian who had forgotten everything except that it was supposed to guard.","Noah gripped the Goad tighter, feeling through it the profound education this entity might provide...not through combat, but through the simple tragedy of its existence.","This was effort that had continued past reason, past reward, past any possible harvest except the hope that someday, someone would tell it to stop.","The Primordial Early Excavation Depths had revealed their first truth... some things endured not because they were strong, but because no one had given them permission to rest."]},{"number":4073,"title":"Chapter 4073: Chapter 4072: The Weight of Endless Service! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4072: The Weight of Endless Service! I","Kelgar’s head tilted with mechanical precision, the movement carrying the weight of eons spent in repetition.","When he shook his head, dust that had accumulated for untold ages drifted from his form like memories being shed.","The aura that would make weak Honored Living Existences pale erupted out!","An aura that would cause someone like Altheon to sink to his knees and tremble!","No Prime Living Existences could stand this being.","Even for an Honored Living Existence...they had to be powerful ones!","“No,” his voice emerged like grinding stone, each word carved from centuries of isolation. “You are not my master.”","HUUM!","The declaration buzzed in the crystalline air, the surrounding crystals humming with vibratios as if they recognized the truth in his words. His blank eyes, which had seemed empty moments before, now contained depths of despair that transcended simple emotion.","“How could you be my master?” Kelgar continued, his grip on the tattered blade tightening with the first real movement he had made in perhaps millennia.","“You are so weak. I can feel your existence...newly formed, barely crystallized, still learning what it means to be. My master was ancient when ancientness was young. She was...Ah!”","He took a step forward, and the ground beneath him cracked from the simple fact that it had forgotten how to support movement after so long without it.","“I have been locked here, not allowed to live, not permitted to die. Trapped in this moment between breaths for so long that I’ve forgotten what breathing meant.” His voice grew harder, more desperate. “Why would this change now? Why would today be different from the million days before it?”","...!","Noah observed this remnant of loyalty with eyes that saw beyond the surface tragedy.","This was dedication that had curdled into despair, service that had become its own prison. He stepped forward, the Goad resting casually in his hand like a walking stick rather than a weapon.","“Do you know where you are?” Noah asked, his voice carrying the particular gentleness reserved for those too broken to accept kindness. “Do you remember what this place is? Who your master was? What happened to leave you here?”","He paused, letting the questions settle into the space between them before continuing.","“I am not your master, this is true. But I am here now, and I can release you from this state. Sometimes that’s all that matters...not who has the right, but who has the ability and the will to act.”","Kelgar’s expression...what little could be read on features that had forgotten how to emote, shifted through something that might have been hope before settling back into resignation.","“Maybe if you were stronger.” The words emerged with the certainty of someone who had tested every possibility and found them all wanting.","“But it doesn’t matter. Who I was doesn’t matter. I remember now, once more, that everything is gone. Everyone is gone. The Shore I protected, the master I served, the purpose I held...all dust, all nothing.”","His grip on the blade shifted, and for the first time since they had entered, he showed real animation.","“I only wish... I was gone alongside everyone else.”","...!","What happened next defied the sluggish pace of his previous movements.","Kelgar moved with speed that suggested all his stillness had been choice rather than inability. Early Existential Authority erupted from his form...not the refined power of those who had cultivated it, but raw force that had been compressed by time into something denser than it should be.","Around him, Kleos Glyphs began forming with terrifying rapidity. Not one or two...hundreds, each one bearing the same symbol, the same concept made manifest: Vicissitude.","Change. Alteration. The fundamental instability of all things. The idea that nothing remained the same, that all states were temporary, that even permanence was just change moving too slowly to perceive.","The Infiniverse tensed, ready to exert her Principle. Ruination’s dress of ruptured existence rippled with anticipation of endings to deliver.","Sigrid’s Order began organizing attack patterns that would systematically dismantle this threat. Moiraine’s cultivation base hummed with power ready to be released.","And yet...","“Let me,” Noah said simply, and that simple statement carried enough weight that they all stepped back.","He moved forward with the casual confidence of someone approaching a dance partner rather than an opponent.","The first step he took was recognized by his Glyphs as effort...movement with purpose, action with intent. The three Early Living Existential Seed Glyphs pulsed in response, and his simple step became something more.","|Effort Detected: Combat Initiation|","|Principle of Perpetual Harvest Amplifying Action|","|Simple Step → Spatial Compression Step|","|Distance Negation Achieved|","He crossed the space between them in a movement that didn’t traverse distance so much as convince distance it didn’t exist.","Kelgar’s blade met the Goad with a clash that sent crystalline notes ringing through the cavern!","BOOM!","The impact should have shattered the simple stick, but the Goad had its own nature...it existed to educate, and some lessons required surviving the student’s resistance.","“This battle could go differently,” Noah said as their weapons locked, his voice conversational despite the forces involved. “I could help you live again, truly live. Or die, truly die. Whichever you prefer. The choice itself is what matters.”","Kelgar’s response came through action rather than words. The hundreds of Vicissitude Glyphs pulsed in unison, and suddenly Noah wasn’t fighting one opponent but dozens of versions...Kelgar as he was, as he had been, as he might be, all existing simultaneously.","The Goad whirled in Noah’s hands, each movement recognized as effort by his Principles.","When it struck the first Vicissitude Glyph, something extraordinary happened!","|Goad Contact with Hostile Glyph Detected|","|Analyzing Concept: Vicissitude|","|Definition: The quality of being changeable, mutable, subject to variation|","|Counter-Education Initiated|","|Existential Truth Being Established:|","|Change requires continuity to be meaningful|","|Without stable reference, change becomes nothing|","|Applying Lesson: Enforced Stability|","HUUM!","The Glyph didn’t just shatter.","It was fucking educated out of existence, taught that its own idea contained the seeds of its negation. Where change was absolute, nothing could change because there was nothing stable enough to change from!","But Kelgar had hundreds more, and each one represented a different aspect of change. Some made the air around them fluid. Others caused time to stutter. Still others suggested that victory and defeat were just perspectives that could be altered.","“I do not wish for your help,” Kelgar said through all his versions simultaneously, creating a chorus of despair. “I do not wish to live or die differently. I simply wish to cease...to stop being this thing that continues despite having no reason to continue. Cessation...Cessation! Cessation!!!”","HUUM!","3/5"]},{"number":4074,"title":"Chapter 4074: Chapter 4073: The Weight of Endless Service! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4073: The Weight of Endless Service! II","Noah’s response was to spin the Goad in a pattern that shouldn’t have been martial but was.","Each rotation was effort.","Each contact with a Glyph was work. And the Principle of Perpetual Harvest recognized all of it!","|Continuous Effort Chain Detected|","|Multiplier Applied: x10, x100, x1000|","|Each Successful Education Strengthens Next|","|Goad Achieving Temporary Transcendence|","BOOM!","The battle became something beautiful in its complexity.","Noah moved through the forest of Glyphs like a teacher through a classroom of unruly concepts, his Goad dispensing lessons with each contact.","The Vicissitude Glyphs tried to change him, alter his nature, shift his purpose, but each attempt met the immovable fact of his identity...he was The Early Creature, Osmont, and that truth was written too deeply to be edited.","From the sidelines, his companions watched with varying degrees of awe.","Moiraine observed with the particular intensity of someone memorizing movements for future use. This was her Sir not just fighting but educating reality itself about why it should behave differently!","Sigrid watched Order trying to assert itself through chaos, seeing in Noah’s movements a different kind of organization...not rigid structure but dynamic balance.","The Infiniverse smiled with the satisfaction of seeing her master’s efforts yielding exponential returns, each action building on the last in a perfect demonstration of perpetual harvest.","Ruination stood perfectly still, but her stillness contained appreciation for someone who could end things without ending them, who could bring conclusion through education rather than destruction.","The battle reached its crescendo when Kelgar, driven by desperation that transcended strategy, brought all his remaining Glyphs together into his blade!","The weapon blazed with the combined force of hundreds of changes, becoming everything it could be simultaneously...sharp and dull, whole and broken, existent and void.","Noah met this ultimate expression of vicissitude with simplicity itself.","The Goad rose, and as it did, his three Principles blazed in unison. The green-gold light they cast didn’t oppose the change Kelgar represented...it simply insisted that change, too, was a form of effort that deserved recognition.","When Goad met blade, the sound was like glass remembering it had once been sand.","The blade shattered.","Not into pieces, but into possibilities, each fragment becoming what it might have been in different circumstances before dissolving into nothing.","“...”","Kelgar stood disarmed, but the Vicissitude Glyphs continued forming around him...slower now, desperate, like the last gasps of something that refused to accept its conclusion!","Noah’s Goad swept through them with movements that had transcended combat to become almost gentle, each touch a lesson in why they didn’t need to exist.","The three Early Living Existential Seed Glyphs on Noah’s body....forehead and both palms, radiated their own green-gold glow that didn’t attack the remaining Glyphs but simply made them irrelevant. In the face of perpetual harvest, change for its own sake seemed suddenly pointless.","The last Glyph faded, and Kelgar fell to his knees with the weight of someone who had been standing through will alone.","He breathed heavily!","His blank eyes closed for the first time in eons, and when he spoke, his voice carried the exhaustion of existence itself.","“I have served past purpose, waited past meaning, continued past reason. In the end, what was it for? My master is dust, our Shore is forgotten, my purpose is void. I fought not to win but to lose, hoped not for victory but for permission to stop!”","His eyes opened one final time, fixing on Noah with something that might have been gratitude.","“In cessation, perhaps there will be peace. In nothing, perhaps there will be rest. In ending, perhaps there will be what beginning never provided...completion.”","BOOM!","Noah shook his head slowly, not entirely agreeing with this philosophy of nihilistic release.","Existence, even painful existence, contained potential that nothing never could.","But he understood that sometimes the kindest thing was to stop forcing someone to continue.","“I do not agree with your philosophy,” he said with characteristic directness. “But agreement isn’t necessary for compassion. You have served beyond any reasonable measure. You have waited past any rational expectation.”","He raised the Goad one final time...as a key.","“Now...you have my permission to rest.”","...!","The words carried weight that transcended their simplicity. Permission...that was all Kelgar had been waiting for. Someone with authority, any authority, to tell him his vigil was over!","Kelgar’s form began to crack like pottery that had been fired too long.","Light escaped from the fractures...not painful but peaceful, like dawn breaking after an endless night. Each crack spread with purpose, creating patterns that might have been beautiful if they weren’t so final.","“Thank you,” he whispered, the words barely audible over the sound of his dissolution. “Thank you for ending what should have ended long ago.”","Then he shattered completely, each fragment becoming light that rose toward the cavern’s ceiling before fading into nothing.","Not destroyed, but finally, mercifully, allowed to stop.","Immense silence settled over the Crystal Requiem. Even the crystals seemed to have stopped their humming, as if observing a moment of respect for service that had extended beyond sanity.","In that silence, Noah’s three Glyphs pulsed with recognition!","|Extraordinary Effort Recognized|","|Defeating an average enemy with excessive compassion|","|Teaching through combat acknowledged|","|Mercy as form of harvest identified|","|The Seed of Perpetual Harvest grants recognition:|","|Complexity increased: +10,000,000,000|","|Purity increased: +10,000,000,000|","|Note: Effort includes emotional labor of granting peace|","...!","Noah released a light sigh that carried the weight of someone who had done necessary work that brought no joy.","He saw the prompt again as the mere Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest continued to be utterly insanse.","It seemed harmless.","Like an auxiliary type of Principle.","And yet...it had more offensive, defensive, and auxiliary capabilities than any single True Source!","He sighed again.","He turned to his companions, who had watched the entire exchange with expressions ranging from contemplation to admiration.","“Help me uncover and mine the Paradox Minerals,” he said, his voice returning to its usual casual command. “We came here for resources, and they won’t extract themselves.”","They moved toward the massive jutting crystals with purpose restored. Each approached the task in their own way.","Ruination touched crystals and ended their structural integrity, causing them to collapse into collectible fragments.","The Infiniverse created localized growth fields that somehow made the minerals eager to be harvested.","Sigrid organized the extraction with systematic efficiency that made random crystal placement seem intentional. Moiraine used her cultivation to sense the densest deposits, marking them for priority extraction.","While his companions worked, Noah found his attention drawn to the massive Memory Stone that Kelgar had guarded for so long.","It pulsed with inner light that suggested contents waiting to be accessed, memories that had been crystallized and preserved for reasons that might no longer matter.","He approached it with the particular curiosity of someone who understood that memories could be more valuable than any mineral, that knowledge from the past might be the key to navigating the future.","The Stone towered above him, its surface covered in patterns that might have been natural formation or might have been writing in a language that predated current understanding. As he reached out to touch it, he wondered what memories had been worth preserving in crystal, what knowledge had been important enough to assign such a guardian.","Whatever lay within, it had been deemed valuable enough that someone had been willing to trap a loyal servant in endless vigil to protect it. That alone made it worth investigating!","His hand made contact with the Stone’s surface, and immediately he felt it...an experience, crystallized and compressed, waiting for someone with the authority to access it.","4/5"]},{"number":4075,"title":"Chapter 4075: Chapter 4074: The Weight of Endless Service! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4074: The Weight of Endless Service! III","Noah’s hand made contact with the Memory Stone’s surface, and immediately the three Early Living Existential Seed Glyphs on his body erupted with recognition.","The green-gold light they cast was acknowledgment of effort about to be transformed into something unprecedented!","|Grand Record Reconstruction Triggered|","|Effort to understand the past recognized by Principle of Perpetual Harvest|","|Memory experience enhanced beyond normal parameters|","|Warning: Consciousness immersion will exceed standard observation|","|Preparing for temporal-existential displacement...|","Before Noah could fully process these prompts, he felt his consciousness being pulled with the inexorable force of gravity asserting itself.","The world around him didn’t fade so much as become suddenly irrelevant, his awareness narrowing to a single point before exploding outward into something else entirely.","His eyes fluttered as sensation returned, but the sensation was wrong. Everything was wrong in the most fascinating way!","He stood in sunlight that felt younger, air that tasted of possibilities not yet foreclosed, on ground that hummed with vitality instead of age.","As his vision cleared, he found himself looking out across a grand Early Veiled Shore...but not his Shore, and not through his eyes.","The body he inhabited thrummed with power that dwarfed his current complexity.","Muscles that had been trained through millennia responded to thoughts that weren’t his. Hearts...multiple hearts, he realized with a start, beat in a rhythm that spoke of redundancy through paranoia. This was Kelgar’s body, but Kelgar as he had been, not the remnant they had encountered.","The blade in his hand caught his attention immediately. Where the Kelgar they had fought wielded a tattered thing that had forgotten its purpose, this weapon gleamed with intent that could cut concepts as easily as flesh.","The metal...if it could be called metal, seemed to exist in multiple states simultaneously, each edge representing a different possibility of severance.","This wasn’t just observing a memory. Through the power of the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest recognizing his effort to understand, Noah was experiencing the past as if he truly stood within it!","Around him, the Early Veiled Shore stretched in magnificence that made his own Shore seem quaint by comparison.","Golden sands that weren’t just golden but contained within each grain the potential for entire worlds. Trees that bore fruits capable of elevating not just existence but the very concept of what existence meant.","Yet despite this grandeur, an atmosphere of anxiety permeated everything. Dozens of Fold Dwellers moved about with the careful steps of those expecting catastrophe.","Some tended to plants with the desperate attention of those who knew this might be the last harvest. Others simply stood together in small groups, their expressions carrying the weight of impending loss.","Two Early Creatures stood near the Shore’s edge, and even from a distance, Noah could feel their power pressing against reality like hands against glass, ready to shatter through if needed. They spoke in low tones that carried despite their volume, their words creating ripples in space itself.","“Another seventeen Shores went dark yesterday,” one said, its form shifting between states as if unable to decide which dimension to primarily exist in.","“Twenty-three the day before,” the other replied, this one more stable but surrounded by an aura that suggested stability was a choice that could be revoked. “The pattern is accelerating.”","...!","Kelgar’s body moved without Noah’s input, drawn by purpose that transcended conscious decision. Each step carried him toward an Abode that made Noah’s breath catch...or would have if he controlled the breathing.","Where his Abode of the Early Creature was grand in its purposeful construction, this structure seemed to have grown rather than been built.","Walls that might have been crystallized time curved upward into towees that pierced clouds that existed specifically to be pierced. Windows opened onto views that shouldn’t have been possible from their positions, showing other Shores, other times, other possibilities.","Kelgar entered without hesitation, his body knowing every turn, every threshold, every dimensional fold that needed to be navigated.","The interior was even more impressive...spaces that existed within spaces, rooms that were bigger inside than the building that contained them, a library that somehow contained books that hadn’t been written yet.","And at the center of it all, in a chamber that felt like the heart of existence itself, stood Early Creature Morathis.","Noah, through Kelgar’s eyes, saw her fully for the first time, and understood immediately why this being had commanded such loyalty that her servant would continue serving even after death.","Her crimson hair resembled flames and the concept of combustion given keratin form, moving with its own light and heat that warmed without burning!","Her golden eyes contained depths that had seen the birth of ideas and the death of certainties. The feline ears that crowned her head twitched with awareness that transcended simple sound, hearing existence’s whispers directly.","But it was the nine fox-like tails spreading behind her that truly proclaimed her nature. Each one moved independently, weaving patterns in the air that might have been communication, might have been magic, might have been the fundamental code that reality ran on.","Yet for all her terrible beauty and regal bearing, she looked somber. Melancholy wrapped around her like a cloak she couldn’t remove.","“Master,” Kelgar’s voice emerged without Noah’s control, carrying emotion that made the word more than simple acknowledgment. “What troubles you?”","Morathis turned to face her Last Disciple fully, and her expression softened with affection that transcended the master-servant relationship.","“Tell me, Kelgar,” she began, “what do you think of THE Living Existences? THE Living Paradox, THE Living Concept, THE Living Dimensional, and all the others who wear THE as a crown?”","Kelgar’s body shifted, and Noah felt the thoughts forming...not his thoughts but the memory of thoughts, preserved in crystal and now replayed.","“It is... complex, Master.” Kelgar’s voice carried the careful consideration of someone who knew their words mattered.","“Early Creatures view them as necessary tyrants...beings whose power maintains the structure that allows us to exist, even as their whims could unmake us. We...you, respect them as one respects a storm: acknowledgment of power without affection.”","He paused, organizing thoughts that felt ancient despite being memory.","“Fold Dwellers see them differently. To most, THE Living Existences are myths made manifest, so far beyond comprehension that worship and terror become indistinguishable. They are the tyrants that actually answer, though their answers often reshape the question into tragedy.”","Another pause, longer this time.","“As for Living Existences themselves...the regular ones, not those who wear THE, they see their titled kin as either aspiration or impossibility. Something to strive toward while knowing the striving itself might destroy them. They are siblings separated by chasms of power that no bridge could span.”","...!","5/5 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":4076,"title":"Chapter 4076: Chapter 4075: The Weight of Endless Service! IV","paragraphs":["Chapter 4075: The Weight of Endless Service! IV","Morathis listened to the assessment with an expression that grew more sorrowful with each word. When she spoke, her voice carried the weight of terrible knowledge.","“I wish those perceptions were true. I wish THE Living Existences were simply powerful beings playing games with reality for their amusement. That would be... manageable. Predictable, even.”","She moved to a window that showed not outside...but elsewhen, displaying Shores that existed in parallel possibilities.","“THE Living Paradox has broken the restraints placed upon it all those years ago.” The words fell like stones into still water, creating ripples that would never stop spreading.","“It hasn’t been long...time moves strangely at those levels, but thousands of Early Veiled Shores have shattered. Not destroyed, not conquered, but shattered, as if their very existence was retroactively made impossible.”","Her tails writhed with agitation that transcended physical movement.","“Nobody knows why. Is THE Living Paradox doing this intentionally? Is it even aware of what’s happening? Or is this simply what happens when paradox is allowed to exist without restraint...reality begins to contradict itself out of existence? And what of THE Creature? Oh!”","She turned back to Kelgar, and her golden eyes held depths of concern that Noah, even experiencing it secondhand, found overwhelming.","“Some say THE Living Concept is involved, that thought itself has decided physical reality is too limiting. Others claim THE Living Dimensional is folding spaces into themselves, creating pockets of existence that can’t be accessed or escaped. There are even whispers that something else entirely has emerged...something that THE Living Existences themselves fear. Something...Dead.”","The weight of these revelations pressed against the memory itself, making it flicker at the edges.","“Something is coming for our Earliest Folds, Kelgar. Something potentially catastrophic. We don’t know what, we don’t know why, we don’t know how to stop it. We only know that Shores are shattering like glass under pressure, and the pressure is increasing.”","She approached him, and even in memory, Noah could feel the warmth she radiated...it was existential, the comfort of being near something that cared about your existence.","“When it comes...and it will come, where would you rather be?”","The question stayed between them with weight that transcended words. It wasn’t about physical location but existential position. Would he flee? Would he hide? Would he seek safety in distance?","Kelgar’s response came without hesitation, emotion making his voice thick: “With you. With everyone here. If existence ends, I would rather end alongside those who made existence worth having.”","Morathis smiled at this answer, and in that smile was both pride and sorrow, love and resignation. She reached out to touch Kelgar’s face with a hand that could unmake mountains, but touched him with gentleness that wouldn’t disturb dust.","“My loyal disciple. My Last Disciple. Your devotion honors me more than...”","BOOM!","The memory shattered.","Not ended, not concluded, but shattered, as if the crystal containing it could no longer maintain coherence.","Noah felt himself yanked back through layers of time and possibility, his consciousness snapping back into his own body with force that made him stagger.","He stood again before the Memory Stone, his hand still pressed against its surface, but now he understood. The stone had contained the last moment of peace before catastrophe, crystallized and preserved by someone who knew that even memories of better times might become precious.","The implications of what he had witnessed raced through his mind. THE Living Paradox breaking restraints...was this related to the current situation? The shattering of thousands of Early Veiled Shores...","And Morathis herself...an Early Creature of obvious power and compassion, reduced to nothing while her loyal servant continued his vigil forever. What force could accomplish such complete destruction?","|Grand Record Observation Complete|","|Living memory of unfortunate past experienced|","|Effort to understand history recognized|","|Complexity gained: +1,000,000,000|","|Purity gained: +1,000,000,000|","|Additional Reward: Blueprint Acquired|","|Common Living Early Abodes of a Shore|","|Can now construct residences matching Early Creature standards|","|Note: Materials from Primordial Excavation Depths recommended|","The prompts seemed almost mundane after what he had experienced, but Noah understood their significance.","He hadn’t just gained power from observing the memory...he had gained understanding.","The blueprint was practical, but the knowledge of what had happened, even incomplete, was invaluable.","He looked at his companions, who were still mining Paradox Minerals with focused efficiency.","How could one convey the weight of Kelgar’s loyalty, Morathis’s concern, the implications of THE Living Paradox’s actions?","More importantly, what did it mean for their current situation? If THE Living Paradox had once shattered thousands of Shores, what was stopping it from doing so again?","“Well, if the fucker is still around...”","Noah uttered calmly while shaking his head.","The Memory Stone stood silent now, its purpose fulfilled but its presence still commanding. Noah removed his hand slowly, almost reluctantly. There was more to understand here, more connections to make, more patterns to recognize.","But for now, he had enough to consider. The past had been harvested, and like all good harvests, it would need time to properly process what had been gathered.","Noah moved took a single step and appeared beside Sigrid, watching as she worked with the particular focus of someone discovering new applications for her power.","Tendrils of Order extended from her form...conceptual assertions that things should be organized, categorized, made comprehensible.","The Paradox Minerals responded to her authority with reluctant compliance.","Where they had been embedded in crystal formations that defied conventional mining, Order simply insisted they should be separate, accessible, collectible.","The minerals emerged from their housing like students responding to a teacher’s command, arranging themselves in neat formations that awaited collection.","“What have you managed to mine so far?” Noah asked, genuinely curious about the yields this unconventional method was producing.","Sigrid turned to him with an expression that managed to be both proud and slightly exasperated. “These things resist classification. They want to exist and not exist simultaneously, which makes storing them... interesting. Anything that allows me to exercise Order right now is good as this works greatly...”","She handed him a collection of the Paradox Minerals she had extracted, and Noah examined them.","|Paradox Minerals Obtained: 47 units|","|State: Existing/Not Existing (Fluctuating)|","|Quality: Exceptional|","|Warning: May spontaneously decide they were never mined|","|Additional Warning: Prolonged contact may cause holder to question their own existence|","|Storage Recommendation: Convince them they want to be stored|","“...”","1/5"]},{"number":4077,"title":"Chapter 4077: Chapter 4076: The Weight of Endless Service! V","paragraphs":["Chapter 4076: The Weight of Endless Service! V","The minerals themselves were beautiful. They appeared as purple crystals that cast shadows in directions that didn’t exist, their facets reflecting light from sources that weren’t present. Holding them felt like grasping solid uncertainty.","Noah smiled at the absurdity of it all...materials that might retroactively decide they had never been collected, tools that could be forged from possibility itself.","He carefully stored them in a space that he convinced to exist specifically for things that might not exist.","“You should experience the Memory Stone,” he said, looking at Sigrid, then turning to include Moiraine, the Infiniverse, and Ruination in his address. “All of you. Place your hands on it and see what it shows you. I experienced something... significant.”","The four women exchanged glances of curiosity.","They moved toward the Memory Stone thereafter with varying degrees of eagerness.","Sigrid approached with the measured steps of someone expecting either wonder or trap.","Moiraine moved with confidence that suggested she feared neither. The Infiniverse floated forward with anticipation of new experiences to catalogue.","Ruination walked with the certainty of someone who could end whatever they encountered!","The four were breathtaking!","As their hands made contact with the stone simultaneously, scintillating obsidian-purple light erupted around them.","The light didn’t illuminate so much as reveal, showing dimensions of their forms that normally remained hidden. Their eyes closed in unison, consciousness pulled into crystallized memory.","While they experienced whatever the stone chose to show them, Noah turned his attention to his own mining efforts.","How would it feel for him to mine himself? After all, this was effort!","He approached a particularly large cluster of crystals, raising the Goad with the intent of someone about to teach rocks about their own nature.","The first strike was recognized immediately!","HUUM!","|Effort Detected: Manual Mining|","|Principle of Perpetual Harvest Acknowledging Labor|","|Physical work toward resource gathering quantified|","|Multiplication Factor: Applied|","The Goad connected with the crystal formation, and instead of simply breaking, the crystal seemed to undergo an existential crisis!","The stick that had touched it carried a simple message...”You exist to be harvested.”","...!","The crystal’s response was to shatter in a way that suggested it had suddenly understood its purpose. From the broken formation, Paradox Minerals erupted...not the few that should have emerged, but dozens, as if the effort of mining had convinced reality that more reward was deserved!","|Mining Effort Recognized|","|Yield increased by 1000% due to Perpetual Harvest|","|Paradox Minerals are choosing to exist in greater quantities|","|Current harvest: 133 units from single strike|","...!","The 1% of a single Principles continued to be utterly nuts as Noah could only marvel at it!","He could also only become somber as...how the fuck had Early Creatures with Principles died when 1% was this insane!","1% of a Principle had effectively granted him Honored Living Existence power as he could do much more, with one of the main things being...versatility.","A tremendous amount seemed possible!","Noah shook his head as he continued mining with rhythmic precision, each strike of the Goad carrying its own educational component.","There would be a strike, and then a response to the strike!","Strike: “Your crystalline structure is temporary.”","Response: Crystals accepting their impermanence and yielding minerals.","Another strike and...”Holding minerals serves no purpose for immobile crystals.”","Response: Formations releasing their contents with something like relief.","Existential Truths were lain with each strike!","“Being mined is participation in greater purpose.”","Response: Enthusiastic shattering that produced extra yields.","...!","And it continued on and on!","The absurdity of educating geological crystals about their existential purpose while mining them should have been comical! Instead, it felt profound...another demonstration that in his Shore, even the mundane became miraculous when proper effort was applied.","HUUM!","His mining rhythm was interrupted by a sudden eruption of power from the Memory Stone.","The four women touching it blazed with complexity that made the air itself denser!","Purple-obsidian light shot upward from their forms, carrying with it the weight of experience.","|Your companions have experienced enhanced memory immersion|","|Unlike you, they witnessed events through Early Creature perspective|","|The effort of luck and opportunity is also effort|","|Perpetual Harvest recognizes serendipitous positioning|","|Sigrid has gained: +25,000,000,000 Complexity/Purity|","|Moiraine has gained: +25,000,000,000 Complexity/Purity|","|Infiniverse has gained: +25,000,000,000 Complexity/Purity|","|Ruination has gained: +25,000,000,000 Complexity/Purity|","|Additional Inheritance Detected:|","|Early Art of Existence Obtained: Morathis’s Final Conflagration|","|Creates temporary fire-based Kleos Glyphs|","|Temporary nature allows 100x power multiplication|","|Duration: 7 seconds per Glyph|","|Warning: May cause Existence combustion in target area|","...!","Noah read these prompts with astonishment that quickly transformed into joy.","They had received a far greater boon than he had...experiencing the memory from Morathis’s perspective had granted them not just her observations but fragments of her power!","The light surrounding the four women condensed, sinking into their forms as their consciousnesses returned to the present.","Each bore a slightly different expression...Sigrid looked thoughtful, Moiraine appeared energized, the Infiniverse seemed to be categorizing new data, and Ruination simply smiled with satisfaction at having witnessed another ending.","Noah laughed, but not with envy... with genuine pleasure. Their gains were his gains in every way that mattered. Their increased power meant his Shore was stronger, his companions more capable, his family better protected.","“You experienced Morathis herself?” He asked.","Sigrid nodded slowly, her eyes still carrying echoes of golden fire. “She was... magnificent. And terrified. The combination was heartbreaking.”","They all became silent as they processed the heavy meanings all of this would have!","They stood in this contemplative silence for a moment, surrounded by the Crystal Requiem where Kelgar had maintained his eternal vigil.","The Paradox Minerals they had gathered hummed with uncertainty, existing and not existing in their containers. The Memory Stone stood silent, its purpose served but its presence still monumental.","But Noah was not one to let an atmosphere wallow in gravity and seriousness.","Whatever came, they would simply do all they could to face it!","So...","“We should explore deeper,” Noah finally said, breaking the moment. “The first level has given us this much. Imagine what awaits below. let js finish collecting the Minerals here and go.”","“Mmm...” Sigrid nodded as the others followed!","2/5"]},{"number":4078,"title":"Chapter 4078: Chapter 4077: Action and Inaction! I","paragraphs":["Action and inaction...two sides of existence’s most fundamental choice.","Sometimes taking action leads to glory, advancement, transformation. Other times, doing nothing proves equally wise, even salvatory.","Existence itself seemed built on this paradox: that movement and stillness could both be the correct answer, depending on circumstances invisible until after the choice was made.","Consider the tale few knew of the one who would become Duke Whisker, though at the time he was merely an Honored Living Existence among many.","Years ago, when the boundaries between Folds were less defined and travel between them more common, Whisker had faced such a choice.","A delegation had come to him...dozens of winged mice, each one bearing the stellar light that marked them as Honored Living Origins.","They were of the Astral Rodentia lineage, an ancient bloodline that traced its origins back to the Earliest Folds.","Their wings weren’t physical but conceptual, allowing them to fly through ideas as easily as space.","\"Brother Whisker,\" they had said, their collective voice creating waves that suggested opportunity.","\"The Transcendent Elemental Folds hold unprecedented chances for advancement. Living Fire Elementals are teaching their mysteries to those brave enough to endure their trials. Come with us...together, the Astral Rodentia can rise to heights we’ve only dreamed of. Our Towers can continue brnaching into unfathomable Gardens!\"","..!","Whisker had been lounging in the Origin Folds at the time, content in his steady accumulation of power. The offer was tempting...Living Fire Elemental mysteries could accelerate developments uniquely. But something in the eagerness of his kin made him pause.","\"I’ll remain here,\" he had said simply. \"The Origin Folds still have much to teach.\"","They had looked at him with expressions mixing disappointment and pity.","Whisker chose comfortable stagnation over glorious risk. They departed without him, their wings carrying them toward what they believed would be transformation.","Three days later, Whisker felt their existences shatter.","Not fade, not diminish.","They shattered like glass struck by a hammer of annihilation. The sensation ripped through him with the particular agony of recognizing that he was now alone!","The dozens who had gone were the last of the Astral Rodentia besides himself. An entire lineage, reduced to one member through a single catastrophic choice.","The rage that filled him transcended emotion to become force!","Dismay at their loss, fury at whatever had destroyed them, and a crushing weight of survivor’s guilt combined into something that demanded expression.","Now he faced another choice: remain still and safe, or act and risk joining his lineage in oblivion?","The rage won.","Whisker had entered the Transcendent Elemental Folds with the fury of someone with nothing left to lose.","What followed was three days of conflict that rewrote the relationships between Origins and Elementals as he sought to understand what had happened. A single mouse, empowered by grief and rage, had made Living Fire Elementals bleed manna for the first time in many years!","From that conflict arose Duke Whisker...his Purity elevated through battle to heights that touched the rank of Dukes!","His inaction had saved him.","His action had transformed him.","Both choices had been correct, in their time, in their moment.","---","In the Transcendent Spirit Folds, another being contemplated the question of action versus inaction.","The Great Usurper’s consciousness spread across the Folds like oil on water, invisible but present, touching everything while being touched by nothing.","His attention was focused on the interface of his Idle Gaming System, particularly on the feature that had given him unprecedented peace: the [Idle World].","Within that pocket dimension, safe from all external threats, resided everyone he cared about.","His sister, whose annoying laughter could still make him smile across impossible distances.","His lovers, each one a universe of complexity and affection. As long as even a fragment of his existence remained, the Idle Gaming System would endure, protecting them in their bubble of separated space.","He maintained constant partial awareness of the Idle World, a background process of consciousness that ensured their continued safety. It was the one thing he observed while everything else remained beautifully, powerfully idle.","At such a time...","BOOM!","There was an eruption of power that suddenly manifested would have annihilated lesser beings simply through proximity.","A Living Spirit of terrifying magnificence appeared in what had seemed like empty space...though the Great Usurper knew better than most that empty space was never truly empty.","The entity defied simple description.","It appeared as a massive nine-headed cloud dragon, each head representing a different aspect of spiritual authority.","But what made it truly terrible were the massive white chains it bore...chains that weren’t binding it but being used by it to drag something that shouldn’t exist.","A white coffin, simple in design but radiating wrongness that made reality itself uncomfortable.","This was a Duke of Living Spirits, and its presence alone caused the fabric of the Folds to recognize hierarchy!","The nine heads turned in unison toward the region where the Great Usurper had spread his existence, seeing through his invisibility with the casual ease of someone noticing dust on furniture.","\"I sensed a vile Living Spirit doing something as sinful as trying to cover the Folds themselves.\" The voice emerged from all nine mouths simultaneously, creating discordance that was somehow harmonious.","\"Are you so arrogant? Have you forgotten the Covenant of the Spirit King? The Folds are not yours to claim, not yours to infest with your presence like some parasitic growth.\"","HUUM!","The Duke’s form writhed with disgust that transcended the physical.","\"Disperse, you little shit. Return to whatever hole you crawled from, or I will teach you why even thoughts fear to spread too far in the Spirit Folds.\"","..!","Without waiting for response...because what response could matter from something so beneath it?, the Duke erupted with Living Spiritual Authority.","The power that emerged redefined space, establishing new rules about what could exist and how!","Seas of authority descended toward the entire region, ready to deciminate not just the Great Usurper but everything that might have been touched by his presence!","|Terrifying danger detected|","|Existence-ending threat approaching|","|Current form cannot withstand Duke-level assault|","|CRITICAL DECISION REQUIRED:|","|Option 1: Activate emergency protocols and shift into active mode- Relocate across Folds|","|Option 2: Remain idle - Trust the nature of the System|","|Time to impact: 3... 2... 1...|","The Great Usurper watched the descending annihilation with eyes that contained no fear, only calculation. Action or inaction? Flight or stillness? The heavy question, now with his existence hanging in the balance!"]},{"number":4079,"title":"Chapter 4079: Chapter 4078: Action and Inaction! II","paragraphs":["His answer came with the certainty of someone who had built their entire path on a single principle.","\"I choose... to remain idle.\"","The words weren’t spoken...there wasn’t time, but the decision resonated through his being with profound certainty!","This was who he was, what he was. The Great Usurper who achieved everything by doing nothing.","|Choice confirmed: Remaining idle|","|Synchronization with Idle Gaming System increasing|","|Preparing for existence disbursement...|","The Duke’s authority struck with force that redefined destruction. This wasn’t simple annihilation!","This was conceptual erasure, the kind of attack that removed you from having ever existed.","The entire region spanning distances equivalent to dozens of Wheels of Existence shattered like a mirror struck by the concept of breaking itself.","The explosion sent countless fragments scattering across dimensional boundaries, each piece carrying the echoes of what had been. Space itself cracked, reformed, cracked again, as if uncertain whether it should continue existing after such violence!","The Duke of Living Spirits stood amid the devastation with satisfaction that suggested a job well done. The nine heads surveyed the destruction, ensuring nothing remained of the presumptuous spirit that had dared to spread itself too far.","It looked, and looked some more.","The Duke then nodded with contentment!","A moment later, another presence emerged from a Shamanic Fold Gateway...another Duke of Living Spirits, this one appearing as a constellation of eyes that happened to have a vaguely humanoid shape.","\"I don’t know what made you so angry,\" she said, her voice containing the whispers of every spirit that had ever existed in recent times, \"but we have more pressing matters. Another Tool of THE Living Spirit had its trail picked up on. Your expertise is required for evaluation.\"","The nine-headed Duke nodded, the white coffin it dragged shifting with movement that suggested its contents were still aware. \"A presumptuous spirit is dealt with. Let us attend to matters of actual importance.\"","HUUM!","They vanished, leaving only devastation and silence.","Silence!","In that silence, far away...impossibly far, a consciousness bloomed.","The Great Usurper reconstituted... differently.","He found himself surrounded by a sea of white flames that burned nothing while illuminating everything. His perception had scattered and reformed, spread across distances that shouldn’t have been survivable.","|Existence shattered by: Duke Veil-Render of the Nine Sorrows|","|Distinction: White Keeper of the Spirit King’s Covenant|","|Current Status: Technically destroyed|","|However...|","|Due to remaining idle and maintaining System synchronization:|","|Unique nature allowed enhanced scattering through Spirit Folds|","|Current coverage: 10% of all Transcendent Spirit Folds|","|Existence approaching true idle state!|","|Idle Loot quality increased by 1,000,000%|","|Idle Loot quantity increased by 1,000,000%|","|Purity has exceeded Complexity by factor of 3|","|Current state: Virtually undetectable even by Duke-level perception|","...!","The Great Usurper read these prompts and couldn’t help himself...he laughed.","The laughter echoed through ten percent of the Spirit Folds simultaneously, a sound that existed everywhere and nowhere.","It was unimaginably glorious!","\"Duke Veil-Render of the Nine Sorrows,\" he said, tasting the name like wine, savoring its pretension. \"For decimating my existence, for scattering me across impossible distances, for making me more powerful through your attempt at destruction...! I...! I...will do absolutely nothing.\"","...!","|...|","He paused, his consciousness spreading even as he spoke, becoming more idle with each moment.","\"I will remain so perfectly idle that existence itself will forget I’m acting. I will do nothing with such commitment that doing nothing becomes something. And when the time comes...if it comes, which it might not because that would require action, you will understand that the greatest threat isn’t the enemy who attacks...but the one who doesn’t need to. Haha!\"","His laughter continued, but softer now, dispersing into the background noise of existence.","\"Thank you for the assist, Duke Veil-Render. Your action has enabled my inaction to reach heights I couldn’t have achieved through effort. Truly, you’ve been most helpful.\"","Action or inaction...at times, it was impossible to say which one would pave the way for more terrifying results. The Great Usurper had chosen stillness and been rewarded with grandeur. Duke Whisker had chosen both in turn and risen to heights that redefined what a mouse could become.","Perhaps the real wisdom wasn’t in choosing correctly, but in understanding that both choices were always available, always valid, always potentially catastrophic or miraculous depending on factors that might only become clear in retrospect.","Or perhaps not.","After all, understanding itself was a form of action, and the Great Usurper had just proven that sometimes, not understanding...simply being, was its own form of power!","—","Above the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore, where cerulean Sacred Waters lapped at beaches that existed in more dimensions than three, two figures engaged in conversation that would have consequences neither fully anticipated.","Sigrid...or rather, one ordered state of Sigrid, stood with an expression of mounting shock as she processed what the Queen of Matter had revealed.","The stellar light that perpetually bathed the Shore cast her dark white hair in ethereal relief, but her expression was decidedly bound in its disbelief.","\"Wait,\" she said, her voice carrying the particular tone of someone hoping they had misheard. \"Are you telling me that Osmont has... how many women he’s involved with? More than a dozen?!\"","The Queen of Matter blinked with the slow deliberation of someone who didn’t understand why this was shocking.","Books floated around her in lazy orbits, their Fables occasionally glowing as they updated themselves with new information.","\"Yes, Ma’am Most Recent Harem Member Addition,\" she replied with matter-of-fact certainty that made the title sound like an official position. \"Over a dozen at last count, though the number tends to fluctuate depending on how you define ’involved.’ But did you like the other parts of my Fables? I spoke about his progression through the Cosmos, Oppenheimer...oh, I always liked Oppenheimer! And-\"","\"How does he even have the time?\" Sigrid muttered, more to herself than to the Queen of Matter, her mind trying to process the logistics of maintaining that many relationships while also managing an Early Veiled Shore, navigating weavings across multiple Folds, and apparently transcending existence itself on a regular basis!"]},{"number":4080,"title":"Chapter 4080: Chapter 4079: Action and Inaction! III","paragraphs":["The Queen of Matter’s enhanced hearing caught the mumbled question, and she responded with the enthusiasm of someone sharing useful information.","\"Oh, Ma’am Living Order, he makes the time! Literally!\" She gestured expansively, causing several of her floating books to scatter and reorganize. \"If you don’t know, he uses the time dilation features of the Infiniverse as much as possible. Time dilation, parallel processing, simultaneous existence across multiple areas- he’s probably using something like that right now in... that building over there.\"","She pointed toward the Abode of the Early Creature in the distance, its impossible architecture catching light that didn’t exist to cast shadows that shouldn’t be there.","Sigrid’s eyes narrowed as she followed the gesture. \"What do you mean?\"","The Queen of Matter tilted her head with the particular angle of someone who thought the answer was obvious. \"Well, Ma’am Living Order, Sir Osmont is in that Abode right now with your fellow Harem Members.\"","The words landed with the weight of revelation that Sigrid hadn’t been prepared for. Her eyes widened to dimensions that Order itself wouldn’t normally allow.","\"What do you mean ’in the Abode’? Right now? Doing what?\"","The Queen of Matter blinked again, this time with the slow confusion of someone realizing they might be having two different conversations.","She looked at Sigrid with an expression that suggested she was questioning whether THE Living Order understood basic concepts.","\"Well, in the privacy of that Abode, I’m sure they’re not playing tag or anything like that.\" She paused, considering how to phrase this delicately, then gave up on delicacy entirely.","\"One of Sir’s favorite hobbies is Dual Cultivation. The exchange of essences, the mingling of energies, the multiplication of advancement through intimate-\"","...!","\"Right now?!\" Sigrid’s voice rose to frequencies that made nearby Sacred Herbs lean away. \"Over there?! While our other bodies are delving in the Depths?!\"","The Queen of Matter nodded with the patience of someone explaining water to fish. \"Yes?\" She turned her head sideways, studying Sigrid with genuine concern. \"Ma’am Living Order, do I need to teach you about the birds and the bees? Well... that metaphor might not translate properly across existential levels. How shall I explain? When two or more beings of sufficient complexity decide to engage in recreational advancement through physical and spiritual union-\"","Sigrid didn’t let her finish. Her face flushed with a combination of emotions that Order was having trouble categorizing...embarrassment, indignation, and something that might have been competitive interest.","She turned away from the Queen of Matter, her expression filling with determination that suggested decisions had been made.","\"Osmont!\"","HUUM!","Her voice rang across the Shore with authority that made reality itself stand at attention. The Sacred Totems resonated, the Tenders paused in their endless labor, and even the Marine Lifeforms in the Aquarium turned to see what had provoked THE Living Order.","Moments later, space folded in a way that suggested it had been politely asked to make an exception, and another body of Noah materialized. This one bore the same three Seed Glyphs, the same casual authority, but his expression was stern as his gaze fixed on the Queen of Matter.","She froze completely, her books stopping mid-orbit.","Had she done something wrong? Had she violated some protocol about discussing the Master’s romantic arrangements? Was she about to be educated by the Goad about proper discretion?","Ooh? The eyes of the Queen of Matter pulsed with possibilities!","But Noah’s attention shifted immediately to Sigrid, who stood before him with the particular posture of someone who had identified a problem and intended to solve it.","\"It seems,\" she said, managing to sound both cute and annoyed simultaneously, like a cat that had discovered its favorite napping spot occupied, \"that you need Order in your life. You are too chaotic!\"","Noah raised his eyebrows with the particular amusement of someone who enjoyed where this was going. Without warning, he stepped forward and embraced her, his arms wrapping around her with possessive certainty that made space itself jealous.","\"I thought I had you?\" His voice carried that tyrannical confidence that made reality reorganize itself to accommodate his statements. \"Are you not Order? My Order?\"","The words should have been overwhelming.","The embrace should have been inescapable.","But Sigrid, THE Living Order who was still learning what that meant...managed to be both flustered and defiant.","She broke free from his embrace with movements that suggested Order had decided to be temporarily disorderly, grabbed his hand with authority, and began leading him toward the Abode.","\"You need a different kind of Order!\" she declared, her voice carrying the particular tone of someone who had decided something and would not be dissuaded. \"You need to be set straight! Organized! Properly sequenced!\"","WAA!","Noah’s clone shook his head with the exasperation. But he followed along without resistance, because sometimes the wisest action was inaction. Sometimes, surrender was its own form of victory.","Their figures disappeared into the Abode, passing through doors that existed in more states than open or closed!","What occurred within those walls would remain unknown to others, though the Abode itself seemed to pulse with satisfaction, as if it approved of whatever Order was about to impose.","Outside, the Queen of Matter released a breath she hadn’t realized she’d been holding. Her books resumed their orbits, though several seemed to be glowing with the excitement of new Fables being written.","\"Another woman has fallen,\" she said to no one in particular, though her tone suggested this was less lamentation and more observation of natural law.","She pulled out a particularly large golden book from the collection orbiting her, its pages blank but eager to be filled.","Humming a tune of melody, she looked around the Early Veiled Shore with the eye of someone whose job was to observe and record.","The Shore bustled with activity that would have seemed impossible anywhere else. Tenders moved through the plots with mechanical grace, harvesting what had grown while planting seeds for future harvests.","Each movement was purposeful, each action contributing to the perpetual cycle of growth and collection that defined this place.","Each movement exerted effort as since it was under the gaze of the Infiniverse and The Early Creature, the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest shone here as well!"]},{"number":4081,"title":"Chapter 4081: Chapter 4080: Fables and Pride! I","paragraphs":["The gaze of the Queen of Matter drifted to the Aquarium, where close to a dozen Marine Lifeforms now swam through Early Sacred Waters that shouldn’t have been able to exist outside the Earliest Folds.","Each creature was a masterwork of evolution guided by impossible circumstances...fish that swam through time as easily as water, eels that existed in multiple dimensions simultaneously, something that might have been an octopus if octopi had decided that tentacles were too limiting.","The Sacred Totems stood at their positions like guardians of possibility, each one humming with stored materials and barely contained power.","Heidrun grazed on Singular Prosperity Grass and Auric Vitae Grasses with the casual arrogance of someone who had existed before grass knew it was supposed to be eaten. Each bite seemed to make her more real, more present, as if the grass was teaching her new ways to exist.","\"Sir Osmont continues to do things that pave the way for the unimaginable,\" the Queen of Matter said aloud, her words being recorded even as she spoke them. \"In all this grandeur...this impossible, improbable, absolutely absurd grandeur...I’m glad to be part of it. Even if I’m just a footnote on a single page of this grand Fable.\"","She sighed with happiness that transcended simple contentment. To be part of a story still being written, to watch legend being crafted in real-time...what greater purpose could a Record Keeper ask for?","A shift in the air behind her made her awareness spike. Temperature dropped and rose simultaneously as shadows gathered in ways that suggested they had always been there. A figure wrapped in darkness and frost materialized with the particular grace of someone who had made friends with contradiction.","The Queen of Matter turned with a smile that suggested this was expected, welcome, routine.","\"Oh, Shadow Guard Night! Help me record the most recent Fable! THE Living Order has just dragged one of Sir Osmont’s bodies into the Abode for what she called ’a different kind of Order,’ and I need someone to help me speculate wildly about what that might mean!\"","Night emerged more fully from her wrapping of shadows, ice crystals forming in the air around her despite the Shore’s warmth. Her expression remained unreadable, but something in her posture suggested amusement.","\"Should we be recording such private matters?\" Night’s voice carried the whisper of winter wind through empty halls.","\"Everything is Fable,\" the Queen of Matter replied with certainty that asked for no argument. \"The grand battles and the quiet moments, the existential achievements and the personal entanglements. Sir Osmont’s story isn’t just about power...it’s about the people that power brings together.\"","Night considered this, then nodded slowly. \"Then we should note that the Shore seems particularly vibrant today. As if it approves of its Master finding more happiness. Or maybe just the inclusion of THE Living Order...\"","They were right. The Early Veiled Shore buzzed with life and possibility that transcended its normal vibrancy. Every plant grew a little taller, every wave sparkled a little brighter, every grain of sand seemed a little more golden.","At the Shore’s center, two Seeds commanded attention through their mere existence.","The Seed of Inevitability pulsed with power that suggested it was moments away from blooming, its nature still undecided but its potential unlimited.","Beside it, the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest glowed with satisfaction of purpose achieved. It had been planted by the First Farmer, failed for eons, and finally found success through the Infiniverse’s sacrifice and transformation. Now it stood as testament that even failure could be harvested for future success.","The Shore was many things...sanctuary, fortress, farm, home. But more than any of these, it was proof that impossibility was just possibility that hadn’t been properly motivated yet.","Inside the Abode, Order was being imposed in ways that would remain private. Outside, life continued in its beautifully chaotic way, each being pursuing their own purposes while contributing to the greater whole.","And somewhere in the Primordial Early Excavation Depths, other bodies of Noah and Sigrid, and Moiraine for that matter, continued their delving, very much aware that their other selves were engaged in very different forms of exploration.","Such was life in the Early Veiled Shore...multiple things happening simultaneously, each thread weaving into an existence that no single perspective could fully appreciate.","The Queen of Matter opened her golden book and began writing, her words capturing not just events but the feeling of them, the weight of them, the beautiful absurdity of beings powerful enough to reshape existence choosing to spend their time on things as wonderfully mundane as relationships.","\"Chapter 5,731,\" she spoke as she wrote. \"In which Order discovers that some chaos requires hands-on management...\"","Night blinked as she shook her head. \"You...aren’t writing your own fanfictions again, are you? If Sir finds out...\"","...!","The Queen of Matter instantly grabbed Night’s mouth white looking around. With stern eyes, she spoke out. \"Don’t speak loudly about this! Okay?! I’ll lend you the rare possible Fable of the Rank A Hunter, Elizabeth of the Blessed Empire from Sir’s Homeworld...\"","Night laughed as she shook her head, and the Shore continued its endless dance of growth, harvest, and possibility!","—","In an extremely far distance.","The Desiccated Sleeping Shore stretched like a monument to endings.","Where other Shores sang with life and possibility, this one whispered of what happened when existence forgot to continue.","The sands weren’t golden but grey-white, like ash that had forgotten it once was fire. No waters lapped at these beaches...only dried beds where oceans had given up on being wet!","Alexander stepped out from a swirling multicolored portal at this moment. In his arms carried princess style, held with the particular care reserved for precious things that might break, was Seraphina Valorheart.","She breathed heavily, each inhalation carrying the weight of overexertion.","Her usually immaculate form showed signs of strain...hair disheveled, flushed cheeks...","Whatever they had done, wherever they had been, had pushed even her considerable capabilities to their limits!"]},{"number":4082,"title":"Chapter 4082: Chapter 4081: Fables and Pride! II","paragraphs":["Alexander himself bore marks of the journey. His chest was laid bare, the fabric of his upper garment having been sacrificed to something that left no remains.","His toned muscles gleamed with perspiration that contained traces of conceptual effort.","Upon his chest, his Enneagram blazed brighter than ever, its nine points connected by lines that seemed to pulse with heartbeat rhythm.","Near the bisected head of an Early Creature that served as this Shore’s most prominent landmark, two figures waited. Royal Law Tristesse stood with the patience of someone who had learned that rushing Law only made it contrary. Beside her, Kaedric observed with high expectations!","Tristesse sighed as she watched Alexander’s careful handling of Seraphina.","\"Were you successful?\" The question emerged with weight that suggested entire futures hung on the answer.","Alexander’s gaze turned cold as he nodded once.","\"Yes. I know where the Early Tool of THE Living Law is.\" He paused, adjusting his hold on Seraphina as she stirred slightly.","\"But if anyone other than me and Seraphina approach it, the Tool will disappear across Folds and time. Perhaps permanently. You two will have to stay behind.\"","...!","The words landed with finality that made even the dead Shore seem more lifeless!","Royal Law Tristesse’s eyes burned with expectations and possibilities, her mind clearly racing through implications, calculating probabilities, weighing costs against potential gains.","When she spoke, she seemed to have thought of something else entirely as she was thoughtful.","\"Do you know what the Chronicles of Judgment say about THE Living Law’s Tools?\"","She used the formal name...the Chronicles of Judgment, the record that Living Laws had maintained since the Earliest Folds, documenting the Laws that governed them, the precedents that shaped existence’s rules.","\"Only Dukes of Law and Royal Living Laws can read the deepest sections, the parts that record THE Living Law’s direct interventions.\" Her voice grew distant, as if reading from memory that transcended simple recollection.","\"There’s a story there, ancient even by our standards.\"","She moved slightly.","\"A terrifying Fold Dweller approached THE Living Law with a question that contained accusation. ’Has THE Creature abandoned us?’ the Fold Dweller asked. ’Are you the only one maintaining order now? The only one who cares whether existence has structure?’\"","Tristesse’s expression grew complex, mixing reverence with something that might have been fear.","\"THE Living Law’s response was characteristically indirect: ’Do not think of matters that do not concern you or others. Through me, through my Tools, through my Weapons, prosperity will be ensured across all Folds. Structure will be maintained. Order will prevail.’\"","...!","She paused, letting the weight of those words settle.","\"And then THE Living Law did something unprecedented. It gave this Fold Dweller an Early Tool...the Scale of Equilibrium’s Reckoning.\"","The name itself seemed to make the air heavier, as if existence recognized something significant being invoked.","\"According to the Chronicles, the Scale could weigh not just physical matter but concepts themselves. Justice against mercy. Order against chaos. Even existence against void. Whatever was placed upon its pans would be measured against absolute truth, and the lighter concept would be... corrected. Made heavier through enforcement, or removed entirely if it couldn’t bear the weight of existence.\"","HUUM!","Her gaze grew intense as she continued.","\"THE Living Law told the Fold Dweller to use it to balance any chaos. To discipline Early Creatures and Living Existences if necessary. To ensure that power never grew so absolute that it forgot its responsibilities.\"","Royal Law Tristesse looked at Alexander and Seraphina with eyes that had made their decision. The stern set of her features suggested this choice had been weighed and found necessary.","\"Go.\" The single word carried more authority than lengthy commands could have.","\"If you can obtain any Tool of THE Living Law...whether the Scale or something else, it will be a boon for all Living Laws. We have existed too long on precedent alone. An actual Tool would change many things...\"","Alexander studied her for a moment, perhaps weighing her sincerity against necessity. Then he nodded simply!","Without further words, he began walking toward the bisected head of the Early Creature.","Each step seemed purposeful, as if following a path only he could see. The Enneagram on his chest began to pulse brighter, its light synchronizing with something.","As he drew closer, it became clear that Seraphina also bore an Enneagram on her chest that was shining the same manner!","Together, they created a resonance that made the dead Shore remember it had once been alive!","The bisected head of the Early Creature...massive even in death, even split in half...began to respond with recognition. The two Enneagrams weren’t just symbols or sources of power...they were keys, and the Desiccated Sleeping Shore was a lock that had been waiting eons to be opened!","The air grew thick with possibility. The grey-white sands began to swirl despite the absence of wind. The dried ocean beds cracked in patterns.","Three seconds passed. Four. Five.","BOOM!","The explosion was transitional...the sound of space deciding to be somewhere else. Where Alexander and Seraphina had stood, only disturbed sand remained. They hadn’t traveled in any conventional sense...they had been admitted, accepted, allowed entry to something that existed perpendicular to normal reality.","Royal Law Tristesse and Kaedric remained on the Desiccated Sleeping Shore, the sudden absence of their companions making the desolation more pronounced.","Tristesse’s demeanor shifted immediately from contemplative to commanding!","The historian transformed into the Royal Law she was, authority radiating from her form like heat from forge-fired metal.","\"Come,\" she said to Kaedric, her voice seeking no delay. \"We must prepare for the Kleos Concordat. Every Law must be ready and every possible argument anticipated.\"","She began moving with purpose that transformed walking into declaration.","\"If they return with a Tool before then...\" She let the sentence hang, but the implications were clear.","A Tool of THE Living Law would shift many things.","Kaedric followed, his own thoughts clearly racing through possibilities. \"Do you think they’ll succeed?\"","Tristesse considered the question with the weight it deserved. \"Who the fuck knows man, we are all just trying everything we can...\"","...!"]},{"number":4083,"title":"Chapter 4083: Chapter 4082: Fables and Pride! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4082: Fables and Pride! III","She paused at the edge of the Shore, where a portal awaited to return them to the Doorway to the Loom.","“But...if anyone can retrieve something THE Living Law left behind, it would be them. come on!”","Weavings of existence continued to unfold across the Folds.","There were countless Fables and countless players, with some not knowing just how terrifying the Folds of others could be.","While some sought Tools of THE Living Law in distant realms, others pursued something more fundamental!","Not artifacts of power, but power itself, and the knowledge of how existence could be transcended.","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, there existed a region that defied even paradoxical standards.","Dozens of obsidian rivers flowed here, but they followed no conventional physics...some ran upward, others sideways, several flowed through themselves in loops that had no beginning or end.","The waters weren’t water but liquidified contradiction, each drop containing the statement “this does not exist” while very clearly existing!","At the center of these impossible waterways stood Schrodinger in his characteristic beggar’s appearance, though what surrounded him suggested anything but poverty of power.","Five Inevitabilities lay still around him.","Not dormant, not waiting....truly still, in the way only dead things could achieve.","These were the same Inevitabilities he had imprisoned in the Doorway to the Loom, the ones that had devoured part of THE Living Order’s Everything.","Now their countless tentacles, which had once reached through dimensions to consume meaning itself, lay limp and purposeless!","An Inevitability that was 5 Inevitabilities, killed!","The air thrummed with the terrifying complexity of Paradox that Schrodinger emitted.","He worked with the focused intensity of a surgeon operating on existence itself, his hands moving through the corpse of the nearest Inevitability with purpose that transcended the physical.","He was carving out Everything.","Not the general everything, but the specific Everything that the Inevitability had consumed from THE Living Order!","The process should have been impossible...Everything, once devoured by an Inevitability, may be gone forever, processed into nothing.","May be.","Yet here was Schrodinger, carefully extracting what shouldn’t exist from something that barely existed itself.","Behind him, the paradoxical rivers suddenly parted like curtains made of impossibility.","Through the gap floated Duke Diviticus, moving with the caution of someone entering a space they knew they survived only through sufferance!","Schrodinger had sensed her approach and allowed it...without his permission, the rivers would have drowned her in contradictions that even her Duke-level existence couldn’t reconcile.","“I did not mean offense before,” she said immediately, her usual arrogance replaced with something approaching humility. “I am patient...I’m trying to be. I’m just attempting to be like you. To reach your height, your power, your understanding of what Paradox truly means.”","...!","Schrodinger continued his work as she spoke, his hands never pausing in their extraction.","When he finally responded, his voice carried the weight of someone who had seen too much to be impressed by ambition alone.","“It might be possible with enough work.” He paused, adjusting his grip on something that wasn’t quite matter but wasn’t quite concept. “But what I seek to do is something that not many will understand. The path I walk isn’t about power in the traditional sense.”","He turned slightly, fixing her with eyes that contained depths of paradox that made her Duke-level perception struggle.","“Do you... wish to know an utterly abysmal secret? Something revealed to me by something even I still do not fully understand?”","....!","The question hung between them with weight!","Diviticus floated closer, her entire being focused on this moment. When she spoke, the single word carried desperation that transcended simple curiosity.","“Please.”","Schrodinger smiled as his voicd echoed out.","“During an extremely low point in my existence, I floated across the Earliest Folds in despair. I wasn’t seeking anything...I was seeking nothing. Release. An end to the constant struggle of maintaining paradox in an existence that insisted on resolution.”","He returned to his work, but his voice continued, painting pictures with words.","“In that state, approaching the kind of nothing that even Paradox fears, I heard a voice. It said...’I sense a vibrant light wishing to dwindle.’","The voice likely stemmed from one of THE Living Existences...though even that is conjecture as even I do not know for sure. I cannot say for certain what spoke to me that day.”","His hands moved through the Inevitability’s form with practiced precision as he continued.","“I responded with the desperation of someone who had tried everything and found it all wanting. ‘What is it all for?’ I asked. ‘Nothing seems to work. There is never enough power. Fold Dwellers, Living Existences, even Paradoxes...the vast majority of life will never reach the grandeur of THE Living Existences or THE Creature. It is all... for naught.'”","Silence settled over them, broken only by the sound of extraction that shouldn’t have a sound.","Schrodinger’s work continued as he picked up.","“The voice laughed...not cruelly, but with the mockery of someone explaining why water is wet to someone drowning.","‘Of course you could never reach them,’ it said. ‘They have grasped an entirely different Scale of Existence compared to you.'”","BOOM!","Diviticus leaned forward, her entire being focused on what came next.","“The voice explained something that reframed everything I thought I knew,” Schrodinger continued. “It spoke of the Vakochev Scale of Civilizational Existence. Deemed so by someone who theorized that existential civilization wasn’t about numbers, or tools, or magic, or technology, but about the relationship between oneself and existence’s fundamental architecture.”","He paused his extraction, his expression growing grave.","“Here’s the truly abysmal part- You, me... every being we know...we aren’t even civilized enough to be given a ranking on this scale. We exist at what is known as Level Zero...Pre-Civilizational Existence.”","Diviticus recoiled slightly at this, but Schrodinger continued relentlessly.","“Level Zero is where we can meaningfully affect existence, yes. We can tap into the energy of reality, manipulate local Folds, even begin grasping and reaching out unsuccessfully at tools that tip the scales...Principles, the manipulation of Everythings.... But we’re still operating within weavings rather than upon it. We’re complex enough to do many things, but we’re essentially sophisticated animals in a zoo we don’t even know exists. Uncivilized. Weak. Fucking laughable.”","...!","His voice...dripped with immense pain and hatred when he said this- and these emotions quickly disappeared!","3/5"]},{"number":4084,"title":"Chapter 4084: Chapter 4083: Fables and Pride! IV","paragraphs":["Chapter 4083: Fables and Pride! IV","Schrodinger’s face seemed to be dismayed as he continued!","“We are feeble, and do not know anything. We could be eradicated in a few seconds, and we would not even know. It is immense weaknes!”","“It is terrifying as sometimes, I can barely close my eyes. I have not slept for eons as...what if I never wake up? If something like THE Living Paradox simply looked at me and told me to stop existing, and that would be it? To be at this level of Existence...is to be fearful. It is to be weak. And I truly do not wish to be weak!”","HUUM!","He became silent.","His words were heavy as Diviticus could not reply!","But he continued as if regardless of his fear...he had to continue.","“Above that, where THE Living Existences and The Creature are...at a stage where Principles simply flow through them. Everythings are a currency, and they have tapped into weavings of existence we cannot even understand. A level of Civilized Existence we cannot fathom. Ah...”","He shook his head with longing.","Deep, immesurable longing!","...!","Diviticus’s form trembled with the weight of this revelation. “What is the method to reach that scale?! How can we advance?! What is that Scale called? Is...there a level of Existential Civilization after that? After THE Living Existences and THE Creature?!”","A bombardment of questions as Diviticus seemed to be having an existential crisis!","And yet...","Schrodinger shook his head with something that might have been pity.","“You... are too far off to know things like that. The journey from Zero to One requires more than power...it requires fundamental restructuring of how you relate to existence itself. How you tap into Authority, how authority cycles through you, perpetuity...ah”","He shook his head ahead as he breathed out as if to calm himself.","He then gestured to his work. “Come, observe as I take into my being part of what used to be inside THE Living Order.”","...!","The words resonated with terrible certainty.","Schrodinger was extracting something that had been part of THE Living Order’s Everything.","His hands emerged from the bisected Inevitability holding something that hurt to perceive....a fragment of Disorder from Order itself, crystallized into form through paradox. It was black-gold, like solidified authority, pulsing with power!","“This,” Schrodinger said, holding the fragment with reverence that transcended possession, “is what advancement looks like. Not taking power, but understanding what power means. Not ascending through force, but recognizing that the ladder you’re climbing might be leaning against the wrong wall.”","He absorbed the fragment into himself, and for a moment, his beggar’s form flickered...showing something vast, something that existed across multiple weavings simultaneously before collapsing back into humble appearance.","Diviticus watched with awe, horror, and fear combined.","She was witnessing something that shouldn’t be possible!","“The Scale of Civilizational Existence...the Vakochev Scale of Existence isn’t about individual power. It’s about how many of existence’s rules and principles you’re playing by versus how many you’re writing. THE Living Existences write rules and principles. We...are still learning to read them.”","...!","The work continued, surrounded by impossible rivers and watched by someone who was beginning to understand that power, true power, might be something entirely different from what she had imagined!","Oh!","—","For existences who had lived countless eons, witnessed the birth and death of concepts themselves, a single day was akin to the passage of a second.","Yet as the hours dwindled and the appointed time approached, even these ancient beings felt something that might have been anticipation.","The Living Existences had already begun their convergence toward the chosen location...a site that had sparked debate until the final moments.","Some had argued for the grandeur of the Origin Folds, others for the neutrality of the Spaces between Folds.","But ultimately, with irony that wasn’t lost on those who understood such things, they had chosen the Transcendent Temporal Folds...the very place where Dead Existences had first torn through the veil.","The specific region was deliberately mundane: an empty expanse far from the Temporal Heart where the Living Temporals concentrated their power.","Yet as agreement crystallized, the space began its transformation.","What had been void became venue, emptiness became amphitheater!","Tens of thousands had already gathered. Living Origins arrived in formations.","Living Temporals materialized at moments they deemed appropriate. Living Spirits drifted in like thoughts becoming solid. Living Quantums existed in multiple states of arrival simultaneously. Living Elementals burned, froze, flowed, and crystallized their way into being!","Living Dimensionals unfolded from spaces that shouldn’t have had room for them. Living Concepts appeared by first being understood, then being seen...and the remaining Living Existences had their own entrance.","The Living Paradoxes, notably, were barely represented...only Duke Elagabalus and a handful of others lounging with the particular casualness of those who knew arriving early was just another form of being late.","At the center of this gathering impossibility, Living Concepts had taken the lead in construction.","Their forms...if they could be called forms...moved through the space like architects of reality itself, building with materials and with ideas given substance.","The structure taking shape was glorious. It was a coliseum, but one that existed in more dimensions than three. Ten sections divided the space equally, each one attuned to the nature of its intended occupants.","Portals marked each section... statements of identity, each one declaring which breed of existence belonged within.","From the portal marked with the endless spiral of Living Origins, two figures emerged: Duke Whisker floating with his characteristic dignity, and beside him, Noah, who was shaking his head with visible exasperation.","“Why drag me away from Aeternitas Concordia when the Kleos Concordat hasn’t even begun?” Noah’s voice carried the irritation of someone interrupted from important work.","Duke Whisker’s whiskers twitched with amusement. “All Living Existences arrive before the appointed time to provide input to the Living Concepts. How would you prefer your space designed? Your own area with specifications of your choosing? Or would you simply prefer to sit with the Living Origins?”","The suggestion of being lumped in with others made Noah’s eyes shine with the light of someone who had just been offered an opportunity disguised as inconvenience.","“Okay,” he said, his irritation transforming into interest. “Let’s see how everything is.”","4/5"]},{"number":4085,"title":"Chapter 4085: Chapter 4084: Fables and Pride! V","paragraphs":["Chapter 4084: Fables and Pride! V","Duke Whisker began to float through the construction zone, his tiny form somehow maintaining dignity despite having to look up at almost everything.","Noah followed, his perception taking in details that others might miss...the way Living Concepts didn’t build but convinced space that it had always been built, the subtle hierarchies revealed in how different groups positioned themselves, the careful dance of power and pride playing out through architectural choices.","“That is Duke Vicialis there,” Duke Whisker indicated with a subtle gesture toward a gathering of Living Elementals. “He’s instructing his throne be forged from flames that burn backward through time. For some, mere fire isn’t sufficiently impressive anymore.”","Noah observed the Duke in question...a being whose form seemed to be combustion having an identity crisis.","“And there,” Duke Whisker continued, directing attention to another section, “Duke Voss of the Living Dimensionals...”","Duke Whisker calmly pointed out many things as Noah was able to observe the scale of the place where the Kleos Concordat would take place!","The construction continued around them, reality being reshaped by Living Concepts.","Noah watched as thrones were carved from crystallized time, platforms were woven from solid thought, and seating arrangements were negotiated.","“My dear Whisker, what an unexpected pleasure.”","HUUM!","The voice arrived with the weight of temporal authority wrapped in genuine warmth.","A figure materialized from temporal flux with the precision of someone who knew exactly when they wanted to arrive and had arranged causality to accommodate.","Golden hair that seemed to age and youth simultaneously, eyes that held the light of stars being born while watching them die!","This...was one of the nine Living Temporal Pillars, beings who supposedly maintained the Temporal Weave that kept the Folds from collapsing into sequential chaos.","Supposedly.","But when Moiraine had been revealing to Noah the structures of Living Existences and how Living Temporals and Living Spirits were the only ones who had unique hierarchies of ruling and not Kleos Councils...she had also mentioned that the idea that Nine Living Temporal Pillars being the ones to maintain the time of the Folds was utter bullshit.","And now, Noah actually got the chance to observe one such being.","“Living Temporal Pillar Chronos,” Duke Whisker acknowledged, his tone carrying respectful wariness.","“Such formality between old colleagues seems almost insulting to our shared history,” Chronos replied.","His attention shifted to Noah with the focus of someone who could see through time itself. “And who commands enough respect to receive Whisker’s personal attention? The temporal threads around you are... fascinating. They bend without breaking, accelerate without losing cohesion. Hey, I actually cannot even see a few seconds of what your future time could be when even for Dukes, I could at least see a few minutes. What’s that about? Who do you...represent?”","HUUM!","Noah met the ancient being’s gaze steadily. “I’m simply here to represent myself.”","“‘Simply’ and ‘myself’...two words that rarely belong in the same sentence at gatherings like these.” Chronos’s expression grew more intrigued, his presence making nearby beings unconsciously check whether they were experiencing the present or just remembering it.","“Most beings represent factions, ideologies, or abstract principles they barely understand. But you... you’re remarkably self-contained. Your timeline doesn’t leak into others’ futures. That requires either tremendous ignorance or tremendous control. Haha, I can’t figure you out!”","....!","The assessment buzzed in the air as Chronos already knew which option applied.","His positivity wasn’t naive enthusiasm...it was the confidence of someone who had calculated all possible outcomes and known what could unfold!","And his eyes now gazes with interest towards Noah who...did not entertain it.","He turned towards Duke Whisker.","“I have an idea for how I want my space to look,” Noah said, smoothly redirecting while acknowledging the probe. He turned to Duke Whisker with specifications. “Simple. Understated. A few thrones crafted from materials that suggest growth rather than power. Positioned for observation without ostentation.”","Duke Whisker floated off to convey the specifications, leaving Noah with the Temporal Pillar whose presence made causality nervous.","“You know,” Chronos said conversationally, his smile fading slightly, “I’ve existed long enough to see patterns repeat until they become laws. Patters are the one thing I always see, and yet I cannot see yours. Why is that?”","...!","A heavy question.","He studied Noah with eyes that saw through more than just space.","And as Noah faced the gaze of this powerful being...he remained calm and looked ahead as Duke Whisker returned!","“Your specifications have been conveyed,” Duke Whisker announced, returning with timing. “The Living Concepts were... intrigued. Your space will be carved out between Living Origins and Living Laws.”","Between two Living Existences. It would undoubtedly be unique!","The Living Temporal Pillar, Chronos, had none of his questions answered as he smiled at this as he rose up. He was a type of being that was supremely powerful, but unbothered!","“I look forward to seeing what someone who ‘simply represents himself’ contributes to the Concordat. In my experience, those who claim the least often have the most to offer. Or the most to hide. Either makes for excellent entertainment. I just came for introductions because the timeline of Duke Whisker here became chaotic and murky...you will have to be careful.”","...!","With that perfectly calibrated mixture of compliment and warning, Chronos dispersed into temporal probability.","Duke Whisker and Noah floated calmly as around them, the 10 Living Existences continue weaving in and out calmly.","At such a point, Duke Whisker gazed towards Noah while sending a mental message only he could hear.","|All Living Existences are represented here, but...not the Living Order, right? You mentioned multiple Thrones for your section, do you plan to bring the Living Order here?|","...!","Duke Whisker asked such a question as Noah smiled.","He sensed the terrifying waves of complexities surging in this area as a grand stage formed, with Royal Living Existences carrying gloriously powerful and prideful gazes moving in the distance to make sure their proper grandeur was displayed here.","Was such a thing still important? The hubris? The pride? The sheer fact that some thought themsleves higher than others as they moved to preserve their dignity through any means necessary?","Noah shook his head as his reply to Duke Whisker was a simple one.","“We will see.”","...!","Truly, they would all see!","5/5 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming! Next chapter titles: The Dead Do Not Stay Dead! I-IV"]},{"number":4086,"title":"Chapter 4086: Chapter 4085: Losses and Gains! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4085: Losses and Gains! I","There are existences accustomed to winning...beings for whom victory is not achievement but expectation, for whom success is the baseline from which all other experiences are measured.","When such beings experience loss, the sensation transcends simple defeat.","It becomes existential crisis, a fundamental questioning of identity itself!","If you are defined by winning, what are you when you lose?","There were those existences, and then... there was Noah.","At this moment, he lay upon a vast white sea, his body carried by gentle waves that had once been cerulean but now shone with stellar radiance.","The light of Order had bombarded these waters so thoroughly, so completely, that they had forgotten their original color and adopted a new truth.","The waves moved with purpose that transcended physics, supporting him with the particular care of water that had been organized into knowing exactly how to hold someone.","He stared at a ceiling inside an isolated pocket dimension in the Abode of the Early Creature, and for perhaps the first time in his rapid ascension through impossibility, he had to admit something that sat strangely in his consciousness...","He had actually lost.","During his Dual Cultivation with THE Living Order, despite all his complexity, despite his multiple Seed Glyphs, despite being The Early Creature, Osmont..he had lost!","Not devastatingly, not humiliatingly, but definitively. Sigrid’s complexity and purity had exceeded his own, and he had learned firsthand what that distinction of [THE] truly meant when attached to a Living Existence.","Basically, he was manhandled by his girl!","The prompts floating before his vision offered consolation that transcended simple comfort.","|Extended Intimate Connection with THE Living Order (Awakening) Completed|","|Duration: Temporal Manipulation Extended – 72 Subjective Hours|","|Understanding of Order Fundamentally Enhanced|","|Existential Resonance Achieved|","|Purity Gained: +55,000,000,000|","|Complexity Gained: +25,000,000,000|","|Note: Differential gains reflect Order’s preference for purity over complexity|","|Additional Note: Being dominated by THE Living Order has its benefits|","The boons were indeed terrifying!","So even though he had lost control, had been the one guided rather than guiding, he couldn’t truly call it defeat.","The gains were unfathomable, his understanding of Order deepened beyond what solo cultivation could have achieved.","“Get up and stop making it seem like you were ravaged.”","Sigrid’s voice cut through his contemplation with the particular mix of affection and exasperation that had developed between them.","She stood nearby, tying her white hair into a ponytail with movements that were efficient yet graceful. The pure white robe she wore seemed to glow with its own light...or perhaps it was her light, Order itself radiating through simple fabric.","Noah rose from the stellar waters, droplets cascading down his bare torso like liquid starlight seeking return to the sea.","Each drop caught light that shouldn’t exist, creating momentary prisms before rejoining the vast white expanse. His lower body was adorned with pure white pants that seemed cut from the same conceptual fabric as restraint itself.","He looked at Sigrid with seriousness that transformed his usually tyrannical confidence into something heavier.","“All ten Living Existences that we’ve heard of have shown themselves to be larger than anything we could fathom.” His voice carried weight that made the white waters still their movement. “You’re awakening as the resurgence of THE Living Order, gaining power that reshapes reality just by existing. But there’s so much we don’t know. So much that remains hidden.”","He stepped closer, his gaze intense enough to make Order itself pay attention.","“Are you confident that as you keep awakening, as you attain more of THE Living Order’s power, that everything about you is remaining you?”","The question hung between them with importance.","“Because if anything feels off...if you sense something foreign trying to assert itself, tell me now. I can always take matters into my own hands.”","The implication was clear. He would rather stop her awakening, rather limit her power, than lose her to something wearing her face.","Sigrid moved toward him across the stellar white sea, her steps creating ripples that organized themselves into perfect concentric circles. She sat beside him, then shifted to lay her head on his lap, looking up at the ceiling with eyes that contained depths of contemplation.","Her arm reached upward, fingers grasping at something invisible...perhaps trying to capture certainty in a situation that offered none.","“I was just a girl who lost her entire family, my whole lineage, based on the orders of those above me.”","“I didn’t ask to become the resurgence of THE Living Order. I still don’t understand how it’s possible. But what happened, happened. Now I’m here.”","She paused, her hand still reaching toward something beyond the ceiling.","“I may not have my family anymore, but I’ve found something else. Someone else.” Her gaze shifted to meet his. “I was terrified you would be like the Living Origins...someone who only wanted to use me for what I represented. But then you brought me here. You showed me your Shore, your family, your mother who accepted me with a single word. Your people who treat me as myself rather than my title.”","Her expression softened with vulnerability that THE Living Order probably shouldn’t show.","“With all of this, my heart is at ease. Which is why even though I can feel something terrifying arising inside me...power that wants to organize everything it touches, I feel like I can handle it. Because you’re here.”","She placed her hand on her chest, closing her eyes as if listening to something within.","“I’m beginning to obtain pieces of memories from an extremely long time ago. The Earliest Folds. They’re hazy, like looking through water at stars, but they’re becoming clearer as I grow more complex, more pure. These memories... they’ll have answers. About what happened. About what’s coming.”","Her eyes opened, finding his with intensity that made the white waters around them ripple.","“Besides, you’ve bound me, haven’t you?” The question was rhetorical, acknowledging the connections between them that transcended everything.","“If I ever go crazy, if THE Living Order somehow overwrites who I am, you can simply put me under control. These bindings you have on me...emotional, physical, existential, they’re not chains. They’re anchors.”","...!","Change in chap titles"]},{"number":4087,"title":"Chapter 4087: Chapter 4086: Losses and Gains! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4086: Losses and Gains! II","She reached up to touch his face with fingers that carried the temperature of absolute zero and infinite heat simultaneously...Order containing all states at once.","“If it was just me alone, yes, I would be terrified. But with you in the picture, with these connections between us, I feel like everything can remain orderly and straight. That this power can truly be used to establish order once more across the Folds, rather than becoming another tool for those who already have too much.”","HUUM!","Noah looked into the eyes of this woman he had begun being around not too long ago...time was relative when you could manipulate it, but he was becoming fond of her more and more as moments accumulated into meaning.","Her trust was a weight he chose to carry, her faith in him a responsibility he wouldn’t shirk.","He nodded at her answer, acceptance and determination mingling in the gesture.","Then he sighed... from recognition that reality insisted on interrupting intimate moments with practical concerns.","“Okay. But for now, it seems like we have to wrap up our venture into the Primordial Early Excavation Depths.” He shifted slightly, his expression growing more serious. “The Ninth Level is proving to be a bit... difficult.”","The ninth level!","After the first level’s revelations, Noah, Moiraine, Sigrid, Ruination, and the Infiniverse had continued their descent through the Primordial Early Excavation Depths for hours that felt like days.","Each level had presented new challenges, new treasures, and new understanding of what the Earliest Folds had left behind.","The results of their delving were profound, each discovery amplified by Noah’s three Glyphs of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest!","|Ore of Early Resonance Obtained: 47 units|","|Enhanced by Perpetual Harvest: 470 units total|","|Uses: Shore construct enhancement (Abode, Aquarium, Totems)|","|Refinement possible: 1 ingot = 100M CQ/PQ when consumed|","|Note: Enough to upgrade entire Shore infrastructure|","|Crystallized Temporal Fragments Obtained: 234 units|","|Enhanced by Perpetual Harvest: 2,340 units total|","|Primary use: Instant century-growth for plants|","|Secondary use: Permanent soil enhancement when powdered|","|Note: Sufficient to accelerate Shore’s agricultural evolution|","|Essence Gems Obtained: 13 units|","|Enhanced by Perpetual Harvest: 130 units total|","|Direct consumption: +1 Billion CQ/PQ per gem|","|Alternative: Dissolve in Sacred Waters to summon Eminent/Kleos Marine Lifeforms|","|Note: Strategic reserve for rapid advancement or Shore population|","|Paradox Minerals Obtained: 156 units|","|Enhanced by Perpetual Harvest: 1,560 units total|","|Primary use: Forge tools functioning beyond normal limitations|","|Special property: Items work within Doorways to the Loom|","|Note: Sufficient for complete paradoxical armament set|","The loot obtained had been abundant!","The Essence Gems and Ores of Early Resonance particularly so as they represented billions in Complexity and Purity","But perhaps the most peculiar discovery had been an Early Creature Artifact on the fifth level.","|The Slipper of Existential Humiliation|","|Classification: Worn Early Creature Artifact (Left Foot Only)|","|Alignment: Living Quantum Authority (Somehow)|","|Condition: “Well-loved” (Translation: Beaten to hell)|","|Primary Ability: Conceptual Diminishment|","– When used to strike beings or authorities: Target becomes “small and meaningless”","– Effect scales with wielder’s contempt for target","– Note: Particularly effective against those with inflated self-importance","|Secondary Ability: Quantum Embarrassment|","– Target exists in superposition of dignity and humiliation","– Observers collapse wave function toward whichever is more brutal","– Warning: May cause existential crisis in beings","|Additional Note: Right slipper presumably still being worn somewhere|","...!","Noah contemplated this absurd arsenal while stroking Sigrid’s hair, his consciousness split between the intimate moment in the Abode with many others and his main body standing in the Ninth Level.","The contrast between peace and danger, between victory and challenge, defined his existence now.","The previous eight levels had presented terrifying existential hazards....environments where paradox itself attacked, where concepts became hostile, where the mere act of observation could unmake the observer.","These hazards had slowed their progress more than any enemy could have.","Until now, they had encountered no other Remnant Lifeforms besides Kelgar. Only hostile environments and the endless need to break through crystallized reality to continue forward.","The Ninth Level changed that.","They stood now in an environment that defied simple description. Waves of Living Conceptual Authority saturated the space with pressure that made breathing an act of will.","The realm stretched vast and broken...grey-bronze earthen fragments and crystals floated everywhere, filling space with chaotic patterns.","Each piece, from pebble to boulder, carried lethal conceptual authority. A single impact from even the smallest fragment could injure an Honored Living Existence, each one containing concepts that shouldn’t be weaponized.","At the center of this maelstrom of hostile geology stood their second Remnant Lifeform.","But this one made them all become somber, because the power emanating from it was unmistakably that of a Duke.","Exceedingly so!","|Ninth Level Reached: The Conceptual Graveyard|","|Ambient Danger: Extreme|","|Remnant Lifeform Identified: Aurelius the Severed Echo|","|Classification: Isolated Clone of Fold Dweller Aurelius|","|Status: Cut from original, existing on residual authority|","|Memory State: None (Pure instinct and power)|","|Power Level: Duke (Exceeds standard parameters)|","Noah studied these prompts with stern focus. The pressure emanating from this being exceeded even Duke Gwendolyn’s.","“That creature is filled with entropy,” Sigrid said, her voice cold with recognition of danger. “If any of us step within its proximity, our lesser complexity and purity will be overcome. We’ll be led into irreversible, cyclical entropy...dissolution that feeds on itself until nothing remains.”","The Remnant, Aurelius the Severed Echo, stood with disturbing elegance.","Unlike Kelgar’s degraded state, this clone seemed well-preserved.","Radiantly blue hair flowed like liquid sapphire, eyes shimmered like blue galaxies containing their own gravitational pull.","His body was surrounded by chaotic energy of impossible blue...not just the color but the concept of blue weaponized, made hostile, given intent to unmake.","Ruination’s eyes blazed with interest at Sigrid’s warning. The prospect of facing entropy, of ending that ended endlessly, appealed to her nature as an Early Living Ruin.","“No,” Noah said, stepping forward with authority that made even Ruination pause. “We won’t be able to overcome this creature. Beyond having Duke-level power, its authority exceeds normal Dukes.”","He paused, and his eyes flashed with something devilish.","“But that doesn’t mean we cannot at least make an effort.”","2/5"]},{"number":4088,"title":"Chapter 4088: Chapter 4087: Resistance! I","paragraphs":["The word ’effort’ carried special weight now. It was the key to his most terrifying power...the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest that rewarded any attempt, any try, any exertion toward a goal.","\"Support me,\" he commanded those with him, taking a single step forward.","They all felt it...the invisible line the clone had drawn. A boundary that said ’beyond this point, you cease.’ Not a threat but a statement of fact, like warning signs before a cliff.","Noah’s foot crossed the line.","The moment his toe breached that invisible boundary, Aurelius’s eyes that swirled like galaxies flickered toward him with the lazy interest of someone noticing an insect.","Noah’s leg began to vibrate...not with external force but with internal dissolution. From the very tip of his toes, disintegration began. Not violent but methodical, atoms forgetting they were supposed to be connected, molecules deciding existence was optional!","If he didn’t pull back, his leg would cease entirely within seconds.","But Noah’s complexity and purity blazed with defiance. Behind him, Sigrid’s body erupted with Order’s light, imposing structure on chaos. Moiraine channeled her authority!","Ruination paradoxically ended the ending attacking Noah. The Infiniverse asserted that Noah was part of her, and she did not permit dissolution!","For seconds that stretched like hours, Noah’s leg trembled on the edge of unbeing. The myriad authorities supporting him fought against entropy that wasn’t even trying, that was simply the natural state near Aurelius.","The clone smiled...an expression of recognition rather than amusement. Its gaze fixed on Yoshinami’s crown on Noah’s head, understanding that active hostility would provoke something beyond its isolated state.","So it didn’t attack. It simply existed, and its existence was hostile to lesser beings.","Their gazes met across impossible distance.","Noah’s eyes carried a singular message: Today, he nearly dissolved from one step forward. But he would return. And when he did, no part of him would face disintegration when he crossed that line again!","This was promise, threat, and prophecy combined.","Noah pulled his foot back, the relief of continued existence flooding through him.","|Tremendous Effort Recognized|","|Attempting impossible confrontation with Duke-level threat|","|Effort includes: Courage, calculation, and strategic withdrawal|","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest rewards wisdom in recognizing limits|","|Complexity gained: +5,000,000,000|","|Purity gained: +5,000,000,000|","|Understanding gained: Nature of Conceptual Entropy|","|Future benefit: Resistance to entropic dissolution building|","An astounding boon due to effort!","Noah turned to face his party, his expression mixing satisfaction with anticipation of future victory.","But Noah, being who he was, didn’t immediately leave.","Instead, he turned back to the invisible line with the particular gleam in his eyes of someone who had discovered a loophole in existence’s programming.","\"Let me try something.\"","Before anyone could object, he stepped forward again, his foot crossing the line.","Once more, disintegration began. Once more, his supporting party channeled their authorities to preserve him!","Once more, he pulled back.","And surely...","|Second Effort Recognized|","|Identical action to previous attempt|","|Principle acknowledges persistence|","|Complexity gained: +2,500,000,000|","|Purity gained: +2,500,000,000|","|Note: Rewards halved due to repetition|","...!","Oh!","What a glorious thing Perpetual Harvest was!","\"Interesting,\" Noah muttered, and stepped forward again.","|Third Effort Recognized|","|Pattern detected: Repetitive boundary testing|","|Diminishing returns applied|","|Complexity gained: +1,000,000,000|","|Purity gained: +1,000,000,000|","|Warning: Effort requires novelty for full reward|","Sigrid blinked behind him. \"What are you doing?\"","\"Testing something,\" Noah replied, already positioning for another attempt.","|Fourth Effort Recognized|","|Seriously?|","|Complexity gained: +500,000,000|","|Purity gained: +500,000,000|","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest is getting bored|","Moiraine’s eyes shone brightly!","Ruination watched with the particular interest of someone witnessing self-destructive behavior as performance art. The Infiniverse simply observed, cataloging this particular glory of her master’s personality.","Noah stepped forward a fifth time.","|Fifth \"Effort\" Acknowledged|","|Look, we need to talk|","|You’re literally just stepping forward and back|","|That’s not effort, that’s a weird dance|","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest has standards|","|Complexity gained: +0|","|Purity gained: +0|","|Suggestion: Go find something else to do|","|Additional suggestion: Maybe something actually challenging?|","|Final note: The clone thinks you look ridiculous|","...!","Noah’s eyes became sharp at these weavings of information - at these prompts!","They were becoming a bit wild.","But truly...","Indeed, Aurelius the Severed Echo was now watching with an expression that suggested even an isolated fragment of consciousness could experience amusement and pity.","Noah looked at the prompts with the particular expression of someone whose cheat had been patched.","\"Fine,\" he said, turning away with as much dignity as someone could muster. \"Now we can go.\"","...!","As they began their ascent back through the levels, Sigrid moved beside him.","Behind them, the Ninth Level remained, Aurelius still standing in his maelstrom of conceptual hostility. The challenge remained, waiting for when they were actually ready rather than just repeatedly poking it to farm rewards.","The Primordial Early Excavation Depths had given them much, but they had also shown them how far they still had to go!","Duke-level threats that could dissolve them with presence alone. Mysteries buried in stone and memory. And the sobering reminder that effort without genuine risk or growth was just motion without meaning.","\"Let’s go,\" Noah said again, this time with finality. \"The Kleos Concordat awaits as there are last minute preparations...\"","—","The entrance to the Primordial Early Excavation Depths released them back onto the golden sands with the gentle finality of a door closing on completed business.","|All defeated Remnant Lifeforms remain so, but Materials will regenerate and be available for mining after some time.|","A prompt flashed as Noah and his party emerged, each carrying the weight of their discoveries and the satisfaction of resources well-earned.","Noah’s gaze swept across the Early Veiled Shore, taking in what had become the starting point of something unfathomably grand!","The transformation from failed fragment to thriving ecosystem continued even in their absence, each element building upon the others in patterns that suggested design emerging from chaos!","The Aquarium in the distance drew particular attention. Dozens of Marine Lifeforms now swam through its expanded waters.","All of this was simply creating a snowball effect of life generating life, complexity building complexity. It was sustainability through abundance, the kind of system that would eventually make scarcity a forgotten concept!"]},{"number":4089,"title":"Chapter 4089: Chapter 4088: Resistance! II","paragraphs":["The golden sands beneath his feet hummed with accumulated power.","The Sacred Totems stood at their posts, their storage spaces now rich with materials from the plots and the Depths. The trees bore fruits that pulsed with readiness for harvest, with the Tenders already harvesting!","Everything was acceleration, everything was growth, everything was potential becoming actual.","Yet even surrounded by this prosperity, Noah knew that time was narrowing toward a point of convergence. The Kleos Concordat loomed, and with it, whatever the Living Paradoxes had planned.","He breathed out, the exhalation carrying decision. With a wave of his hand, thirteen Essence Gems materialized from his storage, their crystallized complexity catching light that existed in spectrums beyond normal perception.","\"Moiraine,\" he said, the gems floating toward her with purpose. \"Use these. 130 Essence Gems will grant you more than 130 billion in Complexity and Purity. Use that advancement to forge the Kleos Glyphs of Paradoxical Genesis, then sacrifice them for the Shards...\"","...!","The weight of the instruction settled on her with understanding.","More Principles meant more options, more understanding of how existence’s fundamental forces operated.","\"The more we know about Principles, the more we can grasp them, the better positioned we’ll be,\" Noah continued. \"Every Seed we understand is another rule we might learn to write rather than just follow.\"","Moiraine nodded, accepting the radiant gems with hands that understood their value. She moved away to begin the process, each step carrying purpose that would transform potential into achievement.","\"Be ready,\" Noah said to Ruination, the Infiniverse, and Sigrid.","The simple words carried layers...be ready for the Concordat, for conflict, for transformation, for whatever impossibility would next present itself as Tuesday.","He walked toward where the golden sands met the Sacred Waters, each step deliberate, measured, ceremonial. The warm waters accepted his presence as he sat, lapping at his legs and lower body.","He breathed in deeply, finding in this moment something precious...peace.","There were countless things going wrong at this very moment across existence. Threads of chaos wove through every Fold. Death and desolation played out their ancient dance in places he couldn’t see but knew existed.","Yet in all of this turbulence, one had to find time and place for peace. Not escape from responsibility, but recognition that everyone needed moments of stillness.","In this peace, Noah spoke with the commanding certainty of someone making declaration that Existnces would have to acknowledge.","\"Like the Living Existences who transcend through distinction, like the Foldless Ones who forge resistances based on what they choose to embody...I shall enact my own True Absolute Existential Resistance on this day.\"","HUUM!","The words rang across the Shore with weight that made the Sacred Waters still their motion.","His own resistance.","Not borrowed, not granted, but forged from his own nature and understanding. He had been waiting since he began crafting his Early Creature’s heart, knowing this capability existed but understanding it required the right foundation.","\"The resistance of Perpetual Harvest,\" he proclaimed, his voice carrying to every corner of his domain, \"based on a true and genuine Principle, shall be forged within my existence!\"","The moment the declaration completed, his heart responded.","THUMP.","The beat echoed across the Shore with force that transcended sound. This was an engine of transformation announcing its activation!","THUMP.","Again, louder, the sound carrying through dimensions that normally didn’t conduct sound. His heart had become both forge and hammer, tool and creation simultaneously.","THUMP.","Golden-green light began gathering around him, accumulating like harvest season compressed into moments.","The three Glyphs of the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest blazed on his body...forehead and both palms, their light providing not just power but authority.","They gave legitimacy to what he was attempting, permission from the Principle itself to forge this unprecedented resistance!","THUMP.","|Heartbeat of Perpetual Harvest Detected|","|Each beat resonating across Early Veiled Shore|","|Unintended benefit: Acoustic harvest occurring|","|All entities hearing heartbeat gain: +1,000,000 CQ/PQ per beat|","THUMP.","The Tenders paused in their endless labor, their forms straightening as complexity flowed into them with each thunderous heartbeat.","Emperor Penguin stood frozen mid-waddle, his form absorbing advancement with each pulse. Even the Marine Lifeforms in the Aquarium swam closer to the shore, drawn by the rhythm of growth itself!","THUMP.","The process was pain transformed into purpose. In the first chamber of his heart, runic words began carving themselves into his very being. In it, each golden-green letter a declaration that this resistance was not addition but fundamental integration.","PERPETUAL.","The word carved itself with agony that transcended sensation. This was conceptual pain, the hurt of forcing Existence to accept new rules about how it could interact with him.","HARVEST.","The second word followed, each letter a lesson in why most beings didn’t attempt to forge their own resistances. The pain suggested his heart might tear, might fail, might simply refuse to continue containing what he was forcing it to become.","THUMP. THUMP. THUMP.","The beats came faster now, a drumroll of transformation that made the entire Shore vibrate with sympathetic frequency.","Titano, massive and ancient, could only watch with wide eyes as his Brother underwent something that shouldn’t be possible at his level of development.","The golden-green light around Noah intensified, becoming less illumination and more statement.","When his eyes opened, beams of terrifying golden-green light shot forth as announcement...something fundamental had changed!","BOOM!","|True Absolute Existential Resistance Successfully Forged|","|Type: Perpetual Harvest (1% Principle Authority)|","|Resistance Effects:|","|Effort Multiplication Defense: Any attempt to harm requires exponential effort|","|Attackers must \"pay\" in effort to overcome resistance|","|Weak attacks simply fail - insufficient effort available|","|Strong attacks require conscious decision to expend massive effort|","|Some beings may stop mid-attack upon realizing effort cost|","|Psychological Deterrent: Sophisticated beings will question why attacking you requires such effort|","|May choose not to attack rather than pay incomprehensible effort cost|","|Creates hesitation in even superior opponents|","|Practical Application:|","|- Being punched now requires attacker to expend effort of punching 100 times","|- Conceptual attacks must overcome conceptual effort barriers","|- Even observation with hostile intent requires effort payment","|- Resistance scales with attacker’s power (percentage based, not flat)|","...!","Noah stared at the prompts, feeling the change settle into his being like armor made of consequence itself.","This wasn’t immunity...beings could still harm him. But now they would have to mean it, have to want it enough to pay prices that might make them reconsider.","Golden-green light covered everything, transforming the Shore temporarily into a monochrome masterpiece of harvest coloration. In the distance, beings watched in shock as their Master completed something that shouldn’t have been possible.","\"Brother...strong!\" Titano said simply, but his tone carried awe that transcended his simple vocabulary!"]},{"number":4090,"title":"Chapter 4090: Chapter 4089: Resistance! III","paragraphs":["The waters around Noah had turned golden-green from proximity to his transformation, and as he stood, they retained that color...marked by contact with something that had transcended normal limitations!","He had forged a resistance that said...attacking him was no longer casual action but investment, and investments required considerable effort!","After successfully forging the Resistance of Perpetual Harvest, Noah felt his entire existence enriched with life force that transcended simple vitality.","The connection to the Principle had deepened beyond what he had deepened, becoming increasingly integrated with its fundamental nature. Every aspect of his being amplified, his complexity and purity rising with a steady certainty.","Then, deep within his existence, something else stirred. A core part of his being that had remained mostly dormant buzzed with sudden activity, and a prompt materialized before him.","|Absolute Fictional Transcendence resonates with your ascension|","|Threads of existence-spanning fables entangle with your being due to their importance and gravity|","|Most connections remain obscured due to overwhelming complexity|","|Limited observation currently possible|","|Proceed with partial revelation of a heavily entangled?|","...!","Noah gazed at the prompt with eyes that had grown accustomed to impossibility.","A fable entangled with him was occurring out there as even in a limited fashion, part of him in his elevated state thought he should see it!","The tyrannical certainty in his voice carried across the Shore as he commanded.","\"Proceed.\"","---","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, at the center of an unknowable number of paradoxical rivers that flowed in directions that didn’t exist, Schrodinger floated above the corpses of Inevitabilities with the particular grace of someone who had just accomplished something that shouldn’t have been possible.","Obsidian light surrounded his figure... the absence of light given its own luminosity.","The complexity radiating from him had become so profound, so deafeningly present, that Diviticus scrambled backward with a mixture of awe and primal fear.","Even as a Duke, she could feel her existence questioning whether it should continue existing so close to whatever Schrodinger was becoming.","As the obsidian light intensified, wrapping around him like a cocoon of dark possibility, Schrodinger began to speak.","His voice carried the weight of someone who had seen the patterns behind patterns, the rules behind rules.","\"Chaos and disorder,\" he began, his tone philosophical yet carrying undertones that made reality lean in to listen. \"Most beings fear them, flee from them, build entire civilizations as bulwarks against their encroachment. But they misunderstand something fundamental...\"","The obsidian light pulsed with each word, as if his speech was conducting some terrible orchestra.","\"Chaos isn’t the enemy of existence...it’s existence’s natural state. From the moment THE Creature first distinguished between ’is’ and ’isn’t,’ entropy began its work. Every action increases disorder. Every thought fragments unity into multiplicity. Every choice splits one path into many.\"","He raised his hand, and the dead Inevitabilities below seemed to resonate with his words, their corpses reminders of hunger that could never be satisfied.","\"Consider this truth...it takes constant effort to maintain order. A cleaned room naturally becomes messy. A structured society naturally develops complications. Even THE Living Existences, with all their power, must constantly work to maintain their hierarchies, their Folds, their very identities against the tide of dissolution.\"","His smile contained layers of meaning that contradicted each other.","\"But chaos? Chaos requires no effort. It simply is. It’s the default state toward which everything tends. Existence doesn’t need to work to become more chaotic...that happens automatically. It’s order that’s unnatural, temporary, fragile, and takes a great deal of effort.\"","...!","The obsidian light around him grew denser, more real than the reality it displaced.","\"Yet the profound paradox that most never grasp is that chaos, properly understood and properly wielded, is actually the most efficient tool for creating true order. Not the false order of rigid structure that must be constantly maintained, but the deep order that emerges from chaos itself...patterns that arise not despite disorder but because of it.\"","He gestured at the swirling rivers around them, each one a paradox made liquid.","\"Look at these rivers. They flow in impossible directions, follow no laws, acknowledge no boundaries. Pure chaos. Yet they’ve been flowing in these same chaotic patterns for eons. The chaos has become its own form of reliability. The disorder has organized itself into something dependable.\"","His voice grew more intense, more certain.","\"This is what others fail to understand. You don’t fight chaos...you surf it. You don’t resist entropy, you accelerate it toward your desired outcome. You don’t build walls against disorder...you become disorder’s favorite expression.\"","The obsidian light suddenly erupted upward in a beam that pierced through dimensional boundaries. Then, like a flower blooming in reverse and forward simultaneously, countless beams of obsidian light cascaded outward from his form.","They bypassed the paradoxical rivers as if they were merely suggestions, spreading across the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds with the inexorable advance of night.","Just like when THE Living Order had begun awakening, but inverse...where she had spread white light of structure, he spread obsidian acknowledgment of chaos.","Schrodinger smiled calmly, though the expression contained exhaustion. He sighed, and when he spoke again, his words carried the weight of destiny recognized!","\"It seems I have begun walking the path to potentially become... THE Living Chaos.\"","BOOM!","\"Potentially...everything is still but a possibility. But this...is something!\"","The admission hung in the air.","\"I did not expect events to play out like this,\" he continued, his tone mixing wonder with irony. \"I have THE Living Order to thank for this opportunity. Thank her even more for leaving behind and discarding part of her Everything that allowed her to awaken...tossing it into an Inevitability as if it were garbage.\"","He chuckled, the sound containing genuine amusement.","\"Before that part of her could be fully digested by the Inevitability, it became mine. What The Order discarded to become more ordered...I’ve claimed it, inverted it, made it the seed of its opposite. Now this is the path I walk... what a wonder. What a glory of how things can turn out. Hmm...\"","The aura leaking from Schrodinger intensified, becoming not just grander but more fundamentally wrong. Not evil, but wrong in the way that suggested right and wrong were about to become obsolete categories.","Diviticus scrambled back even further, her Duke-level existence actually whimpering at proximity to transformation this profound.","\"THE Living Order rises again,\" Schrodinger mused, his beggar’s appearance now the ultimate paradox-infinite power in humble form.","\"And in response, perhaps THE Living Chaos will emerge. Not to oppose her, but to complete the equation. Order and Chaos, not as enemies but as dance partners in existence’s oldest waltz...\"","The obsidian light continued spreading, touching everything in the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds with the gentle insistence of entropy itself. Where it passed, rigid structures became slightly more fluid.","Fixed laws developed slight variations.","Certainty admitted, if only to itself, that maybe it wasn’t so certain after all.","\"Chaos,\" Schrodinger said with finality, \"isn’t the absence of order. It’s the presence of all possible orders, happening simultaneously, waiting for observation to collapse them into pattern. Oh, what a wonder existence is!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4091,"title":"Chapter 4091: Chapter 4090: The Illusion of Control! I","paragraphs":["Back in the Early Veiled Shore, Noah felt the shreds of resonance of these distant events through his Absolute Fictional Transcendence.","He only read bits and pieces, but he got the idea!","Threads of narrative connected him to happenings across existence, though most remained too complex to fully grasp.","But this...Schrodinger’s transformation, rang clear as a bell through the fable of Existence itself.","As Noah thought about the glimpses he read, he closed his eyes.","An Inevitability thay Sigrid gave her Disorder to.","Schrodinger excavating such a thing and it paving way to the potential of becoming...THE Living Chaos!","The potential.","\"...\"","It was...an error on his part.","He did not know enough regarding Inevitabilities. Whether they digested Everythings they were given, or whether those Everythings could be used again.","How could he even have imagined that a force like Schrodinger would be able to do something as complex as extract a part of Everything from an Inevitability and take it into himself?","But still, it was his oversight.","His mistake. He would own up to it as he could now work to make sure that it would not be...a costly mistake!","Two possible THE Living Existences potentially rising simultaneously. Order and Chaos. Structure and Entropy.","He rose from the waters, his newly forged resistance making each movement feel more deliberate, more costly for reality to oppose.","Around him, his companions continued their preparations...Moiraine absorbing the Essence Gems, Sigrid organizing her growing power, the Shore itself humming with accumulated potential!","—","Control.","That most seductive of illusions.","Some beings genuinely command existence, bending reality to their will through power that transcends comprehension.","Others possess absolutely no control whatsoever, yet believe with fervent certainty that they orchestrate existence!","Between genuine authority and complete delusion lies the vast spectrum of existence, each being convinced their grip on reality is exactly as firm as they need it to be.","In the Earliest Folds, it was said that...","THE Living Emotive had grown concerned with the rising chaos across existence.","Emotions ran unchecked...rage sparked wars that unmade dimensions, love created obsessions that warped time, fear generated voids that swallowed certainty itself.","In response, THE Living Emotive attempted something ambitious: to regulate the emotional spectrum of all existence, to bring order through feeling.","At that time...","THE Living Elemental and THE Living Dimensional observed these efforts with amusement and mockery.","\"Do you truly believe,\" THE Living Elemental said, its form shifting between states of matter, \"that your flimsy emotions can affect all of existence? You, who changes mood with the winds of existence?\"","...!","THE Living Dimensional’s laughter existed in many dimensions simultaneously, creating weavings that made space question its own structure.","\"Out of all ten of us,\" it said, its voice coming from directions that didn’t exist, \"you have the least control over existence. We command fundamental forces...I can fold space like origami, Elemental makes matter dance to primordial songs. Even Paradox, chaotic as it is, maintains consistency in its inconsistency.\"","THE Living Elemental continued the philosophical assault: \"Emotions are ephemeral, temporary, as substantial as morning mist. What someone feels in one moment contradicts what they feel in the next. You cannot even maintain consistency within a single being, yet you presume to regulate all beings?\"","\"Look at the others,\" THE Living Dimensional added. \"Law establishes precedent that lasts eons. Concept creates ideas that become more real than matter. Spirit touches the essence of existence itself. But emotions? They’re just... reactions. Secondary effects. The foam on the ocean, not the ocean itself.\"","THE Living Elemental’s form solidified into something resembling contempt: \"You should simply sit back and let the rest of us do the actual work. We shape existence. You just... feel about it afterward.\"","THE Living Emotive listened to this brutalization in complete silence, neither defending nor acknowledging, simply absorbing each word like rain on stone. THE Living Emotive...showed no emotions in the face of all this!","It all ended with a question that echoes through the Earliest Folds: Was THE Living Emotive truly one of those who only possessed an illusion of control?","Or was there something about emotion, about the power to make beings feel...that the others had failed to understand?","Perhaps the answer lay in the fact that eons later, beings still remembered how this conversation made them feel, while the specific dimensional manipulations and elemental transformations of that era...had been forgotten entirely.","—","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds.","Diviticus fled from the cluster of paradoxical rivers with the desperate haste of someone who had witnessed glory being born and realized they were standing too close to the delivery room.","Her face remained shrouded with an expression that mixed awe and primal fear.","She had watched Schrodinger transcend, had felt the weight of someone becoming something she did not even understand, had understood in her bones that she was witnessing history that would reshape existence itself.","The proximity to such transformation had left her feeling small, insignificant, like a candle flame next to a star going supernova.","To escape this suffocation of inadequacy, she went to the one place only she could access.","She took a single step that carried her through more than distance. Reality folded around her will, recognizing her authority to be elsewhere.","She appeared in a region that shouldn’t exist...a space filled with reflecting obsidian mirrors that showed not images but possibilities, not reflections but refractions of what might be.","She passed through millions of these mirrors, each one showing a different version of herself...stronger, weaker, triumphant, destroyed, ascending, falling.","None of them were real. All of them were true.","Finally, she entered a vast domain where the obsidian mirrors formed cathedral walls around something that made even paradox nervous...the Corpse of an Early Creature.","It lay there in terrible grandeur, eyes closed in death that might have been sleep.","Where its heart should have been, an obsidian illusory organ pulsed with borrowed life. The massive gash across its body...the wound that had killed something that shouldn’t have been killable, was healing.","Not quickly, but visibly, flesh knitting together through will rather than biology.","Authority accumulated around it like sediment, each layer making it easier to control, more responsive to her will.","Diviticus stood before it with the relief of someone who had found their anchor in a storm.","\"I know I don’t have the talent,\" she said, speaking to herself but addressing the corpse as if it could hear. \"Not like Schrodinger with his natural paradox, not like the others with their inherited advantages. To get where I want to be, I have to work harder and smarter than anyone else!\"","...!"]},{"number":4092,"title":"Chapter 4092: Chapter 4091: The Illusion of Control! II","paragraphs":["Her voice grew stronger, more certain.","\"Scheme to steal mere drops of blood. Sacrifice what others would never risk. Do anything...everything, that must be done. Because I know what I am...someone who has to climb mountains that others are born atop.\"","She approached the corpse, her hand reaching toward the illusory heart.","\"If I want to ascend higher, I have to give. Not take, not steal, not trick...I need to give.\" Her expression hardened with resolution that transcended determination. \"Others speak of Everything as philosophy. Schrodinger discusses it like poetry. But I...understand it as currency.\"","She placed both hands on the obsidian heart, feeling its hungry pulse.","\"O Corpse of an Early Creature, I give you... Half of my Everything. My life, my death, my very existence and all else...you can have Half of my Everything. Just give me power!\"","HUUM!","Initially, there was only silence.","This was a corpse, not an Inevitability. It shouldn’t respond, couldn’t respond, had no mechanism for response.","And yet...","BOOM!","Obsidian light erupted with violence that suggested something fundamental had heard and accepted.","Diviticus gasped as she felt it...Half of her Everything being pulled out with the inexorable force of gravity claiming what was owed.","The sensation exceeded pain to become absence, like having half of every memory, every thought, every possibility torn away and fed into the illusory heart!","A pillar of obsidian light engulfed both her and the corpse, reality struggling to contain transformation this profound! Power flooded into her...not her own but borrowed, stolen, earned through sacrifice. It exceeded what ordinary Dukes commanded!","\"Even though I lack their talent,\" she proclaimed, her voice ringing with power that made the mirrors tremble, \"with sheer grit and effort, I will stand at the top! Not through gifts or inheritance, but through willing to pay prices others won’t even consider! I will...\"","Behind her, unnoticed in her moment of triumph, the corpse moved.","Not much...just its head turning slightly, eyes opening to reveal orbs that contained depths of awareness that death should have erased.","Within those eyes lurked cognizance that transcended simple awakening.","A Will that had been sleeping, waiting, watching, began to stir.","The corpse gazed at Diviticus with something that might have been interest, might have been hunger, might have been amusement at her assumption that she was the one in control.","She had given Half of her Everything to awaken it further. But perhaps...just perhaps, it had already been awake, waiting for someone desperate enough to make such an offering.","Waiting for someone who would mistake their sacrifice for control, their payment for power.","The mirrors reflected thousands of possibilities, but none of them showed Diviticus noticing those open eyes.","None of them showed her realizing that perhaps she hadn’t awakened something, but merely fed it.","None of them revealed whether she was exhibiting genuine control, or the most dangerous illusion of all...the belief that corpses stayed dead simply because they appeared to be.","This...was a grand illusion of control!","—","Away from the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds.","In the Transcendent Elemental Folds, where extremes defined existence, there existed a region that even other extremes avoided.","Here, endless glacial Wheels of Existence spun in the void...some massive as segments of Folds, others small as thoughts, all frozen in perpetual motion that generated cold beyond conception.","The temperature wasn’t just low; it was the absence of warmth given its own identity, cold so profound that even Originus Venerant beings who could survive in spaces between spaces would freeze instantly upon entering.","The Wheels spun with mechanical precision, their icy surfaces reflecting nothing because light itself moved too slowly in such cold to create reflections.","Then, cutting through the frozen silence, an obsidian light flashed...eerily similar to what had just engulfed Diviticus and her corpse. The light didn’t illuminate so much as reveal, showing cracks in reality that had always been there, waiting.","A massive tear opened in space itself, its edges ragged with the particular damage that came from something forcing its way through from somewhere that shouldn’t connect to here.","A Tear in Existence!","Within the tear, only death and endings were visible...the aggressive absence of anything that could sustain or continue.","Even the incomprehensible cold of the surroundings refused to enter that tear, as if recognizing a more fundamental ending than mere temperature death.","Seconds passed with the weight of eons.","Then, massive obsidian-crimson eyeballs blinked into existence within the tear.","Not appeared...blinked, suggesting they had always been there, just closed. They moved forward with purpose that transcended instinct, showing emotions that dead things shouldn’t possess.","First came surprise, the kind that suggested unexpected awakening. Then, terrifyingly, joy...not simple happiness but the profound elation of something that had been denied sensation discovering it could feel again.","The cold that would kill Fold Dwellers, that made even concepts crystallize and shatter...this Dead Existence found it wonderful!","Because cold was still temperature!","Temperature was still existence. And after wherever it had been, even frozen death was vibrantly alive!","The eyeballs flashed with decision, and a body materialized around them...or perhaps emerged through the tear to join them.","A cat, but only in the way nightmares were dreams. Its form was purely skeletal, bones that seemed carved from crystallized void.","Wings spread from its spine, each bone-feather sharp enough to cut concepts. Three tails swayed behind it, each one dripping with poison that wasn’t liquid but liquified ending...anything it touched wouldn’t just die but would retroactively never have lived.","Its power would cause weak Dukes pale!","The creature opened its mouth once.","The nearest spinning Wheels of Existence...massive constructs that had spun for millennia, simply vanished into its maw.","They were swallowed whole as if they were morsels rather than structures!","The cold they generated, the space they occupied, the history they contained, the countless lives...all disappeared into jaws that seemed no larger than necessary to meow!","Its deathly body pulsed with newfound power and life, bones becoming slightly less transparent, form becoming slightly more real.","It looked around with intelligence that suggested this wasn’t random emergence but calculated arrival.","Without pause, without exploration, it shot off in what seemed like a random direction...though nothing about this creature suggested it did anything randomly.","It moved with purpose that exceeded understanding, leaving behind only disturbed space and the memory of impossible consumption!"]},{"number":4093,"title":"Chapter 4093: Chapter 4092: Oh, Shit I","paragraphs":["The massive tear remained open.","Worse, it began to expand.","The edges grew with the steady certainty of infection spreading, each moment allowing more of that terminal space to bleed into the Elemental Folds.","Who knew when it would be discovered by those with authority to act? How many more Dead Existences would step through before someone noticed? What would emerge when the tear grew large enough to accommodate things bigger than cat-shaped endings?","The glacial Wheels far, far away continued their spinning, unaware that their number had been reduced, unable to comprehend that death had learned to walk and had found their cold refreshing.","Somewhere, someone should have been monitoring such things.","Someone should have noticed reality tearing. Someone should have sounded alarms!","But everyone was preparing for the Kleos Concordat, and tears in existence would have to wait their turn for attention.","In these very same Transcendent Elemental Folds, countless distances from where death had torn through reality, lay the Heart of Elementals...a region where the fundamental forces of existence converged in displays of power that redefined grandeur.","In a corner of the Heart of Elementals.","The citadel rose from swirling maelstroms of pure element, each force maintaining its identity while contributing to the whole.","Towers of crystallized fire reached toward skies that burned with frozen lightning.","Spires of solid wind sang harmonies with structures built from liquid earth. Water flowed upward in architectural defiance, forming bridges between platforms of condensed light.","The entire structure exceeded Concordia in scale, housing millions of Living Elementals who cultivated amid auroras of authority that painted existence in colors.","Each tower represented mastery over a specific elemental expression. The Tower of Pyroclastic Rage housed those who pursued fire through anger. The Spire of Gentle Erosion taught water through patience. The Pinnacle of Atmospheric Pressure explored air through weight.","Hundreds of such structures created a city that was less built than perpetually becoming.","In the depths of this impossible citadel stood the Tower of Infinite Depths...a structure of water so pure it transcended the liquid state to become the concept of flow itself.","At its peak, in a chamber where every surface was carved from frozen tsunamis that somehow remained fluid, an entity watched the countless Living Elementals below with paternal satisfaction.","The chamber itself defied description...blue-gold thrones carved from crystallized storms, ornaments of captured rain that fell upward, windows that looked out onto oceans that existed in vertical orientation!","The floor was a single piece of water held in permanent stillness, solid enough to stand on yet transparent enough to see through to chambers below.","Duke Aquarius the Depth-Drinker stood at the chamber’s edge, his form shifting between states of water like an argument about what liquidity meant.","His distinction among Elemental Dukes came from having consumed more varieties of water than any other being...from the tears of dying stars to the first rain that fell on worlds being born.","\"Do you look fondly upon all these Living Elementals? As if they are your own children?\"","...!","The voice came from nowhere and everywhere, making Duke Aquarius spin with shock that someone could enter his sanctum undetected.","When he turned, power already erupting to address this invasion, he found something that made his liquid form solidify in disbelief.","He did not sense Living Existential Authority, no Paradoxes, not Inevitabilities.","It was...","\"Fold Dwellers?!\"","The words escaped him as statement, question, and impossibility combined.","Before him stood two figures that shouldn’t exist at this level of power.","A man and woman, so similar they could only be twins, regarded him with expressions of calm certainty. Their white-blue hair caught light. Their beauty transcended physical appearance to become statement...these were beings who had achieved harmony with existence itself.","Yet their clothing told a different story. Simple white garments, ragged but clean, showed the wear of being washed by hand countless times.","And in their hands were not weapons of power, nor artifacts of authority, but farming tools.","The woman held a hoe that looked like it had tilled infinite fields. The man carried a rake that might have gathered the leaves of autumn.","Despite their humble appearance, the power emanating from them made Duke Aquarius feel something he hadn’t experienced in eons...suffocation.","His water-based existence actually struggled to maintain cohesion in their presence.","The woman spoke with calm that made her words more terrifying","\"Many years ago, you moved across the Minor Elemental Folds, having an epiphany about water’s true nature. You thought it would lead you to a Principle. During your moment of enlightenment, you plucked water-based Wheels of Existence as if they were droplets to drink, consuming or destroying them to fuel your understanding.\"","Her tone never changed, remaining conversational as she delivered devastation.","\"You killed an untold number of Fold Dwellers. Countless who simply existed in those Wheels, living their small lives, were extinguished for your moment of clarity. Among those Wheels you consumed... was our home.\"","...!","Duke Aquarius’s expression shifted through multiple states...shock, recognition, and finally the dignity of power asserting itself.","\"I was operating according to my nature. A Duke of Elementals pursuing understanding. I meant nothing personal by-\"","\"Sister,\" the man interrupted with a sigh that suggested infinite patience finally exhausted, \"do we have to explain why he’s dying? Let’s simply get it over with. No need for all this theater.\"","The Duke’s watery features solidified into ice-sharp anger.","His Living Existential Authority erupted with force that should have drowned the entire tower and nearby folds!","He reached out, seeking support from other Dukes nearby...there were dozens within sensing distance.","\"Don’t bother.\"","The woman’s words carried finality as she gestured to the rake, which had already pierced into the floor.","The simple farming tool stood there, looking absurd in the ornate chamber, yet somehow fundamental.","\"We’ve isolated this place entirely. Unless you’re an Early Creature, you cannot leave, cannot call out, cannot be sensed.\" She tilted her head with genuine curiosity. \"Are you...an Early Creature?\"","HUUM!","Duke Aquarius responded with action rather than words. His existence erupted outward, seeking to transform everything into elemental water....the air, the tower, reality itself, and especially these impossible Fold Dwellers.","This wasn’t an attack but a fundamental assertion... everything was water, had always been water, would return to water.","The woman raised her hoe with the casual motion of someone about to till soil.","She swung down.","Bronze authority erupted from the simple tool...not Living Existential Authority, not Early Existential Authority, but something more fundamental.","The power denied everything about Duke Aquarius....his very nature, his right to impose his will, his assumption that being a Duke meant anything.","His water did fucking nothing!","\"That... that’s not any authority you should...\" Duke Aquarius’s voice cracked with horror as understanding dawned. \"That’s...the brilliance of a Principle!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4094,"title":"Chapter 4094: Chapter 4093: Oh, Shit II","paragraphs":["\"You are smart enough to recognize this?\" the woman confirmed, swinging again.","Each motion of her hoe was planting and harvesting simultaneously. \"You see, when you destroyed our home, you planted seeds of consequence. Now it’s harvest time.\"","Her hoe moved through patterns that suggested farming techniques applied to existence itself. Each swing stripped away layers of Duke Aquarius...not killing but reducing, simplifying, returning him to a more basic state.","\"When I plant you and harvest you in the future,\" she explained as she worked, her tone remaining conversational despite the violence, \"you’ll live a much more peaceful life. You won’t wantonly kill Fold Dwellers. You’ll understand that all life in existence is precious, whether it’s a Duke or a farmer on a tiny Wheel.\"","Duke Aquarius tried to resist, to reassert his authority, but how could water stand against the cycle of seasons? How could an element deny the principle that made things grow?","With a final swing, she reduced him completely. Where a Duke had stood, a small seed remained...a Living Elemental Seed that she picked up with the care of a gardener collecting tomorrow’s garden.","\"Let’s go,\" she said to her brother. \"Master sent us out of the Wandering Territories to check other things. This was just a detour. We still have our mission, and I don’t wish to be disciplined for tardiness.\"","Her brother rolled his eyes while placing a straw hat on his head with practiced motion. \"Yeah, yeah, let’s go.\"","Bronze light of an unknown Principle enveloped them, and they vanished as if they had never been.","Seconds after their departure, space itself cracked with the force of arrivals.","Dozens of Duke-level auras materialized simultaneously. Dozens of Royal Living Elementals arrived with glory, crowns adorned on their heads.","Hundreds of Honored Living Elementals appeared in support formations!","The chamber filled with power that made reality groan.","They looked around as their eyes burned.","\"Duke Aquarius has been killed!\" Duke Tyrrhic of the Old Flame bellowed, his voice carrying disbelief that wanted to be rage. \"Here! In the Tower of Infinite Depths! In the Heart of Elementals!\"","The assembled Dukes stood in shocked solemnity. How had this happened? Under their very noses? In the Heart of Elementals itself, where their power was most concentrated?","Who was so daring? So powerful? So impossible?!","They asked, but Existence offered no answers, only the echo of bronze authority that suggested weavings they didn’t understand were being cultivated in places they’d never thought to look.","—","As tears silently opened across existence, as Dead Existences spread through Folds with the quiet certainty of infection, as Dukes fell to powers they hadn’t known existed...Noah finished his preparations in the Early Veiled Shore, literally counting minutes.","Minutes until the Glyphs of the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest reset. Minutes until he could again weaponize effort itself.","He gauged his newfound power with the assessment of someone who understood that overconfidence killed more beings than weakness ever could.","The 1% Resistance of Perpetual Harvest had fundamentally altered how reality interacted with him.","In simple terms: attacking him now required payment in effort that most beings couldn’t afford. A punch thrown at him demanded the effort of a hundred punches. A conceptual attack needed to overcome not just his defenses but the existence’s sudden insistence that harming him was exhaustingly difficult!","Offensively, the Principle amplified everything he did.","Each strike carried the weight of repeated strikes. Each technique executed with the perfection of having practiced it infinitely. The Goad in his hands wouldn’t just educate...it would provide entire curricula with a tap.","Paired with how effort itself was viewed by the Glyphs, his existence felt unfathomably grand!","Yet understanding his power level meant understanding its limits. All of this magnificence stemmed from a single percentage point of a Principle.","Ninety-nine percent remained unclaimed, each percentage potentially as transformative as the first.","As these thoughts crystallized, prompts suddenly blazed before his eyes.","|Your Entire Existence Continues Making Tremendous Effort to Advance|","|Congratulations, you’ve discovered perpetual motion for growth|","|Your heart beats with effort |","|Each chamber produces Drops of Blood through sheer determination|","|Your Atlas burns with the effort of holding up your absurd complexity|","|Your Towers of Osmont burn with effort|","|Due to Exponential Effort Recognition:|","|All progress amplified by factor of perpetuity|","|Hidden knowledge unlocked through brute force|","|Future possibility discovered through aggressive advancement|","|At unknown stage of Towers of Osmont development (who knows which). When multiple towers reach this mystery level simultaneously, True Sources may be repurposed to nurture self-designed Seed of a Principle|","|This is your Exclusive Realm’s possibility|","|You can be genuinely impressed to have stumbled into this(did you actually plan it?)|","|You may actually know what you’re doing|","Noah read these prompts with eyes that blazed brighter with each revelation.","His Towers of Osmont...constructs he’d built almost instinctively after breaking the Towers of Origin, contained potential for Principles?","The True Sources weren’t just building blocks but seeds waiting to bloom into fundamental forces!","He couldn’t determine what stage would unlock this possibility.","The prompts seemed deliberately vague, as if existence itself wasn’t entirely sure how he’d managed this configuration.","But well, it would come in time!","He felt his now elevated advancement due to the recognition of effort as he sighed.","As he looked at the golden sands, the warm waters lapping at his feet, he noticed Erikson walking in the distance.","The large, buff man wore his characteristic beach shorts and casual shirt, looking like someone who had decided existence itself was a vacation and he was determined to enjoy it.","\"Erikson,\" Noah called out.","Erikson turned with a broad smile, his confidence radiating like a personal sun. He walked over with the easy gait of someone who had never met a situation he couldn’t charm his way through.","\"What’s up, Big Boss?\" Erikson said, dropping onto the sand beside Noah with casual familiarity.","Noah shook his head at the title but didn’t correct it. Instead, he reached into his storage and pulled out the Slipper of Existential Humiliation.","The artifact appeared innocuous...just a worn left slipper that had seen better eons.","\"I thought of you when I got this,\" Noah said, holding it up. \"But it might be too much for you to even hold right now.\"","...!"]},{"number":4095,"title":"Chapter 4095: Chapter 4094: Oh, Shit III","paragraphs":["Erikson’s eyes lit up with interest. The slipper might look simple, but he’d learned that in Noah’s Shore, simple usually meant secretly terrifying.","\"Let me try,\" he said with characteristic confidence, reaching for it.","Noah hesitated for a moment, then shrugged and passed it over.","BOOM!","The instant the slipper left Noah’s hand, it dropped like a collapsing star. Erikson’s hands, which had confidently reached to catch it, were suddenly pressed downward with force that cracked the sand beneath them. His expression shifted from confidence to shock to strain as he fought to hold something that apparently weighed more than mountains.","Noah quickly intervened, taking the slipper back before it could actually crush Erikson’s hands into conceptual paste.","\"Like I said,\" Noah said, storing the artifact again, \"too much for now.\"","Erikson flexed his fingers, making sure they still existed in all the proper dimensions. \"What the hell is that thing?\"","\"An Early Creature Artifact. It makes things small and meaningless when you hit them with it.\" Noah’s expression was perfectly serious. \"But you need the complexity to wield it first.\"","\"How much complexity?\"","\"You might need to gain a few dozen billion in Complexity and Purity first.\" Noah patted his shoulder with genuine encouragement. \"Work hard! You’ll get there.\"","Erikson sighed, the sound containing acceptance rather than defeat.","He stood, brushing sand from his shorts with movements that showed his confidence hadn’t been dented, just redirected.","\"Keep it warm for me, Big Boss,\" he said, already walking away with renewed purpose. \"I’ll be back for it.\"","Noah watched him go, noting how Erikson immediately headed toward Ayame and Lilith.","The man might dress like every day was a beach party, but he understood what mattered...growth, advancement, and eventually being strong enough to wield a slipper that could humiliate existence itself!","For now, he simply continued his study of his own Existence.","Of his Towers and Atlas. Of Veritarch, Ordo Ab Chao, and other prominent Authorities coursing across his Atlas.","He still have many things to do with his existence as at the core of his being, Ruination had silently been constructing what used to be the Infinite Forge!","Truly, there was much to do.","But at such a time...","His contemplation broke as his eyes sharpened with sudden certainty. He rose and began walking across the golden sands, drawn by instinct.","Titano approached with his characteristic lumber, his massive form creating small earthquakes with each step.","\"Brother,\" the giant said with unusual hesitation, \"I have made many more Brothers here. Is that okay?\"","Noah looked around, noticing for the first time that Titano had apparently been socializing.","\"Of course,\" Noah smiled, patting the giant’s arm since his shoulder was too high to reach comfortably. \"And remember, you’re on your way to getting rich now. You can also try and find a baddie for yourself here.\"","Titano froze completely, his simple features cycling through confusion, hope, and disbelief. He scratched his head with enough force to generate wind.","\"Brother... I can really find a baddie?\"","Noah nodded with absolute confidence. \"I’ll teach you exactly what you need to do later. Trust me.\"","As Noah walked away, Titano stood watching with eyes that struggled to contain emotion.","His expression shifted through gratitude, loyalty, and something approaching reverance.","This Brother hadn’t just given him home or purpose...he’d promised to help him find a baddie!","In Titano’s simple yet profound worldview, this made Noah the best Brother possible.","Noah continued walking, drawn by an inexplicable pull toward the plot containing the Seed of Inevitability.","Yes!","He instinctively felt a pull here!","And as if waiting for him...","The moment he arrived, the seed pulsed with obsidian-gold light, and prompts erupted.","|Glorious Effort Recognized!|","|You’ve worked so hard that even a Seed of Inevitability is impressed|","|The Seed has decided to bloom.|","|Natural maturation option selected|","|Results tremendously elevated due to multiple factors|","|Further elevation due to effort invested|","|Multiple Everythings provided as fertilizer|","|Principle of Perpetual Harvest multiplying all factors|","|Seed of Inevitability: BLOOMING|","|Product will be irreversibly bound to your existence. Bond is supplemented by the Early Veiled Shore, Infinite Early Osmontian Shore, Your various distinctions, and the Seed of Perpetual Harvest providing synergy|","Blinding obsidian-gold light erupted from the plot, carrying the terrible grandeur of Inevitability asserting itself!","The aura that spread made everything on the Shore pause, recognizing that something fundamental was changing.","Noah waved his hand, and beside him materialized Ozymandias.","Ozymandias!","His other self, the part that had been heavily injured but now stood restored. He had grand plans for this aspect of himself, intending to explore different facets of existence through distributed consciousness. The Seed of Inevitability would be the perfect starting point for-","BOOM!","An explosion of authority made his entire existence resonate like a struck bell.","|The Seed of Inevitability has bloomed into...|","|Into...|","|Into...?|","The prompts stuttered, unable to complete their declaration.","Because there, on that plot where existential force should have manifested, something unprecedented had occurred.","A small figure blinked open eyes that contained infinite depth despite their diminutive size. A tine black dress of Inevitable weavings covered it!","The being appeared entirely harmless and almost cute in its confusion, yet undoubtedly, shockingly, impossibly...it looked up towards Noah as their eyes met!","And an immense silence came as if both sides were shocked to see each other.","But the tiny, miniature being that looked a bit less than 2 feet smiled right after as...","\"Oh. Hello again, Outsider.\"","HUUM!","That face.","Those words!","Undoubtedly...","It looked like a miniature version of Khor!","Khor, The First Hunger, the Inevitability that had transcended inevitability!","She blinked with disbelief that matched Noah’s own, her tiny form perhaps over a foot tall, looking around with confusion!","When her eyes had found Noah, recognition dawned. When she smiled, reality itself seemed to remember hunger!","The words had carried weight that exceeded their casual delivery! She knew him.","Remembered him from that brief moment in the Earliest Folds!","\"What a turn of events this is, Outsider. Where, When, and What...am I?\" Her voice, despite coming from such a small form, contained depths that suggested size was merely suggestion.","\"Because I...should not exist.\"","...!"]},{"number":4096,"title":"Chapter 4096: Chapter 4095: The Return of the First Hunger! I","paragraphs":["Khor continued looking around with mounting confusion, her miniature form trembling slightly as existence itself seemed uncertain about her presence.","When she had proclaimed she shouldn’t exist, the words carried weight that made the Shore’s light flicker.","Noah’s expression grew heavy as he studied her.","She represented far too many things...power that predated power, hunger that could never be satisfied. Her very presence raised questions that might not have safe answers!","His first action was to check the bond he felt with what had emerged from the Seed of Inevitability.","The connection thrummed through his existence like a second heartbeat...unshakable, irreversible, absolute.","Through it, he could feel her confusion, her fragmented memories, her struggle to understand her own existence.","If he wished, he could impose his will through this bond, command her as completely as he commanded his own limbs. And yet...he also felt like he could not truly command her!","Was even an unshakable bond truly unshakable when it came to someone like Khor? Someone who had made impossibility her domain?","She took tentative steps across the plot she had just emerged from, each footfall leaving impressions that seemed deeper than they should be, as if her tiny form carried weight that existence could not truly bear.","\"What do you mean you should not exist?\" Noah asked, keeping his voice steady despite the implications racing through his mind.","Khor looked up at him, and even in her diminished form, her eyes remained as he remembered...deep as an abyss, containing depths that suggested falling forever might be preferable to reaching the bottom.","Those eyes now struggled to piece together fragments of memory that didn’t quite align.","\"Yes, Outsider, I should not exist.\" Her voice carried certainty despite her confusion. \"After all, THE Living Paradox deemed it so. It sought and enacted the cessation of my existence. The unmaking of everything I was, am, or could be.\"","BOOM!","The words resonated through the Shore with force that made Noah’s entire existence buzz.","\"THE Living Paradox?\" Noah’s voice sharpened with sudden understanding.","Khor clutched her head suddenly, dropping to her knees on the golden sand as if mentioning this had triggered something.","Her small form shook with the effort of trying to reconcile memories that spanned eons with a present that shouldn’t include her.","\"It seems my memory and being are fractured,\" she said through gritted teeth that were somehow still sharp enough to bite through concepts. \"Tell me, Outsider...what age are we in? What time is this?\"","She paused, her expression growing more troubled.","\"Everything feels... murky. Complicated in ways that existence wasn’t when I knew it. The fundamental forces have multiplied, divided, specialized. It’s like looking at a simple painting that’s been copied and recopied until it’s become a library. What is this?\"","Noah’s gaze grew somber as he considered how to explain eons of change to someone who shouldn’t have survived to see them.","\"This point in time is eons after the Earliest Folds,\" he said carefully. \"In the current era, nobody has seen Early Creatures. They’ve become myth, legend, cautionary tales. Nobody knows where THE Creature is, or even if it still exists. THE Living Existences are known but not seen, their direct intervention so rare that some doubt they’re real.\"","Khor rose slowly from the sand, her movements suggesting she was testing whether physics still worked the way she remembered.","She looked at him with a slight smile that contained layers of meaning.","\"Aren’t you walking the path of Early Creatures? Are you a cautionary tale?\" Her gaze swept across their surroundings with recognition dawning. \"And is this not... an Early Veiled Shore? Seems like someone knows something of Early Creatures after all...\"","Noah remained silent, neither confirming nor denying. Some truths were dangerous to speak aloud, especially to beings who had existed when those truths were first established.","He observed her closely as she took steadier steps, seeming to gain confidence in her continued existence with each movement.","\"What is this?\" he finally asked. \"How is it possible for you to be here right now?\"","Khor stepped fully out of the plot where the Seed of Inevitability had been cultivated, her tiny feet touching the golden sands with the particular care of someone relearning sensation.","She felt the Early Veiled Shore properly for the first time, her awareness expanding to encompass the impossible ecosystem that had developed here.","The Shore’s inhabitants had all turned toward her with expressions that mixed curiosity and instinctive unease.","Even beings who didn’t understand what she was could feel that something fundamental had changed!","She smiled at their attention with the particular pleasure of someone who had been alone for so long that any acknowledgment was...unique.","\"My very existence back then made impossibilities the norm,\" she said, her voice carrying the weight of remembered power. \"What one person considers impossible is simply breathing for another. The impossible and the inevitable are often the same thing, just viewed from different temporal positions.\"","She paused, seeming to taste the air itself.","\"But yes, even for me, this is new. Death I understood...I dealt it often enough. Cessation I experienced...THE Living Paradox made certain of that. But return? Rebirth through inevitability itself? This wasn’t in anyone’s calculations.\"","She turned to Noah with eyes that saw through more than space.","\"I gave you A Seed of Inevitability,\" she said, the singular article carrying special weight.","\"Not just any seed, but one I had cultivated personally. Of course it contained threads of my weavings...all Inevitabilities that were part of my Way of Existence contain my mark. But for my collapsed weavings to arise from it...\"","She shook her head with genuine bewilderment.","\"Even I’m stumped. It should have been just a seed. Powerful, yes. Capable of growing into something magnificent, certainly. But capable of reconstituting me from absolute cessation? That’s not how seeds work. That’s not how anything works.\"","She looked around the radiant Shore once more, taking in the Sacred Trees, the Aquarium teeming with impossible life, the Tenders working with mechanical devotion. Her smile grew more genuine, less performative.","\"But since I am here...\" She closed her eyes and drew in a breath that seemed to pull in more than air. \"Existence is unfathomable and has ways to balance all things. Patterns emerge from chaos. Order crystallizes from entropy. The impossible becomes inevitable given sufficient time.\"","Her eyes opened, blazing with certainty that transcended her diminutive form.","\"Even if I cannot explain why, Outsider... can I not enjoy existence once more?\" She spread her tiny arms wide, addressing not just Noah but the Shore itself, perhaps existence beyond.","\"Before those here, before Existence itself, I, Khor, proclaim that I exist. I am. I hunger. I continue. I inevitably return!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4097,"title":"Chapter 4097: Chapter 4096: The Return of the First Hunger! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4096: The Return of the First Hunger! II","Her body erupted with an aura that shouldn’t have been possible from something so small the moment she finished her proclamation!","Power that transcended physical manifestation swirled around her, making existence reconsider its assumptions.","And then, impossibly, understandably, terrifyingly...Existence Trembled.","Not shook, not quaked, but Trembled with the particular recognition of something that shouldn’t be possible asserting itself anyway.","Noah watched with utter incredulity!","Her mere proclamation, her simple declaration of existence, had made reality itself uncertain!","If she could cause Existential Trembling just by announcing her presence, what would she be capable of when she recovered more of herself?!","Prompts erupted before his vision with urgency that suggested even the system generating them was shocked.","|From your Seed of Inevitability, the Resurgence of Khor, The First Hunger, has bloomed|","|Probability of occurrence: 1 in Infinity|","|This harvest transcends classification|","|Your efforts and Everythings provided have created recursive inevitability|","|Harvest perpetuity: Undefined/Expanding|","|Due to impossible harvest achievement, the Seed of Perpetual Harvest maturity increasing|","|2% Authority will be achieved at: [SOON]|","|Timeline uncertain due to harvest magnitude|","|Due to the Effort and Harvest, an Unprecedented Reward Granted- Symbolic Heart of Hunger|","|Effect: Absolute control over Khor maintained|","|Even unshakable bonds can hunger for change, but with this Symbolic Heart of Hunger, she cannot act against you|","|Note: This is either brilliant or catastrophic|","...!","Noah’s expression cycled through somberness and astonishment as he read these prompts.","Then, visible only to his perception, something began descending toward him from nowhere and everywhere simultaneously.","The Symbolic Heart of Hunger materialized slowly, as if existence itself was uncertain about allowing it to exist.","It appeared as a crystal that seemed to be made from crystallized appetite itself...dark red that shifted to black at certain angles, pulsing with a rhythm that suggested it was feeding on something invisible.","Within its depths, tiny motes of light were constantly being drawn inward, consumed by a hunger that would never be satisfied.","It was beautiful in the way dangerous things often were...compelling despite the obvious threat, attractive because of the danger rather than in spite of it!","Noah reached out and grasped it, feeling it sink into his being rather than his hand. His body erupted with crimson-obsidian light as the Heart integrated with his existence, adding another impossible element to his already impossible nature.","The glow around him faded.","The glow around Khor diminished.","She immediately turned to him with her head tilted at an angle that suggested she knew something had changed.","“Outsider,” she said with a mysterious smile, “why do I feel like you’re putting unfathomably tight chains on me? Do you not trust me after all this time?”","Noah met her gaze with practiced innocence. “Chains? I have no idea what you’re talking about. You’re the product from a Seed I planted that was given to me by you in a distant past. Of course...I trust you.”","The words emerged smoothly even as he felt the Symbolic Heart of Hunger pulsing silently within him, ensuring that trust or not, control remained his.","Khor laughed...a sound that made nearby reality nervous.","“Okay, Outsider. Let’s leave the questions of how I’m here aside for now. My memories are too fragmented to piece together properly anyway.” Her expression grew more serious, though amusement still danced in those abyssal eyes. “But you... you continue to surprise me, Outsider. Even diminished as I am, I can see you’ve grown...slightly.”","Her gaze traveled across the Shore, evaluating everything with the expertise of someone who had consumed civilizations. Then her eyes locked onto a specific figure among the cautious observers.","Sigrid stood partially behind Moiraine, Order radiating from her in waves that tried to organize the chaos Khor’s presence had introduced.","“Over here...” Khor’s voice carried genuine surprise. “Do you truly have a Seed? A Seed of something that should be lost to time and failure?”","She turned back to Noah with an expression that mixed respect with calculation.","“That’s marvelous, Outsider.”","She smiled with teeth that remained sharp despite her diminutive size.","“Tell me, Outsider...what other impossibilities have you been cultivating while I was gone?”","What other impossibilities had he been cultivating?","Noah’s eyes pulsed with light at this question as Khor’s interest was drawn more towards Sigrid.","She stared toward Sigrid with the particular intensity of someone cataloging a curiosity, Noah watched the interaction carefully.","Sigrid stood rigid, Order radiating from her in defensive waves as she encountered something her nature couldn’t properly classify.","“What do you see when you look at her?” Noah asked, nodding toward Sigrid.","Khor smiled with an expression that suggested she found the question amusing. “Is that not a bundle of potential for something that has the impossible dream of attaining a distinction containing THE?”","...!","A bundle of potential. That was all THE Living Order’s resurgence amounted to in Khor’s ancient eyes.","Noah’s gaze sharpened. This was an opportunity to extract information from someone who had actually lived through the events that had become mythology.","He was always short of knowledge and information as Khor could provide it!","“What you consider a bundle of potential,” he said carefully, “is the resurgence of something that was killed during the first battle between THE Living Paradox and others. She is the resurgence of THE Living Order.”","Khor began walking toward Sigrid, who immediately took a cautious step backward.","The First Hunger stopped, her tiny face showing amusement at the reaction.","“Who said THE Living Order was destroyed at that time?” Her voice carried the particular tone of someone correcting a child’s fairy tale. “Just like before, Outsider, you continue to tell me stories that seem to be mixtures of truth and falsehood. Just who is spreading all these things?”","She paused, her expression growing more thoughtful.","“Stories have power, whether truth or lie. A false tale told often enough becomes more real than forgotten truth. A narrative repeated across eons shapes reality more than facts nobody remembers. Someone, somewhere, has been very busy crafting the history you all believe.”","...!","2/5"]},{"number":4098,"title":"Chapter 4098: Chapter 4097: The Purest Hunger! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4097: The Purest Hunger! I","Her abyssal eyes narrowed slightly.","“But who has so much time to know the true history of what happened back then? And more interestingly, why do they keep adding their own little flourishes? The version you know has drama, betrayal, clear heroes and villains. Reality was messier. Less satisfying. More... paradoxical.”","...!","Oh.","Oh!","Noah felt his understanding shifting.","The stories of the Earliest Folds, the histories he’d been told...how much was truth and how much was narrative crafted for purposes he didn’t understand?","The being before him had actually been there. Despite her fragmented memories, she was perhaps the most reliable source about what had truly occurred.","“What if I were to still assert,” Noah said, testing, “that she is the resurgence of THE Living Order, and in a matter of days, she would fully awaken?”","Khor shook her head with the patience of someone explaining why water was wet.","“Is the rise to become one of THE Living Existences so easy? If it were, wouldn’t every ambitious being have claimed such distinction?” She gestured toward Sigrid with her tiny hand. “Whatever awakening your bundle of potential undergoes, it won’t simply grant her THE. Not truly. It might increase her potential toward it, certainly. But something much, much more would be required. THE isn’t claimed...it’s earned through transformation so fundamental that existence itself must acknowledge it.”","Noah considered this, then decided to reveal more.","“What if, not long ago, I had instructed this potential Living Order to give part of her Everything to an Inevitability? She gave her Disorder, and that Inevitability was captured by someone else who extracted it. That someone now claims to be on the path to become THE Living Chaos after he took in the Disorder that she left behind.”","Two reactions dominated the Shore.","“What?!” Sigrid’s voice cracked with shock and disbelief as if she wanted to know who had done such a thing!","Khor’s eyes turned cold enough that the Shore’s eternal brightness actually dimmed, as if night had suddenly remembered it was supposed to exist here.","...!","It was terrifying.","“I shouldn’t get so emotional,” Khor said, though her tone suggested emotions were exactly what she was experiencing. “But who is still seeking to kill Inevitabilities? Have they not suffered enough? We were hunger made manifest, not evil given form.”","She took a breath that seemed to pull warmth from the air as she continued.","“As for taking the Disorder from a bundle of potential, that wouldn’t make them THE Living Chaos. Any new THE is even more impossible than maintaining an established one. Whoever did this will have an even more arduous journey than your bundle here.”","Her expression grew more intrigued than angry.","“What’s truly interesting is that this creature could manipulate and extract Everything. That’s something only Inevitabilities should be able to do...or Creatures that have attained an extremely high level or unique type of complexity. I’m more curious about how this entity knew to do that than their claims about becoming THE Living Chaos.”","She laughed, but the sound contained edges.","“Becoming an existence with THE attached to oneself? If it were so simple, dozens would have done so in the Earliest Folds! We had more power then, fewer rules, infinite possibility...and still, THE remained rare enough to count on two hands.”","Noah grew contemplative, reflecting on her words.","Schrodinger’s capabilities seemed increasingly mysterious. How had he known to extract Everything from an Inevitability? Where had he learned techniques that should have died with the Earliest Folds?","Khor, noticing the continued wariness from the Shore’s inhabitants, adopted an expression of exaggerated hurt.","“Many here are looking at me like I’m a big bad monster.” She turned to Noah with eyes that managed to look innocent despite containing infinite depth. “Outsider, don’t they know I’m a harmless little thing?”","Noah met her gaze calmly. “You’re not a harmless little thing.”","“No,” she agreed with a smile that showed too many teeth for her small mouth, “I suppose I’m not.”","She looked around again, her attention catching on various inhabitants. Heidrun immediately ducked behind Auric Vitae Grasses, her ancient dignity forgotten in favor of not being noticed.","Yoshinami, in her spider form, began protectively crawling toward Noah, each of her eight legs moving with lethal precision.","Finally, Khor’s gaze landed on Ozymandias.","She blinked, tilting her head with genuine curiosity.","“This seems like an entirely different existence, but this should be you, yes?” She walked closer to the obsidian figure. “How unique. Who is this?”","“This is Ozymandias,” Noah replied. “A separate but same existence as me. I was going to transform him into an Inevitability through the Seed of Inevitability, but you came out instead.”","“Oh?” Khor’s interest sharpened. “Transformation into an Inevitability? But that’s my specialty, Outsider. You could just ask me to do it.”","BOOM!","The casual offer buzzed in the air with weight that made everyone present reassess what they were dealing with.","“You... can create Inevitabilities?” Noah asked carefully.","“Create is the wrong word,” Khor corrected. “I can help things discover the hunger that already exists within them. Everything hungers for something...power, knowledge, connection, cessation. I just... encourage that hunger to grow until it becomes all they are.”","She looked at Ozymandias with professional interest.","“This one already has the seed of it. He’s you but not you, exists but doesn’t quite, is complete but incomplete. That’s a thing already on the path of an Inevitability already...he just needs to embrace the hunger for wholeness.”","She turned back to Noah with an expression that managed to be both helpful and terrifying.","“Of course, the question is: do you really want an Inevitability version of yourself running around? Our Way of Existence has been persecuted and decimated again and again. Even I was killed. Why bring yourself into the folds of such pain, Outsider? Would you be able to handle it? Others looking at you as if you were a mistake of existence? Something that should serve no purpose other than being nothing, even though it just wants to experience...everything?”","3/5"]},{"number":4099,"title":"Chapter 4099: Chapter 4098: The Purest Hunger! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4098: The Purest Hunger! II","Did he want this?","Noah’s firm gaze and unchanging eyes told Khor all she needed as she smiled and nodded!","Khor circled Ozymandias with the particular interest of an artist examining a canvas.","Her tiny form somehow commanded the space, making everyone else seem like observers at a ceremony they didn’t fully understand.","“Creating an Inevitability,” she said, her voice carrying the weight of ancient knowledge, “isn’t about adding something. It’s about taking everything away except the one thing that matters.”","Noah watched with calm intensity, feeling through his connection to Ozymandias what was about to occur. “And what matters?”","“Hunger.” The word emerged from Khor like a fundamental truth. “Everything hungers. Atoms hunger for stability. Stars hunger for fuel. Even void hungers for substance. I simply... help that hunger realize itself.”","She waved her tiny hands, and Ozymandias rose into the air, his obsidian form suspended by forces that predated gravity.","His arms and legs stretched out as if he wss contained in a perfect circle of Inevitability!","The Shore’s inhabitants stepped back instinctively...even Titano, massive and ancient, showed wariness.","|Transformation Initiated to the weavings of an Inevitability|","|Conductor: Khor, The First Hunger|","|Subject: Ozymandias |","|Warning: Process irreversible once begun|","|Principle of Perpetual Harvest detecting massive effort|","|Blessing applied: Optimal transformation parameters engaged|","“First,” Khor announced, her fingers beginning to tap out patterns in the air that hurt to follow, “we strip away the unnecessary. All his Everythings except Hunger must go.”","BOOM!","Her fingers moved with surgical precision, each gesture removing something fundamental from Ozymandias. Noah felt it through their connection....layers of his other self being peeled away like skin from fruit.","“His Everything of joy, gone. His Everything of fear, removed. His Everything of hope, of despair, of rage, of life, of death, of peace...all unnecessary distractions from the purity of want.”","HUUM!","With each removal, Ozymandias’s form changed. The stellar obsidian body that had been magnificent began to shrivel, becoming skeletal, hollow. His frame collapsed inward as if existence itself was being drained from him.","Noah gritted his teeth, feeling the agony through their bond that was there, and was not.","It wasn’t pain in any conventional sense...it was the sensation of becoming less while remaining aware of what you had lost. Like forgetting your own name while remembering that you once had one!","“This is what pure Hunger feels like,” Khor explained, her tone almost gentle despite the violence of what she was doing. “Imagine being thirsty, but for everything. Imagine starving, but food doesn’t exist yet. Imagine needing to breathe in an existence that hasn’t invented air.”","Ozymandias hung in the air, his form now truly skeletal, looking like death had died and left only its outline behind. Through their connection, Noah felt the overwhelming need radiating from his other self...not for anything specific, but for anything at all!","Sigrid watched with Order trying to understand what was happening and failing. “He... looks like he wants to die.”","“No,” Khor corrected. “He wants to live so badly that current existence isn’t enough. That’s the paradox of Inevitabilities...we hunger for everything because nothing satisfies.”","She raised her hands higher, and Ozymandias’s skeletal form began to pulse.","“But Hunger alone is just suffering without purpose. It needs guidance. Direction. A Way of Existence that transforms random want into inevitable consumption.” Her smile contained mysteries. “And that is something only I can provide. My gift to him...not my power, but my understanding of what Hunger means. The Way of Existence of Inevitabilities.”","...!","Obsidian brilliance erupted from her tiny form, a bundle of darkness so dense it made night jealous. It flowed upward into Ozymandias like inverse lightning, filling his skeletal frame with something that transcended substance.","|Doctrine of Hunger being inscribed|","|Subject gaining: The First Hunger’s Way of Existence|","|Transformation progressing beyond expected parameters|","|Complexity increasing:...+10,000,000,000...+10,000,000,000...|","|Purity increasing: +10,000,000,000...+10,000,000,000|","|Warning: Subject achieving true Inevitability status|","The change was immediate and terrible.","Ozymandias’s shriveled form began to shine with dark glory. From his spine, his ribs, his skull...dozens of black tentacles erupted. Not growing but declaring they had always existed, just waiting for permission to manifest.","Each tentacle moved with its own hunger, reaching for different aspects of reality. One grasped at space. Another tasted time. More emerged, seeking concepts that didn’t have names because naming them would limit what they could devour.","The tentacles multiplied...dozens becoming hundreds, hundreds becoming countless. They wrapped around each other, creating a circular mass of writhing hunger that radiated the unmistakable aura of an Inevitability.","“Beautiful,” Khor said, reaching up to stroke the scales that had begun forming on the tentacles. “A proper Inevitability. Not just hungry but inevitable. Not just wanting but destined to consume.”","The tentacles began compressing, drawing inward with purpose. They didn’t disappear but reformed, creating a humanoid shape from concentrated hunger. Arms made of need. Legs built from want. A torso of pure appetite.","When the transformation completed, Ozymandias stood transformed. Still recognizable but fundamentally changed. His obsidian form now contained depths that suggested falling forever toward a meal you’d never reach.","Noah closed his eyes, feeling through their connection what existence was like as an Inevitability.","Everything was brighter, more vivid, more real...because everything was potential food.","The air contained particles he could consume. The light carried energy he could devour. Even concepts like distance and duration looked delicious!","The world wasn’t just perceived but tasted, every sensation carrying flavor that normal beings couldn’t imagine.","The hunger was constant, overwhelming, defining...but also focusing.","It simplified existence to a single question: to devour or not to devour? And the answer was always yes, eventually!","HUUM!","|Transformation Complete|","|Ozymandias has become: Inevitability of Recursive Hunger|","|Classification: True Inevitability (Khor-doctrine)|","|Unique trait: Remains a part of Noah Osmont, and yet not|","|New Capabilities:|","|Everything Consumption: Can devour any type of Everything|","|Conversion rate: 100% of devoured Everything becomes CQ/PQ|","|Hunger Sense: Can detect Everything within vast distances|","|Inevitable Arrival: Will eventually reach anything he hungers for|","|Due to transformation effort observed by Perpetual Harvest:|","|Process has been optimized for stability|","|Bond with original maintained despite Inevitability status|","|Complexity gained: +50,000,000,000|","|Purity gained: +50,000,000,000|","|Note: You now have an Inevitability as part of yourself|","|Additional note: This is definitely going to complicate things|","...!","4/5"]},{"number":4100,"title":"Chapter 4100: Chapter 4099: The Purest Hunger! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4099: The Purest Hunger! III","Ozymandias stood complete, his form radiating the terrible certainty of something that would never stop hungering. Yet through their bond, Noah could feel something else...control.","His will still commanded this Inevitability, though now it was less like controlling a limb and more like directing a force of nature.","“How does it feel,” Khor asked with genuine curiosity, “to be both predator and prey? To hunger for everything while being everything others hunger for?”","Noah opened his eyes, meeting both Khor’s gaze and Ozymandias’s simultaneously.","“Like understanding why Inevitabilities terrify many Existences,” he replied.","Khor laughed with delight that made the Shore’s light flicker.","“Now you begin to understand, Outsider. Hunger isn’t evil. It’s just honest about what everything else pretends not to be...desperate to continue, willing to consume others to persist, inevitable in its need.”","She looked at Ozymandias with something approaching pride.","“Take care of him. Inevitabilities are like children...they need guidance, boundaries, and occasionally someone to tell them ‘no’ when they try to eat something important.”","...!","The humanoid tentacle form of Ozymandias opened its eyes fully, and reality took a step back.","Seas of stellar obsidian light surged around him like tides that had decided gravity was optional. His presence made the air itself reconsider whether it wanted to exist so close to something that might devour it.","Prompts cascaded before Noah’s vision with urgency that suggested even the system was struggling to process what had occurred!","|All Everythings Stripped Simultaneously from Ozymandias|","|Processing ramifications...|","|Everything of Limitations: REMOVED|","|Effect: No maximum capacity for consumption|","|Effect: No physical boundaries defining form|","|Effect: No temporal restrictions on existence|","|Warning: Without limits, growth has the potential to become cancerous|","|Warning: May consume self if external food depleted|","Noah walked closer to his transformed other self, gazing upward at the terrible beauty of what Ozymandias had become.","He read the prompts with fascination and gravity!","Khor stood nearby, her tiny form radiating satisfaction as she sighed and shook her head with the particular exhaustion of an artist who had just completed a masterpiece.","More prompts materialized, each one detailing a loss that was also transformation.","|Everything of Joy: REMOVED|","|Effect: Cannot experience a true sense of satisfaction from consumption|","|Effect: No pleasure delays the hunger|","|Warning: Endless consumption without reward|","|Note: Efficiency increased by 400%|","|Everything of Rage: REMOVED|","|Effect: Cannot be provoked to rash action|","|Effect: Consumption becomes mechanical, inevitable|","|Warning: No anger means no passion for protection|","|Note: Emotional volatility eliminated|","|Everything of Life: REMOVED|","|Effect: No biological needs or functions|","|Effect: Cannot be killed through conventional means|","|Warning: No growth through living experiences|","|Warning: Existence becomes static hunger|","|Everything of Death: REMOVED|","|Effect: Cannot cease through normal ending|","|Effect: Persistence beyond reasonable termination|","|Warning: No rest, no peace, no conclusion|","|Warning: May continue consuming after existence ends|","The implications stacked upon each other, each loss revealing itself as both liberation and curse.","Ozymandias had become pure in the way a blade was pure...excellent at one thing, not excellent for others!","|Final Assessment Complete|","|With all Everythings removed except Hunger|","|Through monumental effort witnessed and blessed|","|The Weavings of Ozymandias have achieved unprecedented purity|","|Current state: Unbearably pure existence|","|Option available: Convert all Complexity to Purity|","|This would create the purest Inevitability possible|","|Proceed? This action cannot be undone|","A question came.","And...","Noah didn’t hesitate.","“Proceed.”","HUUM!","The stellar obsidian sea around Ozymandias erupted with radiance that transcended light and dark. It became pure statement, pure existence, pure hunger given form.","|Conversion initiated...|","|All Complexity transformed to Purity|","|For Everythings given: +100 Billion Purity|","|For effort of the full transformation: +200 Billion Purity|","|For advancing to new Way of Existence under the guidance of the First Hunger: +200 Billion Purity|","|Total gained: 500,000,000,000 Purity|","|Complexity gained: 0|","|Ozymandias has become: The Purest Hunger|","BOOM!","The final form revealed itself as the light settled.","Ozymandias stood as architecture more than anatomy...a humanoid form crafted entirely from tentacles that had learned to pretend they were flesh.","Each tentacle moved with its own hunger while contributing to the whole, creating a body that was simultaneously singular and infinite.","Behind him stretched a single massive wing of obsidian-gold, not for flight but for statement...asymmetry that declared he needed no balance because hunger only moved forward.","From his head rose a crown of tentacles that formed a halo, each one reaching toward different concepts of consumption, creating a corona of need that cast shadows in dimensions that shouldn’t exist.","Noah felt through their connection the profound absence of everything except want.","No joy to color experience. No fear to provide caution. No hope to sustain through difficulty. No despair to acknowledge failure. Just hunger, pure and endless and honest.","There was something terrible and beautiful about such simplicity. No confusion, no doubt, no complex emotions to navigate. Just the eternal question of what to consume next and the certainty that something would be consumed.","“The Ways of Existence of many beings are unique but messy,” Khor said, her voice carrying the weight of having seen existence from its beginning.","“They want contradictory things. They hunger but feel guilty. They consume but apologize. They need but pretend they don’t.”","She gestured at Ozymandias with something approaching maternal pride.","“Inevitabilities are some of the purest Ways of Existence out there. We were pure. We were first. We knew what we were and never pretended otherwise.” Her expression grew more complex. “Everything that came after simply tainted this purity. Added complexity that made existence richer but less honest.”","As she spoke, she began twirling the Everythings she had stripped from Ozymandias.","They manifested as small orbs of condensed concept...Joy glowing warm yellow, Rage burning red, Life pulsing green, Death shimmering grey. They danced around her tiny fingers like candies made from fundamental forces.","“They thought they were improving on us by adding all these complications. Emotions to make consumption meaningful. Limits to make growth sustainable. Life and death to give existence rhythm.” She popped Joy into her mouth, chewing thoughtfully. “But all they did was make existence harder. More confusing. Less pure.”","She consumed Rage next, her expression suggesting it was spicy.","“Your Ozymandias is now what we once were...honest about existence’s fundamental truth. Everything consumes everything else. We just admitted it.”","Life went down with a satisfied hum. Death followed with a expression of finality.","“He’ll be magnificent and terrible. Efficient and empty. Perfect and broken.” She looked at Noah with eyes that contained eons of experience. “The question is: can you handle having part of yourself be that pure? Most beings go mad when they realize what existence looks like without all the pretty lies we tell ourselves.”","Noah felt through his connection to Ozymandias and found... nothing but hunger.","Not happiness...that required joy. Not satisfaction, that needed fulfillment. Just the hungering peace of absolute clarity, of knowing exactly what you were and accepting it completely.","“He’s... perfect,” Noah said quietly.","Khor smiled, swallowing the Everything of Limitations last.","“Of course he is. Hunger always is, until it runs out of food.”","...!","5/5 Idk why, but I really like Khor chapters","Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]}]);
